    {
      "id": "terminal-output.resize-parse-barrier",
      "title": "Resize preserves queued parse barriers and following terminal output",
      "maturity": "experimental",
      "protection": "none",
      "owner": "terminal-rendering",
      "layer": "renderer-unit-real-xterm",
      "surfaces": [
        "replay parse waits",
        "output scheduler parse waits",
        "write-pipeline health probes",
        "xterm resize"
      ],
      "platforms": ["macos", "linux", "windows"],
      "providers": ["local", "daemon", "ssh", "remote-runtime"],
      "coveredPlatforms": [],
      "coveredProviders": [],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit1342 intentionally deletes or reduces the listed sources. No fresh execution result validates their reduced selectors. Historical coverage account: Both installed browser and headless xterm packages run real parsing and resize with production replay, scheduler and health code. The shared renderer boundary applies to every provider and workspace kind; native Linux/Windows, live providers, mobile and rendered Electron acceptance are not exercised. Audit1342: src/renderer/src/lib/pane-manager/xterm-parse-barrier.test.ts reduced. Barrier callback/write order, replay/output waits, health probe and repeated-barrier inventory samples disappear. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed.",
      "motivatingLinks": [
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/issues/26950",
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/26956",
        "https://github.com/xtermjs/xterm.js/pull/6201"
      ],
      "invariant": "A resize must preserve every queued byte and invoke parse-barrier callbacks once in FIFO order. Replay and scheduler waits must finish from real parse progress, and a resized live parser must not be certified dead.",
      "oracle": "No current automated execution oracle is claimed for this gate after Audit1342 retired changed-source receipts. Historical oracle account: Queue a barrier between before and after output, resize synchronously, and require both lines and ordered callbacks. Require replay and scheduler waits before timers advance; require live health after the probe deadline. Preserve partial UTF-8 and escape sequences, repeated no-resize barriers and subsequent writes.",
      "commands": [],
      "testFiles": [],
      "assertionRefs": [],
      "evidenceRuns": [],
      "runtimeBudget": {
        "p95Seconds": 5,
        "scope": "Historical prior-selector budget; reduced selector has no new runtime measurement."
      },
      "flakeHistory": {
        "status": "not-started",
        "evidence": "Audit1342 retired changed-source receipts; reduced selector has no new soak result. Historical account: One local focused green run; no soak or cross-platform runtime history."
      },
      "redGreenEvidence": {
        "status": "missing",
        "evidence": "Audit1342 changed referenced test sources; no new red/green validation. Historical account: Current-main production replay, scheduler and health consumers independently fail six real-runtime boundary checks. In the refreshed candidate, replacing only the singleton byte marker with an empty string fails10 of12 checked-in assertions; restoring it passes all12."
      },
      "performanceBudget": {
        "required": true,
        "evidence": "Historical budget only after Audit1342 changed test sources; no new measurement. Previous account: One shared zero-byte array; no new timers, polling, subprocesses or output bytes. One hundred repeated barriers preserve FIFO without per-call marker allocations."
      },
      "promotionCriteria": [
        "Collect stable CI and soak history across macOS, Linux and Windows.",
        "Exercise real local, daemon, SSH and paired-runtime panes through resize and restore."
      ],
      "knownGaps": [
        "No DOM, GPU or rendered Electron validation.",
        "No native Linux/Windows or live provider exercise; mobile terminal implementation is unchanged.",
        "Daemon headless-emulator async fallback empty-string marker is outside this renderer change; its normal synchronous path bypasses that marker.",
        "Separate upstream consumed-prefix replay and async-parser resize defects remain outside this workaround.",
        "Audit1342: src/renderer/src/lib/pane-manager/xterm-parse-barrier.test.ts reduced. Barrier callback/write order, replay/output waits, health probe and repeated-barrier inventory samples disappear. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit1342 retires this complete dated receipt because a source in its selector was deleted or reduced. It does not validate the reduced selector. Original receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-10-23\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"command\": \"ORCA_BACKGROUND_LAUNCH=1 node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/lib/pane-manager/xterm-parse-barrier.test.ts\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 0.257,\n          \"summary\": \"12 tests pass against installed browser6.1.0-beta.304 and headless6.1.0-beta.303. Replacing only the helper marker with an empty string fails10 tests; the two no-resize controls still pass.\"\n        }",
        "Audit1342 historical platform/provider scope before source changes: {\"coveredPlatforms\":[\"macos\"],\"coveredProviders\":[]}. Remaining provider scope applies only to unchanged-source receipts.",
        "Audit1342 historical assertion inventory for deleted/reduced sources; not current validated assertions:\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/lib/pane-manager/xterm-parse-barrier.test.ts\",\n    \"assertions\": [\n      \"fires its callback and keeps the writes queued behind it\",\n      \"lets a replay wait settle without falling back to its stall probe\",\n      \"settles the output scheduler wait before its fallback timer\",\n      \"keeps a resized live terminal healthy after the probe deadline\",\n      \"preserves partial UTF-8 and escape sequences without writing marker bytes\",\n      \"completes repeated barriers without a resize and permits subsequent writes\"\n    ]\n  }\n]",
        "Retired selector metadata during audit1345; historical selector record preserved unchanged: {\"commands\":[\"ORCA_BACKGROUND_LAUNCH=1 node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/lib/pane-manager/xterm-parse-barrier.test.ts\"],\"testFiles\":[\"src/renderer/src/lib/pane-manager/xterm-parse-barrier.test.ts\"],\"assertionRefs\":[]}"
