      "coverageNotes": "Audit3984 retires all four remaining viewport-fixture suites (14 authored/15 finite cases) and the fixture after composing the sender-host deletion. Accepted source-alarm losses include live-region/disclosure continuity, task/question/approval history and revision handling, stale turn status, prompt-dismissal remount/rebind, and pending-send cancellation when approval arrives between body and Enter. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime validation is claimed. Audits3764/3766 retire16 authored/27 expanded mobile cases, including entire HTML-image syntax, Mermaid routing, table styles, file-query encoding, workspace naming and fresh-Git-status adapter suites. Accepted losses include image width/icon filtering, partial-heading streaming, mocked Mermaid key/identity checks, generated table widths/counts, selected-text caret placement, tiny Base64 chunk encoding, twelve query-path roundtrips, locale-import fallback, apostrophe slugging, fresh-status fallback and an intermediate reviewed marker. These are deliberate removals for marginal value; remaining tests are not equivalent replacements. Earlier receipts are historical and do not validate these deleted/reduced drivers. Audit3748 intentionally removes ten authored/ten finite registrations from the surviving media-handle-registry.test.ts driver selected by this full-mobile command. Retired real alarms: nominal minted handle uniqueness/metadata and dimensions; ordinary range/EOF/overread/empty-file/direct chunk-clamp samples; nominal successful release, expired-release false, exact millisecond TTL boundary and ordinary releaseAll replay. Deterministic registry code runs; these examples are removed on marginal value without replacement or fresh execution claims. Seven owner cases retain cap refusal/disposal and sweep-before-admission, nonempty EOF and unknown/released/expired refusal, read TTL refresh, idempotent explicit release and continuation after discard failure. Existing commands, assertions, unrelated wire receipt and timing remain; the driver survives. Audits3738/3742/3743/3744 intentionally remove15 authored/21 finite registrations from six surviving drivers, with no equivalent replacement or fresh execution claim. This gate retains an unfiltered mobile Vitest command. Its mobile/src include patterns admit the partial live-input-commit and native-media drivers:5 authored/5 finite removals. Accepted losses: two Android-labeled replay samples after mocked composition conversion, an immediate Backspace absence check that does not wait for pending commit or prove local edit, and released-handle/double-release adapter examples. Real hook, registry and adapter logic run; no equivalent replacement or native Android/iOS exercise is claimed. Both drivers and selector stay. The unchanged wire-specific dated receipt does not validate these reduced mobile sources. Audit3666 removes30 authored/36 finite mobile cases, including7 whole drivers. It retires direct consent/channel/token/header-payload/fingerprint/route-object inventories, background legacy-dismissal filtering, the two-row520-entry watermark retention workload, reentrant write-batch example, font-before-ready projection, and legacy-segmenter/scrollback/wrap selection examples. Actual policy, parsing, hashing, tray matching, serialization and xterm buffers execute in these tests; their stated alarms are deliberately lost without replacement. Twelve unchanged authored/19 finite cases retain compact browser geometry regressions, an independent fingerprint-to-host protocol vector, serialized watermark/reload isolation, OSC52 live/replay gating, queue boundaries/reset/generation, disposed font completion and Unicode cell mapping. Pairing classification2/2 was already approved by3657 and receives no3666 delta or credit. Static review only; no runtime, native, provider, browser rendering, OS, remote, mobile/folder parity or new historical fault evidence. Previous account (preserved verbatim): Audit3663 removes the complete mobile scan-error message suite (two authored/two finite callbacks). Its4URL assertion loop is one registration. Accept loss of Orca new/legacy Android-download URL classification and other-page invalid-code translated-key mapping. Real URL parsing/classification runs, but the only output observed is an identity-translator key. No camera scan, pairing offer admission, connection or device/UI action is exercised. No equivalent replacement or physical/mobile/mixed-version result claimed. Preserve all historical evidence and metadata bytes. Audit3460 final-v2 composes accepted AUTHOR3454/PEER3455 on actual post263 main: intentionally removes99 authored/106 potential expanded cases across16 selected drivers, including7 whole suites, retaining24 authored/26 potential cases. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime is claimed. The broad mobile runner loses retired-name sequencing and PR action samples while retaining the editor-lifetime and original PR action keeper; commit-message generation is unchanged. Audit3456 composes ROOT-adopted3449/independent3450: intentionally removes62 authored/82 potential expanded cases from16 selected drivers, including7 whole suites, while13 authored/13 potential cases remain. Delete the unused48line legacy workspace-session JSON fixture with zero test credit. These are source-only reductions without equivalent replacement or fresh runtime claims. The broad mobile command loses the entire three-case mocked diff-review controller suite and the stale layout-sequence comparator sample. Keep only the direct layout-versus-scrollback counter distinction; the unchanged dictation retry hook retains complete recording replay. No rendered app, native capture, actual process death or remote execution is claimed. Audit3451 composes ROOT-adopted3444/independent3445: intentionally removes101 authored registrations across16 reviewed sources, deleting7 whole suites and reducing8; one reviewed source is unchanged. Fresh main has123 authored registrations before and22 after because an upstream direct-child shell regression remains verbatim with zero removal credit. Registered removals are100+7*S and explicit-active removals99+7*S, where S is the unprobed count0..3 of admitted bash/zsh/fish shells. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Broad mobile discovery loses whole prompt-presentation, Jira-URL and folder-source-repository suites. The prompt suite exercised presentation projections; it did not provide native mobile prompt acknowledgment acceptance. Existing direct prompt-controller selectors are unchanged. Audit3425 composes root-adopted3420/independent3421: intentionally removes83 authored/112 potential expanded registrations across13 semantic sources, deleting7 whole conventional suites and1 registering helper;7 authored/10 potential expanded cases remain. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. The stale-leaf-liveness suite and its exact command/testFiles selector are removed; its fake terminal refusal/liveness alarms are intentionally lost. Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The entire mocked mobile failure-banner suite and its sole send/previous-banner/new-notice ordering alarm are retired. Its filenames are removed from active selectors. Desktop prompt roots and the independent unchanged terminal wire-codec receipt remain at their stated scopes; no mobile send/recovery proof is claimed.  Audit2251 narrows agent-paste-draft.test.ts from 25 authored cases (26 literal cases) to four. Retained cases cover buffered readiness on PTY binding, separate spawn/composer lifetimes, real per-PTY paste/Enter serialization against a competing paste, and frame closure/no Enter after a rejected content chunk. Intentionally lost alarms include agent marker and fallback examples, direct-write failure/rejection, missing-PTY and Codex process-only timeout paths, exact nonprimary-PTY routing, full large-body chunk reconstruction, escaping/CRLF samples, internal laziness/yield work assertions, oversized preflight refusal, and exact configured delay/budget counts. No equivalent replacement, new execution, real PTY/provider delivery, rendered/native UI, deployment, measured performance or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Mobile owner-layout policy retires whole tests and mixed registrations without equivalent replacement coverage. Retained callbacks and reduced selectors need fresh execution at their stated scope; prior measurements do not validate them. Affected sources: mobile/src/session/mobile-prompt-controller.test.ts, tests/e2e/native-chat-ssh-delivery.unit.test.ts, mobile/src/session/native-chat/use-mobile-native-chat-controller.test.ts, mobile/src/session/native-chat/input/use-mobile-native-chat-cancel-ask.test.ts, mobile/src/session/native-chat/input/use-mobile-native-chat-answer-send.test.ts, mobile/src/session/native-chat/transcript/use-mobile-native-chat-message-send.test.ts. Historical scope: Audit2003: Remove agent-prompt absence routing, throwing/live/missing-probe and cached-probe-count examples from the stale-leaf source. Controller-proven absence, unknown-liveness admission, obsolete-absence clearing and same-ID respawn fences remain at a supplied provider/row seam. Preserve the independent wire-codec receipt only in its original scope. Changed-source prior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, physical provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1991: Remove partial-runtime terminal-send guard/status/floor/query projection and argument-inventory samples. Retained RPC viewport admission, authenticated-client spoof refusal, text admission and stale-binding fences remain bounded mock-boundary behavior. The unchanged wire-codec receipt remains valid only for its original command; it does not validate this reduced RPC selector. Changed-source prior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, physical provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1908 removes the complete prompt-presentation hook and literal interactive-protocol mapping suites and narrows the interactive card and prompt-card input suites. Lost alarms include replacement approval A settling after answered B; collapse/expand composer ownership and partial-answer presentation; identical new waits after an unmounted view; collapsed transcript re-reads; answered/dismissed status-backed persistence and retirement; and literal answer-to-PTY byte arrays. The retained stale-PTY acknowledgment, cancellation/answer retry, and answered-approval remount/rebind assertions remain meaningful but are not equivalent replacement coverage. No fresh reduced-selector result, physical provider, rendered/native-focus, mixed-version deployment, soak, or measured-budget validation is claimed. The unchanged wire-codec receipt remains valid only for its exact command. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1640 removes low-value IPC, SSH, workspace and transcript-watcher tests without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public refusal, cancellation, execution-host and real-filesystem outcomes with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1471 removes the entire interactive-send hook suite. Its mock-writer routing, cancellation-handle, option-digit, interrupt, supplied settlement and inference-argument alarms are retired. No actual PTY bytes, replacement question lifetime or agent delivery were exercised. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution of the reduced reliability selector is claimed; historical receipts retain their original scope. Audit1468 removes the entire runtime-send suite. Its mock PTY clear/body/Enter byte-order, nominal timing, queue cancellation/serialization, attachment escaping, key-group pacing and deferred acceptance callback alarms are intentionally retired. No actual receiving agent or physical terminal delivery was exercised. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution of the reduced reliability selector is claimed; historical receipts retain their original scope. Retained exact unchanged-source receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Reduced selectors have no fresh execution result. Audit1417 intentionally reduces src/renderer/src/lib/agent-paste-draft-submit-retry.test.ts: Loses configured retry gap and single-Enter agent selection alarms alongside forbidden timer-count checks. No equivalent replacement coverage or fresh result is claimed. Historical coverage account: Audit1383 changes referenced sources; no new execution result validates reduced selectors. Retained unchanged receipts apply only to unchanged commands. Historical coverage: Audits1340 and1348 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Audit1316 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Production mobile controller, parser, presentation, overlay, view, question, permission and composer run with native surfaces mocked on macOS. Desktop selector groups traverse the real observed-write queue, verified helper, IPC chunker, SSH provider and transport callbacks; paired sends traverse the real dispatcher and runtime writer into that provider. Local/daemon contracts and released-version terminal codecs are covered. Provider labels describe contracts, not physical deployments; physical WSL/Linux/Windows remain gaps. Audit885 removes the isolated observed-send mock-call suite; no replacement-equivalence claim is made. Audit1107 removes the small healthy ordinary SSH-send byte/callback sample. Its exact clear/body/Enter sample alarm is lost; retained slow-answer, cancellation and simulated older-host sequence checks are not claimed as equivalent replacement coverage. The SSH delivery fixture uses controlled fake provider settlement, and its paired path uses the real runtime/dispatcher without a physical SSH or paired wire transport. Audit1278 removes the mobile Stop display/disabled/placeholder suite; its local Stop presentation, repeat-stop and dispatch-visibility alarms are intentionally lost. No equivalent replacement or runtime stopping proof is claimed. Audit1292: The blind OpenCode readiness warning and late launch success/failure content-plus-submit write samples are removed. Their mocked readiness/inspection/delivery alarms are lost; no real PTY delivery or equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1294 removes mobile/src/session/native-chat/input/mobile-native-chat-permission-send.test.ts. Its mock-only request/capability/private-state/copy alarms are intentionally lost. Remaining tests are not equivalent replacement coverage. Narrowed commands require fresh parent-owned validation; no new runtime, platform or physical mobile evidence is claimed. Audit1302: src/main/ipc/pty/ipc/write-input-acceptance.test.ts: Provider registry and write acceptance/refusal/unverifiable receipts are supplied by fixture; local/daemon/WSL/SSH labels use the same fake provider. Chunking/settlement/remount cases inspect delegated calls or canned receipts without actual provider acceptance/acknowledgement. Lose chunk/refusal/pending/remount and raw-pane routing alarms; no equivalent replacement. Reduced selectors require fresh validation; prior full-suite receipts do not validate removed or changed coverage. No equivalent replacement or physical-provider claim. Audit1303 intentionally removes supplied-state/mock-callback component and hook examples in mobile/src/session/native-chat/input/use-mobile-native-chat-ask-dismiss.test.ts, mobile/src/session/native-chat/input/MobileNativeChatPromptCard.test.tsx. Their exact retired alarms are not equivalent to retained coverage; no new runtime, physical phone or deployed mixed-version evidence is claimed. Audit1310 removes the supplied-geometry/direct-callback chat history-paging suite. Its prepend/scroll-position examples are intentionally lost; no real rendered anchoring, equivalent replacement or physical phone proof is claimed. Narrowed commands need fresh validation. Audit1315 removes/narrows mobile/src/session/native-chat/MobileNativeChatView.composer-lock.test.ts, mobile/src/session/native-chat/MobileNativeChatView.prompt-presentation.test.ts. Exact retired scenarios are intentionally lost; surviving assertions are limited to unchanged retained authored cases. No equivalent replacement, physical phone or deployed mixed-host claim. Fresh validation is required for narrowed commands. Audit1316: src/renderer/src/lib/agent-followup-delivery.test.ts removed. Interpreter wrapper/live child/shell readiness and final readiness recheck delivery mock samples lose alarms. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1322 removes/narrows mobile/src/session/native-chat/MobileNativeChatView.tail-follow.test.ts. Exact retired scenarios are intentionally lost; surviving assertions are limited to unchanged retained authored cases. No equivalent replacement, physical phone or deployed mixed-host claim. Fresh validation is required for narrowed commands. Audit1341 scope1334 removes/narrows mobile/src/session/native-chat/mobile-native-chat-send.test.ts, mobile/src/session/native-chat/transcript/use-mobile-native-chat-message-send.test.ts. Exact retired scenarios are intentionally lost; surviving assertions are limited to unchanged retained authored cases. No equivalent replacement, physical phone or deployed mixed-host claim. Fresh validation is required for narrowed commands. Audit1341 scope1335 removes/narrows mobile/src/session/native-chat/use-mobile-native-chat-controller.test.ts, mobile/src/session/mobile-prompt-controller.test.ts, mobile/src/session/native-chat/input/use-mobile-native-chat-answer-send.test.ts. Exact retired scenarios are intentionally lost; surviving assertions are limited to unchanged retained authored cases. No equivalent replacement, physical phone or deployed mixed-host claim. Fresh validation is required for narrowed commands. Audit1340: src/main/daemon/daemon-pty-write-settlement-recovery.test.ts removed. Ambiguous handoff settlement remains unverifiable when listener throws. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1348: src/main/ipc/pty/ipc/write-input-chunk-yield.test.ts removed. Check-phase yielding and no-yield single-chunk scheduling work. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1352: focused Linux unit selections validated on source head b638e07d395b76af3ba6b03761a1a0fe7e5e026e. Historical statements above retain their original scope. Intentional test losses are recorded in knownGaps; these runs claim no physical-provider, p95, rendered E2E or cross-platform validation. Audit1360: focused Linux unit selections validated on source head 415c9cffc2d10024131ec4b6721767a22195de6d. Historical statements above retain their original scope. Intentional test losses are recorded in knownGaps; these runs claim no physical-provider, p95, rendered E2E or cross-platform validation. Audit1383: src/main/ipc/pty/ipc/write-input-user-input.test.ts reduced. Lose admission provenance spy, direct local Escape write outcome matrix and separate client-side SSH no-evidence control. Provider writes mocked; retained tests protect observation order/facts only. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1401: src/main/ipc/pty/ipc/write-input-user-input.test.ts reduced. Loses local-only post-accept observation and refused/unverifiable settlement delivery alarms. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected receipts remain unchanged and apply only to their unchanged selectors. Changed optional selectors have no new execution result. Audit1402: src/renderer/src/components/native-chat/native-chat-runtime-send-launch-draft.test.ts removed. Intentionally loses clear-confirmation/body/submit and maximal-clear ordering, queued text/image send ordering, ordinary cursor-spanning draft replacement and oversized refusal/queue settlement alarms. No equivalent replacement or real terminal delivery claim. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected receipts remain unchanged and apply only to their unchanged selectors. Changed optional selectors have no new execution result. Audit1426 removes NativeChatComposer.test.tsx. Local pane-remount, draft/cancel/confirmation sequencing and manual IME callback alarms are lost. No equivalent replacement coverage or provider delivery is claimed; historical receipts retain their original scope and the reduced selector has no new execution result. Audit2450 removes the MobileNativeChatView failure-banner callback-only example whose old banner is supplied unchanged by its props. Retain fatal-read gating and the ordering test that preserves a new delivery notice. The removed false-send/old-banner combination has no equivalent replacement; prior raw receipts and budgets retain their original source scope. No new soak, platform, performance or red/green claim.",
      "motivatingLinks": ["https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/25761"],
      "invariant": "A prompt occurrence leaves the input region only when an accepted reply answers it (a current host's provider acknowledgment, or an older host's whole-write acceptance as before) or the user collapses it to a strip above the composer, which writes nothing and keeps the card mounted with its partial answer; status-backed occurrences are told apart by the host wait's start, so view toggles and remounts preserve them while real clear/replacement supersedes them, and a transcript-only one is dropped when the view stops observing it; obsolete results cannot change replacements; selector groups wait for complete writes before pacing; refusal or unknown handoff never causes replay; a card retires an unsubmitted composer send without writing under it or losing its text, and the hidden composer cannot send or interrupt; Collapse or Escape folds a card without writing, never during an in-flight answer, and a new occurrence shows expanded again; the phone blocks only Send while a card is expanded and shows one card per occurrence; cancellation stops unsent groups and active dictation can stop.",
      "oracle": "Audits3764/3766 retire16 authored/27 expanded mobile cases, including entire HTML-image syntax, Mermaid routing, table styles, file-query encoding, workspace naming and fresh-Git-status adapter suites. Accepted losses include image width/icon filtering, partial-heading streaming, mocked Mermaid key/identity checks, generated table widths/counts, selected-text caret placement, tiny Base64 chunk encoding, twelve query-path roundtrips, locale-import fallback, apostrophe slugging, fresh-status fallback and an intermediate reviewed marker. These are deliberate removals for marginal value; remaining tests are not equivalent replacements. Earlier receipts are historical and do not validate these deleted/reduced drivers. Audit3748 intentionally removes ten authored/ten finite registrations from the surviving media-handle-registry.test.ts driver selected by this full-mobile command. Retired real alarms: nominal minted handle uniqueness/metadata and dimensions; ordinary range/EOF/overread/empty-file/direct chunk-clamp samples; nominal successful release, expired-release false, exact millisecond TTL boundary and ordinary releaseAll replay. Deterministic registry code runs; these examples are removed on marginal value without replacement or fresh execution claims. Seven owner cases retain cap refusal/disposal and sweep-before-admission, nonempty EOF and unknown/released/expired refusal, read TTL refresh, idempotent explicit release and continuation after discard failure. Existing commands, assertions, unrelated wire receipt and timing remain; the driver survives. Audits3738/3742/3743/3744 intentionally remove15 authored/21 finite registrations from six surviving drivers, with no equivalent replacement or fresh execution claim. This gate retains an unfiltered mobile Vitest command. Its mobile/src include patterns admit the partial live-input-commit and native-media drivers:5 authored/5 finite removals. Accepted losses: two Android-labeled replay samples after mo