older host's accepted reply dismisses like an acknowledged one; a same-occurrence view toggle retains pending acknowledgment and real replacements discard it. A slow 32 KiB SSH answer completes all chunks before Enter; cancellation preserves issued bytes but omits remaining groups. Paired settlement invokes the actual provider and lost callbacks remain unknown; older hosts deliver ordinary messages, launch and selector groups once and their accepted answers dismiss as before. An answered card stays hidden across a view remount; a collapsed card is a strip that frees the composer and expands back; an identical question in a new wait shows again; a composer send caught by a new card keeps its bubble without submitting or clearing the line under it. Audit2450 removes the MobileNativeChatView failure-banner callback-only example whose old banner is supplied unchanged by its props. Retain fatal-read gating and the ordering test that preserves a new delivery notice. The removed false-send/old-banner combination has no equivalent replacement; prior raw receipts and budgets retain their original source scope. No new soak, platform, performance or red/green claim.",
