        "Audits3764/3766 retire16 authored/27 expanded mobile cases, including entire HTML-image syntax, Mermaid routing, table styles, file-query encoding, workspace naming and fresh-Git-status adapter suites. Accepted losses include image width/icon filtering, partial-heading streaming, mocked Mermaid key/identity checks, generated table widths/counts, selected-text caret placement, tiny Base64 chunk encoding, twelve query-path roundtrips, locale-import fallback, apostrophe slugging, fresh-status fallback and an intermediate reviewed marker. These are deliberate removals for marginal value; remaining tests are not equivalent replacements. Earlier receipts are historical and do not validate these deleted/reduced drivers.",
        "Audit3748 intentionally removes ten authored/ten finite registrations from the surviving media-handle-registry.test.ts driver selected by this full-mobile command. Retired real alarms: nominal minted handle uniqueness/metadata and dimensions; ordinary range/EOF/overread/empty-file/direct chunk-clamp samples; nominal successful release, expired-release false, exact millisecond TTL boundary and ordinary releaseAll replay. Deterministic registry code runs; these examples are removed on marginal value without replacement or fresh execution claims. Seven owner cases retain cap refusal/disposal and sweep-before-admission, nonempty EOF and unknown/released/expired refusal, read TTL refresh, idempotent explicit release and continuation after discard failure. Existing commands, assertions, unrelated wire receipt and timing remain; the driver survives.",
        "Audits3738/3742/3743/3744 intentionally remove15 authored/21 finite registrations from six surviving drivers, with no equivalent replacement or fresh execution claim. This gate retains an unfiltered mobile Vitest command. Its mobile/src include patterns admit the partial live-input-commit and native-media drivers:5 authored/5 finite removals. Accepted losses: two Android-labeled replay samples after mocked composition conversion, an immediate Backspace absence check that does not wait for pending commit or prove local edit, and released-handle/double-release adapter examples. Real hook, registry and adapter logic run; no equivalent replacement or native Android/iOS exercise is claimed. Both drivers and selector stay. The unchanged wire-specific dated receipt does not validate these reduced mobile sources.",
        "Audit3666 removes30 authored/36 finite mobile cases, including7 whole drivers. It retires direct consent/channel/token/header-payload/fingerprint/route-object inventories, background legacy-dismissal filtering, the two-row520-entry watermark retention workload, reentrant write-batch example, font-before-ready projection, and legacy-segmenter/scrollback/wrap selection examples. Actual policy, parsing, hashing, tray matching, serialization and xterm buffers execute in these tests; their stated alarms are deliberately lost without replacement. Twelve unchanged authored/19 finite cases retain compact browser geometry regressions, an independent fingerprint-to-host protocol vector, serialized watermark/reload isolation, OSC52 live/replay gating, queue boundaries/reset/generation, disposed font completion and Unicode cell mapping. Pairing classification2/2 was already approved by3657 and receives no3666 delta or credit. Static review only; no runtime, native, provider, browser rendering, OS, remote, mobile/folder parity or new historical fault evidence.",
        "Audit3663 removes the complete mobile scan-error message suite (two authored/two finite callbacks). Its4URL assertion loop is one registration. Accept loss of Orca new/legacy Android-download URL classification and other-page invalid-code translated-key mapping. Real URL parsing/classification runs, but the only output observed is an identity-translator key. No camera scan, pairing offer admission, connection or device/UI action is exercised. No equivalent replacement or physical/mobile/mixed-version result claimed. Preserve all historical evidence and metadata bytes.",
