    {
      "id": "agent-status.claude-task-wakeup-cycle",
      "title": "Claude task wake-ups cannot finish an automation before its lead turn",
      "maturity": "experimental",
      "protection": "none",
      "owner": "agent-status",
      "layer": "execution-host-hooks-and-runtime-wait",
      "surfaces": [
        "canonical agent status",
        "terminal automation completion",
        "local and relayed cancellation"
      ],
      "platforms": ["macos", "linux", "windows"],
      "providers": ["local", "ssh", "wsl", "remote-runtime"],
      "coveredPlatforms": [],
      "coveredProviders": [],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit1401 intentionally deletes or reduces the listed sources. No fresh execution result validates their reduced selectors. Historical coverage account: The reduced six-file selector passed 125 cases on Linux, exercising real HTTP hook ingress and the existing runtime automation observer. SSH/WSL ownership remains simulated; no physical remote-host, native macOS/Windows, task capacity or timer/resource-budget claim. Audit1318: src/shared/agent-hook-listener/normalization/agent-hook-listener-claude-task-notification.test.ts: Hand-built task notifications/cap inventories plus a manually assembled normalize/cache/expiry-timer host run under fake clocks with production lease constants and private state. No actual main/relay entry or provider delivery. Intentionally lose owed-task/Monitor/teammate/reset/notification expiry and cancellation-restatement alarms; no equivalent replacement claimed. Reduced selectors need fresh validation; historical full-suite receipts do not validate the changed coverage. No equivalent replacement or physical-provider claim. Audit1401: src/main/ssh/ssh-agent-hook-interrupt-reconciliation.test.ts removed. Loses current-host proof, foreign/disposed/unsubscribed and legacy interrupt dispatch fence alarms. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed.",
      "motivatingLinks": [
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/24878",
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/issues/23942"
      ],
      "invariant": "An ended tracked task stays pending until its wake-up and finishing turn end; missing wake-ups expire only after 60 idle seconds. Cancellation remains owned by the executing host, duplicate delivery cannot create a fresh completion veto, and fresh native rest can recover a lost finishing Stop.",
      "oracle": "No current automated execution oracle is claimed for this gate after Audit1401 retired changed-source receipts. Historical oracle account: Replay captured hook ordering through production HTTP entry points and native ready bytes through the actual automation observer. Check local/relay state, cancellation/new-turn fencing, fresh versus retained rest, zero global status reads during indexed runtime waits.",
      "commands": [],
      "testFiles": [],
      "assertionRefs": [],
      "evidenceRuns": [],
