    {
      "id": "runtime.connection-owned-host-status",
      "title": "Host status recovers with its owning connection",
      "maturity": "experimental",
      "protection": "partial",
      "owner": "runtime",
      "layer": "service-integration-and-e2e",
      "surfaces": [
        "sidebar host status",
        "desktop runtime connection",
        "browser primary connection"
      ],
      "platforms": ["macos", "linux", "windows"],
      "providers": ["remote-runtime"],
      "coveredPlatforms": ["macos"],
      "coveredProviders": [],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit 3301 removes the failed-verification/recovery/restart generation and host-contact-epoch, hosting and no-toast example from runtime-status-snapshot.test.ts. Earlier prose describing that example as retained is historical. Disconnect/pairing retirement and delayed catalog replay remain unchanged without equivalent replacement. Archive both complete historical 22-case unit receipts because their selector includes the reduced source; preserve the unrelated rendered receipt, current selectors and other-owner assertion references. No fresh aggregate or live host validation is claimed. Linux coverage from those two unit runs is historical; current covered-platform scope is limited to the preserved macOS rendered receipt. Audit1348 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Real authenticated sockets plus isolated desktop and headless hosts with desktop and browser viewers; deterministic lifecycle tests cover stale results and reader deadlines. The test-value audit removes the standalone runtime-status-snapshot.test.ts example that immediately applied the same supplied snapshots to two isolated slice stores. Its direct sequence-2 then older unavailable sequence-1 acceptance/rejection alarm is intentionally lost; it did not exercise a pending read, subscription delivery or a shared viewer connection. The suite retains failed-verification/recovery, disconnect/pairing retirement and catalog-refresh replay examples, which are not equivalent replacements. Historical executed commands, counts and results remain unchanged; no new live host, process restart or platform evidence is claimed. Audit1348: src/main/ipc/runtime-environments/runtime-environment-status-recovery.test.ts removed. Startup retry/broadcast counts and passive-before-active bootstrap request count. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1352: focused Linux unit selections validated on source head b638e07d395b76af3ba6b03761a1a0fe7e5e026e. Historical statements above retain their original scope. Intentional test losses are recorded in knownGaps; these runs claim no physical-provider, p95, rendered E2E or cross-platform validation. The current assertion index names unchanged owner lifecycle tests from the successful focused run. They do not replace the deleted startup retry/broadcast count alarms. Audit1360: focused Linux unit selections validated on source head 415c9cffc2d10024131ec4b6721767a22195de6d. Historical statements above retain their original scope. Intentional test losses are recorded in knownGaps; these runs claim no physical-provider, p95, rendered E2E or cross-platform validation. Audit1748 removes7 of13 authored host-status-owner definitions: request/polling counts, reconnect/no-request variants, deadline copy and blocked-reason projections. Lost alarms are intentional; no equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing dated evidenceRuns are historical and unchanged, and do not validate this reduced source or current aggregate selectors. Focused candidate execution, if successful, validates only the retained local fake-request/clock tests, not authenticated sockets, rendered clients or platform parity.",
      "motivatingLinks": ["https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/19163"],
      "invariant": "Failed bootstrap and authenticated reconnect converge without UI triggers; one connection owner publishes verified status, with no independent healthy status polling.",
      "oracle": "Audit 3301 removes the failed-verification/recovery/restart generation and host-contact-epoch, hosting and no-toast example from runtime-status-snapshot.test.ts. Earlier prose describing that example as retained is historical. Disconnect/pairing retirement and delayed catalog replay remain unchanged without equivalent replacement. Archive both complete historical 22-case unit receipts because their selector includes the reduced source; preserve the unrelated rendered receipt, current selectors and other-owner assertion references. No fresh aggregate or live host validation is claimed. Linux coverage from those two unit runs is historical; current covered-platform scope is limited to the preserved macOS rendered receipt. Retained local cases check independent waiter deadlines/cancellation, failed-operation recovery, stale deferred results, disposal and explicit reconnect after authentication refusal. Historical aggregate receipts predate audit1748 and are not fresh validation of reduced sources.",
