      "coverageNotes": "Audit1379 changes src/main/native-chat/agent-session-journal/journal-atomic-settlement-oversized.spec.ts (1 authored registrations removed; 1 retained); src/main/native-chat/agent-session-journal/queued-message-edit-leases.test.ts (10 authored registrations removed; 1 retained); src/main/native-chat/agent-session-journal/journal-subagent-item.spec.ts (4 authored registrations removed; 1 retained). Intentional losses: Loses production batch-cap/cursor-count fallback expectations; retained case checks real database rollback and successful retry, with once-per-startup variants. Intentionally removes 10 authored registrations: 'a repeated acquire answers the same lease without extending it'; 'acquire refuses a card that is gone or whose text moved on'; 'reuses an edit key only after its previous target becomes invalid'; 'expires on its own and wakes the queue with no other activity'; 'renewal extends the deadline; a lapsed lease is not revived'; 'release frees only the exact caller and edit, never another editor on the same card'; 'every read re-derives: a card whose %s holds nothing'; 'a save retires every lease on the card; others stay'; 'reads the rows it is given inside a transaction'; 'dispose drops every lease and deadline; a closed handle grants none'. Retained focused cases are not claimed as equivalent replacement for these losses. Loses identity/schema/constant/field-bound and generic revision/turnScope persistence controls; retained recovery checks structured and legacy text twins. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. No passed current receipt validates the reduced selector. Historical coverage account: The real SQLite journal and production subscriber delivery are exercised with a folder workspace and remote host identity. The SQL and pagination code is shared across execution hosts; live SSH transport and Linux/Windows runtime execution are not exercised. PTY, daemon, WSL execution, and mobile rendering are unaffected. Test