      "coverageNotes": "Audit3368 retires the whole hibernation coordinator suite and intentionally loses supplied inventory/liveness/attention/confirmation/changed-workspace/sequential teardown alarms without equivalent replacement. The sole compound dated receipt is retired verbatim; no shortened command inherits its results. With no active evidence, protection/platform/provider evidence clears and ALL current commands/testFiles/assertionRefs are retired as complete original arrays in historical gaps. Other source files remain in the broad suite. Prior red/green/flake accounts are historical only; no fresh runtime/provider/UI/mobile/mixed-version/cross-platform evidence is claimed. Audit2058 intentionally retires the standalone visibility subscription/callback-count alarm without replacement. Audit2310 additionally retires two pane-age getter-map expiry/pruning samples without equivalent replacement. The reduced five-source hibernation selector was freshly run on Linux:52 tests pass. The earlier 54-test receipt is archived verbatim in knownGaps and does not validate the reduced source. Its prior macOS execution receipt/current-command association is archived verbatim in knownGaps and is not current execution evidence for the reduced selector. Current covered platform is Linux; remote replies remain scripted, with no live SSH/WSL/native provider or p95 claim. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Local hibernation, remote inventory authority and folder-workspace identity are covered by coordinator/model contracts on macOS. Daemon, SSH, WSL, relay and native platform execution boundaries and existing RPC payloads are unchanged. Current assertions cover shutdown safety and owning-host selection; historical inventory-count and performance evidence below is retained for provenance and is not current count coverage.",
      "motivatingLinks": [
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/blob/main/src/renderer/src/lib/agent-hibernation-coordinator.test.ts"
      ],
      "invariant": "Automatic hibernation must retain two stable confirmations and fresh execution-host evidence before shutdown. Skipping a workspace with no completed agent must not authorize a newly completed pane using stale client PTYs.",
      "oracle": "Audit3368 retires the whole hibernation coordinator suite and intentionally loses supplied inventory/liveness/attention/confirmation/changed-workspace/sequential teardown alarms without equivalent replacement. The sole compound dated receipt is retired verbatim; no shortened command inherits its results. With no active evidence, protection/platform/provider evidence clears and ALL current commands/testFiles/assertionRefs are retired as complete original arrays in historical gaps. Other source files remain in the broad suite. Prior red/green/flake accounts are historical only; no fresh runtime/provider/UI/mobile/mixed-version/cross-platform evidence is claimed. Audit2058 intentionally retires the standalone visibility subscription/callback-count alarm without replacement. Audit2310 additionally retires two pane-age getter-map expiry/pruning samples without equivalent replacement. The reduced five-source hibernation selector was freshly run on Linux:52 tests pass. The earlier 54-test receipt is archived verbatim in knownGaps and does not validate the reduced source. Its prior macOS execution receipt/current-command association is archived verbatim in knownGaps and is not current execution evidence for the reduced selector. Current covered platform is Linux; remote replies remain scripted, with no live SSH/WSL/native provider or p95 claim. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Working and waiting agents across remote workspaces must not be shut down. A skipped workspace completing while another inventory awaits remains ineligible until two later host-confirmed passes, and so does a workspace that only becomes runtime-owned while an inventory is outstanding — a pass carrying no host evidence for a workspace never counts as one of its two confirmations. Folder and git workspaces hibernate the exact host PTY; rejected/truncated inventories and intervening input/output or state changes block shutdown.",
      "commands": [],
      "testFiles": [],
      "assertionRefs": [],
      "evidenceRuns": [],
