        "Audit1939 (sources1934/1935): The existing directory-level pnpm test selector includes eleven changed source files and automatically omits the three whole deletions. Keep this nonempty discovery command unchanged; no dated receipt uses this broad path. Removed agent admission fields, mock transport routing and terminal-id projection alarms are lost. Retained foreground state, actual headless xterm, redraw, abort/rebind reader and bridge claim progression remain scoped to their unchanged callbacks. No current-source execution, independent replacement, native transport or physical provider result is assigned. Preserve meaningful remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged dated receipts within their original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh gate execution evidence in this metadata packet. No equivalent replacement, physical watcher/PTY/provider, live SSH/remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Exact retired authored alarms: 'bounds a startup title storm to one extra read ladder and never adopts the title as identity'; 'leaves untrackable providers free of client process scans'; 'keeps a legacy remote process hint unverifiable after a startup title'; 'releases a retained capability when disposed mid-read'; 'releases a retained capability when an exit schedules no successor read'; 'releases a retained capability when an untrackable $exit ends the read'; 'does not release when the cancelled read has a successor'; 'settles the visible confirmation when the pty id is gone before the read runs'; 'reports a read in flight when a command-finished read owns the pane'; 'reads the foreground once after a command starts and publishes the recognized agent'; 'does not replace known foreground identity with typed command inference'; 'revokes stale routing immediately while a known pane confirms a new command'; 'reads the foreground for a visible PTY so restored running Codex panes regain identity'; 'does not retry or publish visible PTY reads for an idle shell foreground'; 'retries visible PTY reads only while a foreground wrapper may resolve to an agent'; 'stops after the ladder and publishes no identity for a persistent unknown process'; 'does not treat a nested shell seen mid-command as prompt proof'; 'recognizes an agent started from a nested shell on a ladder re-read'; 'marks shell foreground on command finished without any foreground read'; 'trusts a rapid ordinary command finish without forcing a fresh scan'; 'still marks shell without a read for a duplicate D pair on an idle pane'; 'marks shell on a rapid command start->finish when the foreground is a shell'; 'marks shell foreground when the confirming read shows the agent is gone'; 'confirms a command finished for a launch-known agent pane before any read'; 'accepts a fresh shell result for a launch-known Droid pane'; 'marks a confirmed shell without repeating a post-boundary scan'; 'never reads or publishes for remote or ssh panes'; 'does not let forged OSC 133/777 output assert remote identity'; 'keeps command-only pane inference bounded for large pasted scripts'; 'skips jcode colors for command-only startup %s'; 'keeps explicit pane ownership ahead of a delayed command hint'; 'does not infer a TUI from %s'; 'survives a launch config registered before its identity lands'; 'prefers the tab launch agent over every later signal'; 'falls back through startup, then initial status, then the registered config'; 'ignores a registered agent name that is not a known TUI agent'; 'skips the OSC color answer for jcode and no one else'; 'drops a Done that landed before the command-finished fact'; 'keeps a program Done reported before the command-finished fact'; 'dismisses the kept result when the next command starts'; 'keeps a facet-less OSC Done from a non-agent program'; 'still drops a real agent Done'; 'still drops an interrupted program Done'; 'retires a hook-identified row the foreground tracker never read'; 'leaves a pane with an armed command-finished drop to its own confirming read'; 'leaves a remote pane to its execution host'; 'keeps the row when the host can verify the owner process itself'; 'keeps a row that belongs to a different agent'; 'does not watch the store for an owner it can never name'; 'control: a fresh host image repaints the pane without resizing the program'; 'asks the program to repaint when the image is %s'; 'asks the program to repaint when the host never answers the snapshot request'; 'repaints a full-screen TUI on the alternate screen the same way'; 'leaves the size alone while a phone or another desktop holds it'; 'grows a pane at the host minimum height instead of asking for the same clamped size'; 'does not nudge while the stream is still reconnecting'; 'mounts and remounts the tab owner while an unrelated workspace is active (%s)'; 'continues a recorded live folder owner despite ambiguous inventory (%s)'; 'resolves an encoded split surface using its parent tab and active leaf'; 'does not capture a remote revision for a local terminal'; 'omits incarnation and length for older runtime responses'; 'refuses %s owner before RPC'; 'refuses a resolved terminal belonging to another native PTY'; 'refuses a foreign remote terminal handle despite a matching native PTY ID'; 'refuses a remote handle owned by another environment'; 'refuses a remote terminal with no live native PTY'; 'does not fall back locally when remote lacks RPC'; 'rejects malformed or oversized encoded response %#'; 'maps a unified terminal tab id to its legacy owner id'; 'keeps non-terminal and unknown ids unchanged'; 'keeps an exact terminal owner ahead of a stale unified alias'; 'stays inert on a host that was not kept for the bridge'; 'stays inert for a pane main does not list, so it still dials the host'.",
        "Audit2056 (sources2054/2055): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/ipc/pty-transport-spawn-intent.test.ts: declares the intent only when the spawn resumes an agent; reports a deferral to the pane instead of an error toast. src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/startup/in-place-resume-hold.test.ts: owns the record while the start runs, through a nested start, and releases on settle; holds nothing for a start not resuming a record, or once the pane is disposed. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed.",
        "Audit2061 (sources2059/2060): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/ipc/pty-transport-agent-trust-hold.test.ts: spawns only after the answer, carrying \"let agents ask\" to main for this launch; reattaches a section terminal without asking or changing trust; spawns with today's default when the prompt is released without an answer. src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/host-ownership/pty-connection-ssh-hook-status-authority.spec.ts: leaves SSH IPC OSC 9999 status ownership in the main runtime. src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-completion-and-notification.test.ts: ordinary registration cleanup removes only import { registerPtyConnectionSshHookStatusAuthorityTests } from '../host-ownership/pty-connection-ssh-hook-status-authority.spec'; registerPtyConnectionSshHookStatusAuthorityTests(). Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed.",
        "Audit3086: the transport filename selector loses IPC suspension/input/reattach cases and the entire spawn-errors suite. Unique classification, ownership, fallback retirement, reply-limit, write-failure and teardown-branch alarms are intentionally retired without replacement. Remaining registrations are unchanged; no fresh execution or real provider result is claimed.",
        "Audit3390 composes root-adopted3382/independent3383 and3386/independent3387 and3388/independent3389: intentionally retires216 authored registrations/230 expanded cases in42 whole authored suites plus5 zero-case registration drivers, without equivalent replacement. Lost local alarms include fake PTY identity/routing/startup/replay/mode/title/mouse/IME/scroll matrices, broad startup identity and file-open wiring, mock mailbox title recovery, mobile row parity and whole-v-selective save parity. Retained24 registrations/26 expanded cases in22 suites preserve actual xterm Windows buffer/wrap/scroll, typed TOML scalar, real Promise cancellation/settlement, HTTP Codex scanner/projector semantics, durable recovery admission/newer-schema bytes, federation completion/ACK/SQLite atomicity and failed stale-run-write versus imported durable history. Additional retained clock-domain scheduling, durable freeze/ACK/checkpoint ordering, ABA dirty intent, SQL atomicity, folder-domain retier/last-note deletion, scrollback durable no-sync staging, PanelBridge subscriber lifetime and reserved-send publication preserve narrower concrete behaviors. Current finite owner drift assessed in bounded defining bodies; retained callback bytes unchanged. Historical notes and complete dated receipts keep their original exact scopes. No new execution, equivalent replacement, native focus/device/pixel, live remote or global mixed-version guarantee is claimed.\nOriginal active selector fields (historical raw native JSON values; not current coverage):\ncommands: [\n        \"pnpm test src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm test src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-visibility-and-exit.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm test src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/ipc/pty-transport\",\n        \"pnpm test src/shared/terminal/protocol/escape/terminal-synchronized-output-socket-splits.test.ts\"\n      ]\ntestFiles: [\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts\"\n      ]\nassertionRefs: [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"startup output covered by the snapshot is painted once\",\n            \"new output remains visible\",\n            \"legacy unsequenced and blank snapshots retain bytes\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]",
        "Audit3392 validation correction: no remaining directly selected suite protects prestarted snapshot adoption; protection is none. Remaining broad scan commands do not establish this invariant. Retired gate status, covered scope, commands and complete dated receipt follow as historical raw values:\nprotection: \"partial\"\ncommands: [\n        \"pnpm test src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/ipc/pty-transport\",\n        \"pnpm test src/shared/terminal/protocol/escape/terminal-synchronized-output-socket-splits.test.ts\"\n      ]\ncoveredPlatforms: [\"linux\"]\ncoveredProviders: []\nevidenceRuns: [\n        {\n          \"date\": \"2026-11-04\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"linux\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm --config.verifyDepsBeforeRun=false test src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/foreground-output-scan.test.ts --maxWorkers=2\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 2.31,\n          \"summary\": \"Test Files  1 passed (1); Tests  3 passed (3). Source head 8880357cb420c45f1b808ae545a5bc609324624d. Focused retained foreground-output scan only, not all directory-selected gate cases or live provider behavior. Node24.22.0 with ORCA_BACKGROUND_LAUNCH=1 and an isolated Xvfb display.\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm test src/shared/terminal/protocol/escape/terminal-synchronized-output-socket-splits.test.ts\"\n        }\n      ]"
