      "coverageNotes": "Audit4358 intentionally removes six whole mocked daemon subprocess suites and two extra pre-listener replay variants (18 authored / 20 finite cases). Lost alarms include cancel-during-cwd-validation, root agent startup refusal, output/exit before ConPTY publication, fresh/delayed/unavailable foreground confirmation, cache/decision separation, detached/no-tty child evidence and synthetic agent authorization. The retained lifecycle case checks data and exit replay after handle creation, not startup-time publication or alternate listener order. The retained native Windows Git Bash workflow and host cold-restore seed check have separate scopes. No equivalent replacement or fresh gate execution is claimed. Earlier notes and dated receipts retain their original scope. Audit 3959 retires the whole session.test.ts driver (27 authored / 33 finite cases): startup/echo filtering, readiness input gates, ownership confirmation, detach authority, and termination retry/exit ordering alarms are intentionally lost. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime validation is claimed. Audit1627 removes low-value mocked daemon projections, scalar tables and duplicate terminal examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained terminal content preservation, process ownership refusal and recovery boundaries together with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Real TerminalHost, Session, and subprocess wrapper with injected native I/O failures and mocked OS signals. Local non-daemon and SSH-relay implementations are unaffected; daemon consumers on SSH, WSL, paired runtimes, and mobile retain host-owned semantics. Live Linux/Windows/WSL and remote runs remain gaps. No git or folder-workspace assumptions. The fault-injection suite also runs with simulated darwin/linux/win32 platform branches; these do not constitute native OS coverage. Archived native macOS results previously exercised shell exit and PTY master-fd closure, input/output round trips, and teardown of a paused producer; that suite is now retired without replacement. Windows single-close/job escalation and pre-listener output/status are fault-injected contracts. Audit1302: src/main/daemon/terminal-host-teardown-recreate.test.ts: Fake subprocess handles synthesize exits via real40ms/30s timers or manual exit callback, with descendant retirement mocked away; assertions inspect isNew/refusal/spawn counts. No real subprocess/PTY teardown/recreation or owned-tree retention boundary. Lose artificial teardown/attach/shutdown/cancellation scheduling alarms; no equivalent replacement. Reduced selectors require fresh validation; prior full-suite receipts do not validate removed or changed coverage. No equivalent replacement or physical-provider claim.\nOrcad folder cleanup intentionally retires the Cartesian native failed-I/O test under repository test policy, without equivalent replacement. Remaining selectors retain their narrower scope. Dated evidenceRuns remain historical and do not validate this changed selector.",
      "motivatingLinks": ["docs/terminal-daemon-session-leak-investigation.md"],
      "invariant": "I/O errors must not establish physical exit or disable termination of an owned PTY. Session and native handle disposal require the exit event.",
      "oracle": "Audit4358 intentionally removes six whole mocked daemon subprocess suites and two extra pre-listener replay variants (18 authored / 20 finite cases). Lost alarms include cancel-during-cwd-validation, root agent startup refusal, output/exit before ConPTY publication, fresh/delayed/unavailable foreground confirmation, cache/decision separation, detached/no-tty child evidence and synthetic agent authorization. The retained lifecycle case checks data and exit replay after handle creation, not startup-time publication or alternate listener order. The retained native Windows Git Bash workflow and host cold-restore seed check have separate scopes. No equivalent replacement or fresh gate execution is claimed. Earlier notes and dated receipts retain their original scope. Inject write and resize failures, require graceful and forced signals to reach the native owner, keep producer resume available, suppress repeated failed I/O, deliver output and exit, and suppress signals after exit. Across 32 create/close cycles per failure, retain each session before exit and release its native handle and emulator exactly once afterwards. Mark physical exit before notifying listeners; reentrant kill/forceKill/signal from those listeners must never signal the retired PID. The former native POSIX shell/PID/fd oracle is retired without replacement.",
      "commands": [
