      "coverageNotes": "Audit3663 renews approved3644/3645/3648/amended3651 at privatec1ef: remove10authored/26finite across7changedtestpaths,4whole drivers; retain23authored/24finite including actualcmdkStrictMode defaultcursor race. Retire version1.5.0/1.5.1→shrinksImages capability threshold and launch-to-prompt wiring alarm. Surviving prompt tests explicitly supply capability and do not replace wiring coverage. Retire resolved-before-personOnly precedence; hook-gone/live-dialog guidance; stale-incarnation versus live-looking dialog classification; delayed/clipped warning extraction and wait-for-paint wiring; 3row setting/personOnly approve/deny/disclaimer suggestion composition;13row setting/reason/person/coordinator admission, close/mail attribution, terminal delivery/refusal/preanswered/personOnly/dropped-allow handler propagation alarms. Real state/access/SQLite effects occur; these genuine losses are accepted, not mocked-away. Retire full command extraction from serialized JSON in worker receipt and nontruncation alarm; no rendering, actual worker approval or native shell proof. Retire2row extra-source first/last order and controlled default cursor projection, plus generic open-palette livefolder add/remove render alarm. Explicitly supersede rawexact297KEEP refresh. Keep actualcmdk/StrictMode default cursor race driver; no default-suite loss claim. No equivalent replacement asserted. Retained queue/commit/retryownership/filebudget, terminalfreshness/provenance/competing-answer, RPC DB-effect, qualifiedfolder/runtimehandoff and lingering-reopen cases have distinct scope. Audit3675 preserves the upstream revised unreported-approval close regression, its escalation helper and adapted survivors. Source-only static renewal; no runner/compiler/app/native/remote/CI claim. Upstream41390host-owned approvalwatch/report lifetime reviewed separately; no new lifetime test removed. Preserve all earlier metadata/evidence. Audit3381 intentionally removes the entire Cmd-J host-qualified candidate-ownership suite and its active selectors/assertion. The hidden same-id sibling ambiguity regression alarm is lost without replacement. The complete original dated failed receipt below is retired verbatim, including both command and currentCommand, rather than reassigned as validation of remaining selectors. Other complete receipts retain their exact original scopes; remaining browser/simulator/workspace/e2e selectors do not imply equivalent ownership protection. No fresh execution is claimed. Audit3359 retires the whole ensure-simulator-tab-behavior suite: host-collision reuse, host stamping, inactive creation and unknown-owner routing alarms are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. Its standalone command is removed and four compound commands narrowed. Three complete dated receipts selecting that source through currentCommand are retired verbatim, including their compound historical selectors; no retained test inherits their validation. Seven unrelated macOS receipts retain their original scope. No fresh runtime/UI, simulator, provider, historical-import, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Audit 3301 removes the orphaned mobile file-close fallback and ordinary cross-content MRU examples from tabs-open-close-lifecycle.test.ts. Earlier descriptions of retained MRU coverage are historical. The integrated mobile markdown close/frame-settlement case remains unchanged and is narrower. Preserve the existing administrative failed receipt and all complete retired receipts verbatim, along with selectors and unrelated assertions; no equivalent replacement or fresh Cmd-J, native or remote result is claimed. Audit 3273 removes 14 authored declarations and 19 expanded scenarios across four whole suites and eight partial suites. Retired alarms cover saved-local cancellation/layout ownership, ambiguous-owner warning reset, folder attachment routing, VM false-capability bypass, abandoned reveal warmup cleanup and viewport claim deduplication/rearming, quiet unrelated remote-removal refusal, startup-command one-shot consumption, repository/floating recovery-ledger rows, fake-React pinned-scroll intent, split-ratio state identity/subscriber suppression and fractional change, cross-host project-group join refusal, three PR request-lifetime permutations, upstream-status preservation on error, and unresolved Git-owner refusal. These regression checks are intentionally lost under the test-value audit; retained scenarios are not equivalent replacements. Historical coverage receipts remain historical, including gate35 subscriber claims. Audit2729 reduces browser-page-palette-activation.test.ts: separate SSH/paired-runtime alias forwarding, distinct multigroup views accepted, and remote-folder activation forwarding alarms are removed. Collision refusal, preactivation address-bar focus capture, owning-group activation state and missing-tab refusal remain byte-identical. No equivalent replacement, fresh gate execution or actual host/browser delivery evidence is claimed. Prior coverage account: Audit2697 browser source review (metadata followup2702): Reduce src/renderer/src/lib/browser/palette/browser-palette-page-entries.test.ts by four authored/expanded cases without replacement. The remaining three cases preserve only their existing same-ID execution-host separation, absent stamped-owner refusal and ambiguous legacy-bucket refusal scope. Intentionally lose duplicate backing-tab-ID suppression, multiple unified-browser claims of one workspace, foreign-worktree unified-tab rejection, and the 1000-workspace output/internal getter-read budget alarm. These are real removed alarms; the retained host cases are not equivalent replacements. Current test-value policy rejects internal getter/read budgets; no replacement performance or measured-cost claim is made. Keep existing nonempty selectors and the retained same-ID browser assertionRef. No fresh gate execution or reduced-source validation is su