      "coverageNotes": "Audit3456 composes ROOT-adopted3449/independent3450: intentionally removes62 authored/82 potential expanded cases from16 selected drivers, including7 whole suites, while13 authored/13 potential cases remain. Delete the unused48line legacy workspace-session JSON fixture with zero test credit. These are source-only reductions without equivalent replacement or fresh runtime claims. The recipe-process suite loses its three-row UTF-8 tail-cap subprocess sample; keep the original POSIX process-group timeout case proving descendant death, with Windows explicitly skipped. The active synchronous-graceful-termination assertion reference was already absent from the adopted original source before this reduction; it is preserved verbatim in knownGaps as historical stale metadata rather than replaced by a different claim. Unrelated cross-version rollback receipt and all prior narratives remain exact. Audit3446 composes ROOT-adopted3441/independent3442: intentionally removes100 authored registrations/119 potential expanded cases (118 conditional-active before platform gates) across16 sources, retaining11 authored/13 expanded cases and deleting6 whole suites. Two parent registrar import/call cleanups and the unused68line CLI recording fixture carry zero test credit. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. The rollback suite retains only exact preservation of an unknown future-version provisioning file and refusal of a new provisioning upsert. It retires malformed/oversized/merge/migration and old-reader schema projection examples; no actual old client runtime was executed by those removed cases. The IPC suite retains the immutable recipe snapshot used by an actual destroy child after plugin removal; other IPC validation/lifecycle projections are retired. Existing unrelated pinned rollback reproduction receipt retains its original scope. Audit3413 composes root-adopted3405/independent3406 and3409/independent3410: intentionally removes337 authored registrations/363potential expanded cases from13sources, retaining31authored/32potential cases and deleting one whole clipboard suite, without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. The runtime-service source intentionally loses14of16cases: ordinary lifecycle/retry/configuration/cleanup projections, unreadable-companion refusal and successful post-create compensation examples are retired. Keep only non-JSON credential refusal before provider launch and failed compensation after post-create persistence failure, with old-readable recovery identity across two local injected faults. This does not prove a subsequent retry or actual remote provider cleanup. Existing unrelated rollback reproduction receipt remains exact; no fresh execution, protection change or equivalent replacement claimed.  Audit 3292 retires the direct-SSH failed-project retention, managed-server failed-project retention and ordinary confirmed managed-VM destruction/no-repo.rm examples from repos-ephemeral-vm-cleanup-retention.test.ts. Host-scoped same-workspace isolation and stale renderer catalog reconciliation remain byte-identical. These three supplied-result alarms are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. Existing selectors/assertionRefs, unrelated cross-version rollback receipt and archived complete 122-case cleanup receipt remain exact; no fresh broad runtime, provider, platform or mixed-version result is claimed. Audit2056 (sources2054/2055): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/renderer/src/lib/ephemeral-vm-failed-create-cleanup.test.ts: removes the imported project setup before destroying its VM; retains the VM when setup deletion throws; retains the VM when setup deletion reports no result. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Exact retired assertionRefs, preserved as historical objects only: {\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/lib/ephemeral-vm-failed-create-cleanup.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\"failed or unconfirmed project-host rollback prevents provider destroy\"]\n        } Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1634 removes low-value IPC, filesystem and runtime projections, argument inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained cancellation, ownership, authorization, filesystem and SQLite boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1627 removes low-value mocked daemon projections, scalar tables and duplicate terminal examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained terminal content preservation, process ownership refusal and recovery boundaries together with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1441 removes the complete renderer VM-runtime settings suite: display filter/status/SSH-retry flags, cleanup and stop RPC-to-toast/dialog plumbing, manual-copy plumbing and polling toast silence. The suite did not execute provider teardown or process cancellation. Its rendered stop/retry and hidden-SSH display alarms are intentionally retired; no equivalent replacement or fresh reduced-selector runtime result is claimed. Retained exact unchanged-source receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Reduced selectors have no fresh execution result. Audit1417 intentionally deletes src/renderer/src/lib/ephemeral-vm-workspace-target.test.ts: Loses wrapper-level host rebinding, incompatible provisioned-root refusal and best-effort cleanup-call alarms; all are mock-only orchestration projections. No equivalent replacement coverage or fresh result is claimed. Historical coverage account: Audit1342 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): A pinned exact-source harness runs the pre-#14352 reader and lifecycle service against baseline, affected-main, candidate, and fix-reverted stores. Platform-neutral tests cover store compatibility, user-cancellable cleanup, branch/ref adoption; audit885 removes the direct resume ownership predicate alarms. The direct-SSH provisioned-root Electron journey remains the live transport and destroy proof; this desktop sidecar is not mobile-facing and changes no RPC or remote wire payload. The test-value audit removed the renderer provisioned-root create-options suite. Its two incomplete-identity rejection assertions are lost: one omitted workspaceRunContext and other identity fields, and one supplied the context but omitted ephemeralVmExpectedRefHead. The suite did not test successful option mapping. Retained source-ref and lifecycle suites do not establish equivalent renderer guard coverage. Audit1342: src/renderer/src/lib/ephemeral-vm-runtime-cleanup.test.ts removed. Runtime/SSH ownership, encoded target, retry/failure/listing-error cleanup projection samples disappear. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed.",
      "motivatingLinks": [
        "https://linear.app/stably/issue/STA-4274",
