      "invariant": "A sidecar written by the new build cannot make the previous production build lose otherwise compatible VM runtimes. Downgrade lifecycle writes remain authoritative after re-upgrade, provisioned-root metadata remains recoverable, and corrupt or future feature metadata is preserved without poisoning the rollback-readable v1 store. Destroy attempts have no automatic wall-clock cutoff; a user stop terminates the process tree, retains cleanup ownership, and permits a fresh retry. Provider failure retains the SSH/project context needed for safe cleanup. Unrecoverable recipe context releases only the hidden SSH registration while preserving lifecycle/provider metadata. Provisioned-root create receives the source ref's pinned commit, adoption verifies the requested branch/ref, and resume preserves the connection mode plus stable SSH ownership identity while allowing endpoint rotation.",
      "oracle": "Audit3456 composes ROOT-adopted3449/independent3450: intentionally removes62 authored/82 potential expanded cases from16 selected drivers, including7 whole suites, while13 authored/13 potential cases remain. Delete the unused48line legacy workspace-session JSON fixture with zero test credit. These are source-only reductions without equivalent replacement or fresh runtime claims. The recipe-process suite loses its three-row UTF-8 tail-cap subprocess sample; keep the original POSIX process-group timeout case proving descendant death, with Windows explicitly skipped. The active synchronous-graceful-termination assertion reference was already absent from the adopted original source before this reduction; it is preserved verbatim in knownGaps as historical stale metadata rather than replaced by a different claim. Unrelated cross-version rollback receipt and all prior narratives remain exact. Audit3446 composes ROOT-adopted3441/independent3442: intentionally removes100 authored registrations/119 potential expanded cases (118 conditional-active before platform gates) across16 sources, retaining11 authored/13 expanded cases and deleting6 whole suites. Two parent registrar import/call cleanups and the unused68line CLI recording fixture carry zero test credit. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. The rollback suite retains only exact preservation of an unknown future-version provisioning file and refusal of a new provisioning upsert. It retires malformed/oversized/merge/migration and old-reader schema projection examples; no actual old client runtime was executed by those removed cases. The IPC suite retains the immutable recipe snapshot used by an actual destroy child after plugin removal; other IPC validation/lifecycle projections are retired. Existing unrelated pinned rollback reproduction receipt retains its original scope. Audit3413 composes root-adopted3405/independent3406 and3409/independent3410: intentionally removes337 authored registrations/363potential expanded cases from13sources, retaining31authored/32potential cases and deleting one whole clipboard suite, without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. The runtime-service source intentionally loses14of16cases: ordinary lifecycle/retry/configuration/cleanup projections, unreadable-companion refusal and successful post-create compensation examples are retired. Keep only non-JSON credential refusal before provider launch and failed compensation after post-create persistence failure, with old-readable recovery identity across two local injected faults. This does not prove a subsequent retry or actual remote provider cleanup. Existing unrelated rollback reproduction receipt remains exact; no fresh execution, protection change or equivalent replacement claimed.  Audit 3292 retires the direct-SSH failed-project retention, managed-server failed-project retention and ordinary confirmed managed-VM destruction/no-repo.rm examples from repos-ephemeral-vm-cleanup-retention.test.ts. Host-scoped same-workspace isolation and stale renderer catalog reconciliation remain byte-identical. These three supplied-result alarms are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. Existing selectors/assertionRefs, unrelated cross-version rollback receipt and archived complete 122-case cleanup receipt remain exact; no fresh broad runtime, provider, platform or mixed-version result is claimed. Audit2056 (sources2054/2055): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/renderer/src/lib/ephemeral-vm-failed-create-cleanup.test.ts: removes the imported project setup before destroying its VM; retains the VM when setup deletion throws; retains the VM when setup deletion reports no result. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Exact retired assertionRefs, preserved as historical objects only: {\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/lib/ephemeral-vm-failed-create-cleanup.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\"failed or unconfirmed project-host rollback prevents provider destroy\"]\n        } Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Retained exact unchanged-source receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Reduced selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical pre-audit oracle account for changed sources: The retained unchanged-source receipts are the only current execution evidence; reduced-source assertions await validation. Historical oracle account (not a current claim for changed sources): Write one ordinary schema-v1 runtime and one provisioned-root runtime. Require the exact pre-#14352 reader to return both, run the old destroy lifecycle against the projected provisioned record, then require the candidate to retain the cleaned state while restoring schema-v2 and checkout-mode metadata. The same old reader must reject affected-main and fix-reverted bytes. Malformed, oversized, unknown-record, and future-version feature sidecars must leave rollback-compatible records accessible and must not be overwritten during compatible lifecycle mutations. Require destroy to have no implicit deadline, stop a hung destroy through the public desktop action, require cleanup_failed plus a fresh successful retry, prove provider or project-host rollback failure retains every ownership record required to retry, and prove missing recipe context cannot leave an unremovable hidden SSH registration. Supply the source ref's captured commit to create, reject a provisioned checkout on the wrong branch/ref, and reject a resume that changes connection mode or SSH ownership.",
      "commands": [
        "node config/scripts/runtime-verification/ephemeral-store/run-ephemeral-vm-runtime-store-rollback-repro.mjs config/scripts/runtime-verification/ephemeral-store/ephemeral-vm-runtime-store-cross-version.test.ts",
