      "coveredProviders": ["local", "local-daemon", "ssh-relay", "paired-runtime"],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit 3959 retires the whole session.test.ts driver (27 authored / 33 finite cases): startup/echo filtering, readiness input gates, ownership confirmation, detach authority, and termination retry/exit ordering alarms are intentionally lost. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime validation is claimed. Audit1683 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1627 removes low-value mocked daemon projections, scalar tables and duplicate terminal examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained terminal content preservation, process ownership refusal and recovery boundaries together with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Real macOS node-pty integration covers zsh 5.9 .zshenv/.zprofile and bash 3.2 profile replacement shells, including exec -a names, same-shell and child-process silent reads, a blocking zle-line-init hook, non-shell readline replacements, and a non-shell image renamed zsh. A real Fish PTY proves marker stripping is byte-exact and does not render bracketed-paste control text. Ubuntu 20.04/Bash 5.0 and Ubuntu 24.04/Bash 5.2 containers cover scalar and array PROMPT_COMMAND composition, including real zoxide on 24.04. Deterministic owner contracts cover local, daemon, and SSH relay identity/readiness composition plus provider-owned delivery; explicit terminal-paste remains renderer-owned. Live isolated journeys cover a macOS headed desktop owner with paired web client, headless orca serve with paired web client, and a Docker Linux OpenSSH/Bash target with one readiness-time reconnect. Linux desktop, WSL/Windows, live zsh-over-SSH, and physical remote hosts remain gaps.",
      "motivatingLinks": [
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/issues/13767",
        "https://linear.app/stably/issue/STA-4067",
        "https://linear.app/stably/issue/STA-4068",
