      "coverageNotes": "Audit2003: Remove held-subscription and viewport replay, background suspension, delivery-ambiguity/error propagation, dial-phase/recovery-path projections, relay timing and authentication-failure examples from the logical client. Retain only make-before-break cutover with subscription replay, committed-response/close arbitration and late-event cancellation fencing against fake physical sessions. Retire all dated combined receipts whole; their case counts and sibling results do not validate these changed bytes. Archive all prospective selector/file/assertion and covered-scope fields with the downgraded gate; the three retained logical callbacks are described here only, without active gate authority. Downgrade active protection to none because no independent unchanged receipt survives. Changed-source prior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, physical provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Deterministic React/provider tests cover catalog, missing-host, construction, cancellation, release, forget, refresh, backoff, stale-generation outcomes, and path-aware recovery presentation. Direct sessions cover idle probing and three fair misses. Relay sessions cover a 15s idle probe, rate-limited foreground probes, two fair misses, authenticated activity before semantic decoding, delivery ambiguity, scheduler stalls, and write failure. Physical iOS/Android sleep, carrier/Tailscale loss, and production relay paths remain live-test gaps. Audit1303 intentionally removes supplied-state/mock-callback component and hook examples in mobile/src/transport/connection-health.test.ts. Their exact retired alarms are not equivalent to retained coverage; no new runtime, physical phone or deployed mixed-version evidence is claimed. Audit1315 removes/narrows mobile/src/transport/rpc-session-liveness-