        "evidence": "Audit2003: Remove held-subscription and viewport replay, background suspension, delivery-ambiguity/error propagation, dial-phase/recovery-path projections, relay timing and authentication-failure examples from the logical client. Retain only make-before-break cutover with subscription replay, committed-response/close arbitration and late-event cancellation fencing against fake physical sessions. Retire all dated combined receipts whole; their case counts and sibling results do not validate these changed bytes. Archive all prospective selector/file/assertion and covered-scope fields with the downgraded gate; the three retained logical callbacks are described here only, without active gate authority. Downgrade active protection to none because no independent unchanged receipt survives. Changed-source prior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, physical provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Current main failed six deterministic assertions: terminal catalog failure, zero-owner publication, stale failure clobber, initial direct handshake write throw, one-window direct death, and foreground probe write throw. The candidate passes the same assertions and adds relay parity, backoff, cancellation, and scheduler-fairness coverage."
