      "performanceBudget": {
        "required": true,
        "evidence": "Audit2003: Remove held-subscription and viewport replay, background suspension, delivery-ambiguity/error propagation, dial-phase/recovery-path projections, relay timing and authentication-failure examples from the logical client. Retain only make-before-break cutover with subscription replay, committed-response/close arbitration and late-event cancellation fencing against fake physical sessions. Retire all dated combined receipts whole; their case counts and sibling results do not validate these changed bytes. Archive all prospective selector/file/assertion and covered-scope fields with the downgraded gate; the three retained logical callbacks are described here only, without active gate authority. Downgrade active protection to none because no independent unchanged receipt survives. Changed-source prior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, physical provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Each wanted clientless host owns at most one open and one retry timer with a 60-second capped tail. Direct sessions own one idle or probe timer. Relay sessions own one idle or probe timer and send at most one idle probe per 15 seconds without authenticated frames, about four small round trips per idle foreground minute, and no demand-driven liveness traffic; foreground sequences start at most once per 10 seconds. Each Relay idle probe costs one relay forward and one desktop status.get probe dispatch; no subprocess or wire opcode is introduced. Upstream resource specification after Relay correction (not a measured budget): Each wanted clientless host owns at most one open and one retry timer with a 60-second capped tail. Direct sessions own one idle or probe timer. Relay sessions own one idle or probe timer and start an idle probe 15 seconds after the last authenticated frame, about four small round trips per healthy idle foreground minute. A fair miss on a link that isn't busy sends one retry as soon as its 4-second timeout fires, and a second fair miss closes the session. Demand-driven probes are decisive and run only while a caller's reply is overdue after 4 seconds of authenticated silence, at most one per 4 seconds; foreground sequences start at most once per 10 seconds. Each Relay probe costs one relay forward and one desktop status.get probe dispatch; no subprocess or wire opcode is introduced."
      },
