      "coverageNotes": "Audit4891 removes two isolated serve activation gate cases for coalescing/ready state and blocked-request cancellation/counts. Their exact alarms are intentionally lost. Retain the newly added queued foreground-over-background priority case, which exercises a new request-selection decision; it does not replace blocked/provider/native-window coverage. Historical receipts remain verbatim. Audit4362 intentionally deletes the imported stale-waiter retry and manually assembled OSC9999 mobile-republish cases, plus the mocked missing-worktree cleanup suite (4 authored / 5 finite cases in three suites). Lost alarms include repeated unread worker_done pointers, working-to-waiting mobile status publication, missing-worktree filtering, and scoped daemon shutdown with unrelated duplicate identities. No replacement coverage or new platform proof is claimed. Audit3994 retires two authored callbacks imported by the shared construction test driver: split OSC 9999 carry and rendererless status ownership, plus OpenCode permission text taking priority in status and tui-idle refusal. Remaining imports and selectors keep their scope. No equivalent replacement or fresh gate execution is claimed. Audit3417 composes root-adopted3415v2/independent3416v2: intentionally removes117authored/173potential expanded registrations from12semantic sources, deleting4whole conventional suites and3registration modules and retaining4authored/5expanded cases, without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. The whole main-window attach-services suite is removed: runtime/window attach, notifier wiring, reload/teardown and permission-handler mock orchestration alarms are intentionally lost. Prune its exact deleted command selectors, testFiles entries and notifier assertionRef where present; complete prior selectors/ref are archived. Unrelated dated receipts remain exact and retain their original scope; no fresh reduced-selector, native-window or remote execution is claimed.  Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The retained runtime registration driver loses three complete imported fragments: changed-working-label title facts and suppressed-frame tracked snapshots; refusing SSH GitLab MR-base lookup before local Git/glab calls; and missing folder-workspace path creation/update refusal before spawn/store mutation. These alarms are intentionally lost. Other imported fragments and separately rooted dated receipts are unchanged; they are not equivalent replacement coverage.  Audit2271: Linux coverage is limited to the unchanged serve-signal-exit-diagnostic supervisor selector and the late-handoff-after-child-exit assertion recorded below. It does not cover desktop promotion, renderer continuity, persistent PTYs or native updater behavior. No current local, daemon or SSH provider execution is established; coveredProviders is empty. Historical macOS/provider scope remains only in preserved prior accounts and archived receipts. Audit2252 removes the entire handassembled serve promotion/renderer hydration suite. Retired alarms: queued and repeated activation coalescing, duplicate serve suppression, unavailable-provider diagnostic, and zero resume/replacement accounting on independently supplied renderer state. The fixture never joined actual daemon-to-renderer delivery. These exact alarms have no equivalent replacement assigned. Remaining gate selectors keep their existing narrower scope; historical dated receipts remain verbatim and do not validate this changed selector set. No fresh runtime, native/provider, live remote/mobile, cross-platform or performance result is claimed. Archived removed active entries verbatim: commands: \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/lib/serve-desktop-promotion-session-continuity.test.ts\"\ntestFiles: \"src/renderer/src/lib/serve-desktop-promotion-session-continuity.test.ts\"\nassertionRefs: {\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/lib/serve-desktop-promotion-session-continuity.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"a forced desktop relaunch reaching the headless lock owner opens exactly one window, and only after the persistent provider settles\",\n            \"a duplicate `orca serve` launch never promotes the headless owner\",\n            \"the renderer promoted inside the serve process resumes zero agents while daemon panes survive, before and after those panes rebind their PTYs\",\n            \"no replacement resume tab, startup command, or automatic-resume claim is created, and every surviving session record is left untouched\"\n          ]\n        } Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2095 current-parent preparation2126: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2090 (sources2088/2089): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2086 (sources2082/2083): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2076 (sources2073/2074): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-part-02.spec.ts: recovers a moved SSH pane through the tab it now sits in, not the one its lease froze; reports a plain expired orphan; does not report a pane whose only recent lease was superseded; does not report a pane whose only recent lease had its relay id recycled; picks the eligible orphan over a superseded predecessor that matches first; collects the same tabs the per-tab reader reports, in one sweep of the leases; reports no candidate when no lease names any of the worktree tabs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/runtime-availability.spec.ts: starts unavailable with no authoritative window; reports the configured Windows terminal shell on status; reports floating workspace availability from settings on status; polls floating tabs with targeted PTY liveness and no repo/provider inventory; hydrates persisted tabs when the store cannot report repos; advertises browser screencast only when a renderer window is available; routes mobile Codex reset consumption through the account mutation coordinator; maps a definite pre-provider rejection into an authoritative current snapshot. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2020: Retire CLI supervisor outcome, local-open promotion and paired-open projection alarms; launch retains only the two referenced stream-framing cases. Remaining CLI refusal/timeout cases do not replace headless-promotion coverage. Preserve both independent dated receipts at their original commands. Reduced selectors have no fresh result or equivalent replacement claim. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1589 removes mock-only CLI forwarding, canned provisioning/catalog/error projections and private inventories without equivalent replacement coverage. Retained cases exercise actual local markdown/paste/reconciliation, stream framing/backpressure/output-drain, temporary directory cleanup and persisted handoff with injected host/provider/process boundaries. No real Jira, provisioning, remote launch, native pipe/process-tree authority or deployed provider catalog proof. Assertion references use the surviving handoff registration titles; changed-selector historical receipts are retired and unaffected receipts remain unchanged. Historical scope before this audit: Deterministic unit coverage exercises activation gating, single-instance ownership, local/remote CLI status, headless binding persistence, local daemon identity, SSH identity transfer, the promoted renderer's agent-resume accounting, and the macOS serve update handoff from staged installer through atomic bundle replacement and target-version readiness. Supervisor settlement coverage prevents a late handoff-completion failure from rearming termination after the replacement child exits. A macOS Electron journey covers headless promotion and persistent PTY identity. A disposable locally signed Electron canary exercised real ShipIt and a temporary LaunchAgent with the compiled production supervisor; full packaged Orca and Linux/Windows serve updates remain uncollected. Audit1383: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-native-chat-setup.spec.ts reduced. Lose command-list/receipt/default/background activation matrices whose provider spawn returns canned IDs. Retained test proves actual tab allocation separation, not terminal startup. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected recei