      "invariant": "A safely promotable headless serve process is the single app owner. Desktop activation preserves its daemon-backed sessions. On macOS, a CLI-supervised serve update keeps the node-mode parent alive across ShipIt's atomic bundle swap, restarts with the original serve arguments only after the target bundle is present, and clears handoff state only after that target version reports runtime readiness. Once a supervised child exits or fails to start, no late handoff completion may signal it or arm force-kill escalation. Unsupported or failed handoffs leave the current serving owner intact or recover it once without an install retry loop.",
      "oracle": "Audit4362 intentionally deletes the imported stale-waiter retry and manually assembled OSC9999 mobile-republish cases, plus the mocked missing-worktree cleanup suite (4 authored / 5 finite cases in three suites). Lost alarms include repeated unread worker_done pointers, working-to-waiting mobile status publication, missing-worktree filtering, and scoped daemon shutdown with unrelated duplicate identities. No replacement coverage or new platform proof is claimed. Audit3832 deliberately retires76 authored/79 finite cases:75 runtime compatibility cases/78 finite cases across14 fragments, plus one localization extractor default-flag case. Three whole runtime fragments are deleted;27 authored/30 finite cases remain across the reviewed sources. This gate retains only its own selected scope; no equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/native/remote evidence is claimed. Runtime component A: Audit3828 composes3822 with independent3824: deliberately retires49 authored/52 finite cases from seven compatibility fragments, leaving15 authored/18 finite cases and deleting two entire fragments. Accepted losses: positive folder-worker recovery/materialization and reveal deadline; persisted-key normalization and legacy split/group/focus projection; fixed stale CAS refusal; occupied/alias/restored/preallocated terminal-handle variants; fixed OpenCode/Cursor/Claude/Codex/Antigravity classification, readiness, title and management examples; direct private-map browser authority projections; browser-focus and OMP title projection; already-aborted claim cleanup. Additional3824 loss: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-02.spec.ts :: does not poll a wrapper foreground for a speculative CLI prompt send :: Speculative retryForegroundWrappers:false check must return false on a wrapper after one foreground read, without polling the supplied later codex response. These real bounded alarms are deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained callbacks are unchanged and provide only their own bounded scope, not equivalent replacement. Historical receipts do not validate reduced callbacks. No fresh runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser evidence or full transitive closure is claimed. Runtime component B: Audit3834 deliberately retires26 authored/26 finite cases from seven fresh compatibility fragments, leaving10/10 and deleting the one-case saved-binding reattachment fragment. Original position58 is excluded: its existing substantive3578 KEEP7 review remains historical, with no fresh credit. Accepted losses: fixed hook/provider-session identities and stale metadata refusal; decorative/pre-title foreground ordering variants; saved-binding surface reattachment; saved-row exit ghost removal and silent activation selection; unsupported headless wake; positive pending materialization/group projections; per-caller navigation selection; positive SSH hydration/read partition; laptop mobile publication/buffer and background/pending/status projections; abnormal/unregistered SSH grace, normal-exit refusal, persisted SSH hydration, positive serve reattachment, pending-agent launch arguments and direct seeded running-launch admission guard. These are real bounded alarms deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained cases preserve their own distinct deferred foreground coalescing, usable handle continuity, stale inventory refresh, concurrent browser snapshot preservation, renderer graph fencing, caller dedup isolation, SSH partition writes, runtime split lifetime, independent relay-ready publication, lease admission/state/expiry. The direct running-launch no-spawn guard alarm is deliberately retired; no remaining owning-launch refusal coverage is claimed. Historical runs do not validate reduced callbacks. No equivalent replacement, runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser result or full transitive closure is claimed. Additional extractor loss: config/scripts/localization/source-extraction/audit-localization-native