aiter ownership are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or full transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3798 deliberately retires21 authored/24 finite compatibility cases, including the entire SSH-worktree-lifecycle and repository-project-operations fragments. Accepted losses include navigation-only settings acknowledgement, browser session cleanup and host preservation projections, window positive/policy-state examples, terminal recovery/reload and no-incarnation remint examples, terminal listing compatibility/malformed IDs, directory browse/sort/Windows path smoke, SSH create refusal/manual lineage, recursive parent-folder creation and fork/origin/avatar/icon projections. Real bounded production alarms are consciously retired for marginal value; retained authority races, cleanup/clone ownership, pending waiters, nested-folder and scan invalidation cases are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or full transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3417 composes root-adopted3415v2/independent3416v2: intentionally removes117authored/173potential expanded registrations from12semantic sources, deleting4whole conventional suites and3registration modules and retaining4authored/5expanded cases, without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. The whole main-window attach-services suite is removed: runtime/window attach, notifier wiring, reload/teardown and permission-handler mock orchestration alarms are intentionally lost. Prune its exact deleted command selectors, testFiles entries and notifier assertionRef where present; complete prior selectors/ref are archived. Unrelated dated receipts remain exact and retain their original scope; no fresh reduced-selector, native-window or remote execution is claimed.  Audit3403 composes root-adopt