tion and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2076 (sources2073/2074): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-part-02.spec.ts: recovers a moved SSH pane through the tab it now sits in, not the one its lease froze; reports a plain expired orphan; does not report a pane whose only recent lease was superseded; does not report a pane whose only recent lease had its relay id recycled; picks the eligible orphan over a superseded predecessor that matches first; collects the same tabs the per-tab reader reports, in one sweep of the leases; reports no candidate when no lease names any of the worktree tabs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/runtime-availability.spec.ts: starts unavailable with no authoritative window; reports the configured Windows terminal shell on status; reports floating workspace availability from settings on status; polls floating tabs with targeted PTY liveness and no repo/provider inventory; hydrates persisted tabs when the store cannot report repos; advertises browser screencast only when a renderer window is available; routes mobile Codex reset consumption through the account mutation coordinator; maps a definite pre-provider rejection into an authoritative current snapshot. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2020: Retire CLI supervisor outcome, local-open promotion and paired-open projection alarms; launch retains only the two referenced stream-framing cases. Remaining CLI refusal/timeout cases do not replace headless-promotion coverage. Preserve both independent dated receipts at their original commands. Reduced selectors have no fresh result or equivalent replacement claim. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Existing exact unchanged-selector receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Changed source selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical prior-source oracle account: Unit tests coalesce early activation, preserve daemon and SSH identity, and reproduce the update race with a staged target, old serving child, persistent CLI parent, atomic .app replacement, and replacement readiness message. They assert the parent does not exit for launchd to respawn the old app, the native updater does not launch an interactive GUI, the replacement version is verified before handoff completion, mismatches become durable failures without retries, and unsupported/preflight-failed installs do not invoke native quit or PTY cleanup. Force handoff completion to fail after the replacement child exits and require zero later child signals and zero escalation timers. A joined lock-owner/activation/hydration contract asserts that a forced relaunch opens exactly one window and that the renderer promoted inside the serve process launches zero agent resumes, creates no replacement tab or startup command, and leaves every surviving session record untouched. The Electron journey independently verifies headless promotion retains owner/runtime/daemon/PTY identity and terminal I/O. Audit4587 retires the one-case CLI WebSocket protocol/preflight suite and its hand-built server; its cross-layer non-delivery witness is intentionally lost, with no replacement coverage claimed.",
