      "knownGaps": [
        "Audit3994 retires two authored callbacks imported by the shared construction test driver: split OSC 9999 carry and rendererless status ownership, plus OpenCode permission text taking priority in status and tui-idle refusal. Remaining imports and selectors keep their scope. No equivalent replacement or fresh gate execution is claimed.",
        "Audit3814 per-case accepted runtime losses:\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-07.spec.ts :: resolves tui-idle from a Codex ready prompt even when stale startup lines remain :: Stale MCP startup lines must not block a later Codex ready header.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-07.spec.ts :: resolves tui-idle when a stale Codex prompt is followed by the ready header :: A Codex ready header following a stale resume prompt must satisfy tui-idle.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-07.spec.ts :: resolves tui-idle for an idle Cursor lane past its dismissed trust dialog (#8210) :: Later Cursor idle banner overrides retained trust dialog.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-07.spec.ts :: does not block a mid-run Cursor lane on its dismissed trust dialog (#8210) :: Dismissed trust dialog must not report blocked for later busy Cursor; wait times out.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-07.spec.ts :: does not classify unrelated press-enter prompts as Codex blocked prompts :: Unidentified press-enter text must time out rather than be classified Codex blocked.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-07.spec.ts :: resolves tui-idle for quiet background PTY agents without OSC titles :: Quiet Codex background terminal without OSC title eventually resolves tui-idle.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-07.spec.ts :: sends agent prompts as bracketed paste before submit :: Driving prompt escapes embedded paste-end ESC, writes one framed paste then CR, and counts bytes.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-08.spec.ts :: settles a foreground Codex prompt when launch metadata has not arrived :: Codex inferred from foreground without launch metadata waits for composer marker/quiescence before one CR.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-08.spec.ts :: gives a late Codex render marker a fresh quiescence window :: Marker arriving at7.9s re-arms fresh quiet window instead of submitting at initial cap.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-08.spec.ts :: writes large agent prompt paste frames atomically before delayed submit :: A prompt larger than input chunk budget is a single paste write before delayed CR with exact byte count.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-08.spec.ts :: rejects oversized terminal.send text before provider writes :: Oversized ordinary terminal.send rejects input-too-large before any provider write.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-08.spec.ts :: rejects focusing an exited background terminal session :: focusTerminal refuses terminal_exited before invoking background reveal.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/agent-launch-prompt-submit.spec.ts :: pastes the same bytes the desktop draft paste sent for the prompt :: Launch-ready prompt normalizes CR/LF and renders embedded ESC visibly identically to desktop bracketed paste.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/agent-launch-prompt-submit.spec.ts :: keeps a prompt into a running agent behind the render settle, as before :: Driving prompt remains held through7s repaint activity then submits once by9s.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-09.spec.ts :: reports a queued PTY focus as not navigated when its notifier disappears :: Queued PTY focus and completed active reveal report not navigated after notifier removal; no second reveal.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-09.spec.ts :: does not invoke a stale graph-leaf focus notifier after queued PTY work :: Queued graph-leaf focus must not invoke old notifier after preceding PTY reveal and notifier removal.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-09.spec.ts :: paginates retained terminal output with explicit limits and truncation metadata :: Preview120lines, fractional limits,50/200 pages, retained2000line truncation and future-cursor metadata stay consistent.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-09.spec.ts :: falls back to renderer visible screen when uncursored TUI tail is blank :: Substantial blank uncursored tail uses mounted renderer visible screen with zero scrollback.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-09.spec.ts :: reads and shows the runtime-owned alternate-screen grid without serialization :: Actual runtime alternate-screen grid provides read/show content without renderer/provider serialization.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-09.spec.ts :: classifies older provider alternate-screen snapshots from ANSI :: Older provider without alternateScreen metadata classifies ANSI alternate entry and returns Remote Vim screen.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-09.spec.ts :: honors the last ANSI screen transition when older provider metadata is absent :: Last ANSI alternate exit overrides earlier entry when explicit provider mode metadata is absent.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-10.spec.ts :: rejects a full provider screen frame after live output advances :: Live output arriving during second full-screen capture causes screen-unavailable rather than stale full frame.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-10.spec.ts :: shares one provider snapshot between concurrent read and show calls :: Concurrent read/show share one successful provider snapshot and both receive Shared TUI content.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-10.spec.ts :: keeps cursor reads provider-free on restored alternate-screen PTYs :: Restored alternate-screen cursor transcript reads never acquire provider snapshot.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-10.spec.ts :: backs off after a provider snapshot failure instead of retrying for show :: Failed provider capture is cached/backed off so later show does not retry.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-10.spec.ts :: falls back once to a mounted renderer when a known alternate provider fails :: A known-alternate failed provider capture falls back exactly once to newly mounted renderer.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-10.spec.ts :: bounds provider visible frames for read and show responses :: Provider visible read/show use six bounded lines and300character preview.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-10.spec.ts :: keeps renderer-fallback composer drafts separate from terminal output :: Renderer fallback strips dim composer draft from terminal output and exposes draft separately.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-10.spec.ts :: does not use renderer visible-screen fallback for a short blank shell tail :: Two blank shell lines must not trigger renderer screen fallback.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-11.spec.ts :: trims terminal tail character budget without per-line array shifts :: Tail builder trims to256KiB with correct retained suffix and no Array.shift calls.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-11.spec.ts :: retains ANSI-only status redraws instead of appending every frame :: Repeated erase/redraw replaces preview until newline then publishes one completed cursor row.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-11.spec.ts :: retains split multi-line ANSI footer redraw state across chunks :: CUU state across chunks retains corrected footer rows and publishes new cursor entries.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-11.spec.ts :: does not let stale lower rows hide earlier corrected footer rows from cursor reads :: Earlier corrected footer row must not be hidden by stale lower rows in cursor reads.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-11.spec.ts :: bounds completed transcript entries from a single multi-line redraw chunk :: Single redraw chunk bounds completed transcript to2000retained lines and correct oldest/next/latest cursors.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-11.spec.ts :: retains multi-line ANSI redraws when the last footer row stays partial :: Partial final redrawn row appears in preview but cursor sees it only after newline.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-11.spec.ts :: does not retain split ANSI controls as visible terminal preview text :: Split color/mode escapes never leak preview fragments; long split OSC title truncates at MAX_OSC_TITLE_CHARS.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-11.spec.ts :: retains same-line redraw cursor position across split full-line erase chunks :: Full-line erase preserves column across chunks so XY follows three spaces rather than old ABC.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/conpty-stream-read.spec.ts :: fills the requested line count even when blank rows sit below the prompt :: Blank rows below a ConPTY prompt must not consume the requested nonempty-line count.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-12.spec.ts :: does not retain split ST-terminated string controls as preview text :: Split ST-terminated Kitty/string controls must remain excluded from preview text.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery.spec.ts :: detects split OSC titles before retaining terminal previews :: Split BEL OSC title must update working title/status without leaking into preview.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery.spec.ts :: detects ST-terminated OSC titles split before the final backslash :: ST OSC split before final backslash must update title without leaking framing.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery.spec.ts :: preserves a trailing escape after a completed OSC title :: Completed OSC followed by pending ESC must preserve the next idle-title transition.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery.spec.ts :: seeds newly synced leaves from PTY pending ANSI state :: A newly synced graph leaf inherits pending ANSI so a split color fragment cannot leak.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery.spec.ts :: bounds retained partial terminal output before preview reads :: Partial terminal state stays capped at 4000, preserves retained array identity, and preview truncation/cursor output remains correct.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery.spec.ts :: submits the mail pointer to Cursor Agent only after the paste-burst delay :: Cursor mailbox pointer Enter must wait through the paste-burst delay; this is a real input-timing alarm intentionally retired.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery-part-02.spec.ts :: adopts a v1.4.150-shaped agent, setup, and shell orphan as one topology transaction :: Stale incarnation refuses without topology change; three agent/setup/shell lanes adopt atomically with layout/group/revision and preserved read/input/resize; exact replay is idempotent and competing owner refuses.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery-part-03.spec.ts :: retires the exact worker when it exits after renderer reveal :: Exact worker exit after reveal retires that worker and its surface.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery-part-03.spec.ts :: re-reveals a recovered worker after the renderer graph epoch changes :: Changed renderer graph epoch invalidates reveal receipt and forces another reveal.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery-part-03.spec.ts :: defers recovery when the renderer omits the exact reveal identity :: Missing exact reveal identity defers recovery after two attempts.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery-part-03.spec.ts :: reconciles a same-id process replacement before headless adoption :: A process replacement before headless adoption must fence off stale ownership.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery-part-04.spec.ts :: retires provider resume only after authoritative inventory proves the legacy PTY exited :: Authoritative owning-host inventory overrides false local hasPty, avoids SSH scanning, retires exited provider resume/surface, adopts live workers without headless reveal.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery-part-04.spec.ts :: retries inventory and unknown liveness without revealing a ghost worker :: Inventory failure and unknown liveness must retry without ghost reveal, eventually adopt, and stop retrying.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-12.spec.ts :: refuses a live reserved pane before issuing a handle or revealing it :: A requireFreshPane launch receiving a live reserved owner must reject before handle/reveal/kill, and release its claim. No equivalent replacement claimed.",
        "Audit3806 per-case accepted runtime losses:\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts.spec.ts :: skips a listener unsubscribed mid-fan-out even with mobile exclusions active :: A listener removed by an earlier listener during one fanout is not called, including with a side-effect-excluded mobile listener present.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts.spec.ts :: retains bytes emitted before a fresh daemon spawn resolves :: Bytes and title arriving before an initial zero/reset provider response survive in the serialized headless buffer with their counted sequence.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts.spec.ts :: emits command-finished facts with best-effort exit codes across chunk splits :: A split OSC133 D exit code becomes130 and a missing code becomes null in ordered command-finished facts.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts.spec.ts :: emits pr-link facts once per URL with batch attribution :: A split GitHub PR URL yields42 rather than4, emits42/43 once each, and carries PTY/worktree/tab attribution.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-02.spec.ts :: emits 2031-subscribe facts across chunk splits :: Split ESC[?20 then31h emits exactly one2031-subscribe fact.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-02.spec.ts :: restores a provisional 2031 subscribe when daemon scan authority returns :: Returning daemon scan authority with partial scan seed and pending2031 subscription restores exactly one subscribe fact.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-02.spec.ts :: prefers the tracked title over the renderer snapshot lastTitle :: A synthetic live Cursor title overrides stale renderer lastTitle while preserving renderer snapshot source.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-02.spec.ts :: prefers provider history over a partial headless mirror for requested snapshots :: Authoritative requested snapshots return supplied provider frame/history/seq rather than a partial headless mirror, requesting5000rows.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-02.spec.ts :: tracks live alternate-screen transitions after a provider snapshot :: Provider alternateScreen true is accepted, then live1049l/1049h update isTerminalAlternateScreen false/true.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-02.spec.ts :: translates reset provider snapshots without retaining the old title :: A reset provider snapshot translates new local seq into the runtime domain and replaces Old process title with New process.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-02.spec.ts :: emits the chunk agentStatus events before its side-effect batch :: Agent status callback precedes side-effect batch callback for one coalesced OSC9999/title/bell chunk.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-02.spec.ts :: still emits a throwing chunk’s facts under its own seq, not the next chunk’s :: A tracker throw still flushes first chunk title facts under its own seq, and second chunk does not inherit those facts.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-02.spec.ts :: seeds the lazily created tracker from the daemon-snapshot title :: A lazy tracker hydrated from renderer snapshot title Codex working emits agent-idle on later Codex done.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-03.spec.ts :: emits command-code-working facts only after the banner arms the scrape :: Unarmed Thinking text emits no facts; a Command Code0.27.3 banner then hardcoded colored spinner text emits attributed command-code-working with the submitted prompt.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-03.spec.ts :: emits a command-code-done fact when the idle composer returns :: After hardcoded banner/working text, returned idle composer emits command-code-done with the earlier submitted prompt.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/headless-snapshots.spec.ts :: resizes the headless mirror after an accepted desktop PTY resize :: An external accepted resize produces the resized dimensions and same status-frame lines as a separately driven reference emulator.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/headless-snapshots.spec.ts :: replaces suffix-only headless state with the recovered renderer snapshot :: Replacing suffix-only state removes old suffix, retains renderer history plus later output/cwd, and returns the live47x40PTY grid.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/headless-snapshots.spec.ts :: stamps SSH connection identity on runtime terminal status :: A synthetic mounted-leaf OSC9999 status after registerPty carries the supplied SSH connectionId.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/headless-snapshots.spec.ts :: does not retain WSL context when a PTY id is reused :: After exit and same-ID new null distro context, OSC7 file://server/share/repo uses UNC server path rather than old Ubuntu namespace.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/headless-snapshots.spec.ts :: preserves immutable context while a live daemon attach is unresolved :: preparePtyExecutionContext with preserveExisting refuses a supplied Debian replacement and subsequent OSC7 keeps original Ubuntu namespace.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/headless-snapshots-part-02.spec.ts :: projects frame-independent live state through main buffer snapshots :: Main-buffer snapshot puts focus-report/cursor-visibility modes in frameRestoreAnsi, excludes STATIC-FRAME there and includes it in data.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/agent-status-and-waits.spec.ts :: continues terminal agent status fanout when a callback throws :: Throwing on the first status callback does not prevent second payload delivery and logs contextual error.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-02.spec.ts :: returns a title-only replay snapshot and never historical attention :: Lose replay:true/title-only fact projection despite earlierbell and unknownPTYnull. No actual delivered-history notification or reattach behavior was exercised. No equivalent replacement claimed.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/agent-status-and-waits-part-02.spec.ts :: rejects a handle rebind while a controller-less status check yields :: A handle rebound while the null-controller status continuation yields must throw terminal_handle_stale.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/agent-status-and-waits-part-02.spec.ts :: rejects confirmation evidence when the owning PTY exits :: A pending strong confirmation resolving after owning PTY exit must reject terminal_exited.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/agent-status-and-waits-part-03.spec.ts :: keeps ordinary terminal send suffix failures on the existing not-writable contract :: Ordinary send writes text but refused CR must throw terminal_not_writable with beforeWrite twice and afterWrite once.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness.spec.ts :: refuses a requested shell the execution host cannot apply instead of spawning its default :: Requested Windows shell on POSIX must refuse before spawning a default shell.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness.spec.ts :: quotes the agent startup command for the requested shell, not the host default :: Requested cmd shell must override PowerShell default quoting for agent startup command.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness.spec.ts :: keeps restored receipts outside a targeted worktree scan :: Targeted scan removes the moved-worktree receipt while preserving another worktree receipt.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-06.spec.ts :: observes setup command completion without waiting for its interactive shell to exit :: Nonzero completion marker 17 resolves while interactive shell remains running.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-06.spec.ts :: falls back to setup terminal exit when no completion signal is available :: Setup completion observer without token falls back to actual exit code 9.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-06.spec.ts :: cancels setup completion observation when the caller aborts :: Abort rejects with the original reason and unsubscribes once.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-06.spec.ts :: keeps observing after an uncertain setup terminal status :: Unknown exit waiter result must leave observation pending until completion marker arrives.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-06.spec.ts :: keeps retained PTY transcript memory when controller refresh omits a record :: Controller inventory omission disconnects the record but preserves its retained transcript.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-06.spec.ts :: keeps retained PTY transcript memory when controller refresh times out :: Hung inventory timeout leaves connected record and retained transcript intact.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-06.spec.ts :: resolves tui-idle for adopted background PTY handles from the renderer title :: An adopted background handle resolves tui-idle from ready Codex renderer title.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-06.spec.ts :: resolves live-leaf tui-idle from an OpenCode native title :: A live leaf resolves tui-idle from an OpenCode native title.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-06.spec.ts :: resolves tui-idle from a Codex ready prompt preview :: A supplied Codex prompt preview resolves tui-idle without an actual agent.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-06.spec.ts :: resolves tui-idle from an Antigravity prompt before the model line :: A supplied Antigravity prompt before model line resolves tui-idle.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness.spec.ts :: refuses a requested shell with no workspace instead of creating a default-shell tab :: Workspace-less explicit shell must reject before renderer default-tab request or spawn. This real guard/wiring alarm is deliberately retired.",
        "Audit3798 per-case accepted losses:\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/paired-settings.spec.ts :: awaits navigation-only updates from paired clients (%s) :: Updating only claudeSubagentNavigationEnabled waits for the actual controller call to the supplied pending Claude-view reconcile for both on/off values.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/browser-capabilities.spec.ts :: drops a client page record even when its close command cannot be issued :: A removed workspace loses its runtime client-page record and headless browser projection despite close delivery_required rejection, and emits the asynchronous warning.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/browser-capabilities.spec.ts :: leaves client-hosted pages alone when another host still owns the same worktree id :: Removing runtime:env-b metadata with local ownership leaves the local same-ID client page unchanged and issues no close command.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts :: marks live bindings again when reopening after a promoted window closes :: A reopened window marks its still-registered live worktree in activeWorktreeIdsOnShutdown after the first promoted window closes.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts :: preserves live SSH session identities when promoting a headless runtime :: Headless-to-desktop promotion records active worktree, SSH connection and remoteSessionIdsByTabId from the supplied surviving SSH PTY/session.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts :: restores a surviving renderer when its reload is cancelled :: A sole ready renderer reload cancelled under its current renderer fence returns true and becomes ready.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts :: restores headless authority when desktop promotion navigation is cancelled :: A cancelled desktop promotion with headless recovery returns false while headless authority remains ready.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts :: moves a desktop graph to unavailable when its reload times out :: A ready desktop graph without a headless fallback becomes unavailable at the reload deadline and retains its window/epoch.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts :: recovers a failed headless promotion and accepts a later renderer generation :: A promotion failure restores ready headless authority; a later valid same-window graph publishes ready desktop authority.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles.spec.ts :: clears a failed pane recovery so a later reconnect can retry :: After relay_reconnecting rejection, the pending recovery lock clears and the same pane/handle can call createTerminal a second time and return its supplied replacement.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles.spec.ts :: still preserves a CLI agent leaf when the reloaded renderer has not rebound its PTY :: An empty graph published during renderer reload preserves a preallocated live CLI PTY as one listable terminal before renderer rebind.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-part-02.spec.ts :: keeps a no-incarnation handle across an in-graph pane remint :: Within one graph lifetime an unversioned PTY reminted onto another leaf retains its issued handle and resolves its old exit waiter after onPtyExit.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-listing.spec.ts :: matches explicit-id cwd PTYs when the resolved worktree cache is incomplete :: An explicit target absent from a fresh incomplete resolved cache adopts only its cwd PTY, rejects nested cwd PTY and does not rescan Git.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-listing.spec.ts :: ignores cwd-only controller PTYs for malformed explicit worktree IDs :: Malformed id:repo-1:: returns no terminals, does not adopt cwd-only controller PTY and avoids Git rescanning.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/ssh-worktree-lifecycle.spec.ts :: refuses an SSH-backed create for mobile/runtime callers instead of creating locally :: Loss of this public unserved SSH create error-class/no-local-add/no-local-list alarm.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/ssh-worktree-lifecycle.spec.ts :: records an app-selected parent workspace as a manual action :: Loss of the local runtime folder-parent manual origin, active-workspace source and explicit confidence projection alarm; no claim that SSH or cleanup coverage replaces it.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/repository-project-operations.spec.ts :: browses runtime server directories before projects are added :: Loss of this public runtime alarm for browse availability before registration, directories-first lexical ordering and native path flavor.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/repository-project-operations.spec.ts :: lists drive roots for a server-root browse :: Loss of the Windows public slash-root drive enumeration smoke and presence of the temporary directory drive.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/repository-project-operations-part-02.spec.ts :: creates a missing runtime parent before creating the project directory :: Loss of this runtime createRepo recursive missing-parent/child existence and registered-path alarm.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/project-setup-folder-remote-identity.spec.ts :: preserves selected project %s when a hosted parent is known :: Loss of both parent-selected and origin-selected normal fork-link projection/persisted upstream alarms plus exact single-probe count.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/project-setup-folder-remote-identity.spec.ts :: links a current enterprise remote despite unavailable metadata and a retained %s :: Loss of normal current-enterprise-origin linking with stale automatic GitHub avatar or protected file image, unchanged icon assertion, and serialized project identity under unavailable metadata.",
        "Audit2271: Retire the deleted serve-desktop-promotion-session-continuity suite receipt from structured evidenceRuns. The exact dated original object is preserved below as historical text, including its prior claims; it supplies no current promotion/renderer continuity or equivalent replacement evidence. The replacement structured receipt covers only the unchanged serve-signal-exit-diagnostic selector and its late-handoff-after-child-exit supervisor assertion. No promoted-renderer, persistent-PTY, native Electron, provider, remote or platform execution equivalence is assigned. Historical retired receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-05\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/lib/serve-desktop-promotion-session-continuity.test.ts\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 2,\n          \"summary\": \"Six tests passed joining the serve lock owner, the activation gate, and the promoted renderer's resume accounting. Red evidence: reverting the hidden-pane ownership predicate launched two duplicate codex resume tabs; additionally zeroing the live-PTY check made both hydration passes red; removing the duplicate-serve argv guard opened a window for `--serve`; always marking the gate ready removed the fail-closed diagnostic; refusing to open a window dropped both promotion assertions.\"\n        }",
        "Audit2145 accepts removal of canned runtime metadata/guard/forwarding, fake in-memory persistence, private work-count and wrapper-duplication tests from the construction/orca-runtime.test.ts aggregate, plus the two automation run-context guards from runtime-workspace-launch-contracts.test.ts. Retained race, framing, physical completion and ownership callbacks remain byte-identical. Existing commands remain valid selectors; historical receipts stay unchanged and provide no fresh validation or replacement coverage for the reduced suites.",
