      "invariant": "Every genuine renderer graph reload revision settles exactly once, while a blocked external navigation that preserves the current document never starts a revision. A cancelled renderer-document navigation restores authority only when that same renderer survived; cancellation after an earlier document committed remains fenced until publication or timeout. Replacing a reload cancels only the prior revision; its timer and callbacks cannot settle a newer revision. A desktop reload succeeds only from a publication carrying a new renderer-document generation, while a failed headless promotion may recover only from its originating window. Timeout, renderer loss, and close reach a terminal graph state, and successful desktop publication permanently retires headless sentinel fallback until a new headless runtime is established.",
      "oracle": "Audit4362 intentionally deletes the imported stale-waiter retry and manually assembled OSC9999 mobile-republish cases, plus the mocked missing-worktree cleanup suite (4 authored / 5 finite cases in three suites). Lost alarms include repeated unread worker_done pointers, working-to-waiting mobile status publication, missing-worktree filtering, and scoped daemon shutdown with unrelated duplicate identities. No replacement coverage or new platform proof is claimed. Audit3832 deliberately retires76 authored/79 finite cases:75 runtime compatibility cases/78 finite cases across14 fragments, plus one localization extractor default-flag case. Three whole runtime fragments are deleted;27 authored/30 finite cases remain across the reviewed sources. This gate retains only its own selected scope; no equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/native/remote evidence is claimed. Runtime component A: Audit3828 composes3822 with independent3824: deliberately retires49 authored/52 finite cases from seven compatibility fragments, leaving15 authored/18 finite cases and deleting two entire fragments. Accepted losses: positive folder-worker recovery/materialization and reveal deadline; persisted-key normalization and legacy split/group/focus projection; fixed stale CAS refusal; occupied/alias/restored/preallocated terminal-handle variants; fixed OpenCode/Cursor/Claude/Codex/Antigravity classification, readiness, title and management examples; direct private-map browser authority projections; browser-focus and OMP title projection; already-aborted claim cleanup. Additional3824 loss: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-02.spec.ts :: does not poll a wrapper foreground for a speculative CLI prompt send :: Speculative retryForegroundWrappers:false check must return false on a wrapper after one foreground read, without polling the supplied later codex response. These real bounded alarms are deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained callbacks are unchanged and provide only their own bounded scope, not equivalent replacement. Historical receipts do not validate reduced callbacks. No fresh runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser evidence or full transitive closure is claimed. Runtime component B: Audit3834 deliberately retires26 authored/26 finite cases from seven fresh compatibility fragments, leaving10/10 and deleting the one-case saved-binding reattachment fragment. Original position58 is excluded: its existing substantive3578 KEEP7 review remains historical, with no fresh credit. Accepted losses: fixed hook/provider-session identities and stale metadata refusal; decorative/pre-title foreground ordering variants; saved-binding surface reattachment; saved-row exit ghost removal and silent activation selection; unsupported headless wake; positive pending materialization/group projections; per-caller navigation selection; positive SSH hydration/read partition; laptop mobile publication/buffer and background/pending/status projections; abnormal/unregistered SSH grace, normal-exit refusal, persisted SSH hydration, positive serve reattachment, pending-agent launch arguments and direct seeded running-launch admission guard. These are real bounded alarms deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained cases preserve their own distinct deferred foreground coalescing, usable handle continuity, stale inventory refresh, concurrent browser snapshot preservation, renderer graph fencing, caller dedup isolation, SSH partition writes, runtime split lifetime, independent relay-ready publication, lease admission/state/expiry. The direct running-launch no-spawn guard alarm is deliberately retired; no remaining owning-launch refusal coverage is claimed. Historical runs do not validate reduced callbacks. No equivalent replacement, runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser result or full transitive closure is claimed. Additional extractor loss: config/scripts/localization/source-extraction/audit-localization-native-dialogs.test.mjs :: does not change the existing renderer scan by default :: Default options must omit the five native-only fields in this supplied snippet. No equivalent replacement is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit3814 deliberately retires60 authored/60 finite cases:53runtime compatibility cases,4native XCTest methods and3Python clipboard methods, including the entire StableElementIndexes suite. Clipboard cuts retire the one-over-cap sample, incoming-offer destruction trace and sequential20-copy replay; actual wire, FD/pipe, startup and Xvfb/GTK boundaries remain without equivalent replacement claims. Accepted losses include narrow terminal-send payload/provider projections, legacy and direct no-op/error permutations, timing/work-count examples, private state/title/activity projections and fixture-driven readiness examples, individually enumerated below. These include real bounded production alarms consciously retired for marginal value; retained failed writes, duplicate submission, stale capture, transcript/ring and allocation fences are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or complete transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3806 deliberately retires40 authored/40 finite runtime compatibility cases, including the terminal-side-effect-facts-part03 headless-snapshots-part02 and agent-status-and-waits-part03 fragments, plus20 scalar Swift precondition sites. Lost runtime alarms include status/title/attention projection examples, simple renderer/headless frame restoration and status waiting outcomes detailed in the accepted-loss ledger. Swift cuts retire duplicate generation-map/schema/navigation/bridge and notification-wrapper assertions; no standalone native program is deleted. These include real bounded production alarms consciously retired for marginal value. Retained races, pending writes/reflow, namespace and waiter ownership are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or full transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3798 deliberately retires21 authored/24 finite compatibility cases, including the entire SSH-worktree-lifecycle and repository-project-operations fragments. Accepted losses include navigation-only settings acknowledgement, browser session cleanup and host preservation projections, window positive/policy-state examples, terminal recovery/reload and no-incarnation remint examples, terminal listing compatibility/malformed IDs, directory browse/sort/Windows path smoke, SSH create refusal/manual lineage, recursive parent-folder creation and fork/origin/avatar/icon projections. Real bounded production alarms are consciously retired for marginal value; retained authority races, cleanup/clone ownership, pending waiters, nested-folder and scan invalidation cases are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or full transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3417 composes root-adopted3415v2/independent3416v2: intentionally removes117authored/173potential expanded registrations from12semantic sources, deleting4whole conventional suites and3registration modules and retaining4authored/5expanded cases, without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. The whole main-window attach-services suite is removed: runtime/window attach, notifier wiring, reload/teardown and permission-handler mock orchestration alarms are intentionally lost. Prune its exact deleted command selectors, testFiles entries and notifier assertionRef where present; complete prior selectors/ref are archived. Unrelated dated receipts remain exact and retain their original scope; no fresh reduced-selector, native-window or remote execution is claimed.  Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The retained runtime registration driver loses three complete imported fragments: changed-working-label title facts and suppressed-frame tracked snapshots; refusing SSH GitLab MR-base lookup before local Git/glab calls; and missing folder-workspace path creation/update refusal before spawn/store mutation. These alarms are intentionally lost. Other imported fragments and separately rooted dated receipts are unchanged; they are not equivalent replacement coverage.  Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2095 current-parent preparation2126: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2090 (sources2088/2089): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2086 (sources2082/2083): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2076 (sources2073/2074): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-part-02.spec.ts: recovers a moved SSH pane through the tab it now sits in, not the one its lease froze; reports a plain expired orphan; does not report a pane whose only recent lease was superseded; does not report a pane whose only recent lease had its relay id recycled; picks the eligible orphan over a superseded predecessor that matches first; collects the same tabs the per-tab reader reports, in one sweep of the leases; reports no candidate when no lease names any of the worktree tabs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/runtime-availability.spec.ts: starts unavailable with no authoritative window; reports the configured Windows terminal shell on status; reports floating workspace availability from settings on status; polls floating tabs with targeted PTY liveness and no repo/provider inventory; hydrates persisted tabs when the store cannot report repos; advertises browser screencast only when a renderer window is available; routes mobile Codex reset consumption through the account mutation coordinator; maps a definite pre-provider rejection into an authoritative current snapshot. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Existing exact unchanged-selector receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Changed source selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical prior-source oracle account: Existing exact unchanged-selector receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Changed source selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical prior-source oracle account: Start a blocked external main-frame navigation and require the current renderer graph and notification path to remain authoritative. Start a same-renderer navigation, cancel it before commit, and require the renderer canary and ready authority to survive; coalesce overlapping provisional starts into one fence, and keep an earlier committed reload fenced if a later navigation is cancelled. Drive two genuine reloads half a timeout apart and require the first deadline to leave the second revision reloading while the second deadline alone makes it unavailable. During the second revision publish from the prior renderer document through the still-current main frame and require rejection without graph mutation or timeout cancellation. Restore headless authority after failed promotion, publish from a competing window, and require rejection while the sentinel remains authoritative. Then force a real renderer crash and separately promote an isolated headless serve owner; require runtime graph readiness, stable runtime/main/daemon/PTY identities, recovered visible terminal output, and post-recovery input/output.",
