        "evidence": "Audit1991: Remove membership/timer and error-close inventory aliases and the raw-TCP-cap alias from the changed transport source. Retire the sole dated combined42-case receipt whole. Downgrade to no active evidence; archive all prospective commands, file/assertion aliases and covered-scope fields rather than transfer their authority to unchanged sibling suites. Real oversized-message closure, pre-auth expiry, revocation, half-open cleanup and bounded shutdown callbacks remain in source but have no fresh gate result. Changed-source prior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, physical provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): The transport retains exactly one shared interval, performs one O(N) sweep per tick, and adds no per-socket heartbeat timer, polling, subprocess, network request, or immediate later-socket sweep. Each accepted socket retains only its existing lifecycle listeners and pre-auth timer; deterministic assertions preserve the shared timer identity and bound final cleanup to zero timers."
