cancellation, execution-host and real-filesystem outcomes with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Deterministic main-IPC contract tests cover disconnect-driven close delivery, exactly-once close, per-subscription teardown isolation against a failing socket close and a throwing liveness probe, containment of a throwing renderer send on the unguarded host-close path, and continued suppression of stale payloads from a retired transport. A headed paired-server journey (real Orca host plus a separate paired Orca desktop client) covers hidden-but-mounted reveal, cold-parked reveal, and cold-parked reveal across a disconnect/reconnect. Live Linux and Windows paired-server evidence and real sleep/wake transport loss remain uncollected.",
      "motivatingLinks": ["tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-parked-reveal-interactivity.spec.ts"],
      "invariant": "Every renderer-held runtime subscription receives exactly one terminal close event when its transport is retired, including when the retirement advanced the transport generation first, and a single failing teardown never abandons that environment's remaining subscriptions nor escapes into the transport that reported the close. Payload frames from a retired transport stay suppressed. A revealed remote terminal therefore reattaches over a live multiplex connection: its buffer restores, typed input reaches the host PTY, the echo paints without a tab flip, and the PTY converges on the revealed pane grid.",
      "oracle": "Audit3832 deliberately retires76 authored/79 finite cases:75 runtime compatibility cases/78 finite cases across14 fragments, plus one localization extractor default-flag case. Three whole runtime fragments are deleted;27 authored/30 finite cases remain across the reviewed sources. This gate retains only its own selected scope; no equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/native/remote evidence is claimed. Runtime component A: Audit3828 composes3822 with independent3824: deliberately retires49 authored/52 finite cases from seven compatibility fragments, leaving15 authored/18 finite cases and deleting two entire fragments. Accepted losses: positive folder-worker recovery/materialization and reveal deadline; persisted-key normalization and legacy split/group/focus projection; fixed stale CAS refusal; occupied/alias/restored/preallocated terminal-handle variants; fixed OpenCode/Cursor/Claude/Codex/Antigravity classification, readiness, title and management examples; direct private-map browser authority projections; browser-focus and OMP title projection; already-aborted claim cleanup. Additional3824 loss: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-02.spec.ts :: does not poll a wrapper foreground for a speculative CLI prompt send :: Speculative retryForegroundWrappers:false check must return false on a wrapper after one foreground read, without polling the supplied later codex response. These real bounded alarms are deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained callbacks are unchanged and provide only their own bounded scope, not equivalent replacement. Historical receipts do not validate reduced callbacks. No fresh runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser evidence or full transitive closure is claimed. Runtime component B: Audit3834 deliberately retires26 authored/26 finite cases from seven fresh compatibility fragments, leaving10/10 and deleting the one-case saved-binding reattachment fragment. Original position58 is e