        "Audit3798 per-case accepted losses:\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/paired-settings.spec.ts :: awaits navigation-only updates from paired clients (%s) :: Updating only claudeSubagentNavigationEnabled waits for the actual controller call to the supplied pending Claude-view reconcile for both on/off values.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/browser-capabilities.spec.ts :: drops a client page record even when its close command cannot be issued :: A removed workspace loses its runtime client-page record and headless browser projection despite close delivery_required rejection, and emits the asynchronous warning.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/browser-capabilities.spec.ts :: leaves client-hosted pages alone when another host still owns the same worktree id :: Removing runtime:env-b metadata with local ownership leaves the local same-ID client page unchanged and issues no close command.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts :: marks live bindings again when reopening after a promoted window closes :: A reopened window marks its still-registered live worktree in activeWorktreeIdsOnShutdown after the first promoted window closes.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts :: preserves live SSH session identities when promoting a headless runtime :: Headless-to-desktop promotion records active worktree, SSH connection and remoteSessionIdsByTabId from the supplied surviving SSH PTY/session.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts :: restores a surviving renderer when its reload is cancelled :: A sole ready renderer reload cancelled under its current renderer fence returns true and becomes ready.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts :: restores headless authority when desktop promotion navigation is cancelled :: A cancelled desktop promotion with headless recovery returns false while headless authority remains ready.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts :: moves a desktop graph to unavailable when its reload times out :: A ready desktop graph without a headless fallback becomes unavailable at the reload deadline and retains its window/epoch.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts :: recovers a failed headless promotion and accepts a later renderer generation :: A promotion failure restores ready headless authority; a later valid same-window graph publishes ready desktop authority.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles.spec.ts :: clears a failed pane recovery so a later reconnect can retry :: After relay_reconnecting rejection, the pending recovery lock clears and the same pane/handle can call createTerminal a second time and return its supplied replacement.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles.spec.ts :: still preserves a CLI agent leaf when the reloaded renderer has not rebound its PTY :: An empty graph published during renderer reload preserves a preallocated live CLI PTY as one listable terminal before renderer rebind.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-part-02.spec.ts :: keeps a no-incarnation handle across an in-graph pane remint :: Within one graph lifetime an unversioned PTY reminted onto another leaf retains its issued handle and resolves its old exit waiter after onPtyExit.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-listing.spec.ts :: matches explicit-id cwd PTYs when the resolved worktree cache is incomplete :: An explicit target absent from a fresh incomplete resolved cache adopts only its cwd PTY, rejects nested cwd PTY and does not rescan Git.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-listing.spec.ts :: ignores cwd-only controller PTYs for malformed explicit worktree IDs :: Malformed id:repo-1:: returns no terminals, does not adopt cwd-only controller PTY and avoids Git rescanning.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/ssh-worktree-lifecycle.spec.ts :: refuses an SSH-backed create for mobile/runtime callers instead of creating locally :: Loss of this public unserved SSH create error-class/no-local-add/no-local-list alarm.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/ssh-worktree-lifecycle.spec.ts :: records an app-selected parent workspace as a manual action :: Loss of the local runtime folder-parent manual origin, active-workspace source and explicit confidence projection alarm; no claim that SSH or cleanup coverage replaces it.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/repository-project-operations.spec.ts :: browses runtime server directories before projects are added :: Loss of this public runtime alarm for browse availability before registration, directories-first lexical ordering and native path flavor.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/repository-project-operations.spec.ts :: lists drive roots for a server-root browse :: Loss of the Windows public slash-root drive enumeration smoke and presence of the temporary directory drive.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/repository-project-operations-part-02.spec.ts :: creates a missing runtime parent before creating the project directory :: Loss of this runtime createRepo recursive missing-parent/child existence and registered-path alarm.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/project-setup-folder-remote-identity.spec.ts :: preserves selected project %s when a hosted parent is known :: Loss of both parent-selected and origin-selected normal fork-link projection/persisted upstream alarms plus exact single-probe count.\nsrc/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/project-setup-folder-remote-identity.spec.ts :: links a current enterprise remote despite unavailable metadata and a retained %s :: Loss of normal current-enterprise-origin linking with stale automatic GitHub avatar or protected file image, unchanged icon assertion, and serialized project identity under unavailable metadata.",
        "Audit3788 retires10 authored/11 expanded cases across six changed drivers, including the entire screencast pending-frame-retry and usage-source-cache-streaming suites. Deliberate losses are false-refused last-frame retry/once-only delivery, ordinary stable-pane reattachment, cleared-chat Dispatch completion, terminal-declared chat-caller refusal, at-rest worker liveness projection, nested depth/cap policy, small unsigned6/sealed7 plain-format and verified-bit examples, generic malformed-ISIZE footer refusal examples, and synthetic10k/100k chunk-size/work-count budgets in gzip and general cache I/O. These include real state/disk/RPC outcomes consciously retired for marginal value; retained E2EE-backlog, receipt/custody/uncertain-ack, integrity/migration and staging-cleanup cases are not equivalent replacements. The footer test did not prove early rejection or bounded allocation; staging cleanup did not seed unrelated files. No replacement or fresh native/remote/performance execution is claimed. Earlier raw selectors and dated receipts remain historical.",
        "Audit3779 retires17 authored/17 expanded registrations across six changed drivers, including the entire shared-Codex-home and prompt-telemetry suites. Accepted losses are shared-home wrapper noninterference/opt-out preservation, mocked metric count/provenance filters, SSH activity labeling/clearing and handover idle timing, VM ownership/capability/status projections and asleep-worktree refusal, a link-only external conversation replay sample, and two narrow input-credit noninterference/expiry examples. Retain the direct exact-tab/single-use input-credit case. These bounded real disk/state/routing alarms are intentionally retired for marginal value without equivalent replacement or fresh execution claims; earlier receipts remain historical.",
        "Audit3772 retires18 authored/27 expanded cases, including whole Codex service opt-out, RPC capability-parser, creator-provenance, short-ciphertext and readiness-null suites. Accepted losses include service ledger/symlink/mode cleanup, user TOML substring preservation, old-hash cleanup, description pass-through, malformed-file/pending-hash examples, coordinator write/probe counts, capability array bounds, positive creator projections, early short-payload refusal and readiness helper null shape. Two redundant Codex exit-cause rows are also retired; Pi shares their direct-idle path only in this empty-output immediate-exit fixture, and future agent-config drift coverage is lost. Real bounded filesystem/parser/runtime alarms are deliberately retired for marginal value; no equivalent replacements or fresh execution are claimed. Earlier receipts retain their historical scope.",
        "Audits3754/3755 intentionally remove9 authored/9 finite registrations: the entire one-case usage-source-cache-streaming.test.ts driver and8 cases from the surviving computer-action-validation.test.ts driver. This gate retains an unfiltered root Vitest command; UNIT_INCLUDE admits both source paths. Accepted losses are the real encoder output chunk-size/work-count alarm on repetitive10k/100k ownership payloads through a mocked durable sink, plus CLI diagnostic precedence, fractional window-id rejection, action-call-site window-target exclusivity, plain-text click-count recovery copy, incomplete click/drag targeting, mouse/modifier/direction allowlist samples and inline/stdin text exclusivity. These CLI cases exercise real argument/handler validation before mocked runtime calls; they are deliberately retired for marginal value, not declared tautologies. Retained cache I/O and CLI cases are not equivalent replacements for these alarms. Existing historical raw receipts remain unchanged and do not validate the deleted or reduced drivers. No fresh execution claim is made. Audits3758/3763 intentionally remove9 authored/11 finite registrations from6 changed drivers, including the entire pane-title-notification, window-linear-notices and worktree-card-lifecycle-effects suites. This gate retains an unfiltered root Vitest command admitting these paths. Accepted losses are same-account linked-row success-notice fanout, sidebar-switch channel forwarding, Linear-only notification forwarding/non-terminal-consumer selection/closed-window detach, destroyed-window refusal and first-send-failure suspension through the pane-title adapter, the100-card synthetic focus/poll absence sample, stored-source local folder badge refresh, unobserved-row badge refusal, and immediate reposChanged lineage invalidation. These exercise real owners with controlled ports; they are retired for marginal value, without equivalent replacement claims. The no-badge-work fixture does not seed its title-promised collection-only cache. Preserved historical receipts do not validate deleted or reduced drivers; no fresh execution is claimed. Audit3759 retires the entire one-case Tailwind compiler/scanner smoke. Accept loss of the direct CSS production/test/spec source-exclusion and rescan alarm; no replacement or current execution is claimed.",
        "Audit3752 independently approves audit3749: retire five authored/five finite watcher-process registrations, retaining18 raw-exact registrations. Accept loss of healthy shared-pool joint recovery, last-pending-failure idle retirement/respawn, late VITEST fallback release, missing-entry fail-closed selection and independent-supervisor fuse locality alarms. These are real bounded host-policy alarms intentionally retired for low marginal value; no equivalent replacement is asserted. Remaining driver selections exercise controlled FakeChild supervisor lifecycle, cancellation, physical-exit fencing, recovery and fuse behavior. This source review supplies no fresh native/process/platform/remote/SSH execution; historical receipts retain original source and selector scopes.",
        "Audits3738/3742/3743/3744 intentionally remove15 authored/21 finite registrations from six surviving drivers, with no equivalent replacement or fresh execution claim. This gate retains an unfiltered root Vitest command. Current UNIT_INCLUDE admits the partial push-service, metadata-dialog and two config/scripts browser drivers:10 authored/16 finite removals. Accepted losses: actual retry30s/60s progression and register bucket/refill wiring, explicit seven-day lease arithmetic (its notification lacked seq/epoch and never reached send), equal-name edit latch/save payload, real image/font/meta-refresh/form/popup browser refusal controls, and broad rich-markdown bridge/command/edit-select smoke. Actual production state, callback routing and browser enforcement run in these cases; these alarms are deliberately retired on marginal value. All drivers and selectors survive. Existing unrelated receipts remain historical evidence for their unchanged selectors, not proof of the reduced cases.",
        "Audit3732 removes 2 authored/3 finite registrations from two partial suites: nominal custom/Kimi local naming success and deferred context usage row presentation. Real losses: custom/Kimi successful extraction through conversation-name sanitization and agentLabel composition; separate ordered counted/deferred lists and exact percentage/token formatting. No replacement or equivalent coverage claimed. Retain 11 authored/13 finite raw-exact registrations for bounded naming instruction/refusal/cancellation, menu dismissal focus ownership and hover/composer Escape/timer cleanup. Source-only bounded value review, no runtime/CI/native/remote/mobile/folder workspace or global completion credit.",
        "Audit3733 removes2authored/2finite terminal input checks: fixed custom-cap error/secret fixture and three-emoji cap5refusal whose6UTF16units already trip length fast guard (no UTF8-dependent boundary). Accept exact non-disclosure/oversized-refusal alarm losses; no replacement/equivalence claim. Retain13/13scalar/pending input, OSC state and cron DST/cadence outcomes after bounded material reads. Source-only zero runtime/novelty credit; original historical reasons preserved.",
        "Audit3729 removes1authored/3finite by deleting whole CLI runtime pairing advisory-close suite. Accept losing post-real-close injected EIO preservation of native/script/unreadable pairing, env identity/preservation and exact close/release assertions; no actual failed-close leak or replacement coverage claimed. Two retained URL grammar/identity suites11authored16finite raw unchanged. Bounded source/owner/caller value review, zero novelty/runtime credit; other seven3724deferred closures remain. Historical receipts preserve original limits.",
        "Audit3724 removes3authored/3finite checks by deleting two whole suites: TUI clear burst-size singleton and terminal-file-URL target two-case wrapper suite. Deliberate losses: derived widest burst<64byte alarm, UNC authority+line-column anchor composition, and malformed-percent null refusal. Real production algorithms execute in those tests; no mocked-output tautology, equivalent replacement, actual Claude/file-navigation delivery or universal safety-irrelevance claim. TUI58byte bound and URI examples have low marginal value as standalone suites. Actual1262/1264/1742KEEP superseded explicitly. Remaining14drivers83authored136finite raw unchanged. Bounded source-only review; ten closures deferred, four bounded keep judgments repeated with zero new semantic-frontier credit. No runtime/CI/native/remote/mobile/folder/global completion claim; historical receipts retain original scope.",
        "Audit3723 removes 4 authored/4 finite registrations in two whole suites: keybinding cache freeze/token spellings and host-dependent Orca command name examples. Real losses include returned-object freeze, repeated Mod+P key, Space/PageDown/NumpadSubtract mapping, unknown/empty/prototype-token rejection, and headless Linux versus Windows-server/WSL command choice. No equivalent or replacement coverage claimed. Retain 12 authored/21 finite raw-exact registrations exercising generated scaffold validation, artifact failures, shipped editor/hook/worker/panel tests, actual generated typing compilation, independent CLI root routing and intent-name precedence. Source-only bounded audit; no runtime, CI, native, remote, mobile, folder workspace or global completion credit.",
        "Audit3720 removes17authored/23finite checks: whole main catalog-date adapter2 and shared date-helper7, seven renderer nominal ranking/cap/no-date/composition cases, and one browser registration expanding to seven forced-container/DOM-child boundary cases. Deliberate real losses: community oldest-date UTC forwarding, official/undated omission, date sorting/window/invalid/future/skew/clamp and default/override cap; nominal ranking/cap and combined Featured/Newly-added outputs; real CSS459/460,719/720,1055/1056breakpoint, five-card partial-row and720px two-card first-row alarms. Browser cases really measure rendered geometry but force width/remove DOM children; no fake-pixel or tautology rationale. No replacement/equivalent coverage claimed. Retain14authored/19finite raw-exact registrations across4drivers: adversarial featured category/order/tie and installability, date order/window selection, actual PluginManager failure/escaping/duplicate-card suppression, real browser viewport/odd-count geometry/phone catalog visibility, syntax ingress/depth/include/printability and68dlong-bracket auto-close fill-in. No tests/browser/native/UI/provider/remote/mobile/folder/CI/global execution or completion credit.",
        "Audit3717 removes6 authored/6finite checks in two whole thin-adapter/presentation suites. Deliberate real losses: ordinary recipe repository-URL withholding and provisioned-root credential scrubbing/forwarding; repository label lockstep suffix expansion, host-scoped map identity/collision grouping, Windows crosshost paths and WSL distro suffixes. Actual provision options, label/sort consumers and host/scrubber delegates inspected; no replacement/equivalence claim. Retain40 authored/84finite registrations raw exact in14 drivers with bounded owner/context review. Prior KEEP superseded for removed suites; no runtime/CI/provider/browser/native/mobile/remote/folder/global completion credit.",
        "Audit3714 removes8 authored/39finite checks: whole CLI selector-recovery, task display-text and ANSI grammar suites plus two name joiner/blank tables. Deliberate real losses: selector flag/value/identity and mutation recovery merge/serialization; exact task suffix, transcript fallback, input immutability, cache reuse and edited blocks; independent failed-escape/resumption and OSC/DCS/BEL/ST/C1/nested/unfinished stripping outputs; meaningful-language joiner preservation and invisible/blank-name rejection. These are real bounded alarms, removed as narrow supplied-error examples, helper/token inventories and repeated internal-work fixtures. Prior2936,1195/1196,1214/1215 and1082 KEEP superseded; no replacement or equivalent coverage claimed. Keep9authored/9finite raw-exact registrations in5surviving drivers: screenshot export/failure filesystem behavior, CLI local tree query, event-local reply provenance, vault role-sensitive content and four hostile/UTF16/dangling/tag-name regressions. No native/UI/provider/remote/mobile/folder/runtime/CI/global completion credit.",
        "Audit3711 retires2authored/4finite cases by deleting whole clipboard-image-temp-file signature-to-name inventory (HEIC/TIFF/unrecognised bytes) and workspace-last-active switch-on supplied visit/reason singleton, plus its now-orphan test fixture. This intentionally loses real generated-filename suffix/extensionless alarms and real newer-visit archived7day versus inactive30day filtering/older-visit identity alarms. Filesystem writing and production reason pruning really execute; no equivalent replacement or universal absence of safety relevance is claimed. The clipboard test does not inspect written bytes, native delivery or decode; the visit test supplies candidate/timestamps and does not exercise persisted visit routing or actual removal.20authored/20finite cases remain unchanged across4bounded Git/sidecar/removal drivers. No new runner/test/module evaluation or runtime result; historical notes and receipts remain historical.",
        "Audit3707 removes10 authored/11finite checks: three whole renderer adapter/assembled-stage suites and two native projection cases. Deliberate losses: plugin URL/ref/default-version/local-path and unsafe credential refusal forwarding; real Task hook/store A→B→A late-save/list/count fences, owner disappearance, legacy-host convergence, query/history/eviction and same-ID host history; native child append ordered-ID/replacement and compound fallback/order/optimistic-admission/child-turn/duplicate/shrink/revision alarms. These are real bounded alarms; removal follows thin adapter, manually assembled Task pipeline and repetitive fixture value judgment, with no replacement or equivalent coverage claim. Prior1179/1182,1220/1221 and1885 KEEP superseded as applicable. Keep36 authored/38finite registrations raw exact across13 surviving drivers. No runtime/CI/provider/browser/native/mobile/remote/folder/global completion credit.",
        "Audit3706 removes7authored/7potential cases from3renderer sources: whole usage-label3case and130000-distinct-day usage-overview singleton suites, plus3SSH grouping/ordinary-range examples. Retain11authored/11potential cases across6drivers in this bounded selection; no equivalent replacement or fresh runtime result. Existing bare root-unit commands admit this selection statically; prior command/receipt strings remain historical. Audit3706 intentionally retires first/second-order usage-group label collision alarms; equal50%-weekly bucket versus derived-weekly selection identity and Gemini wk label alarm;130000distinct-day aggregation no-spread-crash/max/intensity alarm; legacy absent-source SSH grouping and ordinary reverse-select/selected-target deselect range alarms. Actual label ambiguity and pathological-input crash are accepted losses. Distinct-day fixture spans~356years; no hard producer/date bound is claimed. Retained filtered-anchor/grouped-order guards do not replace removed deselection/reverse-range/legacy-group coverage. No native SSH, mounted renderer, live provider, remote/folder/mobile end-to-end or current runtime pass was obtained.",
        "Audit3699 removes4 authored/4finite checks, including one whole xterm copy-policy suite and one root/group CLI help case. Deliberate losses: direct copy-chord admission for platform, selection, Kitty mode, defaultPrevented, logical/physical key and key phase; command-group disclosure and group help routing including claude-teams early return without RuntimeClient construction. These are real bounded policy/wiring alarms; no replacement or equivalent coverage claimed. Retain14 authored/19finite raw-exact registrations across6 drivers: unsafe CLI refusal, Claude model event carry and disk reconstruction/OSC-first case, attachment ownership/upload lifetime and mixed BMP file-reference/PNG-chip delivery, actual SQLite authority/admission/mutation, and Electron geometry/hit-testing. No runtime, CI, native-key delivery, external provider, mobile, remote, folder or global completion credit.",
        "Audit3692 removes5 authored/5finite marginal Codex checks: unrelated login URL without notice; ordinary per-account launch resource/config materialization; no-retained-pane skip; preservation of a previously owed full scan through actual preparation and pending-marker update (no actual history scan/settlement); ordinary later-config refresh. Accept these exact branch/wiring alarms as deliberate losses without replacement. Retain32 authored/34finite raw callbacks/registrations/table bytes exact across14suites, including credential/admission refusal, grace/reset readiness, filesystem ownership, commit-dependent queue state, streaming/host trust, path canonicalization and private-state preservation. All14whole suites challenged without keeper quota; no whole deletion warranted on current concrete signals. No runtime/CI/native WSL/remote/mobile/folder/global completion credit",
        "Audit3691 removes two complete runtime-home routing singleton suites (2 authored/2 finite): catalog wrapper mirror login-copy and passive transcript-lookup filesystem noncreation. Exact accepted losses are recorded in knownGaps; no replacement or equivalent coverage claimed. Audit3691: no dedicated alarm remains in the deleted sources for post-launch system login import through prepareHostCodexHomeForReadOnlyAppServer, or for repeated missing-transcript lookups leaving removed Codex account/runtime directories absent and userData entries unchanged. Ownership-marker read avoidance was never independently measured. No real catalog probe, provider, native Windows or crash was validated by those fixtures.",
        "Audit3686 current Claude profile/account review removes5 authored/5 finite cases: whole structured-auth diagnostic-label suite3 and Windows-only command suite1 whose advertised cache alarm is ineffective because cache lifetime is per invocation; remove duplicate setup namespace-link refusal1 at wrapper layer. All5 exact historical KEEP are consciously superseded. Retain49 authored/50 finite unchanged, including filesystem privacy/recovery, route identity and concurrency, built worker/helper, legacy WSL alias compatibility and sign-in handoff. These are deliberate coverage losses without replacement. No runtime/CI/native WSL/macOS Keychain, remote/mobile/folder or global completion credit. Explicit accepted real losses: unknown-account host fallback and mixed-version/WSL-only structured auth diagnostic labels; Windows-only sentinel ENOENT-to-friendly-error translation plus fresh-call successful dispatch smoke; setup catch-to-refused wrapper and no-write outcome for a namespace symlink. The command case does not discriminate removal of its per-invocation noncache guard; it still supplies the error-translation alarm, which is intentionally retired. No replacement/equivalence promise.",
        "Audit3680 removes eleven authored/eleven finite unit cases across four files, including entire launch setup row projection, structured legacy-model metadata, and legacy classifier suites. Accept loss of exact row partition/start selection, Codex supersession/default/unknown and Claude alias/suffix folding examples, other-agent exemption, getter/cache read budgets, same-array per-agent cache isolation, replaced-catalog metadata, and tracked-only model exclusion from structured and PTY legacy inventories. These are real narrow policy/metadata alarms intentionally retired without equivalent replacements. Retain real menu collapse/reopen in dropdown/select, AI picker cancel/accept and stale-effort filing, IME carry/gesture/frame transitions, and typed-flip versus held-dispatch fencing. No production or shared fixtures change. No dead timing entry exists for the three deleted drivers; retained timing keys stay unchanged. Static source-value review only; no project import, test runner, native/app execution or runtime validation established. Earlier receipts retain historical scope.",
        "Audit3678 current-source reassessment removes20 authored/24 finite root-unit cases across7 retained test sources; all10 selected current drivers80 authored/93 finite were read, leaving60 authored/69 finite unchanged. Removed alarms are the in-memory WAL PRAGMA constant, ordinary latest-dispatch/gate-creation inventories, self-reported-failure and explicit-terminal retry policy rows, SSH/unsupported-provider output fallback labels, legacy typing no-op/retain-before-report/manual scheduling rows, exited output status and copied resume-session metadata, incomplete inventory deferral/reset cascade inventory, and nominal release/active-state/corrupt external history/stopped-abandoned outcome/generic close-exception rows. These are intentional coverage losses, not replaced alarms. Retained source includes actual SQLite rollback/custody, mutable transcript/deletion and saved-copy compatibility, cursor mutation, clear lineage, auto-release timing/restart/admission and concurrent recovery seams. Historical KEEP decisions are consciously superseded where stated in decisions.json. Source-only evidence; no runtime, CI, native, provider, remote, mobile/folder or global completion credit.",
        "Audit3672 renewed by3676 removes four authored/four finite cases from federation-output.test.ts: nominal show/read routing and terminal-fallback projection; initial archive-table SELECT failure returning retained/no-close; simulated old-peer read/fleet/refusal and method inventory; and absent archive-release capability refusing release. These actual compatibility/guard alarms are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement; the dropped-table case never reaches capture or commit. Current selected frontier9 becomes5: retain actual temporary transcript parsing/path omission, current no-transcript release/unavailable-output/restart/replay regression, and three home deadline/stop nonmutation cases. Prior held-capture case was already removed upstream and receives no new removal credit; prior redacted snapshot archive behavior was rewritten upstream and is not claimed retained here. The surviving driver timing entry stays. Static review/private composition only; no actual peer/network/native/platform or fresh runtime validation.",
        "Audit3671 removes14 authored/32 finite root-unit cases, including the whole WSL move-handler refusal suite, WSL preload object-presence suite and internal gate spelling truth table. Also retire the weak withheld-command non-array shape assertion, static serve-only Add/capability/mock-remove example, grammar scope equality and basic configuration/payload schema roundtrips. Genuine wrong-window/malformed-request/gate-before-work, exact gate spellings/platform/argv precedence, static serve-only routing, declaration mismatch and empty grammar/pair admission alarms are consciously lost without replacement; prior KEEP decisions are reconsidered. Seven unchanged authored/finite root-unit cases retain real image/provider/line budgets, live policy transition/capability broadcast, grammar resource/reference traversal and strict-versus-tolerant literal salvage. Source-value evidence only; no runner/compiler/build/app/native/provider/remote/mobile/folder validation or historical fault claim. Independently remove one authored/finite Playwright closed-gate app-boot inventory: accept loss of real renderer/preload/main refusal composition, saved-host row and Add/Move hiding/Remove visibility alarms. Keep the unchanged scripted-move rendered dialog lifecycle/reload case. It runs no real WSL migration, host connection, file copy or automation restoration. No selector or Playwright participation cleanup is required because the spec remains.",
        "Audit3663 renews approved3644/3645/3648/amended3651 at privatec1ef: remove10authored/26finite across7changedtestpaths,4whole drivers; retain23authored/24finite including actualcmdkStrictMode defaultcursor race. Retire version1.5.0/1.5.1→shrinksImages capability threshold and launch-to-prompt wiring alarm. Surviving prompt tests explicitly supply capability and do not replace wiring coverage. Retire resolved-before-personOnly precedence; hook-gone/live-dialog guidance; stale-incarnation versus live-looking dialog classification; delayed/clipped warning extraction and wait-for-paint wiring; 3row setting/personOnly approve/deny/disclaimer suggestion composition;13row setting/reason/person/coordinator admission, close/mail attribution, terminal delivery/refusal/preanswered/personOnly/dropped-allow handler propagation alarms. Real state/access/SQLite effects occur; these genuine losses are accepted, not mocked-away. Retire full command extraction from serialized JSON in worker receipt and nontruncation alarm; no rendering, actual worker approval or native shell proof. Retire2row extra-source first/last order and controlled default cursor projection, plus generic open-palette livefolder add/remove render alarm. Explicitly supersede rawexact297KEEP refresh. Keep actualcmdk/StrictMode default cursor race driver; no default-suite loss claim. No equivalent replacement asserted. Retained queue/commit/retryownership/filebudget, terminalfreshness/provenance/competing-answer, RPC DB-effect, qualifiedfolder/runtimehandoff and lingering-reopen cases have distinct scope. Audit3675 preserves the upstream revised unreported-approval close regression, its escalation helper and adapted survivors. Source-only static renewal; no runner/compiler/app/native/remote/CI claim. Upstream41390host-owned approvalwatch/report lifetime reviewed separately; no new lifetime test removed. Preserve all earlier metadata/evidence.",
        "Audit3634: Remove five authored/five finite cases, including the complete structured chat terminal-refusal, terminal-plus-agent worker-start validation, and canonical Git common-directory parser suites. Also remove the gh free-text -R argument projection case. Consciously supersede prior KEEP decisions and accept chat-versus-stale redirect classification, real RPC refusal-before-SQLite-Dispatch, old-Git echoed-option relative-path parsing, WSL execution-space resolution, and free-text preservation/bare-repo qualification alarms. These are genuine narrow alarms, intentionally retired without equivalent replacements. Retain real Git stdin/EOF delivery, bound-account host admission, naming environment/account precedence, upload iterator cancellation and remote path confinement. Shared fixtures and production code remain. Remove only the dead canonical-repo-key timing entry. Static source-value evidence only; all prior evidence retains historical scope.",
        "Audit3636: Remove the entire maintenance opportunity internal-count driver (one authored/two finite cases), the mocked remote worker start-card argument case (one/one), and the follow-up heading mapping table (one/two). Root-unit discovery loses three authored/five finite cases. Independently remove four Python native screenshot methods/five statically enumerated subTest scenarios: grim argv/stub payload, failure-code mapping, X11 mocked capture payload, and capability flags. The Python lane is verify:computer-native and is not root Vitest. Accept loss of exact native command/projection and exception/capability alarms, ready-only card publication arguments/agent forwarding, and serialized follow-up heading mapping; no equivalent replacement is claimed. Retain actual ownership/mail/queue/reopen transitions, remote lost-response fencing and first-result settlement, filesystem/maintenance admission and successor progress, wrong-region screenshot refusal and Sway geometry. The whole-deleted new driver has no timing key; this component requires no timing cleanup. No production changes. Static source-value review only; no project import, runner, app, native desktop or runtime validation established. All prior evidence retains historical scope.",
        "Audit3630 removed orphan delete/toggle capability/precondition and run/edit refusal assertions. Real dispatch, mutation fencing, mixed-version and host outcomes are not established by this removal or by a substitute test.",
        "Audit3624: Remove one authored/five finite positive Gemini identity table from the Claude/Gemini title collision driver. The real normalization, legacy label and explicit title evidence owners execute, so ordinary Gemini marker/name/wrapper recognition and normalized-label composition alarms are consciously retired without equivalent replacement; these five supplied title-to-literal identity examples have low marginal value. Preserve the six-row Claude task-text collision oracle, whose unrelated CLI mentions must not rebrand or destructively normalize titles. The other audited drivers preserve real permission-mode session transitions, prompt secret/fence/bounds defenses, JSON-to-Ask option/preview preservation, and optional GitLab failure summary/trace composition. Root-unit discovery loses one authored/five finite cases; no whole driver or timing key is removed. No actual terminal stream, UI routing, application/native or runtime execution established; all prior evidence retains historical scope.",
        "Audit3618: Remove three authored/three finite browser reload cases, including the complete renderer reload-actions suite. Agent bridge fake did-fail-load plus permanently supplied manager error projects description/code into a rejection. Renderer seeded empty metadata projects a saved URL into plain webview src; its earlier not-ready case projects a live-id/throwing fake reload into absence of a loading patch. Real queue/wait/error/cache/classifier/hook code executes, but these narrow supplied-state and exception-to-callback wirings have low marginal value; no rerender, lifecycle, actual cache generation/retirement or guest commit is asserted. Explicitly supersede audit1822 not-ready KEEP and preliminary3617 cross-module retain opinion, accepting offline-reload failure reporting, empty guest to saved URL routing, native-reload bypass and premature-loading/stranded-state alarms without replacement. Retain distinct main cancellation queue progression and absent queued side-effect dispatch. Root-unit discovery loses three/three. No Electron guest, network failure, restored navigation/commit, app/native focus or runtime execution established; earlier evidence retains its historical scope.",
        "Audit3614: Remove thirty-one authored/thirty-nine finite potential cases across CLI format and argument drivers, including three whole suites: search-result/status sanitation sites, Linear issue/list/warning sanitation sites, and quote-stripped JSON diagnostic secret non-echo. Those real formatter/guard transformations execute on supplied strings; intentionally retire their field-specific CSI/OSC/C1/newline/bell and diagnostic secrecy alarms as low-value caller/output inventories, without replacement. Also retire twenty-one search registrations/twenty-four finite cases covering minimal positional request/default omission, exhaustive all-flags request projection, nominal named query/index routes, repeated syntax/agent examples, enum/agent/path-count/timestamp/numeric/cursor admission examples, unknown/browser flag examples and postcommand last-wins projections; retire one parser sentinel-only case. Keep actual ambiguity, conflicting index request, precommand/crosscommand scoping, variadic reference parsing and missing-repeatable-value controls, without claiming equivalent coverage. Root-unit discovery loses all twenty-nine/thirty-seven. No CLI/RPC/terminal/PowerShell/host/schema/runtime execution is established by this source-only audit; earlier evidence retains its historical scope.",
        "Audit3609: Remove the complete pnpm CLI invocation literal-selection suite (eleven authored/nineteen finite potential cases), with no replacement claimed. Root-unit discovery loses JavaScript-versus-native command selection, npm/npx executable rejection, Windows cmd/bat casing and shell selection, non-Windows cmd behavior, native PNPM_HOME flat/bin preference, explicit-path priority, relative-home rejection, missing-native fallback and non-Windows home-probe refusal alarms. The suite called the real resolver with independently expected objects, but exercised no pnpm/node/cmd process, installed native executable or real filesystem probe. Earlier KEEP decisions are consciously superseded by accepting these narrow branch and probe-inventory alarms as low value. Real symlink entry, Git signing isolation, Bun filesystem/Node child normalization and compiler scheduling/continuation tests remain distinct tests, not equivalent coverage. No runner, compiler, app, platform or remote execution was performed in this source-only audit. Earlier evidence retains its historical scope.",
        "Audit3598: Remove seven authored/nine finite literal-table potential test registrations across workflow routing, Claude cold-start and real-zsh preexec drivers. Root-unit discovery loses six authored/six finite: three test-local workflow parser fixtures, the five-positive/three-negative explicit command-paint route inventory, a boot-banner-before-composer sample and an already-painted bare-title positive sample. The separately selected shell_contracts live-shell driver loses one authored/three finite raw-capture paint-only cases across three hook configurations; its real-wrapper launch-order, four rechunkings (twelve finite) and runtime-wait replay remain, without claiming equivalent replacement. Intentionally lose those parser, exact routing-list, banner, post-paint subscription and native-read-boundary paint alarms. Retained workflow/UNIT_EXCLUDE/classifier cross-source routing checks and readiness-race-to-writer timing are distinct bounded alarms. No runner, real shell, PTY, app, native focus, remote delivery, cross-platform execution or full-feature correctness is established by this source-only audit. Earlier evidence retains its historical scope.",
        "Audit3591: Retire the whole one-case background journal-producer attribution suite and the fabricated malformed-details-block case (two authored/two finite cases). Intentionally lose the fixed own-task versus output/foreign-task attribution examples across flat/message row shapes, missing-root classification, and direct unbalanced/detailsish fabricated-block rejection alarms. Retained parser sibling/depth and editor navigation tests do not replace these alarms. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime, transport, persistence, native focus or rendered UI validation is claimed. Earlier dated text and evidence retain their historical scopes.",
        "Audit3592: Retire the whole three-case shared agent smart-key resolver suite, explicitly superseding its Audit3238/3237 keep decisions. Intentionally lose literal permission-versus-question classification, longest-question digit selection, Codex async-question opener/digit/Enter/skip mapping, and unsupported-agent/state/prompt refusal examples. These were real parser/selection and literal-byte alarms; they did not exercise terminal delivery or timing. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime, native TUI, mobile, remote or performance validation is claimed. Earlier dated text and evidence retain their historical scopes.",
        "Audit3587/3588: Retire six authored/fourteen finite cases, including the whole WSL stopped-notice and connecting-status selector suites. Intentionally lose direct WSL retry connection field/target/ready-epoch/null-guard examples, connecting/reconnecting distro and absent-state selector samples, and stopped/connecting notice text/button/data-attribute examples. Retained host-ready retry and content-loader/reload lifecycles do not replace these alarms. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime, native WSL, remote, rendered UI or performance validation is claimed. Earlier dated text and evidence retain their historical scopes.",
        "Audit3580: Retire the whole one-case runtime host environment prototype/subclass suite. Intentionally lose the exact configured lower-case Windows Claude home to account-identity normalization and host-account override precedence alarm previously retained by Audit3129. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime validation is claimed. Earlier dated keep statements below describe their historical source scope; the current suite is removed.",
        "Audit3563 scope: retire the whole Kiro OSC/hook identity suite and the OpenCode2 identity-only case; reduce Codex cached startup child-retirement and missing-session-ID tables to one case each (2 authored/4 finite removals). Intentionally lose Kiro alias/session continuity, OpenCode2 completed OSC identity continuity, cached replacement without relay-generation restart, and missing-previous-ID context-preservation alarms. Remaining provider, remote compatibility, persistence and cross-session pollution cases are not equivalent replacements. Also remove the private Codex roster-size assertion while retaining public child-absence checks. Historical evidence retains its original source scope; no new execution or transferred pass validates these reductions.",
        "Launch direct-owner cleanup current scope: This gate’s unfiltered unit command now selects a suite reduced by 82 whole registrations  / 159 potential table examples in 10 whole test Programs, including 8 registrations / 15 examples from five once-registered create-message factory closures. Lost alarms include frozen first-message/options and legacy-host fallback; distinct actions and redelivery; uncertain/refused/reloaded input custody, Retry and late proof; rich prompt/attachment upload Stop/close and handback; ordinary draft/editor/IME/StrictMode lifetime and accepted topology; provisional fallback tab placement/group/pin/order and rich worktree handoff. Four whole consent/resume-identity cases remain in two Programs; they do not replace these alarms. This entry governs current reduced-unit scope and qualifies any broader implication of unchanged oracle/coverageNotes history. Entire dated evidenceRuns, original commands/currentCommand values, counts/results and existing history retain their original scopes only; no fresh execution, transferred pass, replacement equivalence or prior upstream-removal credit is claimed.",
        "Audit2133 current-parent preparation (988 authored removals; independently reviewed2099/2107/2115/2116 decisions; upstream clear-buffer and recovery-image regressions retained): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/persistence/worktree-sort-order-write.test.ts: re-ranks every writable row when a blocked row sits in the requested order. src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts: remove only literal registration import/call pairs await import('../orca-runtime-tests/worktree-setup-and-startup.spec'), await import('../orca-runtime-tests/gitlab-and-pr-bases.spec'); no additional authored credit. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/targeting-and-resilience.spec.ts: routes tab switch and capture start by explicit page id; accepts focus on tab switch without altering bridge args (focus is main-side concern); keeps terminal cwd resolution fail-soft when the provider is unavailable. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-and-reconciliation-part-04.spec.ts: drops the bounded scan cache when orphan-cleanup removal completes; clears optimistic reconcile tokens when a CLI worktree removal succeeds; emits drift without mutating when the fetched base fast-forwards created HEAD; emits base_changed without mutation when the fetched base rewrote history; skips stale-token reconciles without mutating or emitting stale status; emits unknown without mutation when fetch fails or the base ref is missing. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-and-reconciliation-part-03.spec.ts: routes runtime preserved-branch force-delete through the selected WSL project runtime; replies to a waiting client with the error of a delete that fails after acceptance; treats forced runtime deletion of an already-missing unregistered worktree as cleanup; treats normal runtime deletion of an already-missing unregistered worktree as cleanup. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-and-reconciliation-part-02.spec.ts: warns that a missing-repo removal only forgot the workspace; restores runtime watchers when CLI worktree deletion fails after teardown; does not re-spend the drain budget on a removal after a wedged install was abandoned; routes runtime worktree removal through the selected WSL project runtime; force-deletes a branch that was preserved by runtime worktree removal. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/gitlab-and-pr-bases-part-02.spec.ts: records GitLab pasted-project recents only after successful runtime lookup; threads explicit origin preference through runtime WSL PR base resolution; resolves local GitLab fork MR bases from the target project MR head ref; captures the fork MR head from a dedicated ref, not the shared FETCH_HEAD; keeps the durable MR head when the head fetch fails but the local ref resolves; routes runtime GitLab fork MR base git calls through the selected WSL project runtime. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/gitlab-and-pr-bases.spec.ts: passes SSH connection ids through GitLab task operations; routes runtime GitLab issue, MR, work-item, and todo actions through the selected WSL project runtime; routes runtime GitLab MR details, review-management, job, and pasted URL actions through the selected WSL project runtime; normalizes runtime GitLab issue list arguments like the desktop IPC path. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-setup-and-startup-part-03.spec.ts: does not warn when setup is explicitly skipped for CLI-created worktrees; puts the agent a create starts in the first default tab, as the window does; keeps the 8s main-runtime startup readiness budget for agents without an override; gives OpenCode the 20s main-runtime startup readiness budget; launches explicit startup agents with prompts for CLI-created worktrees. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-setup-and-startup.spec.ts: returns a setup launch payload for CLI-created worktrees when hooks are explicitly enabled; does not hand the window a setup main never tried to start; passes the selected Windows setup shell into runtime runner generation; follows normal setup policy for CLI-created worktrees without activating them; uses returned WSL setup shell metadata when runtime spawns setup; uses the shell-aware setup runner for windowless creates without a startup command; reports the in-process setup hook as running when nothing can launch the runner. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-sleep-and-teardown-part-02.spec.ts: coalesces two clients sleeping the same host worktree; stops exactly the expected live PTYs for a worktree; explains a refused workspace close instead of throwing the raw refusal enum. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-summaries-part-03.spec.ts: marks the desktop-active worktree as isActive; includes SSH-backed worktrees in the mobile worktree summary; caches repeated malformed path misses before normalizing them again. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-summaries-part-02.spec.ts: keeps title-only foreground work ahead of monitoring in another pane; keeps a local hook row while a connected PTY still backs its pane; keeps an OSC row via its connected PTY after the pane binding is cleared. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-summaries.spec.ts: resolves files through a source-visible linked-checkout worktree; marks saved session tabs with live PTYs as host sidebar activity; attributes live legacy PTYs from saved layout bindings when their panes are hidden; marks saved browser tabs as host sidebar activity like desktop; falls back to the path-keyed GitHub cache entry; includes folder workspaces in compact worktree summaries for mobile; attaches inline agent rows from the latest OSC 9999 status; projects monitoring over a title-derived working status. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-creation-and-orchestration-part-03.spec.ts: pushes to an idle pane when the only live waiter filters out the message type; resolves a registered waiter without PTY-injecting when the leaf is already idle; keeps already-idle status after tui-idle wait for immediate message delivery; resolves message waiters when notifyMessageArrived is called; does not resolve type-filtered message waiters for unrelated message types; removes message waiter abort listeners after message arrival; resolves message waiters on timeout when no message arrives. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-creation-and-orchestration-part-02.spec.ts: delivers pending mail via notifyMessageArrived when the recipient is already idle; does not keep retrying when every pending row was already pointed; repoints pending rows restored with a live-idle coordinator. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-13.spec.ts: rolls back a half-created terminal whose surface never publishes. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-12.spec.ts: rejects startup prompts for agents that require post-ready stdin; uses portable Unix quoting for mobile agent launch commands in WSL project runtimes; keeps PowerShell quoting for mobile agent launch commands in Windows host runtimes; uses cmd.exe quoting for mobile agent launch commands in local Windows host runtimes; publishes headless mobile session agent identity with synthesized PTY status; rejects disabled mobile session agent launches before spawning; validates mobile terminal insertion anchors before resolving agent launch commands. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-11.spec.ts: coalesces a reconnect close burst onto one authoritative PTY inventory; keeps an explicit user close destructive while the PTY is live; builds mobile session agent launch commands on the runtime host; injects mobile quick-command prompts into the host-built agent startup command. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-10.spec.ts: closes persisted headless terminal parents before any prior list call; tears down a serve-owned headless tab on close while a renderer is attached so it cannot resurrect; defers a renderer-published pending tab to the renderer instead of tearing it down; returns a delegated close outcome with no selection tombstone when the renderer owns the outcome; tears down a runtime pending shell the renderer never adopted on close. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-08.spec.ts: materializes a plain shell when the pending tab has no launch agent; hydrates legacy persisted terminal tabs without layout entries; reads and indexes the full agent-status snapshot once per mobile projection; kills persisted SSH PTYs when closing hydrated headless tabs before pane metadata is restored; materializes hydrated pending headless terminals with the persisted session identity. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-07.spec.ts: hydrates a persisted SSH-owned pane before an attached renderer publishes its graph. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-05.spec.ts: publishes the desktop's tab name over the live agent title, and the live title without one; uses fresh neutral PTY titles over stale mobile snapshot and OSC titles; operates PTY-backed mobile session terminals without a renderer graph; reuses pane close for live PTYs that do not own a renderer tab; lists PTY-backed mobile session terminals without a renderer graph; shows and resolves active PTY-backed mobile session terminals without a renderer graph. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-04.spec.ts: creates mobile session terminals for folder workspaces in a headless runtime server; spawns fresh headless SSH mobile session terminals instead of reattaching synthetic local ids; hydrates headless mobile session terminals from the host workspace session; keeps live headless mobile session terminals when a desktop renderer publishes without them; publishes laptop-created remote runtime split terminals to phone session tabs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-02.spec.ts: does not report headless wake degradation without sleeping records; does not wake slept agents for non-mobile session-only activation; does not rewrite unread metadata when a mobile activation finds the worktree already read; returns unread:false from worktree.ps after a mobile activation clears the flag; materializes pending mobile session terminals without focusing desktop clients; closes browser mobile session tabs when addressed by browser workspace id. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs.spec.ts: resolves mobile terminal surfaces by exact split leaf; closes the matching mobile terminal UUID leaf without closing the whole tab; closes the whole mobile terminal tab when addressed by parent tab id; activates the active split leaf when addressed by parent tab id; clears unread metadata on mobile worktree activation without focusing desktop clients; wakes slept agents on the host renderer when a phone activates a worktree. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-05.spec.ts: publishes the hook provider session on a headless mobile tab so native chat can address the transcript; recovers the agent type from the hook row when the pane was launched without an agent hint; reads one agent-status snapshot per projection, not one per terminal tab; waits for unknown-launch foreground owner before publishing Pi-compatible mobile status; keeps Pi-compatible mobile session status as Pi for an unknown-launch foreground pi PTY; keeps renderer-vetted mobile agent status for custom-titled terminals. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-04.spec.ts: publishes terminal surface agent status for paired web clients; preserves authoritative OMP identity for Pi-compatible remote terminal snapshots; normalizes a remote OMP title without republishing omitted launch identity; skips the foreground-process probe when the PTY launch agent is already known; probes the foreground process only on a status transition for unknown launch agents; passes the client signal and the slept-worktree refusal to the spawn. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-03.spec.ts: does not use stale runtime-created PTY status when a neutral PTY title exists; recognizes runtime-created Codex PTY handles from the ready prompt; recognizes runtime-created Antigravity PTY handles from the ready prompt; recognizes live leaf Antigravity terminals from the ready prompt; recognizes a later Antigravity header with a prompt but no model line; keeps mobile terminal surfaces visible while their leaf handle is pending. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-02.spec.ts: lets Claude agents management titles clear stale runtime-created title status; does not recognize live Claude agents panes from a Claude foreground process; does not let stale tab-level agent titles override current neutral pane titles; lists live terminals with fresh pane titles over stale tab titles; lets adopted neutral pane titles use non-shell foreground fallback; lets adopted neutral pane titles retry wrapper foregrounds until recognized; authorizes settled CLI prompts only after positive %s foreground identity; does not recognize arbitrary foreground TUIs as running agents; lets live neutral pane titles retry wrapper foregrounds until recognized; lets current Claude agents PTY titles override stale runtime-created OSC titles; does not let stale Claude agents OSC titles suppress current PTY title activity. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status.spec.ts: keeps preallocated terminal handles valid across renderer reloads; preserves runtime-created PTY process identity after graph unavailable; keeps prompt bindings fenced across runtime restarts without provider incarnation; recognizes runtime-created PTY handles with agent launch titles; does not treat a bare Cursor Agent native title as a running agent session; uses stale runtime-created PTY status when there is no title or foreground evidence. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery-part-07.spec.ts: keeps orphaned list and show writability aligned with the send gate. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery-part-04.spec.ts: cancels a coalesced SSH worker recovery retry when its provider disconnects. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery-part-03.spec.ts: retries renderer reveal before clearing an adopted legacy worker sleeping record. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery-part-02.spec.ts: recovers exported ORCA_TERMINAL_HANDLE from discovered live PTY sessions. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-12.spec.ts: applies ANSI erase-from-start line controls in retained previews; applies ANSI stripping for private or intermediate CSI line controls; applies ANSI stripping for unsupported erase-line modes; reveals an agent terminal under the pane the caller reserved; keeps a fresh %s pane host-owned when a desktop window is available; keeps desktop publication %s separate from the reserved host spawn; mints its own pane when the reserved leaf is malformed, and reports the one it used; starts an agent terminal with the model the caller picked; starts an agent terminal without a model flag when no pick was made; attributes a startup-agent launch named %s as %s; attributes a fresh agent session the host builds as unknown; leaves a bare agent command the user typed out of launch attribution. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-11.spec.ts: trims oversized terminal output bursts without per-line array shifts; builds terminal previews without mapping the full retained tail; keeps recent PTY replay output capped without needing previous data for large chunks; applies terminal redraw controls before retaining previews; applies ANSI terminal redraw controls before retaining previews; retains multi-line ANSI footer redraws instead of appending old frames; keeps the cursor column when erasing full lines in multi-line redraws; applies ANSI split redraw controls without leaking raw params. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-10.spec.ts: returns renderer visible screen lines through terminal.read RPC JSON result; separates composer drafts from provider-owned terminal screens. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-09.spec.ts: reports an in-flight PTY focus as not navigated when its notifier disappears; reports graph-leaf focus as not navigated without a host notifier; grounds the provider mode tracker before a later chunk, in the emulator order; grounds an in-flight provider snapshot capture so it cannot publish the pre-reset screen; waits for terminal exit and resolves with the exit status; keeps terminal read payloads bounded while retained output remains pageable; trims terminal read preview character budget without per-line array shifts. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-08.spec.ts: submits a silent Claude composer once after the bounded render fallback; chunks large terminal.send text before provider writes; yields chunked terminal input through immediates between writes; yields while validating accepted large terminal.send text before provider writes; reveals a background terminal session when focusing its handle; replays captured launch config when focusing a background agent session; reveals background terminal sessions with the freshest PTY title; renames background terminal handles without requiring a visible tab; keeps a background terminal handle stable while reveal adoption is racing. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-07.spec.ts: resolves tui-idle when a stale Codex prompt is followed by Antigravity readiness; returns an agent-neutral blocked wait result for update prompts; returns an agent-neutral blocked wait result for workspace trust prompts; returns an agent-neutral blocked wait result for cwd selection prompts; returns a blocked wait result for Codex model migration prompts; returns a blocked wait result for Codex startup hook review prompts; returns an agent-neutral blocked wait result for generic interactive prompts; splits text and enter writes for background terminal handles; types the lead line for %s: %s; submits through the agent-specific PTY timing policy for %s. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-06.spec.ts: waits for exit on background terminal handles; keeps retained PTY transcript memory when controller refresh fails; resolves tui-idle from an Antigravity ready prompt preview; resolves Antigravity ready prompts with newline-heavy pasted tails without splitting; resolves live-leaf tui-idle from an Antigravity ready prompt preview. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness-part-03.spec.ts: spawns the available Qoder command for a captured same-session resume: %s; does not use the local Windows shell setting for remote Windows bare agent creates; matches canonical bare agent commands when a command override is configured; keeps non-bare agent command terminal creates unchanged; keeps disabled bare agent command terminal creates unchanged; injects runtime hook receiver env into terminal sessions; creates background terminal sessions for a $label; creates background terminal sessions for a $label; enables Claude Agent Teams only for direct Claude launches when configured in-process; reveals Claude Agent Teams launches with the rewritten launch config; preserves Claude Agent Teams for sequenced Claude launches. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-creation-and-readiness.spec.ts: creates visible terminal sessions without asking the renderer to focus a tab; asks the pty controller for the requested shell instead of a startup command; knows the agent a flagged launch command names before any process read; retires a flagged command pane identity when the command exits; retires only receipted restored PTY authority on command completion and exit; forgets synthetic handles when disconnected PTY records are pruned. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/headless-snapshots.spec.ts: returns OSC titles from headless main terminal snapshots; adopts renderer-seeded titles into headless main terminal snapshots; returns cwd metadata from seeded headless main terminal snapshots; adopts OSC7 host metadata from seeded headless terminal scrollback; falls back to the renderer snapshot for hidden-output recovery without headless state; keeps an empty headless snapshot authoritative for hidden-output recovery; advances the absolute output sequence across a daemon stream gap; emits explicit OSC 9999 agent status from runtime PTY data. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-02.spec.ts: falls back to the provider snapshot for a restored PTY with no mounted renderer; falls back to the available mirror when authoritative provider history is unavailable; keeps an empty renderer snapshot when the provider has no retained content; keeps restored provider history authoritative after later live output; uses provider alternate-screen state while a partial model is unsafe; prefers the tracked title over the headless emulator lastTitle; keeps the cursor-agent literal in record-fallback snapshots only without a tracker title; touches mobile snapshots once for decorative spinner ticks, again on idle. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/local-worktree-creation-part-02.spec.ts: creates a same-repo PR branch override from a resolved head SHA and matching push target; skips broad remote fetch for an existing full-SHA PR base; creates a selected Bitbucket PR branch override from a matching remote branch; suffixes an existing PR when a matching push target lacks selected PR metadata; suffixes a matching push target branch when selected PR metadata has no PR number; suffixes a matching push target branch when the existing PR is different; suffixes a selected PR remote conflict when the PR lookup fails; checks out an unused runtime PR branch only when it is at the resolved head SHA; suffixes only the runtime worktree path when an exact PR branch checkout path exists. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/local-worktree-creation.spec.ts: returns runtime local base update suggestions from addWorktree; creates a runtime local worktree from a usable persisted local branch base; does not create a runtime local worktree when the refresh fails and no local base ref exists; creates a branchNameOverride worktree from the selected matching remote base ref. src/main/runtime/integrations/skill/orca-runtime-skill-recovery.test.ts: continues skill management after startup recovery fails. src/main/runtime/orchestration/mailbox/routing/orchestration-mailbox-detached-routing.spec.ts: uses bounded ownership lookup for direct arrivals while the agent cannot take input; wakes a bound Run waiter when same-Run direct mail arrives; keeps an unowned detached-recipient message in its direct mailbox; uses primary-key lookups for bounded routing updates. src/main/runtime/orchestration/mailbox/terminal-pointer/orchestration-mailbox-delivery.test.ts: remove only literal registration import/call pairs import './orchestration-mailbox-pointer-cli-command.spec'; no additional authored credit. src/main/runtime/orchestration/mailbox/terminal-pointer/orchestration-mailbox-pointer-cli-command.spec.ts: renders the %s CLI command in a mailbox pointer. src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/terminal/terminal-multiplex-link-estimate.test.ts: sizes a slow high-latency link near twice its bandwidth-delay product; never paces a LAN, even when its client parses slowly; never paces a fast link; returns to legacy windows when the path RTT jumps. src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/terminal/terminal-snapshot-scrollback-rows.test.ts: steps down the row ladder when history is over