          "summary": "29/29 on the candidate that makes the preview a browser tab. The preview action now creates a page located by the document; reopening the same document activates the tab it is already in rather than minting a second grant on one file; and closing that tab revokes its grant, which nothing else does now that the editor tab's close hook is gone. Red-green with each mutant as the sole delta: dropping the reuse lookup opens a second tab for a document already on screen, and dropping the release on close leaves the document readable through a grant nothing revokes until the process ends. Both are paired with presence preconditions in the same runs — a second, different document still gets its own tab, and a URL tab closed beside the document tab revokes nothing, so a release fired for every close would fail rather than pass. Historical command preserved after removal of the mocked preview test suite in the test-value audit; currentCommand links only the remaining suites. The recorded result, count, duration and mutation narrative describe the historical command. The current command has not been rerun here and does not claim equivalent coverage."
