metadata when a mobile activation finds the worktree already read; returns unread:false from worktree.ps after a mobile activation clears the flag; materializes pending mobile session terminals without focusing desktop clients; closes browser mobile session tabs when addressed by browser workspace id. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs.spec.ts: resolves mobile terminal surfaces by exact split leaf; closes the matching mobile terminal UUID leaf without closing the whole tab; closes the whole mobile terminal tab when addressed by parent tab id; activates the active split leaf when addressed by parent tab id; clears unread metadata on mobile worktree activation without focusing desktop clients; wakes slept agents on the host renderer when a phone activates a worktree. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-05.spec.ts: publishes the hook provider session on a headless mobile tab so native chat can address the transcript; recovers the agent type from the hook row when the pane was launched without an agent hint; reads one agent-status snapshot per projection, not one per terminal tab; waits for unknown-launch foreground owner before publishing Pi-compatible mobile status; keeps Pi-compatible mobile session status as Pi for an unknown-launch foreground pi PTY; keeps renderer-vetted mobile agent status for custom-titled terminals. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-04.spec.ts: publishes terminal surface agent status for paired web clients; preserves authoritative OMP identity for Pi-compatible remote terminal snapshots; normalizes a remote OMP title without republishing omitted launch identity; skips the foreground-process probe when the PTY launch agent is already known; probes the foreground process only on a status transition for unknown launch agents; passes the client signal and the slept-worktree refusal to the spawn. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-03.spec.ts: does not use stale runtime-created PTY status when a neutral PTY title exists; recognizes runtime-created Codex PTY handles from the ready prompt; recognizes runtime-created Antigravity PTY handles from the ready prompt; recognizes live leaf Antigravity terminals from the ready prompt; recognizes a later Antigravity header with a prompt but no model line; keeps mobile terminal surfaces visible while their leaf handle is pending. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-02.spec.ts: lets Claude agents management titles clear stale runtime-created title status; does not recognize live Claude agents panes from a Claude foreground process; does not let stale tab-level agent titles override current neutral pane titles; lists live terminals with fresh pane titles over stale tab titles; lets adopted neutral pane titles use non-shell foreground fallback; lets adopted neutral pane titles retry wrapper foregrounds until recognized; authorizes settled CLI prompts only after positive %s foreground identity; does not recognize arbitrary foreground TUIs as running agents; lets live neutral pane titles retry wrapper foregrounds until recognized; lets current Claude agents PTY titles override stale runtime-created OSC titles; does not let stale Claude agents OSC titles suppress current PTY title activity. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status.spec.ts: keeps preallocated terminal handles valid across renderer reloads; preserves runtime-created PTY process identity after graph unavailable; keeps prompt bindings fenced across runtime restarts without provider incarnation; recognizes runtime-created PTY handles with agent launch titles; does not treat a bare Cursor Agent native title as a running agent session; uses stale runtime-created PTY status when there is no title or foreground evidence. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery-part-07.spec.ts: keeps o