        "Audit2065 (sources2063/2064): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/program-status-osc.spec.ts: retire six private facet/lifecycle-state and hook-order assertions; retained public OSC/wait cases do not replace those alarms. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence.",
        "Audit1709 removes low-value test definitions and retires affected assertion or execution-receipt claims without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews bound retained behavior and injected/native/remote limits. Unchanged assertions and receipts keep their original scope; gates lacking current active evidence are downgraded.",
        "Audit1687 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded.",
        "Audit1630 removes low-value Git, GitHub/GitLab and IPC projections, argument inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained cancellation, ownership, authorization, filesystem and SQLite boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded.",
        "Audit1571 removes mock forwarding, capability/schema inventories, private predicates, supplied error/result replays, and filesystem-mocked persistence checks without equivalent replacement claims. Retained changed tests also exercise real local permission-file reread, registry proxy rollback/credential retirement, site display recovery, and pending sender/credential/document admission with injected Electron/UI producers. Retained network tests exercise owned stream credit/cleanup, generation and retirement fences, real loopback proxy/SOCKS bytes and file-backed binding state. SSH/WSL/paired runtime, native sessions, authority producers and storage clears remain injected; simulated relaunch uses filesystem mocks. The unchanged profile-retirement suite was statically reviewed and not rerun. No actual SSH/WSL runtime, native Chromium jar deletion, durable process restart, remote DNS or external site proof. Receipts selecting changed tests are retired and unaffected receipts remain unchanged.",
        "Audit1568 removes API inventories, supplied mock-value/forwarding assertions, implementation-shape tables and negative/setup cases that do not reach their intended boundary, without equivalent replacement claims. Retained changed definitions exercise owned manager lifetime/queue/refcount/clamp and real synthetic process/files/staging boundaries. Seventeen unchanged native Electron definitions across this combined audit are statically reviewed and not rerun. Changed native suites exercise local popup wire/cookie/session and clean/native process-identity behavior; known popup-admission flaws remain unfixed. Unit native/event/session/registry inputs remain injected. No actual OS focus, registry/host execution, CRX verification or durable restart proof. Receipts selecting changed tests are retired and unaffected receipts remain unchanged.",
        "Audit1564 retires copied cookie key recipes, mock bridge/preview forwarding and flag tables, source-spelling/script inventories and setup-only alarms without equivalent replacement coverage. Retained changed cases exercise actual scoped SQLite merge/rollback/schema refusal, owned cancellation and grant authority/canonical containment, ranged response consistency, replacement guest ownership and executed guest-script promise/DOM cleanup behavior. Session, host response, geometry/observer and transport producers remain injected where documented. One unchanged native extension definition is not rerun locally; no actual remote filesystem, native layout/focus or authentication claim. Receipts selecting modified tests are retired; unaffected exact-selector receipts remain unchanged.",
        "The standalone download-notice throttle suite was removed; its interval, per-grant, revocation-reset and unbound-guest alarms are intentionally lost. Remaining notice suites are not claimed as exact substitutes.",
        "Historical receipt before standalone test removal, preserved with its originally executed command; remaining commands were not rerun for this audit: {\"date\":\"2026-08-27\",\"runner\":\"local\",\"platform\":\"macos\",\"command\":\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/browser/doc-preview-download-block-notice.test.ts src/main/browser/browser-session-partition-policies.test.ts src/main/browser/doc-preview-guest-policy.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.failure-message.test.tsx\",\"result\":\"passed\",\"durationSeconds\":1.78,\"summary\":\"64/64 on the visible download refusal, re-issued at the relocated path. This replaces the 2026-08-27 record of the same four files at 62/62, whose ten mutants — removing the notice from the deny listener, adding it to the routing listener, dropping the guest-registry lookup that names which preview to tell, dropping the shell branch and the row, letting the row survive the failure panel, removing the per-preview throttle, sharing one throttle across previews, never expiring the window, and publishing for a contents no preview is bound to — all failed as sole deltas. The relocation moved no line of any of them.\",\"currentCommand\":\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-download-block-notice.test.ts src/main/browser/sessions/browser-session-partition-policies.test.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-guest-policy.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.failure-message.test.tsx\"}",
        "Live paired-server validation currently covers macOS only.",
        "Multiple simultaneous viewers are not exercised by the Electron journey.",
        "Local workspaces intentionally keep the embedded browser tab at a file URL and are not covered by the preview journey.",
        "The SSH preview owner has unit coverage only; no live SSH host renders a preview in this gate.",
        "The preview journey exercises one self-contained document. Relative subresources, reload re-reading the workspace disk, and the truncated and out-of-worktree refusals are covered by unit contracts only.",
        "Renderer close-to-release mock ledgers were removed; the live journey observes tab disappearance without inspecting main grant registry revocation.",
        "The external-link route trusts a real press on an anchor in a focused preview guest, so it proves the reader pressed that anchor, not that the anchor's visible text matches its target. The tab it opens is visible, which is the remaining containment.",
        "WebRTC is fenced by the IP-handling policy rather than by removing the API; the guest can still construct a peer connection, and the journey measures that it gathers nothing.",
        "The standalone capability-cleanup and browser-placement ledger suites were removed, including their mixed-version rejection, cleanup transfer, capacity and partition alarms. web-runtime-session.test.ts no longer supplies browser creation, rollback or recovery assertions. The grouped workspace-document exclusion remains; the separate no-group publication example was removed. Existing live/browser-store evidence does not establish equivalent replacement alarms. Earlier descriptions of the removed fixtures and their run results are historical.",
        "The client-owned-placement and layout-groups suites are removed. The broad mirror fixture no longer supplies preview placement/reservation/move assertions. Browser rows retain pre-response replay and real local-workspace reuse; focus intent retains response ordering and exact-leaf sibling ordering. Supplied browser-layout and placement/focus projection alarms are lost; retained evidence is narrower and not equivalent.",
        "The test-value audit retires renderer grant-release mock ledgers, direct creation/title/session-field copies, notification/onboarding calls and several placement/per-page projections. Canonical-ID rejection, document reopen/restore and preview URL fences remain; they do not prove close-to-registry revocation or replace every lost alarm. Historical execution evidence is unchanged.",
        "The test-value audit removed the direct legacy editor-preview hydration example from tabs-hydration.test.ts. Dropping legacy preview chrome while preserving the same-document ordinary editor no longer has that alarm. The surviving corrupt-id deduplication case does not cover that migration, and retained preview journeys are not equivalent replacement coverage. Historical run counts and migration mutation findings describe the earlier suite.",
        "Audit1308: src/renderer/src/components/editor/EditorPanelShell.header.test.tsx removed. Header visibility and mocked editor-surface inventory alarms disappear. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit1308 retires this complete dated receipt because a source in its selector was deleted or reduced. It does not validate the reduced selector. Original receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/ipc/browser-preview-tool-authorization.test.ts src/main/browser/browser-manager-annotation-bridge.test.ts src/main/browser/browser-manager-guest-lifecycle.test.ts src/main/browser/offscreen-browser-backend-lifecycle.test.ts src/main/browser/doc-preview-guest-policy.test.ts src/shared/doc-preview-scheme.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/doc-preview-document-actions.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/use-doc-preview-guest-tools.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/editor/EditorPanelShell.header.test.tsx src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 1.52,\n          \"summary\": \"174/174 at the relocated paths, replacing the 2026-08-27 records of the same command at 162/162 and 158/158. Those established, as sole deltas: removing the unregister-channel refusal goes red because the grab disposal beside it drops the intent an in-flight preview grab compares by identity, while an ordinary browser page driven through the identical sequence still has its grab state disposed; removing registration’s already-gone-guest refusal goes red for both a missing and a destroyed guest; removing the map deletion on the refusal path goes red at shutdown; the bridge’s own unregisterGuest branch, restored, tears down a live page over a misaddressed request; and the download fall-through for an unresolved owner hands back a same-named local file under a remote document’s name.\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/ipc/browser/browser-preview-tool-authorization.test.ts src/main/browser/guest-lifecycle/manager/browser-manager-annotation-bridge.test.ts src/main/browser/guest-lifecycle/manager/browser-manager-guest-lifecycle.test.ts src/main/browser/backends/offscreen-browser-backend-lifecycle.test.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-guest-policy.test.ts src/shared/doc-preview-scheme.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/doc-preview-document-actions.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/use-doc-preview-guest-tools.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/editor/EditorPanelShell.header.test.tsx src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\"\n        }",
        "Retired during audit1312 aggregate-driver import cleanup; original complete execution receipt (unchanged): {\"date\":\"2026-08-13\",\"runner\":\"local\",\"platform\":\"macos\",\"command\":\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-browser.test.ts src/renderer/src/hooks/useIpcEvents-browser-tab-create.test.ts src/renderer/src/hooks/useIpcEvents-close-routing-browser-pages.test.ts src/renderer/src/hooks/useIpcEvents-close-routing-session-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/web-runtime-session.test.ts\",\"currentCommand\":\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-browser.test.ts src/renderer/src/hooks/useIpcEvents-close-routing-browser-pages.test.ts src/renderer/src/hooks/useIpcEvents-close-routing-session-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser.test.ts\",\"result\":\"passed\",\"durationSeconds\":10.83,\"summary\":\"Five post-review host, IPC, store, and client lifecycle files passed 1,356 tests with one pre-existing skip, including both shards that failed before the canonical page/workspace identity and typed missing-page cleanup corrections.\"}",
