        "Audit1386: src/renderer/src/lib/doc-preview-grants.test.ts reduced. Repeated-mount mint count, ordinary release/remint and failed-mint cache retry standalone alarms removed; no actual grant server/access test. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit1386 retires this complete dated receipt because a changed source or imported registration driver is in either command field. It does not validate the reduced selector. Original receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/browser/doc-preview-grant-registry.test.ts src/main/browser/doc-preview-file-reader.test.ts src/main/browser/doc-preview-protocol.test.ts src/main/browser/doc-preview-guest-policy.test.ts src/main/browser/doc-preview-failure-notice.test.ts src/shared/doc-preview-scheme.test.ts src/renderer/src/lib/doc-preview-grants.test.ts src/renderer/src/lib/file-preview.test.ts src/renderer/src/lib/file-preview-action-visibility.test.tsx src/main/window/main-window-webview-security.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.failure-message.test.tsx src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/doc-preview-external-link-confirmation.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-file-link-actions.test.ts\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 1.63,\n          \"summary\": \"189/189 over the grant, reader, protocol, guest-policy, scheme-admission, plan-routing, action-visibility, failure-message, external-link and terminal-row contracts. This replaces the 2026-08-27 record of the same command at 174/174, whose thirteenth file was the deleted doc-preview-external-link-bridge.test.ts: the STA-5758 hardening moved that behavior into the reader-facing confirmation (doc-preview-external-link-confirmation.test.ts), which now proves the exact destination is shown and nothing opens on cancel, alongside everything the retired run carried — the stale-mint rejection that must not evict a reopened preview tab, the CSP header and session request filter, the SSH symlink refusal, subframe containment, truncated and over-cap reads, the unservable-asset and empty-file split, the out-of-worktree paired refusal, and the guest deny-only navigation sinks. The count also carries the entry-only rule added on top of the hardening: a grant whose document directory is its own request base — a workspace-root or out-of-workspace document — reads nothing but the entry file until the reader approves a directory, at both the lexical and the canonical containment pass, because that directory is where secrets live and a DNS-prefetch beacon needs no click. Historical command preserved after removal of the mocked preview test suite in the test-value audit; currentCommand links only the remaining suites. The recorded result, count, duration and mutation narrative describe the historical command. The current command has not been rerun here and does not claim equivalent coverage.\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-grant-registry.test.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-file-reader.test.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-protocol.test.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-guest-policy.test.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-failure-notice.test.ts src/shared/doc-preview-scheme.test.ts src/renderer/src/lib/doc-preview-grants.test.ts src/main/window/main-window-webview-security.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.failure-message.test.tsx src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/doc-preview-external-link-confirmation.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-file-link-actions.test.ts\"\n        }",
        "Audit1386 historical platform/provider scope before source changes: {\"coveredPlatforms\":[\"macos\"],\"coveredProviders\":[\"remote-runtime\"]}. Static assertion references are not current execution evidence.",
        "Audit1386 historical assertion inventory for changed sources:\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/lib/doc-preview-grants.test.ts\",\n    \"assertions\": [\n      \"grants are deduped per preview tab so a StrictMode double-mount cannot revoke the surviving webview\",\n      \"a mint that rejects after its tab was released and reopened leaves the reopened tab's grant revocable\"\n    ]\n  }\n]",
        "Audit1401: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-duplicate-pty-repair.spec.ts removed. Loses listing-on-already-repaired-data alarm; it never established runtime repair invocation. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-split-agent-tab.spec.ts removed. Loses actual mobile split sibling shell versus recorded-agent resume command alarms; no equivalent coverage asserted. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-native-chat-setup.spec.ts removed. Loses separate setup/startup tab result in that manually assembled path. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts reduced. Driver registration/import of a whole-deleted selected spec is removed; directly authored cases remain unchanged. No extra authored removal credit. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact primary-selector receipts remain unchanged.",
        "Audit1412: src/main/browser/guest-lifecycle/manager/browser-manager-guest-policy-profile.test.ts removed. Loses workspace-document in-grant navigation/popup refusal, cleanup/re-attach, cross-registry guest authorization and browsing-map separation alarms. No equivalent browser policy coverage is claimed. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit1412 retires this complete dated receipt because a source in its selector was deleted or reduced. It does not validate the reduced selector. Original receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/ipc/browser-preview-tool-authorization.test.ts src/main/ipc/browser-tab-registration-wait.test.ts src/main/ipc/doc-preview-grant-ipc.test.ts src/main/browser/browser-manager-guest-lifecycle.test.ts src/main/browser/browser-manager-guest-policy-profile.test.ts src/main/browser/browser-manager-annotation-bridge.test.ts src/main/browser/offscreen-browser-backend-lifecycle.test.ts src/main/browser/doc-preview-guest-policy.test.ts src/shared/doc-preview-scheme.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/use-doc-preview-guest-tools.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 1.5,\n          \"summary\": \"175/175 at the relocated paths on the unified tool authority, replacing the 2026-08-27 record of the same command at 174/174. That run killed twelve of fourteen mutants as sole deltas — dropping the document branch from the one authority door, removing either browsing-registration refusal or the mint-side refusal that is its converse, deleting the registration notification or widening it to the worktree-wide and any-tab waits, disposing revoked state by grant instead of by page, dropping the hosting-renderer or destroyed-contents check, rebuilding the renderer tool target from the grant, and deleting the teardown identity check under a re-mint — and reported two as ill-posed rather than as kills. The relocation changed no file it names except their directory.\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/ipc/browser/browser-preview-tool-authorization.test.ts src/main/ipc/browser/browser-tab-registration-wait.test.ts src/main/ipc/doc-preview-grant-ipc.test.ts src/main/browser/guest-lifecycle/manager/browser-manager-guest-lifecycle.test.ts src/main/browser/guest-lifecycle/manager/browser-manager-guest-policy-profile.test.ts src/main/browser/guest-lifecycle/manager/browser-manager-annotation-bridge.test.ts src/main/browser/backends/offscreen-browser-backend-lifecycle.test.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-guest-policy.test.ts src/shared/doc-preview-scheme.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/use-doc-preview-guest-tools.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\"\n        }",
        "Audit1412 retires this complete dated receipt because a source in its selector was deleted or reduced. It does not validate the reduced selector. Original receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/browser/browser-manager-guest-policy-profile.test.ts src/main/window/main-window-webview-security.test.ts src/main/browser/doc-preview-guest-policy.test.ts\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 0.32,\n          \"summary\": \"55/55 on the candidate that gives every guest one attach door. A preview used to reach its policies through an installer of its own, which meant the manager's attachment bookkeeping — the set registration consults and the cleanup teardown runs — never knew a preview existed. It is now a profile on `attachGuestPolicies`, and the doc policy is what that profile installs. Red-green with each mutant as the sole delta: deleting the profile branch hands a previewed document the browsing machinery (clicked-link routing, frame routing, popup child windows, anti-detection over the debugger) and lets it navigate off-grant; dropping the manager's destroyed wiring leaves the guest answerable through the grant-keyed authority after it dies and its id marked attached forever; and making the window fork ask for the default profile is caught at the fork itself. The absence assertions are paired with a presence precondition in the same run: a browsing guest attached through the same method observably takes every one of those things, so a profile that fenced nothing, or an attach path that had stopped installing anything at all, fails rather than passing empty.\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/browser/guest-lifecycle/manager/browser-manager-guest-policy-profile.test.ts src/main/window/main-window-webview-security.test.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-guest-policy.test.ts\"\n        }",
        "Audit1412 historical platform/provider scope before source changes: {\"coveredPlatforms\":[\"macos\"],\"coveredProviders\":[]}. Remaining provider scope applies only to unchanged-source receipts.",
        "Audit1421 removes browser-address-bar-suggestions.test.ts. Document suggestion title/path matching, recency merging and path-prefix ranking alarms are lost. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Historical receipts remain scoped to unchanged selectors; the reduced command has no new execution result.",
        "Audit1803 retires this complete dated receipt because doc-preview-scheme.test.ts was reduced. It does not validate the reduced selector. Original receipt verbatim: {\"date\":\"2026-08-27\",\"runner\":\"local\",\"platform\":\"macos\",\"command\":\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx src/shared/doc-preview-scheme.test.ts\",\"result\":\"passed\",\"durationSeconds\":2.05,\"summary\":\"39/39 on the title-parity trio at the relocated path, replacing the 2026-08-27 record of the same three files, which killed five mutants as sole deltas: disabling the document branch restores New Tab for a named document, dropping the grant-URL refusal puts the scheme into the title, the tab mirror and the written session, returning New Tab instead of the file name breaks the fallback, removing the guest listener leaves the document unable to name its tab, and making the scheme test parse rather than prefix-match lets a title that merely looks like a preview URL through.\",\"currentCommand\":\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser/pages/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx src/shared/doc-preview-scheme.test.ts\"}",
        "Audit1853 retires this complete dated receipt because its selector includes reduced test sources. Its historical result, count and duration do not validate the reduced selector or equivalent coverage. Original receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-09-06\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/ipc/doc-preview-grant-ipc.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/link-actions/LinkActionPopover.test.tsx src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/tabs-hydration.test.ts\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 7.12,\n          \"summary\": \"44/44 across all four files after PR #19130 moved the terminal popover suite to the shared LinkActionPopover path; all eight popover cases remain. This replaces the 2026-08-27 command that named the removed test path. Historical evidence from that run (4.77 seconds; mutation checks were not repeated in this rerun): 40/40 on the candidate that removes the editor preview species and moves its two boundary duties onto the browser tab. The publish filter moved with the tab: it used to exclude an editor file by mode, and now excludes a browser workspace by whether it is located by a document — asserted at both the group projection and the tab loop, because a mutant that filters only one of them still publishes. Migration is the other half: sessions written by builds that made previews editor tabs carry chrome whose entity id encodes the document, and whose document was never persisted, so it has always come back naming a surface no restore produces; that chrome is now dropped. Each mutant as the sole delta: filtering neither place publishes the document tab to mobile, filtering only the projection still publishes it, and removing the migration leaves the stale strip entry. Presence preconditions in the same runs: an ordinary browser tab beside the document tab does publish, and the ordinary editor tab for the very same document survives hydration. Historical command and result are preserved after the test-value audit removed the tab-store assertions this run included. currentCommand is only an administrative link to the remaining gate command; the historical run has not validated that command or equivalent coverage.\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/ipc/doc-preview-grant-ipc.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/link-actions/LinkActionPopover.test.tsx src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts\"\n        }",
        "Audit1853 accepts removal of the LinkActionPopover resolved-file-path copy/open-state alarm and Settings callback-order/explicit-omission alarms. The surviving clipboard pending-write and failure-retry cases do not establish equivalent coverage; fake clipboard/toast/popover boundaries do not prove native clipboard or settings navigation. Surviving command and test-file selectors remain.",
        "Audit1899 replays sealed Audit1895: workspace-doc-history.test.ts is entirely removed from its current command and testFiles. Supplied recency/dedupe/cap/title/identity examples and the10000-row getter-read budget alarm are intentionally lost. No current assertionRef or active receipt selects that file. Unrelated active receipts and all prior gap literals remain verbatim; no replacement history/index-work coverage or new browser/paired-preview gate execution is claimed.",
        "Audit1925 (sources1922/1923): The complete terminal-file-link-actions suite is removed. Lose supplied local/remote menu-row inventories, browser label/order/download/reveal callback forwarding, platform-copy and source-group pinning examples. No OS reveal/download, real remote preview or browser navigation was exercised; the other real document-preview sources are not equivalent replacements. Preserve meaningful remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged dated receipts within their original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh gate execution evidence in this metadata packet. No equivalent replacement, physical watcher/PTY/provider, live SSH/remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Exact retired authored alarms: 'offers Orca and system-default actions for a local file'; 'offers a local HTML file the link-routing browsers, primary first'; 'labels workspace switching and omits an impossible remote alternate'; 'offers the same rows for a remote previewable file, downloading before the OS opens it'; 'keeps row parity between local and remote previewable files'; 'drops the remote download row for a path that announces itself as a directory'; 'offers Reveal in Finder for a local file link and reveals it through the shared path'; 'selects a folder link in its parent instead of opening it'; 'uses the platform file manager name'; 'omits the row for a workspace-root link, which has its own Open in Finder row'; 'omits the row for a file owned by an SSH or runtime host'; 'omits the row when the pane shell runs on %s'; 'keeps the row for a local link while a server is focused, and omits it for a runtime-owned link'; 'reveals nothing until the row is clicked'; 'pins the source group with groups $groupIds'; 'omits the row for an unknown source or a workspace switch'.",
        "Audit1973: Delete the browser RPC forwarding/schema/scalar suite and its prospective selector. Preserve all27 unrelated dated receipts; no actual browser operation alarm is replaced. Whole original changed dated receipts are retired, never narrowed or transferred. This metadata review claims no fresh execution, equivalent replacement, provider/PTY, live remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result.",
        "Audit1973 historical original commands object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active execution evidence or replacement coverage:\n\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/browser/client-pages/orca-runtime-browser.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/browser/browser.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/web-session-tabs-sync-focus-intent.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/web-session-tabs-sync-browser-tabs.test.ts\"",
