        "Audit2043 historical original assertionRefs object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active evidence:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/main/window/main-window-webview-security.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"an orca-preview src is admitted only on the preview partition with a live grant\",\n            \"preview guests receive their own policy instead of the browser guest policies\",\n            \"a preview attach is pinned to the preview preload over any renderer-supplied value, and a browsing attach never receives it\",\n            \"grants a renderer can no longer release are cleared at window creation and on reload, and survive an in-document navigation\"\n          ]\n        }",
        "Audit2043 historical original assertionRefs object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active evidence:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/main/ipc/doc-preview-grant-ipc.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"a sender that is not the trusted renderer mints no grant and revokes none\",\n            \"a reported link click reaches the guest policy with its own sender, and a non-string report reaches nothing\"\n          ]\n        }",
        "Audit2052 (source2049): The ordinary orca-runtime.test.ts registrar drops seven imports of deliberately deleted low-value runtime suites. Their mock capability/agent-presence/environment/title/deduplication and batching alarms are intentionally lost without replacement; remaining imports retain their original order. The runtime handle-contract registrar separately drops the deleted tab-collision registration. Unrelated dated evidenceRuns remain unchanged and do not validate reduced-source bytes or selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed.",
        "Audit2056 (sources2054/2055): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts: ordinary registration cleanup removes only await import('./orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-14.spec'). src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-03.spec.ts: arms the stale-title timer for a seeded working title; arms the Command Code scrape from the noted spawn command; prefers the tracked title over a stale renderer lastTitle in the hydration seed; writes recent output into the current runtime output map; uses a later title handler replacement with the runtime receiver; calls the current injected listener with the runtime receiver; keeps optional reconciliation lazy after its callback is removed. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-14.spec.ts: lists them, so a paired client can mirror a migrated editor; closes one by retiring it from the host session; keeps an unsaved draft unless the close is forced; shares aggregate work but leaves a replacement pending promise alone; lets a targeted refresh finish while an aggregate refresh waits; refuses a close when the store lacks %s before the guard; keeps a later missing %s on the original caught failure path. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed.",
        "Audit2061 (sources2059/2060): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts: ordinary registration cleanup removes only await import('./orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-headless-chat-rebuild.spec'); await import('./orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-cold-serve-hydrate.spec'); await import('./orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-execution-host.spec'); await import('./orca-runtime-tests/terminal-spawn-dispatch.spec'). src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/headless-snapshots-part-02.spec.ts: replaces a cwd parsed before late WSL context with the provider cwd; keeps a live WSL cwd that arrives during late-context snapshot recovery; infers local reconstructed WSL context from a WSL UNC worktree; clears stale terminal file URI hostnames after empty-host OSC7 cwd updates; serializes SSH headless OSC7 cwd as POSIX when the desktop runtime is on Windows; keeps Windows SSH OSC7 cwd as a drive path when the desktop runtime is POSIX; serializes Windows SSH headless OSC7 cwd as a drive path on POSIX desktops; infers restored SSH connection identity from app-scoped PTY ids. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-headless-chat-rebuild.spec.ts: survives the rebuild that closing a saved editor tab forces; keeps its place in the tab order when the host lists the workspace again; lists tabs to phones in the order desktop clients draw after a rebuild; keeps the place a window gave a chat across a graph resend before the chat is restored. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-cold-serve-hydrate.spec.ts: lists every persisted terminal of a windowless host after a cold restart; lists every persisted terminal in the all-worktrees inventory after a cold restart; lists persisted editor tabs beside the terminals after a cold restart; restores a persisted split group layout on the cold rebuild; restores the saved active group of a split even when it is not the first group; falls back to the active tab group when the saved active group was not restored; keeps the headless group active when there is no persisted split; keeps phone and CLI creates in the group they joined across a cold restart. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-failed-retry.spec.ts: lists the leftover with its error, though Git no longer does; takes the normal delete once Git registers a checkout at the path again; joins a retry another client started while this Delete listed Git; shows the failed row with its error, not the scan cached before the delete. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-execution-host.spec.ts: refuses an SSH row whose host is unreachable instead of deleting here; refuses a runtime row with no nested SSH target rather than deleting locally; refuses a runtime row that also names a nested SSH target; retains runtime purge dispatch in a recovery job; uses the runtime helper override before resuming an interrupted removal; uses the runtime helper override before retrying a failed removal; captures the watcher callback and retains its job-host receiver; reads the current runtime removal queue. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-spawn-dispatch.spec.ts: reports the spawn request before it leaves for the pty controller; reports it even when the spawn itself then fails; does not report it when the create fails before any spawn request; captures the admission method before reading the incarnation; captures the record method before evaluating its state object; skips database payload serialization when no database exists; skips a throwing database payload when no database exists; keeps the database method and receiver captured before its payload; captures the canonical map method before a binding getter changes it; completes the captured replacement fence without another map lookup. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed.",
        "Module layout policy correction: retire the remaining program-status-osc.spec.ts event-projection case (production/mock-derived pane-key oracle) and sign-in timeout case (real setTimeout wait with Date-only fake clocks). The runtime test registrar no longer imports that file. No replacement coverage or fresh execution is claimed for these losses; historical receipts retain their original source scope.",
        "Module layout policy correction: retire the two remaining worktree-ps-agent-row-dismissal.spec.ts registrations. The remint/dismissal/exit case computed expected snapshotVersion increments from a production snapshot and used real-clock vi.waitFor; the legacy OSC case derived its expected paneKey from the production layout-owner switch. The runtime registrar no longer imports this file. These public projection scenarios have no replacement coverage or fresh execution claimed; all historical receipts and earlier loss notes retain their original source scope.",
        "D01 candidate audit retires this complete dated receipt because a named test source changes in the candidate overlay. It supplies no new execution or equivalent-coverage claim. Original receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.failure-message.test.tsx\",\n          \"result\": \"failed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 1.27,\n          \"summary\": \"Candidate with the sole delta that every failure sets the blocking reason, asset or not, failed 4/14 on the asset-notice assertions — the same mutant the retired 2026-08-26 record measured at 3/10, re-run at the relocated path. A refused subresource must name itself over a document that stays mounted; only the entry document may take the page away.\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.failure-message.test.tsx\"\n        }",
        "D01 candidate audit retires this complete dated receipt because a named test source changes in the candidate overlay. It supplies no new execution or equivalent-coverage claim. Original receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.failure-message.test.tsx\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 1.54,\n          \"summary\": \"14/14 on the reader-facing failure suite at its relocated path. This and the red run below replace the 2026-08-26 pair recorded against the pre-relocation path (10/10 green, 3/10 red), re-measured today so the entry/subresource split keeps a red half rather than only a green one.\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.failure-message.test.tsx\"\n        }",
        "D01 final candidate whole-registration policy removes retired module selectors and obsolete assertion descriptions prospectively. Existing unaffected receipts retain their original scope; reduced selectors have no new execution or equivalent replacement claim. Retired named modules: [\"src/preload/doc-preview-link-interception.test.ts\",\"src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.failure-message.test.tsx\"]. Retired compound assertion refs, preserved as historical data: [{\"file\":\"src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/doc-preview-external-link-confirmation.test.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"an external preview link shows the reader its exact destination and becomes a browser tab only after confirmation\",\"a declined confirmation opens nothing, and a confirmed tab that is refused or fails outright surfaces instead of being dropped\"]}]",
        "Audit2452 removes the whole fake-effect browser-close routing suite. Active selectors and assertion references no longer select it. Its requested-worktree default close, sibling-page close and explicit missing-page typed reply alarms are intentionally retired without equivalent replacement. Prior dated receipts remain unchanged and scoped to their original sources; no fresh execution of the reduced gate, rendered browser, live remote, mobile or cross-platform validation is claimed. Retired assertion reference: {\"file\":\"src/renderer/src/hooks/useIpcEvents-close-routing-browser-pages.test.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"closing an absent renderer page returns browser_tab_not_found instead of an untyped failure\"]}",
        "Audit3108: doc-preview-grants.test.ts now retains only the stale grant-rejection race: a late rejected grant request must not evict a newer grant registry entry, witnessed by later revocation of grant-2. Retire stable minted-location and outside-workspace POSIX/Windows request-projection alarms without replacement. The direct nonempty grant selector remains unchanged; no real grant-server/file authorization, SSH/HTML delivery or native-focus result is claimed.",
        "File/document owner layout retires the complete workspace-doc-address-input unit suite because its sole mixed case asserts internal catalog-enumeration work. The current-workspace HTML-resolution alarm is lost; no equivalent replacement coverage or pass for the reduced unit selector is claimed. Historical receipts and all remaining selectors/assertions retain their original scope.",
        "Module-layout wave2 intentionally retires complete prohibited owning registrations in src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/doc-preview-document-actions.test.ts. Lost alarms: A resolved remote file owner taking precedence over an unresolved workspace owner would lose its routing alarm. A project published on two hosts refusing to open an ambiguous local copy would lose its refusal alarm. An unresolved document refusing both local open and remote download, and including its path in the refusal, would lose the existing alarm. An unknown workspace root preventing an accidental local document open would lose its guard alarm. A restored document using its recorded runtime owner when the worktree resolves none would lose its existing fallback alarm. A restored tab without a recorded owner consulting the resolved worktree owner would lose its existing fallback alarm. No equivalent replacement coverage or reduced-selector pass is claimed.",
        "Audit 3301 removes the caller-chat-target precedence over host selection example from web-session-tabs-sync-focus-intent.test.ts. The snapshot-before-RPC replay and split-sibling-first exact-leaf focus cases remain unchanged and match the existing assertion reference. Preserve current selectors, assertion references, unrelated active receipts and complete archived history. These mocked state-composition survivors provide no equivalent replacement, rendered, native, network or fresh execution proof.",
        "Audit3335 retires the complete three-case browser-tabs snapshot assembly suite: canonical snapshot replay/placement/focus, local host-page adoption and unstamped host echo leaving a local page untouched alarms are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. The surviving focused selector is unexecuted in this source composition. Unrelated dated receipts keep their original scope; no fresh runtime/network, rendered UI, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed.",
        "Audit3342 retires the complete mobile editor/diff tab-publication projection suite: editor/diff serialization, workspace-document privacy withholding, pending/focus and capability/options projections are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. The surviving focused selectors are unexecuted in this source composition. Six complete compound macOS receipts whose command fields select the changed source are retired verbatim as history; their other selected tests receive no promoted evidence. Other dated receipts keep their original scope; no fresh runtime/UI/mobile/mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed.",
        "Audit3342 historical original commands object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active evidence or replacement coverage:\n\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser/pages/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\"",
        "Audit3342 historical original commands object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active evidence or replacement coverage:\n\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/link-actions/LinkActionPopover.test.tsx src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts\"",
        "Audit3342 historical original testFiles object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active evidence or replacement coverage:\n\"src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts\"",
        "Audit3342 historical original assertionRefs object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"keeps a workspace document out of published tab groups as well as the tab list\"\n          ]\n        }",
        "Audit3342 historical original evidenceRuns object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/workspace-doc-page-pane.test.tsx src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser/pages/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"result\": \"failed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 7,\n          \"summary\": \"The adversarial pass answered the request for its own group-projection probe after this round landed, and it had measured a third observable this test was missing: the held-back group also has to leave the published layout tree, or the phone renders a split whose second pane can never hold anything. Adopted as a fourth assertion and re-run against the same sole delta, which now fails on the dangling-reference check and, with that check blinded, on the layout alone — group-left and group-right against the group-right the clean tree publishes. The two probes agreed on everything else, including that the tab list is unchanged under this mutant, which is why an assertion reading only the tab list cannot reach the site at all.\"\n        }",
        "Audit3342 historical original evidenceRuns object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/workspace-doc-page-pane.test.tsx src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser/pages/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 3,\n          \"summary\": \"The adversarial pass's four coverage findings, landed and pinned: 58/58. The third url door now keeps a document page blank and names it by its document, the group projection holds a document back from published groups as well as from the tab list, the pane's focus handoff is pinned in the widening direction as well as the narrowing one, and the handoff is re-offered when the window takes focus back.\"\n        }",
        "Audit3342 historical original evidenceRuns object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/workspace-doc-page-pane.test.tsx src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser/pages/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"result\": \"failed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 3,\n          \"summary\": \"Three sole-delta mutants on the third url door, each failing only the new store test: committing the reported url onto a document page, dropping the document from the title normalizer there (which renames the tab New Tab, since a blank url is what that fallback reads), and marking a blank document page loading. The ordinary-page half of the same test passes under all three, so the door is pinned as a document-only refusal rather than as a door that writes nothing.\"\n        }",
        "Audit3342 historical original evidenceRuns object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/workspace-doc-page-pane.test.tsx src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser/pages/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"result\": \"failed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 3,\n          \"summary\": \"Two sole-delta mutants on the mobile publish boundary. Dropping the document from the group projection's browser ids fails only the new grouped test — the tab list stays correct because the per-tab guard still refuses the tab, and what breaks is a published group whose order and active tab name a tab the phone is never sent. This is the survivor the adversarial pass reported: it survives the whole suite without this test, because no other test in it has tab groups. Dropping the per-tab guard instead fails only the ungrouped test, so the two halves of the boundary are pinned separately.\"\n        }",
        "Audit3342 historical original evidenceRuns object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/workspace-doc-page-pane.test.tsx src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser/pages/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"result\": \"failed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 3,\n          \"summary\": \"Three sole-delta mutants widening the focus handoff, the direction the adversarial pass found uncovered: dropping the page-activity half, dropping the active-tab-type half, and dropping the active-browser-tab half each fail exactly one of the pane's refusals — the inactive page, the terminal in front, and the other browser tab respectively. The presence half of that test passes under all three, so a pane that had stopped offering focus at all would still fail rather than pass the refusals vacuously.\"\n        }",
        "Audit3342 historical original evidenceRuns object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/workspace-doc-page-pane.test.tsx src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser/pages/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph/sync-runtime-graph-editor-diff-tabs.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx\",\n          \"result\": \"failed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 3,\n          \"summary\": \"One sole-delta mutant dropping the window-focus re-offer: the guest is focused once at mount and never again after the window comes back, which is the desktop gap behind it — another app taking the front leaves the preview's only route out shut until the pane remounts. It fails only the new re-offer test, and the refusing-preview case beside it stays green, so the re-offer is pinned as gated rather than unconditional.\"\n        }",
        "Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The retained runtime registration driver loses three complete imported fragments: changed-working-label title facts and suppressed-frame tracked snapshots; refusing SSH GitLab MR-base lookup before local Git/glab calls; and missing folder-workspace path creation/update refusal before spawn/store mutation. These alarms are intentionally lost. Other imported fragments and separately rooted dated receipts are unchanged; they are not equivalent replacement coverage.  Original scope text is retained as the exact suffix of coverageNotes/oracle; historical evidence is unchanged.",
        "Audit3460 final-v2 composes accepted AUTHOR3454/PEER3455 on actual post263 main: intentionally removes99 authored/106 potential expanded cases across16 selected drivers, including7 whole suites, retaining24 authored/26 potential cases. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime is claimed. The complete mocked session-close routing suite is removed, including the explicit cross-worktree cleanup alarm. Remove its active file, command token and assertion reference; historical selectors and receipts retain their original scope. Earlier notes, complete dated receipts and archived gaps retain their original scopes.",
        "Audit3460 historical original active selectors (verbatim JSON values; not current coverage):\ncommands: [\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/browser/client-pages/orca-runtime-browser.test.ts src/renderer/src/runtime/web-session-tabs-sync/navigation/web-session-tabs-sync-focus-intent.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-grant-registry.test.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-file-reader.test.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-guest-policy.test.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-failure-notice.test.ts src/shared/document-preview/doc-preview-scheme.test.ts src/renderer/src/lib/browser/documents/doc-preview-grants.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/doc-preview-external-link-confirmation.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/browser/sessions/partition-policies/browser-session-partition-policies.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/browser/sessions/partition-policies/browser-session-partition-policies.test.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-guest-policy.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/browser/document-preview/doc-preview-guest-policy.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser/pages/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser/pages/browser-workspace-doc-location.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/browser-pane/workspace-doc/HtmlDocPreview.toolbar.test.tsx src/shared/document-preview/doc-preview-scheme.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/browser/pages/browser-workspace-do