      "coverageNotes": "Audit4014 removes the complete browser client page command integration suite and its active command token, test selector and assertion reference. Its synthetic guest lifecycle still exercised real executor/dispatcher/Session/WebContents registry composition: navigation normalization, generation reclaim, spontaneous destruction inventory revocation, and exactly-once route/policy retirement alarms are intentionally lost. Electron guest navigation, proxy resolution and renderer lifecycle were supplied test ports; no equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. The three unrelated active dated receipts and all prior historical strings remain unchanged. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit3381 intentionally removes the entire browser network tunnel protocol suite and active selectors/assertion. Static envelope/dispatch protocol alarms are lost without equivalent replacement. Remaining tunnel session and stream tests have narrower scopes. All three unrelated complete dated receipts are preserved verbatim with their original selectors; no fresh execution claimed. Module layout SSH policy: Retire the dynamic-forward launch argument/default inventory. The retained actual startup-cancellation entry case covers cancellation classification and termination/probe cleanup requests with supplied process/socket boundaries, not real SSH launch flags or live forwarding. Remove only the retired launch-flags assertion; unrelated dated receipts and their executed commands remain unchanged. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1991: Remove the ordinary browser-host release/sub-cap and exact socket-close counter aliases. Retain the two actual admitted-device fairness and shared ask/browser/wait budget callbacks, which call server handlers with fake WebSockets and controlled pending RPCs. Preserve all3 unrelated dated receipts. No real browser placement or remote tunnel deployment is proved by this admission suite. Changed-source prior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, physical provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1983: Delete the mocked browser placement mutation and projection suites and both prospective selectors. Preserve3 unrelated receipts. Changed-source prior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1973: Remove stale production-registration and negotiated metadata aliases, compound refusal/cleanup aliases, isolated descriptor/route/memory/cleanup microcases. Retain exact negotiated command settlement, duplicate/conflict fencing, ready/replay ordering, superseded-connection cleanup, second-host refusal, ungranted target refusal, public connector redaction, revocation race and route replacement aliases within injected-port scope. Reconciliation and all3 unrelated dated receipts remain unchanged. Whole original changed dated receipts are retired, never narrowed or transferred. This metadata review claims no fresh execution, equivalent replacement, provider/PTY, live remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1918 narrows browser-host-command-ledger-capacity: intentionally loses injected per-page/global cache expiry-count ceilings and authority/command/result cloning inventory alarms. Retain valid commands/testFile and the oversized-wire pre-admission and delivery-failure outstanding-outcome assertions, backed by unchanged retained real-ledger callbacks with supplied browser delivery. These survivors are not equivalent replacement coverage for the deleted cache/cloning examples. Existing three exact unrelated tunnel/wire receipts retain their original scope; no fresh reduced-gate, real browser/provider, native/platform, soak or measured-budget result is added. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1900 reduces ws-outbound-backpressure-queue by seven authored definitions while retaining ten. Current source19 assertions still describe distinct direct/queued aggregate admission, cooperative drain ordering and aggregate claim release. Existing commands, testFiles and all three source19 assertions remain valid and unchanged. The affected2026-11-04 Linux44tests/4files/5.58s receipt is retired whole as historical evidence. The other three unchanged-selector browser receipts retain their exact original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh integrated, physical-device, mixed-host, soak or measured-budget result. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1709 removes low-value test definitions and retires affected assertion or execution-receipt claims without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews bound retained behavior and injected/native/remote limits. Unchanged assertions and receipts keep their original scope; gates lacking current active evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1687 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1686 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1640 removes low-value IPC, SSH, workspace and transcript-watcher tests without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public refusal, cancellation, execution-host and real-filesystem outcomes with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1571 removes mock forwarding, capability/schema inventories, private predicates, supplied error/result replays, and filesystem-mocked persistence checks without equivalent replacement claims. Retained changed tests also exercise real local permission-file reread, registry proxy rollback/credential retirement, site display recovery, and pending sender/credential/document admission with injected Electron/UI producers. Retained network tests exercise owned stream credit/cleanup, generation and retirement fences, real loopback proxy/SOCKS bytes and file-backed binding state. SSH/WSL/paired runtime, native sessions, authority producers and storage clears remain injected; simulated relaunch uses filesystem mocks. The unchanged profile-retirement suite was statically reviewed and not rerun. No actual SSH/WSL runtime, native Chromium jar deletion, durable process restart, remote DNS or external site proof. Receipts selecting changed tests are retired and unaffected receipts remain unchanged. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1563 retires mock cookie inventories, summary/flag/counter checks, historical replacement/replay narratives and setup-only alarms without equivalent replacement coverage. Retained changed cases exercise owned admission and cleanup, real staged-file lifetime, JSON/SQLite/WAL/schema compatibility, synthetic encryption and native Electron SameSite storage. Session/CDP/credential/write/renderer producers remain injected where recorded. Seven unchanged native definitions are not rerun locally; known stale registry-stub fixtures are not executable proof. Receipts selecting modified tests are retired; unaffected exact-selector receipts remain unchanged. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1559 removes mocked host/lease/reconciliation, event/flag/counter, forwarding, inventory and retry-budget alarms without equivalent replacement coverage. Retained cases establish owned promise, registry, rollback, admission and cleanup boundaries with injected Electron/renderer/host inputs; actual local sockets, file staging and Buffer collection are scoped in the PR. Receipts selecting modified tests are retired; unaffected exact-selector receipts remain historical evidence only. No live paired runtime, rendered browser/profile/TLS or device claim. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1401 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Audit1340 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Deterministic protocol, registry, injected-socket, and loopback-listener tests cover strict framing, remote-DNS targets, exact destination-write and source-consumption credit, at most 256 streams per route with pending opens counted inside that cap, 1024 admitted opens per 10-second monotonic window, an 8 MiB per-route application-buffer ledger, shared 32 MiB browser-host and 128 MiB process ledgers across application copies, encrypted client queues, and native WebSocket bufferedAmount, bounded byte/claim/socket-source counts, a four-frame queued-drain quantum, authority epochs, exact host selection, one host per authenticated connection, four hosts per paired device, eight global browser-host polls with four per authenticated paired device, a shared ask/host ceiling that retains one quarter for waits, bounded initial and reconnect runtime_busy recovery, long-poll metering and disconnect abort, monotonic host/page/route generations without page tombstones, two-phase exact page retirement with cancellation, connection-owned cleanup, exact client revocation, stale and replaced fences, retired stream IDs, half-close and close ordering, SOCKS CONNECT, bind/close races, listener wildcard normalization, unsupported commands, unavailable routes, and raw/terminal binary-handler isolation. Page commands use a separately echoed v1 attach negotiation, exact authority/host/page generations, bounded command IDs and sequences, and bounded create/navigate payloads; legacy attaches still receive only the unchanged ready/revoked event shapes. A second optional reconciliation subprotocol gates bounded reclaim, close, and restore payloads behind exact attach/ready echo, complete inventory, command negotiation, reconnect authority, and command-result authority; the production client advertises it only with the matching command and inventory capabilities. Exact guest or app-renderer loss marks one page generation outcome-unknown, coalesces a bounded negotiated inventory reattach, closes or retires the dead generation, and allocates a fresh generation before URL restore; explicit close is not misclassified as a crash. Mixed-version mutation tests project hidden client pages before activate, close, split, reorder, and move-to-group admission, preserve hidden raw order slots, translate visible insertion indices, and project mutation snapshots. A production server orchestrator consumes each immutable inventory once, reserves target generations without exposing placement, emits only negotiated ledger commands, commits after exact completed proof, preserves unrelated and server placements, aborts an attempt when connection authority enters reconnect grace, and requires fresh inventory after failure or abort. The production client dispatcher additionally proves per-page FIFO execution, exact payload-matched duplicate replay, frozen command/result snapshots, a global retired-generation floor, transactional admission, bounded pages/active commands/queues/per-page and global result cache/concurrency, create dependency failure, cancellation, deduplicated retirement joining, and bounded close without late-result overwrite. The server ledger owns issue order and immutable command/result snapshots, bounds outstanding commands, active pages, and per-page/global replay caches, releases active-page capacity after an exact completed close while retaining bounded result replay, validates the shared wire payload before admission, requires live delivery and exact placement, authenticates results to the negotiated connection and paired lease, rejects gaps and conflicting replay, and fences outstanding outcomes at exact retirement. Negotiated command results reuse the authenticated attach socket through bounded nested JSON requests; exact ID routing, reverse-order replies, unknown and duplicate IDs, timeout teardown, serialization failure, aggregate queue accounting, acknowledgement validation, and the unchanged non-v1 path are deterministic. A stable local listener rejects CONNECT while offline or reconnecting, retains its address across replacement, requires a strictly increasing tunnel generation, ignores late superseded callbacks, propagates tunnel protocol failure to the route owner, and recycles exhausted stream IDs only after generation replacement. Reconnect uses the unchanged native v1 attach payload and capability pair; SSH descriptors alone add an execution-host capability and require a runtime-minted grant bound to the exact browser-host lease. Exact SSH provider epoch and connection generation fence ssh2 forwardOut and one non-interactive standalone system-SSH dynamic forward per route. Unit tests preserve domain-form SOCKS requests, sanitize remote errors, bound stderr, cancel startup, release timed-out and synchronously failed sockets, and release routes once. An ephemeral Docker sshd resolves a container-only domain and returns a unique HTTP marker through both ssh2 and the actual system-OpenSSH dynamic-forward adapter without touching the user's SSH files; authority loss fences the ssh2 route. The execution runtime charges route application bytes to the same per-host/process policy; its existing E2EE owner separately caps native outbound buffers process-wide. Production-registered browser-host and paired-runtime methods lease one exact host, prove attach, command delivery, and result settlement share one exact connection identity, then carry SOCKS and HTTP bytes over a dedicated E2EE socket to the fenced execution-host revision and prove route close destroys the destination socket. The production desktop adapter now composes one exact host per environment pairing revision with the page executor, current renderer selector, route Session/WebContents registries, and one reference-counted route per canonical execution-host key. Negotiated same-client control reconnect retains exact authority, placements, grants, dispatcher dedupe, executor guests, and listener addresses; it fences tunnels immediately, blocks route admission, reattaches command delivery only after ready, and replays unsettled commands without repeating completed mutations. Terminal release, replacement, legacy disconnect, and reconnect-grace expiry make only the exact host generation's client placements non-cancellable retirement-pending while retaining capacity until exact cleanup; reconnect grace preserves them. Environment replacement and app shutdown still serialize transport closure before page cleanup and force-close every remaining route. The production placement preparation starts the exact desktop adapter and advertises host/tunnel capabilities only when the paired Electron client is eligible. Node stream-internal high-water bytes, strict cross-route scheduling, and physical cross-platform evidence remain uncovered. The two Docker remote-only SSH browser routing journeys now run in the dedicated Linux ssh-browser-network-route CI job on full runs and their mapped source/test changes; 2 baseline and 6 repeated cases passed with no skips/retries on 2026-09-06. The removed retry-arithmetic and attach-request inventory suites are not current coverage; retained lease and composition suites exercise admission retry, cleanup, inventory negotiation, and reconnect behavior. Test-value audit1293 removes src/main/browser/network/tunnels/browser-network-tunnel-client-memory-budget.test.ts (4 authored cases). Their isolated assertions no longer run; surviving tests are not claimed as equivalent coverage. Fresh execution against the candidate SHA is required. Audit1302: src/main/browser/client-pages/lifecycle/browser-client-page-unavailability.test.ts: Every route/guest lifecycle/currentness/navigation/renderer/automation authority is supplied by fake callbacks, then unavailability listener is invoked manually and private inventory/mock calls are checked. No guest destruction, renderer disconnect or actual reconciliation/close consumer. Lose generation fence/reconcile-once/missing-renderer-close branch alarms; no equivalent replacement. Reduced selectors require fresh validation; prior full-suite receipts do not validate removed or changed coverage. No equivalent replacement or physical-provider claim. Audit1318: src/shared/remote-runtime/requests/remote-runtime-subscription-request.test.ts: Retain actual local encrypted WebSocket subscription concurrency routing when host replies out of order, plus an exception thrown by a real ws consumer callback being turned into a subscription error. Server is a test-shaped