termination/probe cleanup requests with supplied process/socket boundaries, not real SSH launch flags or live forwarding. Remove only the retired launch-flags assertion; unrelated dated receipts and their executed commands remain unchanged. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1991: Remove the ordinary browser-host release/sub-cap and exact socket-close counter aliases. Retain the two actual admitted-device fairness and shared ask/browser/wait budget callbacks, which call server handlers with fake WebSockets and controlled pending RPCs. Preserve all3 unrelated dated receipts. No real browser placement or remote tunnel deployment is proved by this admission suite. Changed-source prior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, physical provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1983: Delete the mocked browser placement mutation and projection suites and both prospective selectors. Preserve3 unrelated receipts. Changed-source prior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1973: Remove stale production-registration and negotiated metadata aliases, compound refusal/cleanup aliases, isolated descriptor/route/memory/cleanup microcases. Retain exact negotiated command settlement, duplicate/conflict fencing, ready/replay ordering, superseded-connection cleanup, second-host refusal, ungranted target refusal, public connector redaction, revocation race and route replacement aliases within injected-port scope. Reconciliation and all3 unrelated dated receipts remain unchanged. Whole original changed dated receipts are retired, never narrowed or transferred. This metadata review claims no fresh execution, equivalent replacement, provider/PTY, live remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1918 narrows browser-host-command-ledger-capacity: intentionally loses injected per-page/global cache expiry-count ceilings and authority/command/result cloning inventory alarms. Retain valid commands/testFile and the oversized-wire pre-admission and delivery-failure outstanding-outcome assertions, backed by unchanged retained real-ledger callbacks with supplied browser delivery. These survivors are not equivalent replacement coverage for the deleted cache/cloning examples. Existing three exact unrelated tunnel/wire receipts retain their original scope; no fresh reduced-gate, real browser/provider, native/platform, soak or measured-budget result is added. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1900 reduces ws-outbound-backpressure-queue by seven authored definitions while retaining ten. Current source19 assertions still describe distinct direct/queued aggregate admission, cooperative drain ordering and aggregate claim release. Existing commands, testFiles and all three source19 assertions remain valid and unchanged. The affected2026-11-04 Linux44tests/4files/5.58s receipt is retired whole as historical evidence. The other three unchanged-selector browser receipts retain their exact original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh integrated, physical-device, mixed-host, soak or measured-budget result. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1709 retires changed-source assertion and execution scope without equivalent replacement coverage. Existing unchanged-selector receipts remain scoped to their original sources. Historical prior-source oracle: Audit1687 retires changed-source assertion and execution scope without equivalent replacement coverage. Existing unchanged-selector receipts remain scoped to their original sources. Historical prior-source oracle: Audit1686 retires changed-source assertion and execution scope without equivalent replacement coverage. Existing unchanged-selector receipts remain scoped to their original sources. Historical prior-source oracle: The retained unchanged-source receipts are the only current execution evidence; reduced-source assertions await validation. Historical oracle account (not a current claim for changed sources): The retained unchanged-source receipts are the only current execution evidence; reduced-source assertions await validation. Historical oracle account (not a current claim for changed sources): Attach two browser hosts and require unqualified selection to fail ambiguous while exact selection succeeds. Reject a second identity on one connection and a fifth identity for one paired device, release one exact lease, then admit its replacement without starving another device. Admit four hosts from one authenticated device and a host from a second, reject the first device's fifth host, and release only the first device's exact counters while the second remains live. Fill asks and hosts to their shared ceiling, retain a quarter of the total budget for ordinary waits, close both sockets, and prove every global, class, and device counter releases. Reject one initial host attach with the unchanged runtime_busy response, then require bounded client-specific jitter to attach when capacity returns; repeated rejection and explicit close must release every timer and subscription. Replace one same-device connection, require the old subscription and route to fence, then prove late old cleanup leaves the new generation live. Mint an exact execution-host grant, reject a different key, prove late old grant cleanup leaves its replacement, and invalidate every grant with lease replacement. Reject client-to-client, client-to-server, server-to-server, and server-to-client placement overwrite until exact retirement. Begin retirement once idempotently, reject client use and every replacement while pending, cancel the exact token to restore the same placement, and reject delayed cancellation or completion after a newer retirement begins. On explicit release, replacement, legacy disconnect, and reconnect-grace expiry, require only the exact host generation's client placements to become non-cancellable retirement-pending before lease settlement; preserve negotiated grace, other hosts, server placements, replacements, and capacity until exact completion. Complete only the exact pending token, retain capacity until completion, and require a reused client page ID to receive a higher global generation without retaining a tombstone. Require a client page through the exact runtime, epoch, host, and page tuple; reject every mismatch, released or replaced leases, retirement-pending pages, retired pages, server placements, invalid identities, and the 257th live placement. Admit 1024 opens in one monotonic 10-second window and reject the 1025th until the window expires. Fill 8 MiB across destination-to-client queues and separately across unsettled client-to-destination writes, release one exact retired stream, admit one replacement, and require the next byte claim to close the route without stale-callback or reentrant-close underflow. Across multiple routes, charge application copies, encrypted queue entries, and dynamic native socket bytes to one 32 MiB browser-host and 128 MiB process ceiling; reject zero-byte claim/socket-source floods, fence released leases, synchronously release JavaScript queue claims while retaining native claims through exact socket close, and yield a parked queue after four frames without reordering. Route nested responses by exact ID under reordering, reject unknown and duplicate IDs, cap pending requests and queued bytes, and tear down every concurrent waiter once on timeout or close. Drive one real paired attach, command, and result through one exact connection ID; reject missing send support and malformed or wrong-runtime acknowledgements while preserving old non-v1 attaches. Drop an authenticated transport, require the same listener to reject CONNECT before and during reconnect, attach the exact existing native v1 payload and capability pair to a strictly newer generation, ignore late old callbacks, and roll an exhausted stream-ID ledger only by replacing the generation. Require SSH descriptors to add an execution-host capability and exact grant, reject missing grants and stale provider authority before resolver or binary registration, pass exact domains to ssh2 and system-SSH SOCKS without local resolution, sanitize connector diagnostics, and close every stream and standalone route process once on timeout, synchronous failure, or rotation. Drive the accepted lease through real paired E2EE native SOCKS-to-HTTP and ephemeral Docker ssh2 remote-only DNS journeys, then exercise exact frame, credit, half-close, stale-stream, remote-DNS, unsupported-command, offline, and teardown assertions.",
