      "providers": ["remote-runtime", "ssh", "wsl"],
      "coveredPlatforms": [],
      "coveredProviders": [],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit1396 intentionally deletes or reduces the listed sources. No fresh execution result validates their reduced selectors. Historical coverage account: Deterministic main-process tests cover versioned delimiter-safe aggregate partition derivation, path-safe opaque names, durable collision metadata, oversized or corrupt metadata refusal, missing-sidecar Chromium-data refusal, bounded binding/live-page admission, immediate SOCKS5 setup with Chromium loopback bypass disabled, inherited-connection closure, exact proxy verification before allowlisting, concurrent setup coalescing, live proxy-retarget refusal, token-safe page replacement, existing browser-profile policy installation, active Orca-profile storage scoping, blank-only initial attachment, arbitrary initial-navigation denial, and fail-closed per-guest WebRTC policy through delayed or failed cleanup. The production client-page executor prepares, registers, and grants the exact route page. Archived standalone Electron experiments measured TCP routing and a forced persisted-worker wake using fixture-owned proxy setup; they did not exercise production route preparation and are no longer current test coverage. A separate capture proves the protected guest sends zero direct STUN packets. An archived standalone H3 experiment measured WebTransport and forced-QUIC controls through fixture-owned proxy setup and checked the shipped Direct Sockets feature list. It did not exercise Orca route preparation or admission and is no longer current product coverage. An archived DNS-prefetch experiment observed an accepted Electron 43 residual: prefetched hostnames resolved on the desktop outside the tunnel. It asserted the leak and was removed; current production-path TCP, persisted-worker, and DNS-prefetch egress coverage remains incomplete. Network-service restart and WSL provider journeys remain uncovered. Four Linux Docker SSH browser baseline scenarios passed: direct-host routing, unavailable-host local escape, forwarding refusal, and paired client-hosted reconnect. All four scenarios subsequently passed three repetitions each (12 passes, no skips or retries) in Linux CI run 34040309638, with unchanged assertions and timeouts. Audit1396: src/main/browser/network/egress/browser-route-webrtc-egress.electron.test.ts removed. Deletes entire one-registration native Electron baseline/protected UDP probe, including fixture shell and packet observer. No equivalent actual network egress proof is claimed; actual Orca policy owner reviewed separately. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed.",
      "motivatingLinks": [
        "https://linear.app/stably/issue/STA-4150/refactor-remote-browser-to-client-hosted-electron-webviews",
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/actions/runs/34039986047",
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/actions/runs/34040309638"
      ],
      "invariant": "A client-hosted partition is derived only in main from stable Orca-profile, browser-profile, authority-connection, and execution-host identities. Raw identities and individually linkable component hashes never enter its path-safe partition name. Durable binding metadata must match and precede Chromium partition data before reuse. One live partition never changes execution host or proxy endpoint. Fixed SOCKS5 setup starts immediately after Session creation, before policy installation can yield or a persisted worker is awakened; no partition enters the webview allowlist until browser policy is installed, inherited connections are closed, and resolveProxy returns exactly that one listener. Initial route-partition attachment is blank-only. Its exact WebContents is quarantined before applying non-proxied WebRTC denial and remains navigation- and popup-denied if policy application or cleanup fails. Distinct live partitions, retained logical page generations, durable bindings, and binding-file reads remain bounded. No UDP transport a route-partition page can reach — WebRTC, WebTransport, or forced QUIC — emits a datagram to the desktop, the Direct Sockets constructors stay absent from every guest so no page can kill its renderer, and the process never enables a DoH host-resolver mode.",
      "oracle": "No current automated execution oracle is claimed for this gate after Audit1396 retired changed-source receipts. Historical oracle account: Derive two delimiter-adversarial identities and require distinct full-digest path-safe partitions with no raw IDs or component hashes. Persist one binding, reload it, and reject replacement, malformed or oversized state, Chromium data without matching metadata, and the 513th binding. Prepare one partition and require setProxy with <-loopback> to be invoked immediately after getSession and before policy setup, then closeAllConnections and exact SOCKS5 resolveProxy while isAllowedPartition remains false; only then may it become live. Reject DIRECT, endpoint retargeting, and capacity overflow. Require quarantine before disable_non_proxied_udp and admission; under real Electron require the unprotected control to emit STUN and the protected guest to emit zero direct UDP packets.",
      "commands": [],
      "testFiles": [],
      "assertionRefs": [],
      "evidenceRuns": [],
      "runtimeBudget": {
