      "coverageNotes": "Audit1709 removes low-value test definitions and retires affected assertion or execution-receipt claims without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews bound retained behavior and injected/native/remote limits. Unchanged assertions and receipts keep their original scope; gates lacking current active evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1687 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1686 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1571 removes mock forwarding, capability/schema inventories, private predicates, supplied error/result replays, and filesystem-mocked persistence checks without equivalent replacement claims. Retained changed tests also exercise real local permission-file reread, registry proxy rollback/credential retirement, site display recovery, and pending sender/credential/document admission with injected Electron/UI producers. Retained network tests exercise owned stream credit/cleanup, generation and retirement fences, real loopback proxy/SOCKS bytes and file-backed binding state. SSH/WSL/paired runtime, native sessions, authority producers and storage clears remain injected; simulated relaunch uses filesystem mocks. The unchanged profile-retirement suite was statically reviewed and not rerun. No actual SSH/WSL runtime, native Chromium jar deletion, durable process restart, remote DNS or external site proof. Receipts selecting changed tests are retired and unaffected receipts remain unchanged. Historical scope before this audit: Fresh-build Playwright journeys run the same production store action against an isolated headed Electron server and a real headless orca serve host. They prove one immutable client placement owns one real retained guest on the viewing desktop, the server owns no duplicate guest, no screencast frame renders, browser.snapshot reaches the client guest, disabling the setting preserves that guest, and the next page uses the legacy server engine. Deterministic contracts cover omitted placement, missing capabilities, explicit server placement, exact renderer-store materialization after delayed publication, no fallback after client-create failure, folder workspaces, git worktrees, browserless hosts, native and WSL routes, exact connected SSH authority, reconnect command replay, lease replacement, imported-inventory cleanup, bounded retirement, and shared remote screencast fanout for multiple independent viewers. A published v1.4.184 package runs both skew directions: an old client omits placement against the current host, while a current client capability-downgrades against the old host; each creates one server guest, no client guest, and returns the exact snapshot marker. A current iOS Simulator client paired to that legacy packaged host visibly loads Example Domain through the preserved server-hosted surface. A Docker OpenSSH target proves container-only DNS and localhost through both ssh2 and system-SSH routes. Physical Windows/Linux Electron and physical mobile journeys remain gaps. The two Docker remote-only SSH browser routing journeys now run in the dedicated Linux ssh-browser-network-route CI job on full runs and their mapped source/test changes; 2 baseline and 6 repeated cases passed with no skips/retries on 2026-09-06. Schema-only placement/navigation acceptance is excluded from behavioral and mixed-version evidence. The mocked client-placement and immediate create-failure suites were removed, including parameter selection, delayed mocked materialization and no-fallback call ledgers. The remaining live journeys and contracts do not establish equivalent unit alarms. Earlier descriptions and executed results for those fixtures are historical.",
      "motivatingLinks": [
