        "Audit1623 removes low-value mocked daemon projections, scalar tables and duplicate terminal examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained terminal content preservation, process ownership refusal and recovery boundaries together with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded.",
        "A zero-width injected reset does not advance outputSequence, so the mobile renderer-snapshot stability oracle cannot detect a reset landing inside its serialize round-trip; the resulting tear is transient and self-heals on the next repaint (same exposure as the pre-existing device-attributes release emission).",
        "Bytes the dying command printed before its OSC 133;D (pre-boundary output into the still-active alternate screen, e.g. a final panic line) are discarded with the dead frame; only post-boundary shell output is preserved.",
        "Direct local provider and degraded (daemon-less) sessions get ownership proof and the renderer-side reset, but no in-stream normalization — pre-reveal prompt output is not preserved there.",
        "Visible Electron evidence is macOS-only.",
        "Direct SSH intentionally fails closed to current-main behavior because foreground proof would inherit transport timeout and enumeration ambiguity.",
        "WSL and Windows ConPTY process-membership behavior has no physical-host proof yet.",
        "Any stopped (Ctrl-Z) descendant in the shell's tree refutes the proof, so a suspended unrelated job silently disables recovery for that pane (fails closed to incumbent behavior).",
        "Attach is deliberately settle-free: a viewer connecting inside an in-flight proof (~100ms typical) receives the pre-reset snapshot as its first frame and self-heals when the in-stream reset arrives; snapshot RPC and remote serialize paths still inherit a bounded (750ms) settle wait while a proof is in flight.",
        "Paired headed and headless remote-runtime topologies have not yet run the full pointer-input oracle.",
