      "coverageNotes": "Current adopted test policy at native 6f2e: retire the sampled PTY/focus permutation callback and its assertion reference. This loses its ownership-uniqueness, rooted-focus, immutability and idempotence alarms over those combinations. Eleven direct component callbacks and the depth/store/E2E file selectors remain; no equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Previous metadata account (preserved verbatim): Audit1925 (sources1922/1923): Partial ownership suite loses fixed first-leaf/rootless/dangling-selection/idempotence/identity examples. Both existing active assertion aliases stay backed by exact retained active-leaf metadata pruning and idempotence across PTY/focus permutation callbacks; metadata collision and repeated-leaf challenges survive. No deleted fixed example is assigned replacement coverage. Preserve meaningful remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged dated receipts within their original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh gate execution evidence in this metadata packet. No equivalent replacement, physical watcher/PTY/provider, live SSH/remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Component unit tests cover persisted replay, rootless layouts, repeated leaf ids, metadata repair, and 12,000 nested duplicate leaves; retained store tests cover live/future pane-authority transfer and a prior detach destination. A two-launch macOS Electron journey covers a real surviving local-daemon PTY, persisted duplicate ownership, synchronized streaming output, and tab hide/reveal. Live Linux, Windows, SSH, WSL, and remote-runtime restore journeys remain gaps. The audit removed a mocked duplicate-replay wrapper suite. Its callback-count alarms are no longer covered here; retained ownership tests and historical Electron evidence do not establish equivalent wrapper coverage. The broad mirror fixture no longer supplies the duplicate-remote-PTY assertion referenced here. The terminal-mirroring fixture also lost its separate duplicate-PTY example and now retains host-finalized pending-binding composition only. Duplicate-PTY and topology fixture alarms are lost; remaining gate evidence is not replacement coverage. The test-value audit removed store duplicate/layout-only, hydration, legacy-leaf, and cross-tab layout-state examples. Their direct normalization, hydration authority, legacy compatibility, and cross-tab preservation alarms are lost. The retained store cases exercise live/future authority transfer and a prior detach destination; component and historical Electron evidence do not establish equivalent replacement coverage.",
      "motivatingLinks": [
