      ],
      "invariant": "Within one terminal tab, each PTY has at most one layout leaf, pane manager surface, and xterm renderer owner. Restore and remote mirroring must normalize duplicate ownership before replay while retaining active-leaf focus, scrollback, pane authority, agent metadata, and distinct sibling PTYs.",
      "oracle": "Current adopted test policy at native 6f2e: retire the sampled PTY/focus permutation callback and its assertion reference. This loses its ownership-uniqueness, rooted-focus, immutability and idempotence alarms over those combinations. Eleven direct component callbacks and the depth/store/E2E file selectors remain; no equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Previous metadata account (preserved verbatim): Audit1925 (sources1922/1923): Partial ownership suite loses fixed first-leaf/rootless/dangling-selection/idempotence/identity examples. Both existing active assertion aliases stay backed by exact retained active-leaf metadata pruning and idempotence across PTY/focus permutation callbacks; metadata collision and repeated-leaf challenges survive. No deleted fixed example is assigned replacement coverage. Preserve meaningful remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged dated receipts within their original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh gate execution evidence in this metadata packet. No equivalent replacement, physical watcher/PTY/provider, live SSH/remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Launch Orca with a real daemon PTY running a synchronized full-screen stream, close the desktop client without killing the daemon process, seed the persisted tab layout with two leaves bound to that PTY, and relaunch. Hide the restored tab behind a sibling and reveal it, then require the stream to remain visible with exactly one manager pane, one xterm DOM node, one root leaf, one PTY binding, and one unique PTY. Component contracts cover persisted replay, rootless and repeated-leaf layouts, metadata repair, and deeply nested input. Retained store contracts cover live/future authority transfer onto a retained leaf and preservation of a prior detach destination.",
