        "Audit1925 (sources1922/1923): Partial ownership suite loses fixed first-leaf/rootless/dangling-selection/idempotence/identity examples. Both existing active assertion aliases stay backed by exact retained active-leaf metadata pruning and idempotence across PTY/focus permutation callbacks; metadata collision and repeated-leaf challenges survive. No deleted fixed example is assigned replacement coverage. Preserve meaningful remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged dated receipts within their original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh gate execution evidence in this metadata packet. No equivalent replacement, physical watcher/PTY/provider, live SSH/remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Exact retired authored alarms: 'keeps the first layout leaf when focus belongs to another PTY'; 'repairs rootless duplicate ownership in one idempotent pass'; 'repairs dangling rooted selection during direct ownership normalization'; 'preserves PTY ownership while collapsing repeated live leaf ids'; 'preserves valid split layouts by identity'."
