    {
      "id": "terminal-session.split-activation-ordering",
      "title": "Terminal splits activate before inherited-CWD lookup settles",
      "maturity": "experimental",
      "protection": "none",
      "owner": "terminal-renderer-lifecycle",
      "layer": "renderer-unit-and-local-transport",
      "surfaces": [
        "terminal pane split",
        "inherited working directory",
        "pre-connect terminal input",
        "split close cleanup",
        "pre-bind pane detach"
      ],
      "platforms": ["macos", "linux", "windows"],
      "providers": ["local", "local-daemon", "ssh", "wsl", "remote-runtime"],
      "coveredPlatforms": [],
      "coveredProviders": [],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1925 (sources1922/1923): Delete the complete mocked inherited-CWD split orchestration suite: local/server delegation, async CWD forwarding, stale-manager refusal, nested lookup reuse and layout-owner call-argument/no-call alarms are lost; no real pane/PTY/remote split ran. The partial CWD resolver loses supplied OSC7/cache/remote-ID/deferred-field and stale-cleanup examples, so its entire three-title deferred-fence assertion object retires. Its actual timer admission/fallback callbacks remain selected. Handoff loses simple promise/input projection, direct clear and direct discard-as-restored-PTY samples; retire only that projection title while retaining stale-owner handoff, released-owner/input limits, eviction and expiry mappings. Preserve meaningful remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged dated receipts within their original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh gate execution evidence in this metadata packet. No equivalent replacement, physical watcher/PTY/provider, live SSH/remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1903 removes whole mocked detach, supplied geometry and/or close-request suites selected by this gate. Their pending-CWD/PTY-binding argument/order, fabricated hit-test and close bookkeeping alarms are intentionally lost without replacement. Valid remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged-selector execution receipts retain their original scope. Reduced unit selections have no fresh broad gate, real PTY/provider, rendered focus, or measured-budget validation. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1342 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Deterministic renderer contracts hold CWD resolution behind an explicit promise, require the new pane to be created synchronously, and prove that close cancels the pending connection. A module-level stable-pane-key handoff preserves the exact CWD promise and bounded pre-connect input across whole-tab remounts, including a tab rehome between worktree buckets; stale owners are fenced, concrete PTY bind and definitive spawn failure clear the record, and explicit pane close discards it. Detach contracts reject cwd-pending and cwd-resolved deferred splits before PTY bind without mutation, carry resolved cwd for other unbound panes, and preserve persisted or live PTY handoff. Local IPC transport contracts exercise the real bounded pre-connect buffer and one live input FIFO across seeded and newly typed ordinary, acknowledged, and immediate writes, concurrent flushes, in-flight teardown, late spawn success or failure, attach failure, failed spawn, same-id reuse, stale-spawn retirement ownership, destroy, and mutable recovery metadata. The handoff registry is capped at 64 records for 15 seconds and shares the existing 1,024-entry/conservative UTF-16 input ceilings. A mocked direct-SSH authority-rotation contract proves a rejected stale spawn releases its deferred-CWD fence. The schema-v2 headful Electron benchmark records exact revision identity and attributes CWD request/settlement, PTY spawn request/result, bind, fixture unlock request/IPC write, fixture readiness, input, and first echo across 3 warmups and 20 measured cold-CWD cycles, requiring a distinct child PTY and observed child pty:exit before the next cycle. Remote-runtime coverage proves delegation remains host-owned; its host-delegated split path does not consume the local pre-connect input options, so remote-runtime input-remount replay and physical local-daemon, SSH, WSL, Linux, Windows, and folder-workspace latency journeys remain gaps. The test-value audit retires the benchmark artifact and report unit suites. Their direct JSON write/readback, unwritable-path, path-redaction/string-bound, synthetic phase-attribution, revision/percentile and missing-unlock-event alarms are lost. The real benchmark and its capture/report/writer helpers remain; they do not provide equivalent isolated helper validation. Historical executed commands, counts and results remain historical. Audit1342: src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-split-cwd-resolution.test.ts reduced. Happy inherited-cwd wait and transport-option forwarding sample loses its individual alarm. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed.",
      "motivatingLinks": ["https://github.com/stablyai/orca/commit/572ed1a8882"],
      "invariant": "A terminal split creates and activates its renderer pane before an inherited-CWD lookup settles, starts its PTY only after the resolved directory is available, and cannot be externally detached while that deferred spawn remains unbound. A whole-tab remount or worktree rehome preserves the same stable pane's CWD promise and admitted local pre-connect bytes in order until a successor binds or the intent is definitively abandoned; stale owners cannot append or clear the successor's record. Other unbound panes preserve resolved cwd as startupCwd when detached. Bounded pre-connect input and later live local input share byte order, and teardown settles acknowledged writes without creating or rebinding a stale PTY. A disconnected or detached pending connect cannot bind its late fresh spawn, report its late failure through current callbacks, or ID-retire a newer same-ID owner; rejecting a stale direct-SSH spawn also releases the matching deferred-CWD fence. Natural exit cannot deliver queued work into a reused PTY id. Bound and remote-runtime splits remain owned by their execution host.",
      "oracle": "Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1925 (sources1922/1923): Delete the complete mocked inherited-CWD split orchestration suite: local/server delegation, async CWD forwarding, stale-manager refusal, nested lookup reuse and layout-owner call-argument/no-call alarms are lost; no real pane/PTY/remote split ran. The partial CWD resolver loses supplied OSC7/cache/remote-ID/deferred-field and stale-cleanup examples, so its entire three-title deferred-fence assertion object retires. Its actual timer admission/fallback callbacks remain selected. Handoff loses simple promise/input projection, direct clear and direct discard-as-restored-PTY samples; retire only that projection title while retaining stale-owner handoff, released-owner/input limits, eviction and expiry mappings. Preserve meaningful remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged dated receipts within their original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh gate execution evidence in this metadata packet. No equivalent replacement, physical watcher/PTY/provider, live SSH/remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1903 removes whole mocked detach, supplied geometry and/or close-request suites selected by this gate. Their pending-CWD/PTY-binding argument/order, fabricated hit-test and close bookkeeping alarms are intentionally lost without replacement. Valid remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged-selector execution receipts retain their original scope. Reduced unit selections have no fresh broad gate, real PTY/provider, rendered focus, or measured-budget validation. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): The retained unchanged-source receipts are the only current execution evidence; reduced-source assertions await validation. Historical oracle account (not a current claim for changed sources): Hold CWD resolution behind a controllable promise, invoke the production split path, and require manager.splitPane plus split telemetry before resolving it. Before PTY bind, require both cwd-pending and cwd-resolved deferred detach attempts to return null without layout, pane, tab, ownership, or focus mutation; separately require resolved cwd on an allowed unbound detach and unchanged persisted/live PTY adoption. Exercise the stable-pane handoff registry through repeated remounts and a worktree rehome, requiring the identical CWD promise, ordered ordinary/acknowledged/immediate seed replay, stale-owner fencing, 64-record/15-second bounds, and discard on bind, failure, or explicit close. Rotate a mocked direct-SSH authority while its delayed spawn is in flight, reject and disconnect the stale PTY claim, then require exactly one deferred-CWD cleanup when the delayed connect settles. At the local IPC PTY boundary, require zero connect calls while pending, the resolved CWD in spawn and local recovery metadata, one shared FIFO across seeded/new pre-connect and live ordinary/acknowledged/immediate input, prompt predecessor acknowledged-promise settlement on teardown, retirement of an unowned late fresh spawn, preservation of a newer same-ID owner, and zero stale delivery after failure, close, destroy, detach, natural exit, or same-id reuse. Capture callback exceptions must not change admission results. In visible Electron, press the real split shortcut for 3 warmup cycles, then after a cold inherited-CWD interval for each of 20 measured cycles, require an exact clean revision identity, complete focus/CWD/spawn/bind/fixture/input/echo attribution, distinct child PTYs, pane count, and child exits for every cycle; a timed-out, missing-event, or cleanup-aborted run must publish no headline latency and fail.",
      "commands": [],
      "testFiles": [],
      "assertionRefs": [],
      "evidenceRuns": [],
      "evidenceProcedure": "Run the benchmark spec in a visible macOS Electron project from a clean primary worktree, complete 3 warmups followed by 20 measured cold-CWD cycles, require zero missing events and successful cleanup, save the schema-v2 JSON report, and record its SHA-256 plus embedded revision identity. The four older records are schema-v1 historical audit records whose labels do not verify the checkout or include phase attribution; the clean schema-v2 record is the current candidate evidence. A paired baseline/final rerun with one revision-verifying harness remains required before promotion or a readiness comparison claim.",
      "runtimeBudget": {
        "p95Seconds": 240,
        "scope": "Historical pre-audit selector budget; changed selectors have no new runtime measurement. Unchanged receipts remain scoped to their own commands."
      },
      "flakeHistory": {
        "status": "not-started",
        "evidence": "Changed selectors have no new soak result after Audit1342; any retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their own commands. Historical account: The focused promise-barrier, remount-handoff, benchmark-artifact, and schema-v2 attribution suite passes locally in 99 tests; the clean visible benchmark passes 3/3 warmups and 20/20 measured cycles with zero missing events. Its first attempt hit a transient warmup cleanup-dialog click timeout, then the exact command passed on retry without a launch, profile, or port workaround. Routed CI and soak history have not started. Historical benchmark labels do not verify the product checkout or embed revision identity."
      },
      "redGreenEvidence": {
        "status": "missing",
        "evidence": "Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Changed test bytes/selectors have no fresh red/green validation. Unrelated retained-source historical evidence keeps its original scope. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1342 changed referenced test sources; no new red/green validation of the reduced set. Historical account: Before the production seam landed, the split assertion failed with zero manager calls while CWD was pending, and the transport assertion rejected the first pre-connect input. Before the detach fence, a deferred split could be removed after CWD resolved but before PTY bind, dropping its pre-connect input. Before the single-flight hardening, the concurrent-flush oracle delivered ordinary input before the earlier acknowledged write and clear left the in-flight promise pending. Before stale-spawn ownership fencing, the combined deferred-connect and newer same-ID attach fixture called kill on the current PTY. An intentional one-line revert of deferred-CWD cleanup in the stale direct-SSH claim branch failed its focused callback assertion with zero calls instead of one; restoring it passed the prior focused tests. The remount-handoff, transport, artifact-write, and schema-v2 attribution regressions are green in the 99-test twelve-path run, but isolated intentional-revert evidence for each cleanup branch remains outstanding."
      },
      "performanceBudget": {
        "required": true,
        "evidence": "Historical account for the pre-audit test set; removed work-count alarms and changed selectors have no fresh measurement. Pane creation and focus add no timer, polling, provider inventory, or subprocess work. CWD resolution remains one existing bounded request off the visible activation path, and detach admission adds only bounded map and record lookups. The remount handoff adds one module-level map lookup per pane lifecycle, a 64-record cap, and a 15-second expiry; it retains no unbounded payload. Pre-connect input, including an in-flight acknowledged write and remount seed replay, is capped at 1,024 entries and a conservative UTF-16 ceiling derived from the existing terminal-input byte limit, drains through one worker in order, and clears on teardown or failed connect. The historical schema-v1 same-mode pair recorded shortcut-to-focus p50/p95/max changing from 65.7/88.7/102.6 ms to 12.8/14.4/16.5 ms; those labels do not embed revision identity, so the comparison is directional evidence only. The clean schema-v2 candidate attributes focus at 12.0/13.6/14.7 ms while CWD lookup takes 40/97/103 ms and spawn request-to-result takes 48/120/122 ms, demonstrating that provider/process startup follows activation rather than blocking it. In that clean run, shortcut-to-bind is 113.5/161.3/162.7 ms, fixture IPC-write-to-ready is 35.1/87.4/141.8 ms, and input-to-echo is 1.3/3.5/3.9 ms; these readiness phases are diagnostic, one-host descriptive measurements, and no clean schema-v2 baseline exists to support a readiness improvement or regression claim. The n=20 empirical p95 values are descriptive, are not a distribution guarantee, and are not CI-enforced."
      },
      "promotionCriteria": [
        "Record complete red/green evidence for close, remount/rehome handoff, mixed-input ordering, metadata, and failure cleanup.",
        "Collect 100 consecutive focused CI passes or 14 days without an unexplained flake.",
        "Run the committed real-shortcut Electron benchmark in routed CI or soak before enforcing a latency budget.",
        "Collect physical local-daemon, SSH or WSL plus Linux, Windows, and folder-workspace evidence before claiming provider-complete coverage."
      ],
      "knownGaps": [
        "Audit2133 current-parent preparation (988 authored removals; independently reviewed2099/2107/2115/2116 decisions; upstream clear-buffer and recovery-image regressions retained): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-main-probe.ts: dedicated zero-case helper retirement; no authored test credit. tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-phases.ts: dedicated zero-case helper retirement; no authored test credit. tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts: records attributed CWD, spawn, bind, fixture-ready, input, and echo phases. tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-artifact.ts: dedicated zero-case helper retirement; no authored test credit. tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-report.ts: dedicated zero-case helper retirement; no authored test credit. Current changed source bytes, wrapper registrations and reduced selectors have no fresh execution or red/green credit. Unrelated surviving receipt objects keep their original narrow scope; current literal graph reachability does not establish historical import closure or equivalent replacement coverage. Current conservative command/import graph reaches tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-main-probe.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-phases.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-artifact.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-report.ts. Unresolved local/computed edges remain explicit debt. Complete dated receipts with direct selectors or current literal graph reaching tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-phases.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-main-probe.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-artifact.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-report.ts are retired below as historical raw objects; their counts do not validate reduced commands. Retired active assertionRefs (raw original objects retained as historical only): {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-main-probe.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"attributes CWD and PTY spawn request/settlement events to the source and child PTYs\",\n            \"captures the fixture unlock carriage return on both ordinary and acknowledged IPC channels\",\n            \"restores the intercepted IPC handlers and listener when the probe is disposed\"\n          ]\n        }\n{\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-phases.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"merges main-process events by operation and PTY identity without cross-cycle attribution\",\n            \"requires every activation, fixture, input, echo, pane, PTY, and cleanup observation for success\",\n            \"reports each attributed phase distribution with non-negative cross-clock durations\"\n          ]\n        }\n{\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"requires a visible BrowserWindow and visible document before sampling\",\n            \"records schema-v2 revision identity plus attributed CWD, spawn, bind, fixture-ready, input, and echo phases\",\n            \"records 3 warmups, then 20 measured real-shortcut cycles after cold inherited-CWD intervals\",\n            \"requires every split to focus, bind a PTY distinct from its source, and echo immediate input\",\n            \"observes each closed child PTY exit before starting the next cycle\",\n            \"publishes headline latency only for a fully successful 3-warmup/20-measured run\"\n          ]\n        } All 5 affected passing receipts are retired, so protection becomes none pending a fresh run. Original current selectors and assertion inventory, preserved as historical data only: {\"commands\":[\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/layout/split/resolve-split-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/startup/pty-connection-split-cwd-resolution.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/input/pty-preconnect-input-buffer.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/ipc/pty-transport-input-write.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/layout/split/deferred-split-pane-handoff.test.ts tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-main-probe.ts tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-phases.ts --reporter=dot\",\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/layout/split/resolve-split-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/startup/pty-connection-split-cwd-resolution.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/input/pty-preconnect-input-buffer.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/ipc/pty-transport-input-write.test.ts --reporter=dot\",\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/layout/split/resolve-split-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/startup/pty-connection-split-cwd-resolution.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/input/pty-preconnect-input-buffer.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/ipc/pty-transport-input-write.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/layout/split/deferred-split-pane-handoff.test.ts --reporter=dot\",\"ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_BENCH=1 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_LABEL=baseline-df14d1a2983d8339e788d0e521f1c4affd9c6d5f-headful-run1 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_OUTPUT=/private/tmp/orca-terminal-split-activation-baseline-df14d1a2983d8339e788d0e521f1c4affd9c6d5f-headful-run1.json pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headful --workers=1\",\"ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_BENCH=1 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_LABEL=candidate-d453ffcdb704764daced1b2917fddee7224389f0-headful-run2 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_OUTPUT=/private/tmp/orca-terminal-split-activation-candidate-d453ffcdb704764daced1b2917fddee7224389f0-headful-run2.json pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headful --workers=1\",\"ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_BENCH=1 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_LABEL=candidate-962faacec8c-headful-current ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_OUTPUT=/private/tmp/orca-terminal-split-activation-962faacec8c-headful.json pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headful --workers=1\",\"ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_BENCH=1 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_LABEL=candidate-962faacec8c-headful-run2 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_OUTPUT=/private/tmp/orca-terminal-split-activation-962faacec8c-headful-run2.json pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headful --workers=1\",\"ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_BENCH=1 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_LABEL=candidate-073e6c7b0eb-headful-clean ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_OUTPUT=/private/tmp/orca-terminal-split-activation-073e6c7b0eb-headful-clean.json pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headful --workers=1\"],\"testFiles\":[\"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/layout/split/resolve-split-cwd.test.ts\",\"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/startup/pty-connection-split-cwd-resolution.test.ts\",\"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/input/pty-preconnect-input-buffer.test.ts\",\"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/ipc/pty-transport-input-write.test.ts\",\"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/layout/split/deferred-split-pane-handoff.test.ts\",\"tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-main-probe.ts\",\"tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-phases.ts\",\"tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts\"],\"assertionRefs\":[{\"file\":\"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/input/pty-preconnect-input-buffer.test.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"concurrent flush calls share one worker and preserve mixed input order\",\"clear settles an in-flight acknowledged write before its late resolve or reject\",\"in-flight acknowledged input remains charged to entry and code-unit caps\"]},{\"file\":\"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/ipc/pty-transport-input-write.test.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"ordinary, acknowledged, and immediate pre-connect input flushes in byte order\",\"pending acknowledged input settles on connect, destroy, and spawn failure\",\"disconnect, destroy, and natural exit cancel an in-flight acknowledged write without blocking connect\",\"live acknowledged input blocks later ordinary and immediate writes at its invocation position\",\"the preconnect-to-live transition preserves the same input FIFO\",\"disconnect and detach retire a late fresh spawn and suppress late failures before they reach current callbacks\",\"natural exit fences queued ordinary and acknowledged chunks across same-id reuse\",\"buffered exit and attach failure clear retained input\",\"ordinary and acknowledged write failures drop later input without leaving promises pending\",\"entry and code-unit ceilings bound pre-connect input retention\",\"local recovery metadata observes the resolved split CWD\",\"a stale fresh-spawn completion cannot retire a newer same-ID owner\"]},{\"file\":\"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/layout/split/deferred-split-pane-handoff.test.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"keeps input across repeated remounts and fences stale owners\",\"releases an unmounted owner without dropping its pending handoff\",\"retains input within the shared preconnect entry and code-unit caps\",\"evicts the oldest handoff when the record cap is reached\",\"expires an abandoned handoff after the bounded remount window\"]},{\"file\":\"tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-main-probe.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"attributes CWD and PTY spawn request/settlement events to the source and child PTYs\",\"captures the fixture unlock carriage return on both ordinary and acknowledged IPC channels\",\"restores the intercepted IPC handlers and listener when the probe is disposed\"]},{\"file\":\"tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-phases.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"merges main-process events by operation and PTY identity without cross-cycle attribution\",\"requires every activation, fixture, input, echo, pane, PTY, and cleanup observation for success\",\"reports each attributed phase distribution with non-negative cross-clock durations\"]},{\"file\":\"tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"requires a visible BrowserWindow and visible document before sampling\",\"records schema-v2 revision identity plus attributed CWD, spawn, bind, fixture-ready, input, and echo phases\",\"records 3 warmups, then 20 measured real-shortcut cycles after cold inherited-CWD intervals\",\"requires every split to focus, bind a PTY distinct from its source, and echo immediate input\",\"observes each closed child PTY exit before starting the next cycle\",\"publishes headline latency only for a fully successful 3-warmup/20-measured run\"]}],\"coveredPlatforms\":[\"macos\"],\"coveredProviders\":[\"local\",\"remote-runtime\"]}. No claim that retained test bodies disappeared. Historical retired receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-30\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"command\": \"ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_BENCH=1 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_LABEL=baseline-df14d1a2983d8339e788d0e521f1c4affd9c6d5f-headful-run1 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_OUTPUT=/private/tmp/orca-terminal-split-activation-baseline-df14d1a2983d8339e788d0e521f1c4affd9c6d5f-headful-run1.json pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headful --workers=1\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 72,\n          \"summary\": \"At baseline df14d1a2983d8339e788d0e521f1c4affd9c6d5f, the visible BrowserWindow and document completed 3/3 warmups followed by 20/20 measured cold-CWD cycles with every event present, distinct child PTYs, and observed child exits. Shortcut-to-focus p50/p95/max was 65.7/88.7/102.6 ms, PTY bind was 122.8/154.0/159.7 ms, and first echo was 203.8/264.2/332.7 ms. Artifact SHA-256: 6d860cd0cd210f55f2349a197318248af488042117b20c08b6831160950c3277.\"\n        } Historical retired receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-30\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"command\": \"ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_BENCH=1 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_LABEL=candidate-d453ffcdb704764daced1b2917fddee7224389f0-headful-run2 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_OUTPUT=/private/tmp/orca-terminal-split-activation-candidate-d453ffcdb704764daced1b2917fddee7224389f0-headful-run2.json pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headful --workers=1\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 72,\n          \"summary\": \"At candidate d453ffcdb704764daced1b2917fddee7224389f0, the visible BrowserWindow and document completed 3/3 warmups followed by 20/20 measured cold-CWD cycles with every event present, distinct child PTYs, and observed child exits. Shortcut-to-focus p50/p95/max was 12.8/14.4/16.5 ms, PTY bind was 177.0/316.1/333.3 ms, and first echo was 268.6/627.4/710.7 ms. Artifact SHA-256: 9aef7fa842c732eb74f0066a77b2a0336e8f956a06ca61387f9999d6e76213cc.\"\n        } Historical retired receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-31\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"command\": \"ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_BENCH=1 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_LABEL=candidate-962faacec8c-headful-current ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_OUTPUT=/private/tmp/orca-terminal-split-activation-962faacec8c-headful.json pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headful --workers=1\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 72,\n          \"summary\": \"At exact HEAD 962faacec8c, the visible BrowserWindow and document completed 3/3 warmups followed by 20/20 measured cold-CWD cycles with every event present, distinct child PTYs, and observed child exits. Shortcut-to-focus p50/p95/max was 12.6/13.7/13.7 ms, PTY bind was 140.5/399.1/464.1 ms, and first echo was 192.0/519.3/2343.1 ms. Artifact SHA-256: 875e9d37dc711472a81438e4bbdbc8cbc7aada8c961d14195c024d8da350b9e2.\"\n        } Historical retired receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-31\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"command\": \"ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_BENCH=1 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_LABEL=candidate-962faacec8c-headful-run2 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_OUTPUT=/private/tmp/orca-terminal-split-activation-962faacec8c-headful-run2.json pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headful --workers=1\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 72,\n          \"summary\": \"At exact HEAD 962faacec8c, the visible BrowserWindow and document completed 3/3 warmups followed by 20/20 measured cold-CWD cycles with every event present, distinct child PTYs, and observed child exits. Shortcut-to-focus p50/p95/max was 12.8/14.0/14.3 ms, PTY bind was 236.5/654.0/687.3 ms, and first echo was 566.8/1191.5/1219.7 ms. Artifact SHA-256: 4f66b93e5c936ade05f880010f4ec027385d5c89893430169af91c7fdfbe1d06.\"\n        } Historical retired receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-31\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"command\": \"ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_BENCH=1 ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_LABEL=candidate-073e6c7b0eb-headful-clean ORCA_TERMINAL_SPLIT_LATENCY_OUTPUT=/private/tmp/orca-terminal-split-activation-073e6c7b0eb-headful-clean.json pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headful --workers=1\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 87.6,\n          \"summary\": \"At exact clean HEAD 073e6c7b0eb1c0ccbb115db1528b641901997c73, the schema-v2 artifact records dirty=false, a visible BrowserWindow/document, and 3/3 warmups plus 20/20 measured cycles with every missing-event counter at zero, distinct child PTYs, and observed child exits. Measured focus p50/p95/max was 12.0/13.6/14.7 ms; attributed CWD lookup was 40/97/103 ms, CWD-settle to spawn request 1/4/4 ms, spawn request to result 48/120/122 ms, and spawn result to bind 2.1/2.5/2.5 ms. Fixture unlock request to IPC write was 0.5/0.8/0.9 ms, IPC write to fixture-ready parse was 35.1/87.4/141.8 ms, and input to first echo was 1.3/3.5/3.9 ms. Total shortcut-to-bind was 113.5/161.3/162.7 ms and shortcut-to-first-echo was 158.5/240.7/291.2 ms. Artifact SHA-256: 1e7ff9e658b717056273d64ecdf662cc6b5776bb6dae1827ed213b7647e4a5fb.\"\n        }",
        "The clean schema-v2 candidate run and the historical schema-v1 comparison records ran on one Apple-silicon macOS host with a synthetic POSIX echo shell and a git-backed workspace; their n=20 empirical p95 values are descriptive and not CI-enforced.",
        "No physical local-daemon, SSH, WSL, Linux, Windows, or folder-workspace latency journey has run; the synthetic fixture is currently skipped on Windows because it requires a POSIX shell.",
        "Remote-runtime split creation remains host-delegated and its transport does not consume the local pre-connect seed/capture options; CWD handoff is covered, but remote-runtime pre-connect input replay has no implementation or evidence.",
        "The four stored schema-v1 artifacts predate the final harness attribution/reporting and do not embed revision identity; the clean schema-v2 candidate artifact is revision-verified, but both product revisions still need a paired schema-v2 rerun with one committed harness before promotion.",
        "No forced-failure visible benchmark artifact has been recorded. The audit removed the focused artifact-write and missing-event report contracts, so neither their isolated failure handling nor full-run failure-report serialization has current verification here.",
        "No clean schema-v2 baseline phase artifact exists, so the attributed CWD, spawn, fixture-ready, bind, and echo timings diagnose where time is spent but do not establish a shell-readiness improvement or regression.",
        "The audit removed a fake-DOM split/close suite. Its mocked focus, scroll, fit and WebGL alarms lose dedicated checks; surviving tests and historical runs do not establish equivalent coverage. Historical commands retain executed roots, while currentCommand maps surviving roots without claiming a new run.",
        "The test-value audit retires the benchmark artifact and report unit suites. Their direct JSON write/readback, unwritable-path, path-redaction/string-bound, synthetic phase-attribution, revision/percentile and missing-unlock-event alarms are lost. The real benchmark and its capture/report/writer helpers remain; they do not provide equivalent isolated helper validation. Historical executed commands, counts and results remain historical.",
        "Audit1342: src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-split-cwd-resolution.test.ts reduced. Happy inherited-cwd wait and transport-option forwarding sample loses its individual alarm. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit1342 retires this complete dated receipt because a source in its selector was deleted or reduced. It does not validate the reduced selector. Original receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-30\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-pane-split-with-inherited-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/lib/pane-manager/pane-split-close.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/resolve-split-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-split-cwd-resolution.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-pane-tab-detach.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-preconnect-input-buffer.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport-input-write.test.ts --reporter=dot\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-pane-split-with-inherited-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/resolve-split-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-split-cwd-resolution.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-pane-tab-detach.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-preconnect-input-buffer.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport-input-write.test.ts --reporter=dot\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 56.59,\n          \"summary\": \"Seven focused files and 78 tests passed. Vitest reported 49.92 seconds and the measured wall time was 56.59 seconds; coverage includes split creation and focus ordering, nested CWD lineage, promise-identity and SSH authority-rotation cleanup fencing, full pre-bind detach fencing, resolved-CWD detach handoff, close-cancellation, single-FIFO ordering, late-spawn retirement and error suppression, preservation of a newer same-ID owner, generation fencing, in-flight settlement across explicit teardown and natural exit, attach cleanup, bounded retention, and existing input-write contracts.\"\n        }",
        "Audit1342 retires this complete dated receipt because a source in its selector was deleted or reduced. It does not validate the reduced selector. Original receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-31\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-pane-split-with-inherited-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/lib/pane-manager/pane-split-close.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/resolve-split-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-split-cwd-resolution.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-pane-tab-detach.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-preconnect-input-buffer.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport-input-write.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/deferred-split-pane-handoff.test.ts tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-artifact.unit.test.ts --reporter=dot\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-pane-split-with-inherited-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/resolve-split-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-split-cwd-resolution.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-pane-tab-detach.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-preconnect-input-buffer.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport-input-write.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/deferred-split-pane-handoff.test.ts --reporter=dot\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 44.43,\n          \"summary\": \"Nine focused files and 96 tests passed. Vitest reported 37.78 seconds and measured wall time was 44.43 seconds; the run adds stable-pane CWD/input handoff, repeated-remount stale-owner fencing, bounded 64-record/15-second retention, seeded-input caps, ordered ordinary/acknowledged/immediate replay, predecessor acknowledged-promise settlement, capture-callback failure containment, and benchmark-artifact write-failure coverage to the existing split, detach, CWD, and local transport contracts.\"\n        }",
        "Audit1342 retires this complete dated receipt because a source in its selector was deleted or reduced. It does not validate the reduced selector. Original receipt verbatim:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-31\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-pane-split-with-inherited-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/lib/pane-manager/pane-split-close.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/resolve-split-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-split-cwd-resolution.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-pane-tab-detach.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-preconnect-input-buffer.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport-input-write.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/deferred-split-pane-handoff.test.ts tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-artifact.unit.test.ts tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-main-probe.ts tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-phases.ts tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-report.unit.test.ts --reporter=dot\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-pane-split-with-inherited-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/resolve-split-cwd.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-split-cwd-resolution.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-pane-tab-detach.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-preconnect-input-buffer.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport-input-write.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/deferred-split-pane-handoff.test.ts tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-main-probe.ts tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-phases.ts --reporter=dot\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 4.14,\n          \"summary\": \"The updated twelve-path focused command passed 99 tests (10 runnable test files plus 2 benchmark support modules), including schema-v2 main-process phase attribution, report revision identity, fixture IPC-write validation, stable-pane handoff, ordered pre-connect/live input, cleanup, detach, failure, and same-ID ownership contracts.\"\n        }",
        "Audit1342 historical platform/provider scope before source changes: {\"coveredPlatforms\":[\"macos\"],\"coveredProviders\":[\"local\",\"remote-runtime\"]}. Remaining provider scope applies only to unchanged-source receipts.",
        "Audit1342 historical assertion inventory for deleted/reduced sources; not current validated assertions:\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-split-cwd-resolution.test.ts\",\n    \"assertions\": [\n      \"starts no PTY connection before inherited CWD resolves\",\n      \"applies the resolved directory to transport options\",\n      \"disposing the split before resolution cancels the pending spawn\",\n      \"invokes deferred-CWD cleanup exactly once after an authority-rotated direct-SSH spawn is disconnected and its delayed connect settles\"\n    ]\n  }\n]",
        "Audit1903 removes whole mocked detach, supplied geometry and/or close-request suites selected by this gate. Their pending-CWD/PTY-binding argument/order, fabricated hit-test and close bookkeeping alarms are intentionally lost without replacement. Valid remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged-selector execution receipts retain their original scope. Reduced unit selections have no fresh broad gate, real PTY/provider, rendered focus, or measured-budget validation. Exact lost direct alarms: 'moves chat mode only with its owning leaf %s'; 'creates a new terminal tab with the detached leaf layout and PTY id'; 'preserves the moved PTY shell override when the source uses %s'; 'syncs PTY ownership when the primary source pane is detached'; 'names the new tab as the client that already drew it did'; 'reports a refused move as a toast only for %s'; 'moves the detached tab into the requested group slot'; 'uses the live transport PTY id when the snapshot has not persisted it yet'; 'rejects a deferred split while inherited cwd is pending'; 'rejects a pending cwd even when the deferred marker is absent'; 'still rejects a deferred split after cwd resolves but before PTY bind'; 'carries resolved cwd when detaching an unbound non-deferred pane'; 'finds a same-worktree tab strip under overlay elements'; 'resolves the insertion slot from the hovered tab side'; 'ignores strips from another worktree'.",
        "Audit1903 historical retired assertion inventory; these are not current validated assertions. Complete original raw assertion objects follow verbatim:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/layout/detach/terminal-pane-tab-detach.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"rejects a deferred split while inherited CWD is pending without mutation\",\n            \"continues rejecting after CWD resolves until PTY bind\",\n            \"carries resolved CWD as startupCwd for an allowed unbound detach\",\n            \"preserves persisted and live remote PTY detach handoff\"\n          ]\n        }",
        "Audit1925 (sources1922/1923): Delete the complete mocked inherited-CWD split orchestration suite: local/server delegation, async CWD forwarding, stale-manager refusal, nested lookup reuse and layout-owner call-argument/no-call alarms are lost; no real pane/PTY/remote split ran. The partial CWD resolver loses supplied OSC7/cache/remote-ID/deferred-field and stale-cleanup examples, so its entire three-title deferred-fence assertion object retires. Its actual timer admission/fallback callbacks remain selected. Handoff loses simple promise/input projection, direct clear and direct discard-as-restored-PTY samples; retire only that projection title while retaining stale-owner handoff, released-owner/input limits, eviction and expiry mappings. Preserve meaningful remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged dated receipts within their original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh gate execution evidence in this metadata packet. No equivalent replacement, physical watcher/PTY/provider, live SSH/remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Exact retired authored alarms: 'hands the same cwd promise and buffered input to a remounted leaf in order'; 'clears the current owner'; 'drops a stale record when an authoritative restored PTY wins the key'; 'returns the confirmed OSC 7 entry without calling IPC'; 'falls through to the unconfirmed cached entry when IPC returns empty'; 'skips local PTY IPC for remote runtime PTY ids'; 'preserves a deferred split fence until the PTY binds'; 'keeps a newer pending deferred lookup when an older callback arrives'; 'splits on the server from the terminal the server published for it'; 'refuses rather than splitting here with %s'; 'delegates remote %s splits without creating a competing local pane'; 'keeps the existing local split-and-focus path unchanged'; 'creates and records the split before asynchronous cwd resolution settles'; 'reuses one pending cwd lookup across rapid nested splits'; 'does not resolve cwd or split a stale manager when the live manager is gone'; 'never asks main in a window-owned build'; 'in a layout-owner build, asks main to split and start the pane, and leaves drawing it to main’s frame'; 'in a layout-owner build, splits here when main answers as today'; 'in a layout-owner build, splits as today where a paired server owns the layout'; 'in a layout-owner build, leaves a handle-less pane’s split to the server whose frames draw it'.",
        "Audit1925 historical original assertion object, preserved verbatim; removed aliases are retired, any surviving aliases remain limited to unchanged retained callbacks:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/layout/split/terminal-pane-split-with-inherited-cwd.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"creates and records the split before pending CWD resolution\",\n            \"passes the resolved CWD promise without reviving a stale manager\",\n            \"rapid nested splits reuse one pending CWD lookup\",\n            \"keeps remote-runtime split ownership on its execution host\"\n          ]\n        }",
        "Audit1925 historical original assertion object, preserved verbatim; removed aliases are retired, any surviving aliases remain limited to unchanged retained callbacks:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/layout/split/resolve-split-cwd.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"preserves a deferred split fence when OSC 7 updates cwd\",\n            \"clears a settled deferred entry only for matching promise identity\",\n            \"keeps a newer deferred lookup when an older cleanup callback arrives\"\n          ]\n        }",
        "Audit1925 historical original assertion object, preserved verbatim; removed aliases are retired, any surviving aliases remain limited to unchanged retained callbacks:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/layout/split/deferred-split-pane-handoff.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"hands the same cwd promise and buffered input to a remounted leaf in order\",\n            \"keeps input across repeated remounts and fences stale owners\",\n            \"releases an unmounted owner without dropping its pending handoff\",\n            \"retains input within the shared preconnect entry and code-unit caps\",\n            \"evicts the oldest handoff when the record cap is reached\",\n            \"expires an abandoned handoff after the bounded remount window\"\n          ]\n        }"
      ],
      "demotionRule": "Keep experimental or demote if pane activation waits on CWD, a deferred split can detach before PTY bind, a remount or rehome loses its stable CWD/input handoff, stale owners mutate a successor record, detached cwd is lost, input reorders or remains pending after cleanup, a closed pane can spawn, stale retirement kills a newer same-ID owner, remote-runtime delegation creates a competing local pane, or the focused suite flakes without an identified product or harness cause."
    },
    {
      "id": "terminal-session.kill-all-surface-cleanup",
      "title": "Kill all sessions removes only the confirmed terminal surfaces and current bindings",
      "maturity": "experimental",
      "protection": "none",
      "owner": "terminal-runtime",
      "layer": "renderer-main-contract",
      "surfaces": [
        "terminal lifecycle",
        "terminal tab cleanup",
        "PTY shutdown",
        "Manage Sessions",
        "Resource Manager"
      ],
      "platforms": ["macos", "linux", "windows"],
      "providers": ["local", "daemon", "ssh", "wsl", "remote-runtime", "mobile-relay"],
      "coveredPlatforms": [],
      "coveredProviders": [],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit1640 removes low-value IPC, SSH, workspace and transcript-watcher tests without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public refusal, cancellation, execution-host and real-filesystem outcomes with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Local macOS deterministic evidence covers the renderer snapshot/coordinator, exact local and SSH-shaped PTY request settlement, active-last and pinned terminal-tab routing, component-unmount continuation, and the existing current/legacy daemon management contract. Windows Electron process absence, live SSH/WSL behavior, and remote-runtime/mobile host completion remain explicit gaps. The audit removed the isolated terminal-tab close routing suite. Forced-pin close-call shape, editor-before-browser fallback, browser fallback, empty-worktree deactivation and no replacement-terminal routing lose their supplied-store spy assertions. Remaining lifecycle/coordinator suites are not claimed to reproduce those isolated routing alarms.",
      "motivatingLinks": ["https://github.com/stablyai/orca/issues/8001"],
      "invariant": "Every terminal surface confirmed in the invoking renderer is force-closed exactly once after daemon management settles, later-created surfaces and non-terminal tabs survive, and exact shutdown requests are limited to deduplicated current non-runtime PTY bindings of the confirmed surfaces.",
      "oracle": "Snapshot terminal entity IDs before the first await; mutate ownership, active selection, bindings, and tab presence while daemon management is pending and between bounded close batches; then assert only the immutable targets disappear from both terminal stores, active targets close last with valid editor/browser/deactivated post-state, every captured exact PTY promise settles before callbacks, and no provider inventory sweep or late-tab kill occurs.",
      "commands": [],
      "testFiles": [],
      "assertionRefs": [],
      "evidenceRuns": [],
      "runtimeBudget": {
        "p95Seconds": 10,
        "scope": "focused renderer/main unit and performance-count tests"
      },
      "flakeHistory": {
        "status": "unknown",
        "evidence": "The focused 27-test slice passed locally once; it needs CI and soak history before promotion."
      },
      "redGreenEvidence": {
        "status": "partial",
        "evidence": "The initial 100-tab implementation exposed an oversized close batch; two-close event-loop batching fixed the structural issue. The gate now uses deterministic batch instrumentation because full-suite CPU saturation made wall-clock assertions flaky; saved CI artifacts and intentional-break evidence are still needed."
      },
      "performanceBudget": {
        "required": true,
        "evidence": "The coordinator performs one management sweep, builds an initial live-owner index, and revalidates at most once after each two-close yield when the Zustand state changed (at most 49 replans for the 100-tab fixture). It closes each present unique target once and sends at most one exact kill per unique current non-runtime PTY not already settled by daemon management. The fixture asserts 100 close attempts, 100 local kill calls, at least 100 store writes, and 49 yields; planner-level tests prove each individual plan build scans terminal and unified ownership stores once. Production diagnostics report measured close-batch duration, while the deterministic gate makes no machine-load-sensitive latency claim."
      },
      "promotionCriteria": [
        "Run the focused gate for at least 100 consecutive passes or 14 days across required CI platforms.",
        "Attach Windows Electron evidence for both entry points, empty and established terminals, later-tab survival, xterm removal, and initial PTY absence after settlement.",
        "Exercise the SSH fixture and WSL when available, or keep their live process-absence gaps explicit.",
        "Propagate and align runtime-host tab-close completion before claiming verified remote-runtime shutdown."
      ],
      "knownGaps": [
        "Audit1640 removes low-value IPC, SSH, workspace and transcript-watcher tests without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public refusal, cancellation, execution-host and real-filesystem outcomes with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded.",
        "Windows Electron screenshots and live process/xterm absence evidence were not produced by this local macOS run.",
        "Live SSH and WSL process absence, Linux local/daemon behavior, and mobile/relay shutdown remain unproved.",
        "Runtime-host terminal close is best-effort because closeTerminalTab still discards the existing async host result and its close-intent lifetime is shorter than the possible RPC flow.",
        "Daemon adapter listing failures remain suppressed by the existing management API, so reported daemon counts are not authoritative verification of every process.",
        "The audit removed the isolated terminal-tab close routing suite. Forced-pin close-call shape, editor-before-browser fallback, browser fallback, empty-worktree deactivation and no replacement-terminal routing lose their supplied-store spy assertions. Remaining lifecycle/coordinator suites are not claimed to reproduce those isolated routing alarms."
      ],
      "demotionRule": "Keep experimental or demote to protection none if the gate flakes, permits a late-created tab or unrelated PTY to close, duplicates provider shutdown, or performs more than one ownership replan per bounded yield."
    },
    {
      "id": "terminal-session.explicit-close-retirement",
      "title": "Explicit terminal close retires parked PTYs and agent authority exactly once",
      "maturity": "experimental",
      "protection": "partial",
      "owner": "terminal-runtime",
      "layer": "main-preload-renderer-electron-contract",
      "surfaces": [
        "terminal tab close",
        "split pane close and detach",
        "hidden terminal parking",
        "agent resume authority"
      ],
      "platforms": ["macos", "linux", "windows"],
      "providers": ["local", "daemon", "ssh", "runtime"],
      "coveredPlatforms": ["macos"],
      "coveredProviders": ["local", "daemon", "ssh", "runtime"],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit4368 intentionally drops seven mocked teardown cases: duplicate single-chat rollback, forced stuck-close warning/retirement, post-close-throw exit acceptance, mixed live/unconfirmed wording, exact serial-close budget work, missing runtime selector success and runtime-sweep rejection. Four structured-session and three PTY teardown cases remain; no replacement or fresh native/process/remote proof is claimed. Historical assertion anchors and receipts are not refreshed by this source-only reduction. Audit4362 intentionally deletes the imported stale-waiter retry and manually assembled OSC9999 mobile-republish cases, plus the mocked missing-worktree cleanup suite (4 authored / 5 finite cases in three suites). Lost alarms include repeated unread worker_done pointers, working-to-waiting mobile status publication, missing-worktree filtering, and scoped daemon shutdown with unrelated duplicate identities. No replacement coverage or new platform proof is claimed. Audit4351 removes the physical-exit timeout/retry and kill-failure/retry local-PTY shutdown cases. The retained shutdown case proves pending ownership until the injected node-pty exit callback only. These two narrow error-path alarms are intentionally lost; retained commands still select the reduced suite. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime execution is claimed. Earlier notes and dated receipts retain their original scopes. Audit3994 retires two authored callbacks imported by the shared construction test driver: split OSC 9999 carry and rendererless status ownership, plus OpenCode permission text taking priority in status and tui-idle refusal. Remaining imports and selectors keep their scope. No equivalent replacement or fresh gate execution is claimed. Audit 3959 retires the whole session.test.ts driver (27 authored / 33 finite cases): startup/echo filtering, readiness input gates, ownership confirmation, detach authority, and termination retry/exit ordering alarms are intentionally lost. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime validation is claimed. Audit3437 composes ROOT-adopted3431/independent3432: intentionally removes127 authored/174 potential expanded cases across12 sources, deleting7 whole suites and one267line unused helper without test credit. Retain8 authored/13 potential cases. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Lose the complete completed-worker-retirement-resume suite: exact terminal-close resume-record revocation, PTY-exit recovery retention and settled-worker release examples. Remove its exact command token or standalone command, testFiles entry and assertionRef, archiving complete prior fields. Independent receipts retain original scopes. Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The retained runtime registration driver loses three complete imported fragments: changed-working-label title facts and suppressed-frame tracked snapshots; refusing SSH GitLab MR-base lookup before local Git/glab calls; and missing folder-workspace path creation/update refusal before spawn/store mutation. These alarms are intentionally lost. Other imported fragments and separately rooted dated receipts are unchanged; they are not equivalent replacement coverage.  Audit3323 (reconciled source audit3320) intentionally retires seven low-value renderer authority/retirement examples: retires one pane, clears resume authority, and rejects late status without harming siblings — Late status reviving a retired pane, sibling damage, or resume authority left behind.; can retire live pane authority while retaining its sleeping session — Retiring live authority accidentally dropping a retained sleeping session.; keeps a physical pane routed through chained detaches until its current owner closes — Chained detach alias routing broken after original owner closes, or alias survives final close.; forgets routing aliases for purged tabs — Purged-tab routing aliases lingering.; retires split, relay, deferred, and pending sessions for a parked tab — Split, relay, deferred or pending session omitted from teardown, sleeping-record sibling damaged, parked disposer skipped.; retires parked ownership before teardown and sweeps published state before unified close — Parked cleanup/provider teardown/state removal/sweep/unified-close ordering changes.; starts mixed provider teardown and classifies both rejection kinds after synchronous retirement — Mixed teardown failures blocking retirement, or local/runtime warning counts misclassified.. Remove the exact-pane-retirement and chained-detach assertion references because their source cases are gone. Other retained cases do not replace these alarms. Preserve all dated evidenceRuns and prior history with their original source scope; no fresh execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2095 current-parent preparation2126: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2090 (sources2088/2089): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2086 (sources2082/2083): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2076 (sources2073/2074): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-part-02.spec.ts: recovers a moved SSH pane through the tab it now sits in, not the one its lease froze; reports a plain expired orphan; does not report a pane whose only recent lease was superseded; does not report a pane whose only recent lease had its relay id recycled; picks the eligible orphan over a superseded predecessor that matches first; collects the same tabs the per-tab reader reports, in one sweep of the leases; reports no candidate when no lease names any of the worktree tabs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/runtime-availability.spec.ts: starts unavailable with no authoritative window; reports the configured Windows terminal shell on status; reports floating workspace availability from settings on status; polls floating tabs with targeted PTY liveness and no repo/provider inventory; hydrates persisted tabs when the store cannot report repos; advertises browser screencast only when a renderer window is available; routes mobile Codex reset consumption through the account mutation coordinator; maps a definite pre-provider rejection into an authoritative current snapshot. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1904 reduces persistence-pty-binding-reconciliation from six to four definitions, intentionally losing legacy remap-load and first-binding projection alarms. Current selector/testFile remains valid, with no selected-source assertionRef or active matching receipt. The six unchanged close/continuity receipts keep their exact original scope; no new broad gate or replacement evidence is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1683 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1674 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1640 removes low-value IPC, SSH, workspace and transcript-watcher tests without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public refusal, cancellation, execution-host and real-filesystem outcomes with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1630 removes low-value Git, GitHub/GitLab and IPC projections, argument inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained cancellation, ownership, authorization, filesystem and SQLite boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1627 removes low-value mocked daemon projections, scalar tables and duplicate terminal examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained terminal content preservation, process ownership refusal and recovery boundaries together with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Live macOS Electron tests prove exact local PTY disappearance after parked-tab close and detached-pgid descendant death after agent close. A deterministic final-pane interleaving now proves durable tab retirement commits before externally owned PTY teardown can publish graph loss, and preserves an unrelated live canary through duplicate exit retirement. Deterministic tests also cover final-pane CLI close durability and same-incarnation handle continuity; persisted-empty restart suppression remains historical Electron evidence, alongside replacement and hard graph-loss stale fencing, preallocated-handle supersession, daemon and SSH routing, local/daemon pending-snapshot ownership across natural exit, stale-root descendant-signal suppression, graceful-to-immediate kill upgrades, duplicate-kill completion sharing, locale-stable bounded/fresh/coalesced process-table reads, deadline-safe successor scans, cycle-safe linear descendant traversal, target-only escalation indexing, 32-wide bulk teardown, source-scan timestamp identity, same-second PID ambiguity, ordinary runtime close ownership, unified-only hydration, split ownership, pane detach transfer, restart alias hydration, and late-hook suppression; live Linux, Windows, WSL, SSH, and remote-runtime process evidence remains pending. A paired macOS Electron journey (real attached-window desktop host plus a separate real paired desktop client, isolated profiles) covers the inverse authority direction for host-created terminals: a renderer graph sync must not retire a tab that `orca terminal create` made. The retained paired journey covers the incident shape the real CLI produces - a repo's FIRST host-created terminal, since src/cli/handlers/terminal.ts sends no clientMutationId. The repeated target-after-unrelated-terminal journey was retired; its separate ordering alarm is no longer provided. An earlier reading of this gate called a preceding host-created terminal and a `clientMutationId` protective; main-process instrumentation refuted that. The renderer's stale session write deleted the host tab from persistence in every variant, and only the delete's timing relative to the measured sync differed, so those rows were false negatives of a single-sync oracle. The defect was in persistence: persistPtyBinding did not raise the repo's terminal topology fence for the first host-admitted tab, leaving the renderer's pre-create tab list free to replay over it. Elapsed time and paired-client mirroring never decided anything. A windowless `orca serve` parity arm runs the identical oracle and passes on both the merge-base and the branch, confirming that topology does not exhibit the defect (the gate it turns on is window-conditioned) and that making the host binding unconditional did not regress it. All of this is macOS-local only. The reported incident occurred on a physical Windows host; we did not run against one. The claim that the mechanism is platform-independent rests on the authoritative-window gate and publication-epoch inheritance being OS-agnostic, not on Windows evidence, so no ConPTY, Windows window-lifecycle, update, or sleep behavior is covered here. The synthetic default-tabs unit suite was retired: its explicit-empty/default-tab assertions no longer supply unit evidence. This retirement supplies no new persisted-restart, runtime-routing, cross-platform, or mobile evidence; existing historical runs and counts remain historical. The test-value audit removes the isolated re-retirement-token/epoch, activity-cutoff, idle-reattach and sibling-restore examples. The cited exact retirement and chained-detach cases remain unchanged, alongside closed-tab revival fencing and alias churn bounds. Their retained evidence is not equivalent coverage for every removed permutation; historical execution evidence is unchanged. The test-value audit removed shared-owner snapshot/cold-restore reference examples, a direct absent-tab PTY-index update, caller-supplied host-owned teardown boolean/no-dispatch, and a single local-provider rejection example. It also removed hand-built detach-retention comparator examples for different runs, handles, provider identities, and handle-less rows without independent identity ingress. Their specific snapshot, missing-tab, host-decision, rejection-count, and comparator alarms are lost. Current exact authority/ordering and chained-detach cases remain retained; they do not establish equivalent coverage for the removed examples. Historical commands, counts, results, and red-green narratives remain historical. The test-value audit retires terminals-explicit-empty-hydration.test.ts in full: its direct git/folder empty-tombstone assertions and literal-flag auto-create helper check are lost. The store test never mounted the initial-terminal effect or performed a persisted restart. The audit also removes terminal-tab-retirement.test.ts pure ownership/alias/routing plan inventories and sleeping-record map assertions; its former 100-tab scan-count case was subsequently retired too; no assertion remains in that suite. These retained and historical cases do not establish equivalent tombstone, default-create, provider teardown, cross-platform, or mobile coverage. Historical commands, results, counts, and red-green narratives remain historical. The subsequent test-value audit deletes the remaining terminal-tab-retirement.test.ts suite. Its 100-tab case asserted only returned plan count and one outer scan per ownership store; it never inspected per-tab plans or provider teardown. Those direct cardinality/work-count alarms are intentionally lost. Historical executed commands, results, counts and red-green narratives remain historical; no equivalent replacement or new runtime, platform or mobile evidence is claimed. Audit1383: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-native-chat-setup.spec.ts reduced. Lose command-list/receipt/default/background activation matrices whose provider spawn returns canned IDs. Retained test proves actual tab allocation separation, not terminal startup. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected receipts and their platform/provider/budget claims remain scoped to unchanged selectors. Changed optional selectors have no new execution result. Audit1392: src/main/agent-hooks/server-pane-authority.test.ts reduced. Retires one duplicate-transfer no-op listener count and latest pty/timestamp callback fixture. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected receipts remain unchanged and apply only to their unchanged selectors. Changed optional selectors have no new execution result. Audit1401: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-duplicate-pty-repair.spec.ts removed. Loses listing-on-already-repaired-data alarm; it never established runtime repair invocation. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-split-agent-tab.spec.ts removed. Loses actual mobile split sibling shell versus recorded-agent resume command alarms; no equivalent coverage asserted. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-native-chat-setup.spec.ts removed. Loses separate setup/startup tab result in that manually assembled path. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts reduced. Driver registration/import of a whole-deleted selected spec is removed; directly authored cases remain unchanged. No extra authored removal credit. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected receipts remain unchanged and apply only to their unchanged selectors. Changed optional selectors have no new execution result.",
      "motivatingLinks": [
        "https://linear.app/stably/issue/STA-4327",
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/14590",
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/8628",
