      ],
      "invariant": "Close permanently removes the owned provider session, agent descendants, persisted tab/layout authority, and resume authority even when no TerminalPane is mounted; final-pane CLI close commits durable tab retirement before PTY stop can publish graph loss, does not acknowledge before that retirement, and treats the later exit retirement as idempotent. Workspace-wide CLI close applies that same durable contract to every terminal in exactly one worktree, including pinned and persisted-only surfaces, without touching sibling-worktree PTYs or resume records. A persisted explicit-empty state prevents initial-tab fallback from repopulating the workspace after reload or restart. A handle remains valid while the same provider-attested PTY incarnation survives renderer reload or re-key, and becomes stale without adopting a replacement incarnation. A terminating id remains reserved through natural exit, duplicate callers await the same completion, and immediate teardown upgrades any graceful request without signalling a recycled PID or a descendant tree after root ownership is lost; process-table work is locale-stable, bounded, fresh for each post-start request, same-turn coalesced, and begins within the requesting caller's deadline, including bulk worktree cleanup; detach and park preserve ownership; aliases prevent a detached agent's immutable physical pane key from being retired with its former tab.",
      "oracle": "Audit4368 intentionally drops seven mocked teardown cases: duplicate single-chat rollback, forced stuck-close warning/retirement, post-close-throw exit acceptance, mixed live/unconfirmed wording, exact serial-close budget work, missing runtime selector success and runtime-sweep rejection. Four structured-session and three PTY teardown cases remain; no replacement or fresh native/process/remote proof is claimed. Historical assertion anchors and receipts are not refreshed by this source-only reduction. Audit4362 intentionally deletes the imported stale-waiter retry and manually assembled OSC9999 mobile-republish cases, plus the mocked missing-worktree cleanup suite (4 authored / 5 finite cases in three suites). Lost alarms include repeated unread worker_done pointers, working-to-waiting mobile status publication, missing-worktree filtering, and scoped daemon shutdown with unrelated duplicate identities. No replacement coverage or new platform proof is claimed. Audit4351 removes the physical-exit timeout/retry and kill-failure/retry local-PTY shutdown cases. The retained shutdown case proves pending ownership until the injected node-pty exit callback only. These two narrow error-path alarms are intentionally lost; retained commands still select the reduced suite. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime execution is claimed. Earlier notes and dated receipts retain their original scopes. Audit3832 deliberately retires76 authored/79 finite cases:75 runtime compatibility cases/78 finite cases across14 fragments, plus one localization extractor default-flag case. Three whole runtime fragments are deleted;27 authored/30 finite cases remain across the reviewed sources. This gate retains only its own selected scope; no equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/native/remote evidence is claimed. Runtime component A: Audit3828 composes3822 with independent3824: deliberately retires49 authored/52 finite cases from seven compatibility fragments, leaving15 authored/18 finite cases and deleting two entire fragments. Accepted losses: positive folder-worker recovery/materialization and reveal deadline; persisted-key normalization and legacy split/group/focus projection; fixed stale CAS refusal; occupied/alias/restored/preallocated terminal-handle variants; fixed OpenCode/Cursor/Claude/Codex/Antigravity classification, readiness, title and management examples; direct private-map browser authority projections; browser-focus and OMP title projection; already-aborted claim cleanup. Additional3824 loss: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-02.spec.ts :: does not poll a wrapper foreground for a speculative CLI prompt send :: Speculative retryForegroundWrappers:false check must return false on a wrapper after one foreground read, without polling the supplied later codex response. These real bounded alarms are deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained callbacks are unchanged and provide only their own bounded scope, not equivalent replacement. Historical receipts do not validate reduced callbacks. No fresh runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser evidence or full transitive closure is claimed. Runtime component B: Audit3834 deliberately retires26 authored/26 finite cases from seven fresh compatibility fragments, leaving10/10 and deleting the one-case saved-binding reattachment fragment. Original position58 is excluded: its existing substantive3578 KEEP7 review remains historical, with no fresh credit. Accepted losses: fixed hook/provider-session identities and stale metadata refusal; decorative/pre-title foreground ordering variants; saved-binding surface reattachment; saved-row exit ghost removal and silent activation selection; unsupported headless wake; positive pending materialization/group projections; per-caller navigation selection; positive SSH hydration/read partition; laptop mobile publication/buffer and background/pending/status projections; abnormal/unregistered SSH grace, normal-exit refusal, persisted SSH hydration, positive serve reattachment, pending-agent launch arguments and direct seeded running-launch admission guard. These are real bounded alarms deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained cases preserve their own distinct deferred foreground coalescing, usable handle continuity, stale inventory refresh, concurrent browser snapshot preservation, renderer graph fencing, caller dedup isolation, SSH partition writes, runtime split lifetime, independent relay-ready publication, lease admission/state/expiry. The direct running-launch no-spawn guard alarm is deliberately retired; no remaining owning-launch refusal coverage is claimed. Historical runs do not validate reduced callbacks. No equivalent replacement, runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser result or full transitive closure is claimed. Additional extractor loss: config/scripts/localization/source-extraction/audit-localization-native-dialogs.test.mjs :: does not change the existing renderer scan by default :: Default options must omit the five native-only fields in this supplied snippet. No equivalent replacement is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit3814 deliberately retires60 authored/60 finite cases:53runtime compatibility cases,4native XCTest methods and3Python clipboard methods, including the entire StableElementIndexes suite. Clipboard cuts retire the one-over-cap sample, incoming-offer destruction trace and sequential20-copy replay; actual wire, FD/pipe, startup and Xvfb/GTK boundaries remain without equivalent replacement claims. Accepted losses include narrow terminal-send payload/provider projections, legacy and direct no-op/error permutations, timing/work-count examples, private state/title/activity projections and fixture-driven readiness examples, individually enumerated below. These include real bounded production alarms consciously retired for marginal value; retained failed writes, duplicate submission, stale capture, transcript/ring and allocation fences are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or complete transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3806 deliberately retires40 authored/40 finite runtime compatibility cases, including the terminal-side-effect-facts-part03 headless-snapshots-part02 and agent-status-and-waits-part03 fragments, plus20 scalar Swift precondition sites. Lost runtime alarms include status/title/attention projection examples, simple renderer/headless frame restoration and status waiting outcomes detailed in the accepted-loss ledger. Swift cuts retire duplicate generation-map/schema/navigation/bridge and notification-wrapper assertions; no standalone native program is deleted. These include real bounded production alarms consciously retired for marginal value. Retained races, pending writes/reflow, namespace and waiter ownership are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or full transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3798 deliberately retires21 authored/24 finite compatibility cases, including the entire SSH-worktree-lifecycle and repository-project-operations fragments. Accepted losses include navigation-only settings acknowledgement, browser session cleanup and host preservation projections, window positive/policy-state examples, terminal recovery/reload and no-incarnation remint examples, terminal listing compatibility/malformed IDs, directory browse/sort/Windows path smoke, SSH create refusal/manual lineage, recursive parent-folder creation and fork/origin/avatar/icon projections. Real bounded production alarms are consciously retired for marginal value; retained authority races, cleanup/clone ownership, pending waiters, nested-folder and scan invalidation cases are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or full transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3437 composes ROOT-adopted3431/independent3432: intentionally removes127 authored/174 potential expanded cases across12 sources, deleting7 whole suites and one267line unused helper without test credit. Retain8 authored/13 potential cases. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Lose the complete completed-worker-retirement-resume suite: exact terminal-close resume-record revocation, PTY-exit recovery retention and settled-worker release examples. Remove its exact command token or standalone command, testFiles entry and assertionRef, archiving complete prior fields. Independent receipts retain original scopes. Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The retained runtime registration driver loses three complete imported fragments: changed-working-label title facts and suppressed-frame tracked snapshots; refusing SSH GitLab MR-base lookup before local Git/glab calls; and missing folder-workspace path creation/update refusal before spawn/store mutation. These alarms are intentionally lost. Other imported fragments and separately rooted dated receipts are unchanged; they are not equivalent replacement coverage.  Audit3323 (reconciled source audit3320) intentionally retires seven low-value renderer authority/retirement examples: retires one pane, clears resume authority, and rejects late status without harming siblings — Late status reviving a retired pane, sibling damage, or resume authority left behind.; can retire live pane authority while retaining its sleeping session — Retiring live authority accidentally dropping a retained sleeping session.; keeps a physical pane routed through chained detaches until its current owner closes — Chained detach alias routing broken after original owner closes, or alias survives final close.; forgets routing aliases for purged tabs — Purged-tab routing aliases lingering.; retires split, relay, deferred, and pending sessions for a parked tab — Split, relay, deferred or pending session omitted from teardown, sleeping-record sibling damaged, parked disposer skipped.; retires parked ownership before teardown and sweeps published state before unified close — Parked cleanup/provider teardown/state removal/sweep/unified-close ordering changes.; starts mixed provider teardown and classifies both rejection kinds after synchronous retirement — Mixed teardown failures blocking retirement, or local/runtime warning counts misclassified.. Remove the exact-pane-retirement and chained-detach assertion references because their source cases are gone. Other retained cases do not replace these alarms. Preserve all dated evidenceRuns and prior history with their original source scope; no fresh execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2095 current-parent preparation2126: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2090 (sources2088/2089): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2086 (sources2082/2083): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2076 (sources2073/2074): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-part-02.spec.ts: recovers a moved SSH pane through the tab it now sits in, not the one its lease froze; reports a plain expired orphan; does not report a pane whose only recent lease was superseded; does not report a pane whose only recent lease had its relay id recycled; picks the eligible orphan over a superseded predecessor that matches first; collects the same tabs the per-tab reader reports, in one sweep of the leases; reports no candidate when no lease names any of the worktree tabs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/runtime-availability.spec.ts: starts unavailable with no authoritative window; reports the configured Windows terminal shell on status; reports floating workspace availability from settings on status; polls floating tabs with targeted PTY liveness and no repo/provider inventory; hydrates persisted tabs when the store cannot report repos; advertises browser screencast only when a renderer window is available; routes mobile Codex reset consumption through the account mutation coordinator; maps a definite pre-provider rejection into an authoritative current snapshot. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1904 reduces persistence-pty-binding-reconciliation from six to four definitions, intentionally losing legacy remap-load and first-binding projection alarms. Current selector/testFile remains valid, with no selected-source assertionRef or active matching receipt. The six unchanged close/continuity receipts keep their exact original scope; no new broad gate or replacement evidence is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1683 retires changed-source assertion and execution scope without equivalent replacement coverage. Existing unchanged-selector receipts remain scoped to their original sources. Historical prior-source oracle: Audit1674 retires changed-source assertion and execution scope without equivalent replacement coverage. Existing unchanged-selector receipts remain scoped to their original sources. Historical prior-source oracle: Existing exact unchanged-selector receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Changed source selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical prior-source oracle account: Existing exact unchanged-selector receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Changed source selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical prior-source oracle account: Capture exact tab, pane, PTY, handle, incarnation, and persisted layout identities. Final-pane terminal.close must invoke one durability-acknowledged tab retirement before exact PTY teardown; controlled PTY exit and graph removal afterward must remain idempotent, omit the target from persistence and provider inventory, and leave an unrelated canary handle live. terminal.closeAll must force-retire every pinned and unpinned target surface, clear its persisted agent-resume and incarnation records, await authoritative PTY exit, preserve a sibling worktree's tab, PTY, and resume authority, and return an unverifiable failure instead of claiming exit when the owning host does not confirm a stop. The ordinary path stays pending until the persisted row is removed and never falls back to the fire-and-forget pane event; reload/restart must keep the explicitly emptied worktree at zero terminal tabs and provider sessions. Reloading the renderer with the same tab/pane/PTY/incarnation must keep the handle readable; changing only the incarnation behind the same PTY id, losing the authoritative graph, or superseding the renderer handle with a preallocated handle must reject the old handle with terminal_handle_stale. Parked-close tests prove the exact PTY disappears; descendant/process tests keep natural exits reserved, upgrade teardown safely, bound/coalesce process-table work, and protect recycled identities.",
      "commands": [
