metadata when a mobile activation finds the worktree already read; returns unread:false from worktree.ps after a mobile activation clears the flag; materializes pending mobile session terminals without focusing desktop clients; closes browser mobile session tabs when addressed by browser workspace id. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs.spec.ts: resolves mobile terminal surfaces by exact split leaf; closes the matching mobile terminal UUID leaf without closing the whole tab; closes the whole mobile terminal tab when addressed by parent tab id; activates the active split leaf when addressed by parent tab id; clears unread metadata on mobile worktree activation without focusing desktop clients; wakes slept agents on the host renderer when a phone activates a worktree. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-05.spec.ts: publishes the hook provider session on a headless mobile tab so native chat can address the transcript; recovers the agent type from the hook row when the pane was launched without an agent hint; reads one agent-status snapshot per projection, not one per terminal tab; waits for unknown-launch foreground owner before publishing Pi-compatible mobile status; keeps Pi-compatible mobile session status as Pi for an unknown-launch foreground pi PTY; keeps renderer-vetted mobile agent status for custom-titled terminals. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-04.spec.ts: publishes terminal surface agent status for paired web clients; preserves authoritative OMP identity for Pi-compatible remote terminal snapshots; normalizes a remote OMP title without republishing omitted launch identity; skips the foreground-process probe when the PTY launch agent is already known; probes the foreground process only on a status transition for unknown launch agents; passes the client signal and the slept-worktree refusal to the spawn. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-a