        "Audit2090 (sources2088/2089): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-windowless-sleep-resume.spec.ts: keeps the recorded permission flags of the launch it resumes; still refuses a session another pane also records; resumes in the pane with a window present too: main is the one executor; keeps the original provider and current retry intent through a refused main start; resumes once; a second open after it finished attaches to the same terminal; a reloaded window's open attaches to the terminal main started, never a second resume. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-output-and-worker-recovery-part-05.spec.ts: defers live workers without exact controller identity evidence; defers an SSH folder legacy worker while its folder path is unavailable. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence.",
        "Audit2086 (sources2082/2083): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-06.spec.ts: suppresses saved mobile agent status when live evidence is the Claude agents screen; suppresses saved mobile agent status when the current terminal title is neutral; suppresses saved mobile agent status when fresh live OSC title is Claude agents; keeps saved PTY bindings pending until the runtime knows the PTY is connected; refreshes daemon PTY liveness before publishing mobile session tabs; does not invalidate a newly spawned SSH pane from an overlapping stale process list. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/pty-title-status.spec.ts: associates controller PTYs with mixed-case Windows and UNC cwd paths; uses OSC titles rather than controller process names for rendererless PTYs; ignores the bare cursor-agent native title so synthesized spinner state survives; only records the bare Cursor native title via the stale-working clear; refuses a bare Cursor title while the foreground read is unavailable; does not treat a bare Cursor title as an agent once the shell owns the foreground; accepts a bare Cursor title when the foreground read confirms cursor-agent; refuses a bare Cursor title on a runtime pty with no controller attached; clears a stale working title after 3s of title-less output; cancels the stale-title timer when the PTY exits; keeps stale-title timers isolated per PTY. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/paired-settings.spec.ts: projects runtime-backed settings to paired clients; updates quick commands without widening general paired settings payloads; applies native-chat option deltas atomically on the runtime host; keeps a future-launch default when an older client asks to prune from inventory; preserves concurrent additions after forty quick commands; accepts runtime-backed setting updates from paired clients; broadcasts visibility default changes to paired clients; reconciles hooks only when paired-client hook settings change; rejects relative paths for runtime nested repo scan/import. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence.",
        "Audit2076 (sources2073/2074): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-part-02.spec.ts: recovers a moved SSH pane through the tab it now sits in, not the one its lease froze; reports a plain expired orphan; does not report a pane whose only recent lease was superseded; does not report a pane whose only recent lease had its relay id recycled; picks the eligible orphan over a superseded predecessor that matches first; collects the same tabs the per-tab reader reports, in one sweep of the leases; reports no candidate when no lease names any of the worktree tabs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/runtime-availability.spec.ts: starts unavailable with no authoritative window; reports the configured Windows terminal shell on status; reports floating workspace availability from settings on status; polls floating tabs with targeted PTY liveness and no repo/provider inventory; hydrates persisted tabs when the store cannot report repos; advertises browser screencast only when a renderer window is available; routes mobile Codex reset consumption through the account mutation coordinator; maps a definite pre-provider rejection into an authoritative current snapshot. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence.",
        "Audit2070 (sources2068/2069): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts: ordinary registration cleanup removes only await import('./orca-runtime-tests/hooks-and-hosted-review.spec'). src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-archive-hook-gate.spec.ts: removes and records the waiver when the failure is explicitly overridden; removes without an override record when the hook succeeds; removes when the hook is configured but not requested; removes when no archive hook is configured; holds a desktop removal in the same repo until this one is accepted; joins a desktop removal of the same worktree accepted while this one waited. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-ps-agent-row-dismissal.spec.ts: drops the row as soon as the user dismisses it, without waiting for the PTY to exit; tells paired clients to republish on the transition and on the dismissal; rejoins a row through its %s handle after pane ownership clears. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/hooks-and-hosted-review.spec.ts: reports an error when the SSH filesystem provider is unavailable; reports an SSH orca.yaml as an error without reading any filesystem; reports ok for a local repo hook check; reads SSH issue commands as absent and drops writes without touching any filesystem; allows host integration slug helpers for SSH repos through provider-aware GitHub clients; routes runtime GitHub repo identity helpers through the selected WSL project runtime; routes runtime GitHub issue and work-item actions through the selected WSL project runtime; pins explicit origin preference on runtime open-by-number work item lookups; forwards check-details cancellation without local Git overrides. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence.",
        "Audit2065 (sources2063/2064): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/program-status-osc.spec.ts: retire six private facet/lifecycle-state and hook-order assertions; retained public OSC/wait cases do not replace those alarms. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence.",
        "Audit1683 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded.",
        "Audit1674 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded.",
        "Audit1640 removes low-value IPC, SSH, workspace and transcript-watcher tests without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public refusal, cancellation, execution-host and real-filesystem outcomes with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded.",
        "Audit1630 removes low-value Git, GitHub/GitLab and IPC projections, argument inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained cancellation, ownership, authorization, filesystem and SQLite boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded.",
        "Audit1627 removes low-value mocked daemon projections, scalar tables and duplicate terminal examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained terminal content preservation, process ownership refusal and recovery boundaries together with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded.",
        "The live Electron proof currently covers macOS local PTYs only.",
        "Disconnected SSH relay death still requires reconnect-aware provider ownership.",
        "Daemon owner leases and durable retry inventory remain follow-up hardening.",
        "Windows ConPTY, SSH-hosted PTYs, app-quit killAll, and daemon dispose retain foreground-tree-only teardown.",
        "A process born in the capture second is SIGTERMed but not SIGKILLed because ps cannot prove its recycled-PID identity.",
        "A descendant orphaned before or during root ownership loss requires the separate crash-orphan sweep and is not recovered from a stale kill-time snapshot.",
        "recordTerminalSurfaceRetirement advances the INCOMING session's terminal topology revision, so a tombstoned close whose write carries a revision at or below the store's own is rebased away instead of persisting. Pre-existing for every repo already past revision 0 and unchanged by the host-admitted membership fix, which only makes more repos reach that state sooner; the authoritative close path (stageTerminalSurfaceRetirements) computes from the store's session and is unaffected. Known, unaddressed, and deliberately out of scope here: the safe correction is per-tab rather than per-worktree rebase arbitration, because raising the incoming revision wholesale would re-open the host-tab loss whenever a close coincides with a host create.",
        "The SSH relay reattach binding (src/main/ssh/ssh-relay-session.ts persistPtyBinding) is NOT flagged host-admitted, so a lease rebind that has to mint a missing tab raises no fence. It rebinds an existing lease rather than admitting a new surface, so it is believed not to need one, but that was not established either way. Known, unaddressed, and deliberately out of scope here.",
        "The host-created retention journey is macOS-local; the reported incident was on a physical Windows host, which we did not run against.",
        "The test-value audit removes the isolated re-retirement-token/epoch, activity-cutoff, idle-reattach and sibling-restore examples. The cited exact retirement and chained-detach cases remain unchanged, alongside closed-tab revival fencing and alias churn bounds. Their retained evidence is not equivalent coverage for every removed permutation; historical execution evidence is unchanged.",
        "The test-value audit removed shared-owner snapshot/cold-restore reference examples, a direct absent-tab PTY-index update, caller-supplied host-owned teardown boolean/no-dispatch, and a single local-provider rejection example. It also removed hand-built detach-retention comparator examples for different runs, handles, provider identities, and handle-less rows without independent identity ingress. Their specific snapshot, missing-tab, host-decision, rejection-count, and comparator alarms are lost. Current exact authority/ordering and chained-detach cases remain retained; they do not establish equivalent coverage for the removed examples. Historical commands, counts, results, and red-green narratives remain historical.",
        "The test-value audit retires terminals-explicit-empty-hydration.test.ts in full: its direct git/folder empty-tombstone assertions and literal-flag auto-create helper check are lost. The store test never mounted the initial-terminal effect or performed a persisted restart. The audit also removes terminal-tab-retirement.test.ts pure ownership/alias/routing plan inventories and sleeping-record map assertions; its retained 100-tab case measures one scan of each ownership store only. These retained and historical cases do not establish equivalent tombstone, default-create, provider teardown, cross-platform, or mobile coverage. Historical commands, results, counts, and red-green narratives remain historical.",
        "The subsequent test-value audit deletes the remaining terminal-tab-retirement.test.ts suite. Its 100-tab case asserted only returned plan count and one outer scan per ownership store; it never inspected per-tab plans or provider teardown. Those direct cardinality/work-count alarms are intentionally lost. Historical executed commands, results, counts and red-green narratives remain historical; no equivalent replacement or new runtime, platform or mobile evidence is claimed.",
        "The duplicate paired CLI graph-sync journey with an earlier unrelated host-created terminal was retired. The first-host-created-terminal journey retains the same original-PTY reply, host/client inventory and unrelated live canary oracles; target-after-unrelated ordering is no longer separately asserted. A single sync does not prove persisted restart durability. Historical evidence runs/results/counts remain unchanged.",
        "Audit1383: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-native-chat-setup.spec.ts reduced. Lose command-list/receipt/default/background activation matrices whose provider spawn returns canned IDs. Retained test proves actual tab allocation separation, not terminal startup. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit1392: src/main/agent-hooks/server-pane-authority.test.ts reduced. Retires one duplicate-transfer no-op listener count and latest pty/timestamp callback fixture. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Historical removed assertion inventory: []",
        "Audit1401: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-duplicate-pty-repair.spec.ts removed. Loses listing-on-already-repaired-data alarm; it never established runtime repair invocation. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-split-agent-tab.spec.ts removed. Loses actual mobile split sibling shell versus recorded-agent resume command alarms; no equivalent coverage asserted. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-native-chat-setup.spec.ts removed. Loses separate setup/startup tab result in that manually assembled path. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts reduced. Driver registration/import of a whole-deleted selected spec is removed; directly authored cases remain unchanged. No extra authored removal credit. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Historical removed assertion inventory: [{\"file\":\"src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"workspace-wide close force-retires pinned and unpinned tabs, clears resume/incarnation state, awaits both target PTYs, preserves the sibling worktree, and reports an unconfirmed stop as unverifiable\"]}]",
        "Audit1863 removes the standalone local pane-to-PTY equality example. Its direct local-PTY authority alarm is intentionally lost; retained canonical runtime-handle tests do not replace it or prove physical pane/session retirement. Existing E2E and continuity receipts remain scoped to their original commands and counts.",
        "Audit1904 reduces persistence-pty-binding-reconciliation from six to four definitions, intentionally losing legacy remap-load and first-binding projection alarms. Current selector/testFile remains valid, with no selected-source assertionRef or active matching receipt. The six unchanged close/continuity receipts keep their exact original scope; no new broad gate or replacement evidence is claimed. Lost direct alarms: 'remaps legacy SSH lease leaf ids by PTY when the layout is already normalized'; 'promotes an empty tab layout to a durable UUID root when persisting the first PTY binding'.",
        "Audit2052 (source2049): The ordinary orca-runtime.test.ts registrar drops seven imports of deliberately deleted low-value runtime suites. Their mock capability/agent-presence/environment/title/deduplication and batching alarms are intentionally lost without replacement; remaining imports retain their original order. The runtime handle-contract registrar separately drops the deleted tab-collision registration. Unrelated dated evidenceRuns remain unchanged and do not validate reduced-source bytes or selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed.",
        "Audit2056 (sources2054/2055): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts: ordinary registration cleanup removes only await import('./orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-14.spec'). src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-03.spec.ts: arms the stale-title timer for a seeded working title; arms the Command Code scrape from the noted spawn command; prefers the tracked title over a stale renderer lastTitle in the hydration seed; writes recent output into the current runtime output map; uses a later title handler replacement with the runtime receiver; calls the current injected listener with the runtime receiver; keeps optional reconciliation lazy after its callback is removed. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-14.spec.ts: lists them, so a paired client can mirror a migrated editor; closes one by retiring it from the host session; keeps an unsaved draft unless the close is forced; shares aggregate work but leaves a replacement pending promise alone; lets a targeted refresh finish while an aggregate refresh waits; refuses a close when the store lacks %s before the guard; keeps a later missing %s on the original caught failure path. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed.",
        "Audit2061 (sources2059/2060): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts: ordinary registration cleanup removes only await import('./orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-headless-chat-rebuild.spec'); await import('./orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-cold-serve-hydrate.spec'); await import('./orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-execution-host.spec'); await import('./orca-runtime-tests/terminal-spawn-dispatch.spec'). src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/headless-snapshots-part-02.spec.ts: replaces a cwd parsed before late WSL context with the provider cwd; keeps a live WSL cwd that arrives during late-context snapshot recovery; infers local reconstructed WSL context from a WSL UNC worktree; clears stale terminal file URI hostnames after empty-host OSC7 cwd updates; serializes SSH headless OSC7 cwd as POSIX when the desktop runtime is on Windows; keeps Windows SSH OSC7 cwd as a drive path when the desktop runtime is POSIX; serializes Windows SSH headless OSC7 cwd as a drive path on POSIX desktops; infers restored SSH connection identity from app-scoped PTY ids. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-headless-chat-rebuild.spec.ts: survives the rebuild that closing a saved editor tab forces; keeps its place in the tab order when the host lists the workspace again; lists tabs to phones in the order desktop clients draw after a rebuild; keeps the place a window gave a chat across a graph resend before the chat is restored. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-cold-serve-hydrate.spec.ts: lists every persisted terminal of a windowless host after a cold restart; lists every persisted terminal in the all-worktrees inventory after a cold restart; lists persisted editor tabs beside the terminals after a cold restart; restores a persisted split group layout on the cold rebuild; restores the saved active group of a split even when it is not the first group; falls back to the active tab group when the saved active group was not restored; keeps the headless group active when there is no persisted split; keeps phone and CLI creates in the group they joined across a cold restart. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-failed-retry.spec.ts: lists the leftover with its error, though Git no longer does; takes the normal delete once Git registers a checkout at the path again; joins a retry another client started while this Delete listed Git; shows the failed row with its error, not the scan cached before the delete. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-execution-host.spec.ts: refuses an SSH row whose host is unreachable instead of deleting here; refuses a runtime row with no nested SSH target rather than deleting locally; refuses a runtime row that also names a nested SSH target; retains runtime purge dispatch in a recovery job; uses the runtime helper override before resuming an interrupted removal; uses the runtime helper override before retrying a failed removal; captures the watcher callback and retains its job-host receiver; reads the current runtime removal queue. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-spawn-dispatch.spec.ts: reports the spawn request before it leaves for the pty controller; reports it even when the spawn itself then fails; does not report it when the create fails before any spawn request; captures the admission method before reading the incarnation; captures the record method before evaluating its state object; skips database payload serialization when no database exists; skips a throwing database payload when no database exists; keeps the database method and receiver captured before its payload; captures the canonical map method before a binding getter changes it; completes the captured replacement fence without another map lookup. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed.",
        "Module layout policy correction: retire the remaining program-status-osc.spec.ts event-projection case (production/mock-derived pane-key oracle) and sign-in timeout case (real setTimeout wait with Date-only fake clocks). The runtime test registrar no longer imports that file. No replacement coverage or fresh execution is claimed for these losses; historical receipts retain their original source scope.",
        "Module layout policy correction: retire the two remaining worktree-ps-agent-row-dismissal.spec.ts registrations. The remint/dismissal/exit case computed expected snapshotVersion increments from a production snapshot and used real-clock vi.waitFor; the legacy OSC case derived its expected paneKey from the production layout-owner switch. The runtime registrar no longer imports this file. These public projection scenarios have no replacement coverage or fresh execution claimed; all historical receipts and earlier loss notes retain their original source scope.",
        "Audit3323 (reconciled source audit3320) intentionally retires seven low-value renderer authority/retirement examples: retires one pane, clears resume authority, and rejects late status without harming siblings — Late status reviving a retired pane, sibling damage, or resume authority left behind.; can retire live pane authority while retaining its sleeping session — Retiring live authority accidentally dropping a retained sleeping session.; keeps a physical pane routed through chained detaches until its current owner closes — Chained detach alias routing broken after original owner closes, or alias survives final close.; forgets routing aliases for purged tabs — Purged-tab routing aliases lingering.; retires split, relay, deferred, and pending sessions for a parked tab — Split, relay, deferred or pending session omitted from teardown, sleeping-record sibling damaged, parked disposer skipped.; retires parked ownership before teardown and sweeps published state before unified close — Parked cleanup/provider teardown/state removal/sweep/unified-close ordering changes.; starts mixed provider teardown and classifies both rejection kinds after synchronous retirement — Mixed teardown failures blocking retirement, or local/runtime warning counts misclassified.. Remove the exact-pane-retirement and chained-detach assertion references because their source cases are gone. Other retained cases do not replace these alarms. Preserve all dated evidenceRuns and prior history with their original source scope; no fresh execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed.",
        "Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The retained runtime registration driver loses three complete imported fragments: changed-working-label title facts and suppressed-frame tracked snapshots; refusing SSH GitLab MR-base lookup before local Git/glab calls; and missing folder-workspace path creation/update refusal before spawn/store mutation. These alarms are intentionally lost. Other imported fragments and separately rooted dated receipts are unchanged; they are not equivalent replacement coverage.  Original scope text is retained as the exact suffix of coverageNotes/oracle; historical evidence is unchanged.",
        "Audit3437 composes ROOT-adopted3431/independent3432: intentionally removes127 authored/174 potential expanded cases across12 sources, deleting7 whole suites and one267line unused helper without test credit. Retain8 authored/13 potential cases. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Lose the complete completed-worker-retirement-resume suite: exact terminal-close resume-record revocation, PTY-exit recovery retention and settled-worker release examples. Remove its exact command token or standalone command, testFiles entry and assertionRef, archiving complete prior fields. Independent receipts retain original scopes.  All prior notes and dated/archived evidence retain original scopes.",
        "Audit3437 complete prior commands before completed-worker-retirement-resume retirement: [\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/terminal/surface/orca-runtime-terminal-close-continuity.test.ts\",\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts\",\"pnpm dlx node@24 ./node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/agent-hooks/server/testing/authority/server-pane-authority.test.ts src/main/ipc/agent-hooks.test.ts src/main/ipc/agent-pane-authority-ownership.test.ts src/main/persistence/terminal-topology/persistence-pane-identity-migration.test.ts src/main/persistence/terminal-topology/persistence-pty-binding-reconciliation.test.ts src/renderer/src/store/slices/agent-status/agent-pane-authority.test.ts src/renderer/src/store/terminals/terminal-pane-detach-agent-identity.test.ts src/renderer/src/store/terminals/terminal-tab-retirement-store.test.ts tests/e2e/completed-worker-retirement-resume.unit.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/shared/kill-all-terminal-surfaces.test.ts\",\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/pty/process-retirement/pty-descendant-termination.test.ts src/main/daemon/sessions/testing/session.test.ts src/main/daemon/terminal-host/testing/terminal-host.test.ts src/main/providers/local-pty/local-pty-provider-shutdown.test.ts src/main/runtime/workspaces/removal/worktree-teardown.test.ts\",\"pnpm run test:e2e -- tests/e2e/terminal-tab-close-restart-persistence.spec.ts --workers=1\",\"pnpm run test:e2e -- tests/e2e/terminal-parked-close-retirement.spec.ts --workers=1\",\"pnpm run test:e2e -- tests/e2e/agent-descendant-process-kill.spec.ts --workers=1\",\"pnpm run test:e2e -- tests/e2e/paired-cli-terminal-graph-sync-tab-retention.spec.ts --workers=1\",\"pnpm run test:e2e -- tests/e2e/headless-serve-cli-terminal-retention-parity.spec.ts --workers=1\"]",
        "Audit3437 complete prior testFiles before completed-worker-retirement-resume retirement: [\"src/main/runtime/terminal/surface/orca-runtime-terminal-close-continuity.test.ts\",\"src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts\",\"src/main/agent-hooks/server/testing/authority/server-pane-authority.test.ts\",\"src/main/ipc/agent-hooks.test.ts\",\"src/main/ipc/agent-pane-authority-ownership.test.ts\",\"src/main/persistence/terminal-topology/persistence-pane-identity-migration.test.ts\",\"src/main/persistence/terminal-topology/persistence-pty-binding-reconciliation.test.ts\",\"src/main/pty/process-retirement/pty-descendant-termination.test.ts\",\"src/main/daemon/sessions/testing/session.test.ts\",\"src/main/daemon/terminal-host/testing/terminal-host.test.ts\",\"src/main/providers/local-pty/local-pty-provider-shutdown.test.ts\",\"src/main/runtime/workspaces/removal/worktree-teardown.test.ts\",\"src/renderer/src/store/slices/agent-status/agent-pane-authority.test.ts\",\"src/renderer/src/store/terminals/terminal-pane-detach-agent-identity.test.ts\",\"src/renderer/src/store/terminals/terminal-tab-retirement-store.test.ts\",\"tests/e2e/completed-worker-retirement-resume.unit.test.ts\",\"src/renderer/src/components/shared/kill-all-terminal-surfaces.test.ts\",\"tests/e2e/terminal-tab-close-restart-persistence.spec.ts\",\"tests/e2e/terminal-parked-close-retirement.spec.ts\",\"tests/e2e/agent-descendant-process-kill.spec.ts\",\"tests/e2e/paired-cli-terminal-graph-sync-tab-retention.spec.ts\",\"tests/e2e/headless-serve-cli-terminal-retention-parity.spec.ts\"]",
        "Audit3437 complete prior assertionRefs before completed-worker-retirement-resume retirement: [{\"file\":\"src/main/runtime/terminal/surface/orca-runtime-terminal-close-continuity.test.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"final-pane terminal.close remains pending until one renderer durability acknowledgement retires the persisted tab and layout\",\"final-pane externally owned teardown commits session retirement before PTY stop, tolerates duplicate exit retirement, and preserves an unrelated live canary\",\"post-ack workspace-session loss falls back to renderer cleanup and verified PTY teardown while every pre-ack retirement error remains non-destructive\",\"renderer reload with the same provider-attested PTY incarnation preserves the exact handle\",\"same-id replacement incarnation publishes a new handle and makes the old handle deterministically stale\",\"hard graph loss and preallocated-handle supersession make the retained renderer handle deterministically stale\"]},{\"file\":\"tests/e2e/terminal-tab-close-restart-persistence.spec.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"a durability-acknowledged whole-tab close leaves zero terminal tabs and provider sessions after restart\"]},{\"file\":\"tests/e2e/completed-worker-retirement-resume.unit.test.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"explicit close revokes the exact live recovery record both before and after PTY exit removes the tab, while PTY exit alone preserves interrupted-session recovery\"]},{\"file\":\"tests/e2e/terminal-parked-close-retirement.spec.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"a long-lived exact PTY remains alive after its terminal view is parked\",\"closing the parked tab removes the exact PTY from the provider inventory and the visible tab model\"]},{\"file\":\"tests/e2e/paired-cli-terminal-graph-sync-tab-retention.spec.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"an attached-window desktop host publishes the CLI-created terminal under the renderer publication epoch it inherits, proving the vulnerable classification path was taken rather than a headless or serve/SSH-shaped one\",\"with the target as the first host-created terminal, a renderer graph sync leaves the `terminal.create` tab in the host session inventory still naming its original daemon PTY\",\"the original fixture process answers a write through that handle with its own pid and a single READY line, so a respawned replacement cannot pass as a survivor\",\"the paired client applied that same sync and kept the tab with no replacement or resume tab appended\",\"an unrelated workspace keeps its own CLI terminal and PTY, and the client raises no direct local connection attempt or uncaught renderer error\"]},{\"file\":\"tests/e2e/headless-serve-cli-terminal-retention-parity.spec.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"a windowless serve host publishes host-created terminals under a headless epoch, never a renderer one, which is why it cannot reach the window-conditioned prune the desktop arm reproduces\",\"a later CLI dispatch leaves the earlier host-created terminal in the serve-host inventory still bound to its original PTY\",\"both original fixture processes answer writes through their own handles after the later dispatch\",\"the paired client mirrors exactly those two tabs with no replacement or resume tab appended, no direct local connection attempt, and no uncaught renderer error\"]},{\"file\":\"src/main/ipc/agent-pane-authority-ownership.test.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"pane authority transfer accepts only the canonical legacy/scoped runtime handle bound to the authoritative pane\"]},{\"file\":\"src/main/runtime/workspaces/removal/worktree-teardown.test.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"owned provider shutdowns start together so process-table snapshots can coalesce within a batch\",\"inventories above 32 sessions never exceed 32 concurrent provider shutdowns\"]},{\"file\":\"tests/e2e/agent-descendant-process-kill.spec.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"a detached-pgid descendant is alive before agent PTY kill and absent afterward\"]}]",
        "Audit3832 deliberately retires76 authored/79 finite cases:75 runtime compatibility cases/78 finite cases across14 fragments, plus one localization extractor default-flag case. Three whole runtime fragments are deleted;27 authored/30 finite cases remain across the reviewed sources. This gate retains only its own selected scope; no equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/native/remote evidence is claimed. Runtime component A: Audit3828 composes3822 with independent3824: deliberately retires49 authored/52 finite cases from seven compatibility fragments, leaving15 authored/18 finite cases and deleting two entire fragments. Accepted losses: positive folder-worker recovery/materialization and reveal deadline; persisted-key normalization and legacy split/group/focus projection; fixed stale CAS refusal; occupied/alias/restored/preallocated terminal-handle variants; fixed OpenCode/Cursor/Claude/Codex/Antigravity classification, readiness, title and management examples; direct private-map browser authority projections; browser-focus and OMP title projection; already-aborted claim cleanup. Additional3824 loss: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-02.spec.ts :: does not poll a wrapper foreground for a speculative CLI prompt send :: Speculative retryForegroundWrappers:false check must return false on a wrapper after one foreground read, without polling the supplied later codex response. These real bounded alarms are deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained callbacks are unchanged and provide only their own bounded scope, not equivalent replacement. Historical receipts do not validate reduced callbacks. No fresh runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser evidence or full transitive closure is claimed. Runtime component B: Audit3834 deliberately retires26 authored/26 finite cases from seven fresh compatibility fragments, leaving10/10 and deleting the one-case saved-binding reattachment fragment. Original position58 is excluded: its existing substantive3578 KEEP7 review remains historical, with no fresh credit. Accepted losses: fixed hook/provider-session identities and stale metadata refusal; decorative/pre-title foreground ordering variants; saved-binding surface reattachment; saved-row exit ghost removal and silent activation selection; unsupported headless wake; positive pending materialization/group projections; per-caller navigation selection; positive SSH hydration/read partition; laptop mobile publication/buffer and background/pending/status projections; abnormal/unregistered SSH grace, normal-exit refusal, persisted SSH hydration, positive serve reattachment, pending-agent launch arguments and direct seeded running-launch admission guard. These are real bounded alarms deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained cases preserve their own distinct deferred foreground coalescing, usable handle continuity, stale inventory refresh, concurrent browser snapshot preservation, renderer graph fencing, caller dedup isolation, SSH partition writes, runtime split lifetime, independent relay-ready publication, lease admission/state/expiry. The direct running-launch no-spawn guard alarm is deliberately retired; no remaining owning-launch refusal coverage is claimed. Historical runs do not validate reduced callbacks. No equivalent replacement, runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser result or full transitive closure is claimed. Additional extractor loss: config/scripts/localization/source-extraction/audit-localization-native-dialogs.test.mjs :: does not change the existing renderer scan by default :: Default options must omit the five native-only fields in this supplied snippet. No equivalent replacement is claimed."
      ],
      "demotionRule": "Keep experimental or demote to protection none if exact PTY disappearance flakes, a sibling/detached pane is retired, late hooks can recreate closed authority, or a renderer graph sync retires a host-created tab that no explicit close retired."
    },
    {
      "id": "terminal-session.daemon-generation-reconnect-safety",
      "title": "Negotiated close intent protects live daemon-generation terminals",
      "maturity": "experimental",
