      "coveredPlatforms": ["linux", "macos", "windows"],
      "coveredProviders": ["daemon", "runtime"],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit4362 intentionally deletes the imported stale-waiter retry and manually assembled OSC9999 mobile-republish cases, plus the mocked missing-worktree cleanup suite (4 authored / 5 finite cases in three suites). Lost alarms include repeated unread worker_done pointers, working-to-waiting mobile status publication, missing-worktree filtering, and scoped daemon shutdown with unrelated duplicate identities. No replacement coverage or new platform proof is claimed. Audit3994 retires two authored callbacks imported by the shared construction test driver: split OSC 9999 carry and rendererless status ownership, plus OpenCode permission text taking priority in status and tui-idle refusal. Remaining imports and selectors keep their scope. No equivalent replacement or fresh gate execution is claimed. Audit3881 intentionally removes the entire legacy E2EE channel and mobile socket-wiring test suites and the v2 additive runtime-capability refusal callback, without equivalent replacement. Those deleted suites leave current selectors and that v2 assertion alias is retired. Retained v2 replay/queue-counter cases do not establish the removed capability refusal. Reduced test bytes/selectors have no fresh execution in this static packet; independent dated daemon E2E receipts retain their complete original scope. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Git owner cleanup retires the mixed request-connection suite under repository test policy, including its encrypted request cancellation and cached paired-desktop authentication alarms, without equivalent replacement. Current commands and assertion references omit the retired suite; dated evidence retains its original scope and does not validate this reduced set. Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The retained runtime registration driver loses three complete imported fragments: changed-working-label title facts and suppressed-frame tracked snapshots; refusing SSH GitLab MR-base lookup before local Git/glab calls; and missing folder-workspace path creation/update refusal before spawn/store mutation. These alarms are intentionally lost. Other imported fragments and separately rooted dated receipts are unchanged; they are not equivalent replacement coverage.  Audit2153: Reduced sources intentionally lose the forwarding smoke and retire an unrelated current selector; historical runs do not validate changed source bytes. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2095 current-parent preparation2126: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2090 (sources2088/2089): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2086 (sources2082/2083): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2076 (sources2073/2074): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-part-02.spec.ts: recovers a moved SSH pane through the tab it now sits in, not the one its lease froze; reports a plain expired orphan; does not report a pane whose only recent lease was superseded; does not report a pane whose only recent lease had its relay id recycled; picks the eligible orphan over a superseded predecessor that matches first; collects the same tabs the per-tab reader reports, in one sweep of the leases; reports no candidate when no lease names any of the worktree tabs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/runtime-availability.spec.ts: starts unavailable with no authoritative window; reports the configured Windows terminal shell on status; reports floating workspace availability from settings on status; polls floating tabs with targeted PTY liveness and no repo/provider inventory; hydrates persisted tabs when the store cannot report repos; advertises browser screencast only when a renderer window is available; routes mobile Codex reset consumption through the account mutation coordinator; maps a definite pre-provider rejection into an authoritative current snapshot. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2020: The CLI WebSocket source retains old-protocol refusal only; its paired-open, capability, timeout and admission projection examples are removed. No daemon-generation coverage is transferred to that callback. Both independent daemon E2E receipts remain unchanged at their original commands; the reduced unit selector has no fresh result. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1983: Delete the reasonless-close scalar suite and optional-capability socket forwarding alias. Delete the mocked close-attribution topology field-inventory suite and its aliases/selectors; preserve independent dated receipts. Changed-source prior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1959 (sources 1957:11, 1957:35, 1957:36): The fixture-supplied repository roundtrip, isolated capability metadata readback, parser/default-timer/size-threshold/internal failure-counter examples and standalone handshake-only replay example are removed. Source11 retains real encrypted multi-client event ordering, reconnect snapshot and multiplex delivery under synthetic runtime state, and does not establish the broad handshake-to-reasonless-close refusal alias; retire that whole assertion object. Source36 capability metadata readback alias is retired. Source35 retains the actual v2 runtime-only metadata/downgrade refusal callback and captured mutating-trace fresh-nonce rejection; its mapped mobile-v2 refusal alias remains within modeled credential lookup scope. Both independent daemon E2E dated receipts remain byte-exact with their original commands and results. No historical passed receipt is narrowed or transferred to changed source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, physical provider/PTY, live remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed by this metadata packet. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1939 (sources1934/1935): Retain actual parked exit/disposal/cancel/leaf progression using injected exit and close adapters. The retained last-watcher case checks exact lifecyclePtyId, but no retained callback establishes the whole existing replacement-or-sibling-incarnation alias. Retire that broad assertion object rather than transfer partial support. Capability admission, static fields and duplicate routing examples are intentionally lost; unchanged daemon E2E receipts remain scoped to their own commands. Preserve meaningful remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged dated receipts within their original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh gate execution evidence in this metadata packet. No equivalent replacement, physical watcher/PTY/provider, live SSH/remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): The browser auth capability-advertisement case is removed in this audit; its direct encrypted-auth literal alarm is lost. Retained lifecycle evidence is not an equivalent replacement. Historical run commands and results remain historical. Recorded native Windows evidence covers the v21/v22/v23/v24/v25 named-pipe matrix. The deterministic daemon harness covers capable and legacy paired-runtime request shapes against live v25/v26 PTYs in separate worktrees, plus an unrelated control. Host/renderer tests cover old servers, missing liveness, stale publications, reused claims, split parents, explicit user intent, cross-profile isolation, remote runtime clients, SSH-provider routing, and WSL boundaries. A headed host paired to a separate live client, headless serve parity, Linux, SSH, and WSL remain explicit gaps. The audit removed private-router tests of mocked kill results and log fields. Their isolated success/failure attribution and pending-spawn tolerance alarms are no longer registered here; live lifecycle evidence does not establish equivalent log coverage. The isolated close-intent suite was removed. web-runtime-session.test.ts no longer supplies the lifecycle-close or old-server method-not-found assertions formerly referenced here. Their direct partition and RPC-shape alarms are lost; retained live daemon evidence does not establish equivalent coverage. The broad mirror fixture retains user-close suppression, refused-close reconciliation and optimistic reorder only. Its earlier reconnect/incarnation and projection examples no longer establish current daemon-generation coverage. Those narrow alarms are lost; other daemon evidence is not equivalent replacement coverage. Audit1318: src/shared/remote-runtime/control/remote-runtime-shared-control-connection.test.ts: Retain real local encrypted WebSocket regressions for pre-ready socket replacement preserving a request, close-before-ready logical subscription cleanup, unrelated RPC surviving another deadline, and pending setup abort leaving a sibling pending. Host server is synthetic and uses production crypto; kept scenarios also retain internal diagnostics/memory assertions unchanged. Remove happy routing, authority-envelope, unknown-ID/log, cleanup enum, binary, keepalive/liveness and production-budget/private socket inventories; intentionally lose those alarms, no physical host authorization, independent crypto or remote provider claim. Reduced selectors need fresh validation; historical full-suite receipts do not validate the changed coverage. No equivalent replacement or physical-provider claim. Audit1383: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-native-chat-setup.spec.ts reduced. Lose command-list/receipt/default/background activation matrices whose provider spawn returns canned IDs. Retained test proves actual tab allocation separation, not terminal startup. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected receipts and their platform/provider/budget claims remain scoped to unchanged selectors. Changed optional selectors have no new execution result. Audit1401: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-duplicate-pty-repair.spec.ts removed. Loses listing-on-already-repaired-data alarm; it never established runtime repair invocation. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-split-agent-tab.spec.ts removed. Loses actual mobile split sibling shell versus recorded-agent resume command alarms; no equivalent coverage asserted. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-native-chat-setup.spec.ts removed. Loses separate setup/startup tab result in that manually assembled path. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts reduced. Driver registration/import of a whole-deleted selected spec is removed; directly authored cases remain unchanged. No extra authored removal credit. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected receipts remain unchanged and apply only to their unchanged selectors. Changed optional selectors have no new execution result.",
