      "invariant": "Reconnect, replay, or lifecycle observations from a viewer that negotiated explicit close intent must never kill a live PTY. A capable reasonless close must keep and republish; a legacy paired viewer must retain current-main behavior because its intentional close and cleanup echo are wire-identical. Lifecycle close requires the exact observed publication, terminal, environment, and authoritative liveness, never signals a process, and leaves renderer-owned or partial-split retirement to its owner. Legacy daemon hello and warm reattachment remain non-destructive.",
      "oracle": "Audit4362 intentionally deletes the imported stale-waiter retry and manually assembled OSC9999 mobile-republish cases, plus the mocked missing-worktree cleanup suite (4 authored / 5 finite cases in three suites). Lost alarms include repeated unread worker_done pointers, working-to-waiting mobile status publication, missing-worktree filtering, and scoped daemon shutdown with unrelated duplicate identities. No replacement coverage or new platform proof is claimed. Audit3881 intentionally removes the entire legacy E2EE channel and mobile socket-wiring test suites and the v2 additive runtime-capability refusal callback, without equivalent replacement. Those deleted suites leave current selectors and that v2 assertion alias is retired. Retained v2 replay/queue-counter cases do not establish the removed capability refusal. Reduced test bytes/selectors have no fresh execution in this static packet; independent dated daemon E2E receipts retain their complete original scope. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit3832 deliberately retires76 authored/79 finite cases:75 runtime compatibility cases/78 finite cases across14 fragments, plus one localization extractor default-flag case. Three whole runtime fragments are deleted;27 authored/30 finite cases remain across the reviewed sources. This gate retains only its own selected scope; no equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/native/remote evidence is claimed. Runtime component A: Audit3828 composes3822 with independent3824: deliberately retires49 authored/52 finite cases from seven compatibility fragments, leaving15 authored/18 finite cases and deleting two entire fragments. Accepted losses: positive folder-worker recovery/materialization and reveal deadline; persisted-key normalization and legacy split/group/focus projection; fixed stale CAS refusal; occupied/alias/restored/preallocated terminal-handle variants; fixed OpenCode/Cursor/Claude/Codex/Antigravity classification, readiness, title and m