reservation, renderer graph fencing, caller dedup isolation, SSH partition writes, runtime split lifetime, independent relay-ready publication, lease admission/state/expiry. The direct running-launch no-spawn guard alarm is deliberately retired; no remaining owning-launch refusal coverage is claimed. Historical runs do not validate reduced callbacks. No equivalent replacement, runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser result or full transitive closure is claimed. Additional extractor loss: config/scripts/localization/source-extraction/audit-localization-native-dialogs.test.mjs :: does not change the existing renderer scan by default :: Default options must omit the five native-only fields in this supplied snippet. No equivalent replacement is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit3814 deliberately retires60 authored/60 finite cases:53runtime compatibility cases,4native XCTest methods and3Python clipboard methods, including the entire StableElementIndexes suite. Clipboard cuts retire the one-over-cap sample, incoming-offer destruction trace and sequential20-copy replay; actual wire, FD/pipe, startup and Xvfb/GTK boundaries remain without equivalent replacement claims. Accepted losses include narrow terminal-send payload/provider projections, legacy and direct no-op/error permutations, timing/work-count examples, private state/title/activity projections and fixture-driven readiness examples, individually enumerated below. These include real bounded production alarms consciously retired for marginal value; retained failed writes, duplicate submission, stale capture, transcript/ring and allocation fences are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or complete transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3806 deliberately retires40 authored/40 finite runtime compatibility cases, including the terminal-side-effect-facts-part03 headless-snapsho