        "Audit2086 (sources2082/2083): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-06.spec.ts: suppresses saved mobile agent status when live evidence is the Claude agents screen; suppresses saved mobile agent status when the current terminal title is neutral; suppresses saved mobile agent status when fresh live OSC title is Claude agents; keeps saved PTY bindings pending until the runtime knows the PTY is connected; refreshes daemon PTY liveness before publishing mobile session tabs; does not invalidate a newly spawned SSH pane from an overlapping stale process list. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/pty-title-status.spec.ts: associates controller PTYs with mixed-case Windows and UNC cwd paths; uses OSC titles rather than controller process names for rendererless PTYs; ignores the bare cursor-agent native title so synthesized spinner state survives; only records the bare Cursor native title via the stale-working clear; refuses a bare Cursor title while the foreground read is unavailable; does not treat a bare Cursor title as an agent once the shell owns the foreground; accepts a bare Cursor title when the foreground read confirms cursor-agent; refuses a bare Cursor title on a runtime pty with no controller attached; clears a stale working title after 3s of title-less output; cancels the stale-title timer when the PTY exits; keeps stale-title timers isolated per PTY. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/paired-settings.spec.ts: projects runtime-backed settings to paired clients; updates quick commands without widening general paired settings payloads; applies native-chat option deltas atomically on the runtime host; keeps a future-launch default when an older client asks to prune from inventory; preserves concurrent additions after forty quick commands; accepts runtime-backed setting updates from paired clients; broadcasts visibility default changes to paired clients; re