        "Audit2076 (sources2073/2074): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-part-02.spec.ts: recovers a moved SSH pane through the tab it now sits in, not the one its lease froze; reports a plain expired orphan; does not report a pane whose only recent lease was superseded; does not report a pane whose only recent lease had its relay id recycled; picks the eligible orphan over a superseded predecessor that matches first; collects the same tabs the per-tab reader reports, in one sweep of the leases; reports no candidate when no lease names any of the worktree tabs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/runtime-availability.spec.ts: starts unavailable with no authoritative window; reports the configured Windows terminal shell on status; reports floating workspace availability from settings on status; polls floating tabs with targeted PTY liveness and no repo/provider inventory; hydrates persisted tabs when the store cannot report repos; advertises browser screencast only when a renderer window is available; routes mobile Codex reset consumption through the account mutation coordinator; maps a definite pre-provider rejection into an authoritative current snapshot. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence.",
        "Audit2070 (sources2068/2069): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts: ordinary registration cleanup removes only await import('./orca-runtime-tests/hooks-and-hosted-review.spec'). src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-archive-hook-gate.spec.ts: removes and records the waiver when the failure is explicitly overridden; removes without an override record when the hook succeeds; removes when the hook is configured but not requested; removes when no archive hook is configured; holds a desktop removal in the same repo until this one is accepted; joins a desktop removal of the same worktree accepted while this one waited. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-ps-agent-row-dismissal.spec.ts: drops the row as soon as the user dismisses it, without waiting for the PTY to exit; tells paired clients to republish on the transition and on the dismissal; rejoins a row through its %s handle after pane ownership clears. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/hooks-and-hosted-review.spec.ts: reports an error when the SSH filesystem provider is unavailable; reports an SSH orca.yaml as an error without reading any filesystem; reports ok for a local repo hook check; reads SSH issue commands as absent and drops writes without touching any filesystem; allows host integration slug helpers for SSH repos through provider-aware GitHub clients; routes runtime GitHub repo identity helpers through the selected WSL project runtime; routes runtime GitHub issue and work-item actions through the selected WSL project runtime; pins explicit origin preference on runtime open-by-number work item lookups; forwards check-details cancellation without local Git overrides. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current liter