        "Audit1959 (sources 1957:11, 1957:35, 1957:36): The fixture-supplied repository roundtrip, isolated capability metadata readback, parser/default-timer/size-threshold/internal failure-counter examples and standalone handshake-only replay example are removed. Source11 retains real encrypted multi-client event ordering, reconnect snapshot and multiplex delivery under synthetic runtime state, and does not establish the broad handshake-to-reasonless-close refusal alias; retire that whole assertion object. Source36 capability metadata readback alias is retired. Source35 retains the actual v2 runtime-only metadata/downgrade refusal callback and captured mutating-trace fresh-nonce rejection; its mapped mobile-v2 refusal alias remains within modeled credential lookup scope. Both independent daemon E2E dated receipts remain byte-exact with their original commands and results. No historical passed receipt is narrowed or transferred to changed source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, physical provider/PTY, live remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed by this metadata packet.",
        "Audit1959 historical original assertionRefs object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active execution evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/remote-runtime-request-connection.integration.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"the real encrypted WebSocket handshake binds close-intent capability through authenticated socket state and RPC context to reasonless-close refusal\"\n          ]\n        }",
        "Audit1959 historical original assertionRefs object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active execution evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/rpc/e2ee-channel.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"runtime capabilities are accepted only from encrypted authentication metadata, not the unauthenticated hello\"\n          ]\n        }",
        "Audit1983: Delete the reasonless-close scalar suite and optional-capability socket forwarding alias. Delete the mocked close-attribution topology field-inventory suite and its aliases/selectors; preserve independent dated receipts. Changed-source prior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed.",
        "Audit1983 historical original commands object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active execution evidence or replacement coverage:\n\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts src/main/runtime/remote-runtime-request-connection.integration.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/runtime-close-attribution-topology.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/session-tabs/session-tabs.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/e2ee-channel.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/e2ee-channel-v2.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile-socket-wiring.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/runtime-client-capabilities.test.ts src/shared/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-client.test.ts src/shared/remote-runtime/requests/remote-runtime-request-connection.test.ts src/shared/remote-runtime/control/remote-runtime-shared-control-connection.test.ts src/cli/runtime/websocket-transport.test.ts src/renderer/src/web/web-runtime-client.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-tab-actions.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-close-incarnation.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/parking/output-watchers/terminal-parked-tab-watchers.test.ts\"",
        "Audit1983 historical original testFiles object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active execution evidence or replacement coverage:\n\"src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/session-tabs/session-tabs.test.ts\"",
        "Audit1983 historical original assertionRefs object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active execution evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/session-tabs/session-tabs.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"in-process and capable-runtime reasonless closes refuse while legacy runtime/mobile and explicit current user closes retain current-main destructive semantics\"\n          ]\n        }",
        "Audit1983 historical original assertionRefs object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active execution evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile-socket-wiring.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"the optional client capability is captured from legacy encrypted authentication and bound to the authenticated runtime-scoped socket identity\"\n          ]\n        }",
        "Audit1983 historical original testFiles object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active execution evidence or replacement coverage:\n\"src/main/runtime/rpc/runtime-close-attribution-topology.test.ts\"",
        "Audit1983 historical original assertionRefs object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active execution evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/rpc/runtime-close-attribution-topology.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"remote, legacy, reconnect, stale, concurrent, cross-worktree, and unowned close spans retain authoritative runtime, target, requester, decision, and outcome identities without serializing the bearer credential\",\n            \"close attribution adds no terminal inventory scan or provider fanout\"\n          ]\n        }",
        "Audit2020: The CLI WebSocket source retains old-protocol refusal only; its paired-open, capability, timeout and admission projection examples are removed. No daemon-generation coverage is transferred to that callback. Both independent daemon E2E receipts remain unchanged at their original commands; the reduced unit selector has no fresh result.",
        "Audit2052 (source2049): The ordinary orca-runtime.test.ts registrar drops seven imports of deliberately deleted low-value runtime suites. Their mock capability/agent-presence/environment/title/deduplication and batching alarms are intentionally lost without replacement; remaining imports retain their original order. The runtime handle-contract registrar separately drops the deleted tab-collision registration. Unrelated dated evidenceRuns remain unchanged and do not validate reduced-source bytes or selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed.",
        "Audit2056 (sources2054/2055): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts: ordinary registration cleanup removes only await import('./orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-14.spec'). src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-side-effect-facts-part-03.spec.ts: arms the stale-title timer for a seeded working title; arms the Command Code scrape from the noted spawn command; prefers the tracked title over a stale renderer lastTitle in the hydration seed; writes recent output into the current runtime output map; uses a later title handler replacement with the runtime receiver; calls the current injected listener with the runtime receiver; keeps optional reconciliation lazy after its callback is removed. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-14.spec.ts: lists them, so a paired client can mirror a migrated editor; closes one by retiring it from the host session; keeps an unsaved draft unless the close is forced; shares aggregate work but leaves a replacement pending promise alone; lets a targeted refresh finish while an aggregate refresh waits; refuses a close when the store lacks %s before the guard; keeps a later missing %s on the original caught failure path. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed.",
        "Audit2061 (sources2059/2060): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts: ordinary registration cleanup removes only await import('./orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-headless-chat-rebuild.spec'); await import('./orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-cold-serve-hydrate.spec'); await import('./orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-execution-host.spec'); await import('./orca-runtime-tests/terminal-spawn-dispatch.spec'). src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/headless-snapshots-part-02.spec.ts: replaces a cwd parsed before late WSL context with the provider cwd; keeps a live WSL cwd that arrives during late-context snapshot recovery; infers local reconstructed WSL context from a WSL UNC worktree; clears stale terminal file URI hostnames after empty-host OSC7 cwd updates; serializes SSH headless OSC7 cwd as POSIX when the desktop runtime is on Windows; keeps Windows SSH OSC7 cwd as a drive path when the desktop runtime is POSIX; serializes Windows SSH headless OSC7 cwd as a drive path on POSIX desktops; infers restored SSH connection identity from app-scoped PTY ids. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-headless-chat-rebuild.spec.ts: survives the rebuild that closing a saved editor tab forces; keeps its place in the tab order when the host lists the workspace again; lists tabs to phones in the order desktop clients draw after a rebuild; keeps the place a window gave a chat across a graph resend before the chat is restored. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-cold-serve-hydrate.spec.ts: lists every persisted terminal of a windowless host after a cold restart; lists every persisted terminal in the all-worktrees inventory after a cold restart; lists persisted editor tabs beside the terminals after a cold restart; restores a persisted split group layout on the cold rebuild; restores the saved active group of a split even when it is not the first group; falls back to the active tab group when the saved active group was not restored; keeps the headless group active when there is no persisted split; keeps phone and CLI creates in the group they joined across a cold restart. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-failed-retry.spec.ts: lists the leftover with its error, though Git no longer does; takes the normal delete once Git registers a checkout at the path again; joins a retry another client started while this Delete listed Git; shows the failed row with its error, not the scan cached before the delete. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-execution-host.spec.ts: refuses an SSH row whose host is unreachable instead of deleting here; refuses a runtime row with no nested SSH target rather than deleting locally; refuses a runtime row that also names a nested SSH target; retains runtime purge dispatch in a recovery job; uses the runtime helper override before resuming an interrupted removal; uses the runtime helper override before retrying a failed removal; captures the watcher callback and retains its job-host receiver; reads the current runtime removal queue. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-spawn-dispatch.spec.ts: reports the spawn request before it leaves for the pty controller; reports it even when the spawn itself then fails; does not report it when the create fails before any spawn request; captures the admission method before reading the incarnation; captures the record method before evaluating its state object; skips database payload serialization when no database exists; skips a throwing database payload when no database exists; keeps the database method and receiver captured before its payload; captures the canonical map method before a binding getter changes it; completes the captured replacement fence without another map lookup. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed.",
        "Module layout policy correction: retire the remaining program-status-osc.spec.ts event-projection case (production/mock-derived pane-key oracle) and sign-in timeout case (real setTimeout wait with Date-only fake clocks). The runtime test registrar no longer imports that file. No replacement coverage or fresh execution is claimed for these losses; historical receipts retain their original source scope.",
        "Module layout policy correction: retire the two remaining worktree-ps-agent-row-dismissal.spec.ts registrations. The remint/dismissal/exit case computed expected snapshotVersion increments from a production snapshot and used real-clock vi.waitFor; the legacy OSC case derived its expected paneKey from the production layout-owner switch. The runtime registrar no longer imports this file. These public projection scenarios have no replacement coverage or fresh execution claimed; all historical receipts and earlier loss notes retain their original source scope.",
        "Audit2153: Intentionally retire the ordinary fake-create event-forwarding registration from src/main/runtime/rpc/server/remote-runtime-request-connection.integration.test.ts. The two retained callbacks prove encrypted fanout/reconnect and physical connection multiplexing under a fake business runtime; neither establishes close-intent authorization, actual terminal sleep, or equivalent replacement for the removed forwarding smoke. Remove this unrelated current close-safety selector. Existing assertionRefs and dated evidenceRuns remain byte-identical and scoped to their own source/commands. No fresh execution or platform/provider coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit2153 historical original commands item, preserved verbatim; retired selector is not active execution evidence: \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/server/remote-runtime-request-connection.integration.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/e2ee-channel.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/e2ee-channel-v2.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile-socket-wiring.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/runtime-client-capabilities.test.ts src/shared/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-client.test.ts src/shared/remote-runtime/requests/remote-runtime-request-connection.test.ts src/shared/remote-runtime/control/remote-runtime-shared-control-connection.test.ts src/cli/runtime/websocket-transport.test.ts src/renderer/src/web/web-runtime-client.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-tab-actions.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-close-incarnation.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/parking/output-watchers/terminal-parked-tab-watchers.test.ts\"",
        "Audit2153 historical original testFiles item, preserved verbatim; retired selector is not active execution evidence: \"src/main/runtime/rpc/server/remote-runtime-request-connection.integration.test.ts\"",
        "Terminal/runtime defining-owner cleanup retires complete parking timer, lifecycle, mocked close/disposal and render/flip/mount work-count cases under repository test policy. The retained watcher source has only two literal-oracle coverage decisions; the retained cold-parking hook source has only the layout-PTY exemption invalidation case. Lost alarms include cooldown/measure/pin wakeups, split exit/close attribution and cancellation, watcher disposal/restart, flood timer rearm, worktree verdict damping, and destroyed-transport cold restore. No equivalent replacement coverage or execution pass for the reduced cases is claimed; prior dated receipts retain their original scope.",
        "Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The retained runtime registration driver loses three complete imported fragments: changed-working-label title facts and suppressed-frame tracked snapshots; refusing SSH GitLab MR-base lookup before local Git/glab calls; and missing folder-workspace path creation/update refusal before spawn/store mutation. These alarms are intentionally lost. Other imported fragments and separately rooted dated receipts are unchanged; they are not equivalent replacement coverage.  Original scope text is retained as the exact suffix of coverageNotes/oracle; historical evidence is unchanged.",
        "Git owner cleanup retires the mixed request-connection suite under repository test policy, including its encrypted request cancellation and cached paired-desktop authentication alarms, without equivalent replacement. Current commands and assertion references omit the retired suite; dated evidence retains its original scope and does not validate this reduced set.",
        "Audit3774 (independent peer expansion of3773): deliberately retire7authored/13potential expanded registrations across4whole suites: standalone truncated8-byte E2EE guard; open/empty readiness null fast-path; capability parser acceptance/atomic malformed-array bounds; phone/delegated-parent/desktop/in-process creator provenance projections. These are real guard/policy alarms accepted as low marginal value, not tautologies. No equivalent replacement, authenticated-refusal, observer delivery, persisted visibility, synchronous scheduling or fresh execution is claimed. Prior dated receipts retain their exact original scopes and do not validate the changed/reduced current selector. Independent daemon E2E receipts remain scoped to their own unchanged commands.",
        "Audit3774 historical original active selector/assertion arrays, preserved verbatim; no replacement coverage claim.\ncommands:\n[\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/e2ee/e2ee-channel.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/e2ee/e2ee-channel-v2.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/mobile-socket-wiring.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/callers/runtime-client-capabilities.test.ts src/shared/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-client.test.ts src/shared/remote-runtime/control/remote-runtime-shared-control-connection.test.ts src/cli/runtime/websocket-transport.test.ts src/renderer/src/web/web-runtime-client.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-tab-actions.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-close-incarnation.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/parking/output-watchers/terminal-parked-tab-watchers.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/daemon-generation-reconnect-safety.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headless --workers=1\",\n        \"pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/daemon-generation-legacy-close-safety.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headless --workers=1\"\n      ]\ntestFiles:\n[\n        \"src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/e2ee/e2ee-channel.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/e2ee/e2ee-channel-v2.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/mobile-socket-wiring.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/rpc/callers/runtime-client-capabilities.test.ts\",\n        \"src/shared/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-client.test.ts\",\n        \"src/shared/remote-runtime/control/remote-runtime-shared-control-connection.test.ts\",\n        \"src/cli/runtime/websocket-transport.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/web/web-runtime-client.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-tab-actions.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-close-incarnation.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/parking/output-watchers/terminal-parked-tab-watchers.test.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/daemon-generation-reconnect-safety.spec.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/daemon-generation-legacy-close-safety.spec.ts\"\n      ]\nassertionRefs:\n[\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/daemon-generation-legacy-close-safety.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"one identified capable viewer and one legacy viewer issue byte-identical sequential reasonless closes while a third viewer lists every target before, between, and after but issues zero closes\",\n            \"capable v25/v26 PTY root/descendant incarnations in separate worktrees survive, answer post-close input, and produce zero shutdown calls and zero daemon session-killed events\",\n            \"legacy v25/v26 PTY root/descendant incarnations die through ordered immediate shutdown calls with one daemon session-killed event each, matching current-main behavior\",\n            \"an unaddressed fifth-worktree PTY root and descendant survive with zero kill events, excluding global fanout\",\n            \"the JSON reconstruction records request order, negotiated capabilities, viewer connection, worktree/tab/PTY ids, daemon PID/protocol, call site, and exact before/after process liveness\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/daemon-generation-reconnect-safety.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"the production scanner discovers v21/v22/v23/v24/v25 from v26 and every generation accepts repeated client hellos while every exact daemon, PTY-root, and descendant incarnation remains alive\",\n            \"desktop and two remote profiles repeat lifecycle closes before and after client relaunch with zero session-killed events\",\n            \"shutdown-dispose-failed drops named-pipe authority within the deadline and exact fixture cleanup leaves no process tree\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/e2ee/e2ee-channel-v2.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\"mobile E2EE v2 continues to reject additive runtime capability metadata\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/rpc/callers/runtime-client-capabilities.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"the authenticated capability parser accepts only bounded string arrays and rejects malformed or oversized input\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/shared/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-client.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"one-shot and subscription runtime clients remain compatible while sending encrypted client authentication\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]",
        "Audit3832 deliberately retires76 authored/79 finite cases:75 runtime compatibility cases/78 finite cases across14 fragments, plus one localization extractor default-flag case. Three whole runtime fragments are deleted;27 authored/30 finite cases remain across the reviewed sources. This gate retains only its own selected scope; no equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/native/remote evidence is claimed. Runtime component A: Audit3828 composes3822 with independent3824: deliberately retires49 authored/52 finite cases from seven compatibility fragments, leaving15 authored/18 finite cases and deleting two entire fragments. Accepted losses: positive folder-worker recovery/materialization and reveal deadline; persisted-key normalization and legacy split/group/focus projection; fixed stale CAS refusal; occupied/alias/restored/preallocated terminal-handle variants; fixed OpenCode/Cursor/Claude/Codex/Antigravity classification, readiness, title and management examples; direct private-map browser authority projections; browser-focus and OMP title projection; already-aborted claim cleanup. Additional3824 loss: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-02.spec.ts :: does not poll a wrapper foreground for a speculative CLI prompt send :: Speculative retryForegroundWrappers:false check must return false on a wrapper after one foreground read, without polling the supplied later codex response. These real bounded alarms are deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained callbacks are unchanged and provide only their own bounded scope, not equivalent replacement. Historical receipts do not validate reduced callbacks. No fresh runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser evidence or full transitive closure is claimed. Runtime component B: Audit3834 deliberately retires26 authored/26 finite cases from seven fresh compatibility fragments, leaving10/10 and deleting the one-case saved-binding reattachment fragment. Original position58 is excluded: its existing substantive3578 KEEP7 review remains historical, with no fresh credit. Accepted losses: fixed hook/provider-session identities and stale metadata refusal; decorative/pre-title foreground ordering variants; saved-binding surface reattachment; saved-row exit ghost removal and silent activation selection; unsupported headless wake; positive pending materialization/group projections; per-caller navigation selection; positive SSH hydration/read partition; laptop mobile publication/buffer and background/pending/status projections; abnormal/unregistered SSH grace, normal-exit refusal, persisted SSH hydration, positive serve reattachment, pending-agent launch arguments and direct seeded running-launch admission guard. These are real bounded alarms deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained cases preserve their own distinct deferred foreground coalescing, usable handle continuity, stale inventory refresh, concurrent browser snapshot preservation, renderer graph fencing, caller dedup isolation, SSH partition writes, runtime split lifetime, independent relay-ready publication, lease admission/state/expiry. The direct running-launch no-spawn guard alarm is deliberately retired; no remaining owning-launch refusal coverage is claimed. Historical runs do not validate reduced callbacks. No equivalent replacement, runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser result or full transitive closure is claimed. Additional extractor loss: config/scripts/localization/source-extraction/audit-localization-native-dialogs.test.mjs :: does not change the existing renderer scan by default :: Default options must omit the five native-only fields in this supplied snippet. No equivalent replacement is claimed.",
        "Audit3881 intentionally removes the entire legacy E2EE channel and mobile socket-wiring test suites and the v2 additive runtime-capability refusal callback, without equivalent replacement. Those deleted suites leave current selectors and that v2 assertion alias is retired. Retained v2 replay/queue-counter cases do not establish the removed capability refusal. Reduced test bytes/selectors have no fresh execution in this static packet; independent dated daemon E2E receipts retain their complete original scope.",
        "Audit3881 historical original selector/assertion arrays, preserved verbatim; retired entries are not active execution evidence or replacement coverage.\ncommands:\n[\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/e2ee/e2ee-channel.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/e2ee/e2ee-channel-v2.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/mobile-socket-wiring.test.ts src/shared/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-client.test.ts src/shared/remote-runtime/control/remote-runtime-shared-control-connection.test.ts src/cli/runtime/websocket-transport.test.ts src/renderer/src/web/web-runtime-client.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-tab-actions.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-close-incarnation.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/parking/output-watchers/terminal-parked-tab-watchers.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/daemon-generation-reconnect-safety.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headless --workers=1\",\n        \"pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/daemon-generation-legacy-close-safety.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headless --workers=1\"\n      ]\ntestFiles:\n[\n        \"src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/e2ee/e2ee-channel.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/e2ee/e2ee-channel-v2.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/mobile-socket-wiring.test.ts\",\n        \"src/shared/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-client.test.ts\",\n        \"src/shared/remote-runtime/control/remote-runtime-shared-control-connection.test.ts\",\n        \"src/cli/runtime/websocket-transport.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/web/web-runtime-client.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-tab-actions.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-close-incarnation.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/parking/output-watchers/terminal-parked-tab-watchers.test.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/daemon-generation-reconnect-safety.spec.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/daemon-generation-legacy-close-safety.spec.ts\"\n      ]\nassertionRefs:\n[\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/daemon-generation-legacy-close-safety.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"one identified capable viewer and one legacy viewer issue byte-identical sequential reasonless closes while a third viewer lists every target before, between, and after but issues zero closes\",\n            \"capable v25/v26 PTY root/descendant incarnations in separate worktrees survive, answer post-close input, and produce zero shutdown calls and zero daemon session-killed events\",\n            \"legacy v25/v26 PTY root/descendant incarnations die through ordered immediate shutdown calls with one daemon session-killed event each, matching current-main behavior\",\n            \"an unaddressed fifth-worktree PTY root and descendant survive with zero kill events, excluding global fanout\",\n            \"the JSON reconstruction records request order, negotiated capabilities, viewer connection, worktree/tab/PTY ids, daemon PID/protocol, call site, and exact before/after process liveness\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/daemon-generation-reconnect-safety.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"the production scanner discovers v21/v22/v23/v24/v25 from v26 and every generation accepts repeated client hellos while every exact daemon, PTY-root, and descendant incarnation remains alive\",\n            \"desktop and two remote profiles repeat lifecycle closes before and after client relaunch with zero session-killed events\",\n            \"shutdown-dispose-failed drops named-pipe authority within the deadline and exact fixture cleanup leaves no process tree\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/e2ee/e2ee-channel-v2.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\"mobile E2EE v2 continues to reject additive runtime capability metadata\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/shared/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-client.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"one-shot and subscription runtime clients remain compatible while sending encrypted client authentication\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]",
        "Audit4389 retires the entire terminal-tab-actions mock-projection suite (8 authored/10 finite cases). Real local/host mutation, confirmation settlement and transport are mocked; routing/reason/pin/sibling spy alarms intentionally lost, with no replacement or equivalence claim. Historical entries remain archival only. Original active command: pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/mobile/e2ee/e2ee-channel-v2.test.ts src/shared/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-client.test.ts src/shared/remote-runtime/control/remote-runtime-shared-control-connection.test.ts src/cli/runtime/websocket-transport.test.ts src/renderer/src/web/web-runtime-client.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-tab-actions.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal/terminal-close-incarnation.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/parking/output-watchers/terminal-parked-tab-watchers.test.ts"
      ],
      "demotionRule": "Keep experimental or quarantine if reconnect emits session-killed for a live canary, an exact root/descendant dies, an old server receives fallback destructive close, cleanup leaks a fixture process/pipe, or the gate flakes without a proven harness defect."
    },
    {
      "id": "terminal-session.startup-cwd-missing-dir-recovery",
      "title": "Terminal working-directory recovery stays scoped and provider-safe",
      "maturity": "experimental",
      "protection": "none",
      "owner": "terminal-runtime",
      "layer": "shared-main-renderer-and-posix-shell-contract",
      "surfaces": [
        "terminal lifecycle",
        "tab creation",
        "PTY spawn",
        "startup cwd persistence",
        "long-lived Bash and Zsh OMP launches"
      ],
      "platforms": ["macos", "linux", "windows", "mobile"],
      "providers": ["local", "daemon", "ssh", "wsl", "remote-runtime"],
      "coveredPlatforms": [],
