      "coverageNotes": "Audit3368 retires whole sleeping-agent-resume and host-session-launch suites: provider-claim/deduplication, stable-pane reattach, recipe/WSL startup, callback/cancel/create-close and compatibility examples are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. The sole dated receipt is retired verbatim. With no active evidence, protection/platform/provider evidence clears and ALL commands/testFiles/assertionRefs are retired as complete original arrays in historical gaps, including selectors of surviving other sources; those sources remain in the broad suite. Prior red/green/flake accounts are historical only. No fresh runtime/provider/process/UI/mobile/mixed-version/cross-platform evidence is claimed. Audit2236: pane-fit.test.ts is reduced to terminal-identity reveal, stale-handle replacement ownership and withheld-animation-frame completion. The existing withheld-frame assertion remains exact; additional scheduling/breadcrumb, cancellation, display-none and synthetic metric examples are removed. No new execution or equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Historical dated receipts and budgets are preserved verbatim and do not validate these reduced source bytes. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2095 current-parent preparation2126: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2090 (sources2088/2089): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2086 (sources2082/2083): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2076 (sources2073/2074): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-part-02.spec.ts: recovers a moved SSH pane through the tab it now sits in, not the one its lease froze; reports a plain expired orphan; does not report a pane whose only recent lease was superseded; does not report a pane whose only recent lease had its relay id recycled; picks the eligible orphan over a superseded predecessor that matches first; collects the same tabs the per-tab reader reports, in one sweep of the leases; reports no candidate when no lease names any of the worktree tabs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/runtime-availability.spec.ts: starts unavailable with no authoritative window; reports the configured Windows terminal shell on status; reports floating workspace availability from settings on status; polls floating tabs with targeted PTY liveness and no repo/provider inventory; hydrates persisted tabs when the store cannot report repos; advertises browser screencast only when a renderer window is available; routes mobile Codex reset consumption through the account mutation coordinator; maps a definite pre-provider rejection into an authoritative current snapshot. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1685 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1683 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1640 removes low-value IPC, SSH, workspace and transcript-watcher tests without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public refusal, cancellation, execution-host and real-filesystem outcomes with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1627 removes low-value mocked daemon projections, scalar tables and duplicate terminal examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained terminal content preservation, process ownership refusal and recovery boundaries together with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1623 removes low-value mocked daemon projections, scalar tables and duplicate terminal examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained terminal content preservation, process ownership refusal and recovery boundaries together with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Retained exact unchanged-source receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Reduced selectors have no fresh execution result. Audit1417 intentionally deletes src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-hidden-tui-snapshot-replay.spec.ts: Loses rich hidden snapshot sequence replay/grid resize and forced repaint after hidden snapshot alarms, including live-trigger deduplication. No equivalent replacement coverage or fresh result is claimed. Historical coverage account: Renderer ownership/dedupe contracts cover provider-session claims. Local and daemon attach-only contracts prove an existing stable-pane owner is adopted without provider creation, while remote-runtime transport contracts preserve adopted ownership through cancellation. The Electron oracle covers a local macOS runtime and daemon with real agent, Setup, and unrelated-canary processes; SSH, WSL, paired-server, Linux, and Windows remain contract-only or unrun. Audit1383: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-native-chat-setup.spec.ts reduced. Lose command-list/receipt/default/background activation matrices whose provider spawn returns canned IDs. Retained test proves actual tab allocation separation, not terminal startup. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected receipts and their platform/provider/budget claims remain scoped to unchanged selectors. Changed optional selectors have no new execution result. Audit1391: src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-remote-pause-drop-notice.spec.ts reduced. Lose repeated quiet switches avoiding snapshots and legacy host without drop-report capability requesting a snapshot. Retained imported registrar uses fake transport/xterm writes, exercising real gap/restore lifecycle rather than actual terminal rendering. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. The existing primary-selector receipt and its claims remain scoped to their unchanged