      "invariant": "Workspace activation, launch, restore, sleep, hibernate, dedupe, clearing, mount, remount, and reconnect code must not replay or resume a provider session id already owned, queued, pending, live, or durably bound to a host PTY in that workspace. A renderer with missing projection state must adopt the exact runtime-owned PTY for the original tab and leaf rather than create a replacement.",
      "oracle": "Audit3368 retires whole sleeping-agent-resume and host-session-launch suites: provider-claim/deduplication, stable-pane reattach, recipe/WSL startup, callback/cancel/create-close and compatibility examples are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. The sole dated receipt is retired verbatim. With no active evidence, protection/platform/provider evidence clears and ALL commands/testFiles/assertionRefs are retired as complete original arrays in historical gaps, including selectors of surviving other sources; those sources remain in the broad suite. Prior red/green/flake accounts are historical only. No fresh runtime/provider/process/UI/mobile/mixed-version/cross-platform evidence is claimed. Current assertionRefs retain separate provider-session non-replay and exact-PTY adoption checks in resume-sleeping-agent-session, completed-worker-retirement-resume, remote-runtime-pty-transport-host-session-launch and live-background-terminal-mount-authority. This batch changes only pane-fit's contribution: its three surviving cases check terminal-identity reveal, stale-handle replacement and withheld-frame completion; they do not prove provider-session ownership or exact-PTY adoption. Other assertionRefs and selectors remain unchanged; no fresh execution of those separate contracts is claimed. Audit2236: pane-fit.test.ts is reduced to terminal-identity reveal, stale-handle replacement ownership and withheld-animation-frame completion. The existing withheld-frame assertion remains exact; additional scheduling/breadcrumb, cancellation, display-none and synthetic metric examples are removed. No new execution or equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Historical dated receipts and budgets are preserved verbatim and do not validate these reduced source bytes. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2095 current-parent preparation2126: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2090 (sources2088/2089): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2086 (sources2082/2083): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2076 (sources2073/2074): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-part-02.spec.ts: recovers a moved SSH pane through the tab it now sits in, not the one its lease froze; reports a plain expired orphan; does not report a pane whose only recent lease was superseded; does not report a pane whose only recent lease had its relay id recycled; picks the eligible orphan over a superseded predecessor that matches first; collects the same tabs the per-tab reader reports, in one sweep of the leases; reports no candidate when no lease names any of the worktree tabs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/runtime-availability.spec.ts: starts unavailable with no authoritative window; reports the configured Windows terminal shell on status; reports floating workspace availability from settings on status; polls floating tabs with targeted PTY liveness and no repo/provider inventory; hydrates persisted tabs when the store cannot report repos; advertises browser screencast only when a renderer window is available; routes mobile Codex reset consumption through the account mutation coordinator; maps a definite pre-provider rejection into an authoritative current snapshot. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1685 retires changed-source assertion and execution scope without equivalent replacement coverage. Existing unchanged-selector receipts remain scoped to their original sources. Historical prior-source oracle: Audit1683 retires changed-source assertion and execution scope without equivalent replacement coverage. Existing unchanged-selector receipts remain scoped to their original sources. Historical prior-source oracle: Retained exact unchanged-source receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Reduced selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical pre-audit oracle account for changed sources: Existing exact unchanged-selector receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Changed source selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical prior-source oracle account: Renderer-state tests assert provider-session ownership across preserved and queued panes. Main/provider contracts assert atomic attach-only adoption, stable host/worktree/tab/leaf identity, no fresh spawn on adoption, and safe paired-runtime cancellation. The Electron oracle creates inactive runtime-owned Codex and Setup PTYs plus an unrelated canary, seeds an exact resumable provider session, removes only the target renderer projections, and activates the workspace. It requires byte-stable handle, PTY, incarnation, tab, leaf, process PID, renderer graph, persisted binding, runtime id, graph epoch, and daemon PID across first mount and reload; PID-specific DOM keyboard I/O must remain live with one launch, zero resume argv, zero signals, zero interruption text, and no canary mutation.",
