      "knownGaps": [
        "NEXT65 current scope qualification: The NEXT65 knownGaps entries below govern the changed selectors and qualify any broader coverage implication in this gate’s unchanged oracle/coverageNotes narratives. Those narratives and preserved dated evidenceRuns retain their historical text and original exact execution scopes only; no fresh execution, transferred pass or equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Upstream case removals remain upstream; original NEXT65 proposal descriptions grant no duplicate retirement credit.",
        "NEXT65 active selector scope reduction (including directory-selected whole-file retirements): src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts. Remove complete registrations or registrar files within the selected scope for src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/reattach/pty-connection-daemon-snapshot-replay.spec.ts, src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/reattach/pty-connection-stale-daemon-snapshot-replay.spec.ts. Intentionally lose these named regression alarms without replacement: clears the captured pen for a normal-buffer fallback reattach — Fallback normal-buffer reattach clearing captured pen and dirty background loses this direct example.; waits for a recovered destination fit before forwarding its grid or live output — Recovered destination fitting before forwarding grid or live output loses this direct example.; suppresses the deferred reattach grid push when mobile claims the PTY while hidden — Mobile takeover while hidden suppressing deferred reattach grid forwarding loses this direct example.; drops stale callbacks but delivers fresh replacement output after an old replay clear — Fresh replacement output winning over stale callbacks after old replay clear loses this direct example.. Surviving parent statements and sibling registrations are preserved, but these reduced parent selectors have no fresh execution or transferred historical pass. Unrelated complete dated receipts retain only their original exact scopes; no equivalent replacement, rendered UI, provider, mobile, or cross-platform coverage is claimed.",
        "NEXT65 historical original active parent-selector fields (verbatim native JSON values; not current coverage):\ncommands: [\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/lib/agent-session/resume/resume-sleeping-agent-session.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts tests/e2e/completed-worker-retirement-resume.unit.test.ts --reporter=verbose\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/lib/agent-session/resume/resume-sleeping-agent-session.test.ts src/main/providers/local-pty/local-pty-provider-spawn-session.test.ts src/main/daemon/terminal-host/testing/terminal-host.test.ts src/main/daemon/providers/adapter/testing/daemon-pty-adapter.test.ts src/main/ipc/pty/pty-pane-reservation-settlement.test.ts src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-pty-transport-host-session-launch.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm exec electron-vite build --mode e2e && SKIP_BUILD=1 pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/live-background-terminal-mount-authority.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headless --workers=1\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/agent-session/lifecycle/structured-agent-cli-writers.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/structured-sessions/creation/structured-agent-session-adoption-replay.test.ts src/main/providers/agent-foreground-process-git-bash.win32.test.ts\"\n      ]\ntestFiles: [\n        \"src/renderer/src/lib/agent-session/resume/resume-sleeping-agent-session.test.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/completed-worker-retirement-resume.unit.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/providers/local-pty/local-pty-provider-spawn-session.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/daemon/terminal-host/testing/terminal-host.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/daemon/providers/adapter/testing/daemon-pty-adapter.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/ipc/pty/pty-pane-reservation-settlement.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-pty-transport-host-session-launch.test.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/live-background-terminal-mount-authority.spec.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/agent-session/lifecycle/structured-agent-cli-writers.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/structured-sessions/creation/structured-agent-session-adoption-replay.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/providers/agent-foreground-process-git-bash.win32.test.ts\"\n      ]\nassertionRefs: [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/structured-sessions/creation/structured-agent-session-adoption-replay.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\"captures source before routing (unary=%s)\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/providers/agent-foreground-process-git-bash.win32.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\"sets aside a detached ssh-agent for adoption, but not a background job\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/completed-worker-retirement-resume.unit.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"completed and explicitly retired workers retain no provider-resume authority on first workspace activation\",\n            \"the original tab, leaf, PTY, provider session, release state, replacement count, queued resume argv, emitted restored banner, and unrelated canary remain exact across restart\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/lib/agent-session/resume/resume-sleeping-agent-session.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"preserved panes claim their provider session and only stale duplicates are cleared\",\n            \"one launch per provider session: skipped duplicates are cleared instead of relaunched\",\n            \"active stable-pane records owned by preserved or visible panes are not resumed again\",\n            \"hibernated stable panes with cleared live PTY bindings are skipped\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"same-generation explicit reattach drains the authoritative snapshot before immediate live bytes and ACKs their delivery credit\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-pty-transport-host-session-launch.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"paired-runtime stable-pane adoption reports reattach without fresh-spawn ownership\",\n            \"cancellation after a paired-runtime adoption cannot close the original owner\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/live-background-terminal-mount-authority.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"first mount and renderer reload preserve exact agent and Setup handle, PTY, incarnation, tab, leaf, and PID identity\",\n            \"PID-specific keyboard input and output remain user-visible in both mounted panes\",\n            \"runtime inventory, renderer graph, persisted session, runtime epoch, and daemon PID converge without replacement or resume\",\n            \"the unrelated canary remains writable and receives no signal across target projection repair\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]",
        "Audit3053 reduces hidden-replay coverage by retiring nominal overlap, resize, cursor metadata and standalone stalled-restore variants. Timeout, overflow, identity/generation fences and retained live-output coordination remain; the removed alarms are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. Existing commands, assertion references and dated evidence retain their original scope.",
        "Audit2236: pane-fit.test.ts is reduced to terminal-identity reveal, stale-handle replacement ownership and withheld-animation-frame completion. The existing withheld-frame assertion remains exact; additional scheduling/breadcrumb, cancellation, display-none and synthetic metric examples are removed. No new execution or equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Historical dated receipts and budgets are preserved verbatim and do not validate these reduced source bytes.",
        "Audit2145 accepts removal of canned runtime metadata/guard/forwarding, fake in-memory persistence, private work-count and wrapper-duplication tests from the construction/orca-runtime.test.ts aggregate, plus the two automation run-context guards from runtime-workspace-launch-contracts.test.ts. Retained race, framing, physical completion and ownership callbacks remain byte-identical. Existing commands remain valid selectors; historical receipts stay unchanged and provide no fresh validation or replacement coverage for the reduced suites.",
        "Audit2133 current-parent preparation (988 authored removals; independently reviewed2099/2107/2115/2116 decisions; upstream clear-buffer and recovery-image regressions retained): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts: structural support changed only; no new authored removal credit. src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts: remove only literal registration import/call pairs await import('../orca-runtime-tests/worktree-setup-and-startup.spec'), await import('../orca-runtime-tests/gitlab-and-pr-bases.spec'); no additional authored credit. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/targeting-and-resilience.spec.ts: routes tab switch and capture start by explicit page id; accepts focus on tab switch without altering bridge args (focus is main-side concern); keeps terminal cwd resolution fail-soft when the provider is unavailable. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-and-reconciliation-part-04.spec.ts: drops the bounded scan cache when orphan-cleanup removal completes; clears optimistic reconcile tokens when a CLI worktree removal succeeds; emits drift without mutating when the fetched base fast-forwards created HEAD; emits base_changed without mutation when the fetched base rewrote history; skips stale-token reconciles without mutating or emitting stale status; emits unknown without mutation when fetch fails or the base ref is missing. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-and-reconciliation-part-03.spec.ts: routes runtime preserved-branch force-delete through the selected WSL project runtime; replies to a waiting client with the error of a delete that fails after acceptance; treats forced runtime deletion of an already-missing unregistered worktree as cleanup; treats normal runtime deletion of an already-missing unregistered worktree as cleanup. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-and-reconciliation-part-02.spec.ts: warns that a missing-repo removal only forgot the workspace; restores runtime watchers when CLI worktree deletion fails after teardown; does not re-spend the drain budget on a removal after a wedged install was abandoned; routes runtime worktree removal through the selected WSL project runtime; force-deletes a branch that was preserved by runtime worktree removal. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/gitlab-and-pr-bases-part-02.spec.ts: records GitLab pasted-project recents only after successful runtime lookup; threads explicit origin preference through runtime WSL PR base resolution; resolves local GitLab fork MR bases from the target project MR head ref; captures the fork MR head from a dedicated ref, not the shared FETCH_HEAD; keeps the durable MR head when the head fetch fails but the local ref resolves; routes runtime GitLab fork MR base git calls through the selected WSL project runtime. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/gitlab-and-pr-bases.spec.ts: passes SSH connection ids through GitLab task operations; routes runtime GitLab issue, MR, work-item, and todo actions through the selected WSL project runtime; routes runtime GitLab MR details, review-management, job, and pasted URL actions through the selected WSL project runtime; normalizes runtime GitLab issue list arguments like the desktop IPC path. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-setup-and-startup-part-03.spec.ts: does not warn when setup is explicitly skipped for CLI-created worktrees; puts the agent a create starts in the first default tab, as the window does; keeps the 8s main-runtime startup readiness budget for agents without an override; gives OpenCode the 20s main-runtime startup readiness budget; launches explicit startup agents with prompts for CLI-created worktrees. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-setup-and-startup.spec.ts: returns a setup launch payload for CLI-created worktrees when hooks are explicitly enabled; does not hand the window a setup main never tried to start; passes the selected Windows setup shell into runtime runner generation; follows normal setup policy for CLI-created worktrees without activating them; uses returned WSL setup shell metadata when runtime spawns setup; uses the shell-aware setup runner for windowless creates without a startup command; reports the in-process setup hook as running when nothing can launch the runner. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-sleep-and-teardown-part-02.spec.ts: coalesces two clients sleeping the same host worktree; stops exactly the expected live PTYs for a worktree; explains a refused workspace close instead of throwing the raw refusal enum. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-summaries-part-03.spec.ts: marks the desktop-active worktree as isActive; includes SSH-backed worktrees in the mobile worktree summary; caches repeated malformed path misses before normalizing them again. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-summaries-part-02.spec.ts: keeps title-only foreground work ahead of monitoring in another pane; keeps a local hook row while a connected PTY still backs its pane; keeps an OSC row via its connected PTY after the pane binding is cleared. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-summaries.spec.ts: resolves files through a source-visible linked-checkout worktree; marks saved session tabs with live PTYs as host sidebar activity; attributes live legacy PTYs from saved layout bindings when their panes are hidden; marks saved browser tabs as host sidebar activity like desktop; falls back to the path-keyed GitHub cache entry; includes folder workspaces in compact worktree summaries for mobile; attaches inline agent rows from the latest OSC 9999 status; projects monitoring over a title-derived working status. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-creation-and-orchestration-part-03.spec.ts: pushes to an idle pane when the only live waiter filters out the message type; resolves a registered waiter without PTY-injecting when the leaf is already idle; keeps already-idle status after tui-idle wait for immediate message delivery; resolves message waiters when notifyMessageArrived is called; does not resolve type-filtered message waiters for unrelated message types; removes message waiter abort listeners after message arrival; resolves message waiters on timeout when no message arrives. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-creation-and-orchestration-part-02.spec.ts: delivers pending mail via notifyMessageArrived when the recipient is already idle; does not keep retrying when every pending row was already pointed; repoints pending rows restored with a live-idle coordinator. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-13.spec.ts: rolls back a half-created terminal whose surface never publishes. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-12.spec.ts: rejects startup prompts for agents that require post-ready stdin; uses portable Unix quoting for mobile agent launch commands in WSL project runtimes; keeps PowerShell quoting for mobile agent launch commands in Windows host runtimes; uses cmd.exe quoting for mobile agent launch commands in local Windows host runtimes; publishes headless mobile session agent identity with synthesized PTY status; rejects disabled mobile session agent launches before spawning; validates mobile terminal insertion anchors before resolving agent launch commands. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-11.spec.ts: coalesces a reconnect close burst onto one authoritative PTY inventory; keeps an explicit user close destructive while the PTY is live; builds mobile session agent launch commands on the runtime host; injects mobile quick-command prompts into the host-built agent startup command. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-10.spec.ts: closes persisted headless terminal parents before any prior list call; tears down a serve-owned headless tab on close while a renderer is attac