    {
      "id": "agent-session.remote-host-authority",
      "title": "Remote agent sessions have one host-authoritative PTY and durable surface lifecycle",
      "maturity": "experimental",
      "protection": "partial",
      "owner": "agent-session",
      "layer": "runtime-controller-provider-renderer-contract",
      "surfaces": [
        "remote agent launch and explicit resume",
        "multi-client remote runtime sessions",
        "paired viewer-local structured agent focus",
        "headed desktop remote-server pairing",
        "headless remote-server parity",
        "daemon and relay reconnect",
        "remote completion classification across disconnect and reconnect",
        "terminal exit retirement and restart restore",
        "mixed-version fallback"
      ],
      "platforms": ["macos", "linux", "windows"],
      "providers": ["local", "daemon", "ssh", "wsl", "remote-runtime"],
      "coveredPlatforms": ["macos"],
      "coveredProviders": ["local", "daemon", "ssh", "wsl", "remote-runtime"],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit4362 intentionally deletes the imported stale-waiter retry and manually assembled OSC9999 mobile-republish cases, plus the mocked missing-worktree cleanup suite (4 authored / 5 finite cases in three suites). Lost alarms include repeated unread worker_done pointers, working-to-waiting mobile status publication, missing-worktree filtering, and scoped daemon shutdown with unrelated duplicate identities. No replacement coverage or new platform proof is claimed. Audit4352 deletes the whole mocked daemon router, session-owner resolver, degraded-provider, terminal-host CWD-readability and foreground-inspection suites plus the native-process-CWD fixture suite; recovery retains only public multi-pane proactive socket-death notification/remount. Intentionally lose retirement admission, stale-inventory/fenced-kill authority, attach-only re-resolution/absence, fast-exit routing, sleep CWD checkpoint/wake, diagnostic cancellation/shutdown and foreground census/session-change alarms. No equivalent replacement or fresh gate execution is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit3994 retires two authored callbacks imported by the shared construction test driver: split OSC 9999 carry and rendererless status ownership, plus OpenCode permission text taking priority in status and tui-idle refusal. Remaining imports and selectors keep their scope. No equivalent replacement or fresh gate execution is claimed. Audit3425 composes root-adopted3420/independent3421: intentionally removes83 authored/112 potential expanded registrations across13 semantic sources, deleting7 whole conventional suites and1 registering helper;7 authored/10 potential expanded cases remain. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. The Codex restart suite and exact command/testFiles/assertionRef are removed; its mock account-change/remote-pane restart alarms are intentionally lost. Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The retained runtime registration driver loses three complete imported fragments: changed-working-label title facts and suppressed-frame tracked snapshots; refusing SSH GitLab MR-base lookup before local Git/glab calls; and missing folder-workspace path creation/update refusal before spawn/store mutation. These alarms are intentionally lost. Other imported fragments and separately rooted dated receipts are unchanged; they are not equivalent replacement coverage.  Audit3368 retires the whole host-session-launch unit source, including host-authority/create/ensure/legacy/Kimi/refusal/draft/options/prompt/cancel/kill/shared-disconnect and passive-sleep output callback alarms, without equivalent replacement. Its unit command token and test-file entry retire. Five unrelated macOS receipts remain verbatim and keep only their original scope; no fresh changed-selector/runtime/provider/process/UI/mobile/mixed-version/cross-platform evidence is claimed. Audit3359 retires the whole create-handoff suite. Supplied disposition, late completion, close-callback and metadata-bookkeeping alarms are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement; the compound unit selector and test-file entry narrow accordingly. Five unrelated macOS receipts retain their original scope. No fresh runtime, process-deduplication, physical provider/network, historical-import, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Audit 3301 removes the caller-chat-target precedence over host selection example from web-session-tabs-sync-focus-intent.test.ts. The snapshot-before-RPC replay and split-sibling-first exact-leaf focus cases remain un