      "coveredPlatforms": ["macos", "linux"],
      "coveredProviders": [],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit3362 retires the whole settings suite, including dirty-draft focus, background-host keepalive, protocol/catalog compatibility, stale/failure and refresh examples. The compound unit selector and test-file entry narrow; all prior owner-routing retirements/history remain. Four unrelated selected-runtime macOS E2E receipts remain verbatim and do not validate the changed unit selector. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/provider/UI/mobile/mixed-version/cross-platform evidence is claimed. Audit3349 retires the explicit runtime-owner, explicit SSH-owner and missing-owner-after-catalog-change examples from worktrees-fetch-owner-routing. Of those four named assertions, only the missing-owner-after-provider-reconnect assertion remains; the command and test-file selector survive. Those three alarms are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. Four unrelated physical selected-runtime macOS E2E receipts remain verbatim; the frozen static closure does not select changed tests through their literal roots. No fresh runtime, provider, historical-import, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Audit3326 adopts reconciled source audit3324 and intentionally retires these low-value examples and their regression alarms: drops older same-host group and folder responses that finish last — Copies group and folder fixtures plus four deferred responses to re-test the same generic catalog generation fence in two wrappers. Retires stale same-host response rejection at these API copies.; drops pre-reconnect group and folder responses without pruning the new catalog — Directly replaces pairing/catalog fixtures then resolves scripted old group/folder replies; repeats identity-fence contract in two catalog wrappers without real reconnect. Retires pre-reconnect catalog pruning refusal example.. Retained tests do not replace these alarms. Dated unrelated evidence remains scoped to its original execution; no historical source/import-closure equivalence, fresh execution, real network/provider/SSH, rendered UI, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Audit2371 reduces all-host-folder-workspace-catalogs.test.ts by removing the repeated offline compatibility-probe budget and its incidental local-fallback/restored-owner samples, and catalog-settlement-notifications.test.ts by removing the four-route ten-equal-refresh notification/reference matrix. Those probe, quietness, identity and fallback alarms are intentionally lost. Remaining stale-response and revision-fencing examples do not supply equivalent replacement coverage. No fresh execution or red/green evidence validates the reduced sources; the four unrelated physical selected-runtime E2E receipts retain their original commands and scope. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2360 removes src/renderer/src/hooks/useIpcEvents-terminal-create-surfacing.test.ts and its exclusive fake-effect harness. Lose local default-runtime persistence across navigation; focused/background terminal request/create/reveal and no-focus recovery; startup cwd/config/agent/view-mode forwarding; explicit runtime-session routing; remote/ambiguous/missing owner refusal; history focus; existing PTY reuse/title preservation; pending tab PTY/layout/identity adoption; split tree, focus, identity and telemetry samples. No equivalent replacement claimed. Changed selectors have no fresh execution or red/green credit. Unrelated retained receipt objects keep their original narrow scope. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2056 (sources2054/2055): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/renderer/src/store/project-groups/nested-repository-operations.test.ts: routes local nested scan progress by scanId and unsubscribes after completion. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1640 removes low-value IPC, SSH, workspace and transcript-watcher tests without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public refusal, cancellation, execution-host and real-filesystem outcomes with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1488 deletes NonGitFolderDialog tests. The hand-assembled scan/import pipelines, supplied host and folder outcomes, registration callback receipts and static host confirmation alarms are retired. No equivalent replacement coverage or fresh routing validation is claimed. Historical receipts and assertions describe their original sources only. Audit1487 deletes AddProjectFromFolderDialog and project-added-default-checkout tests and reduces AddRepoStartSteps to custom ArrowDown navigation. Mocked admission/activation and static host-control assertions are retired. No equivalent replacement coverage or fresh routing validation is claimed. Historical receipts and assertions below describe their original sources only. Retained exact unchanged-source receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Reduced selectors have no fresh execution result. Audit1417 intentionally reduces src/renderer/src/store/slices/repos-stale-fetch.spec.ts: Loses startup catalog admission/reconnect preservation and settlement failure gating alarms. No equivalent replacement coverage or fresh result is claimed. Historical coverage account: Audit1391 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Audits1342 and1337 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Audit1320 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): This audit removes browser generic Active Server settings isolation and unknown-choice examples; their direct preference and rejection alarms are lost. Other routing evidence is not an equivalent replacement. Historical commands and results remain historical. Platform-neutral deterministic tests separate the durable Active Server preference from per-client connection, selected-workspace, browser-session, Add Project, and execution-host routing. The composed regression models Local desktop -> connect/navigate Windows 2 -> reveal a local terminal -> restart. Multi-client browser host overrides, multi-server profile caches, generic settings IPC rejection, local and remote workspace ownership, Add Project eligibility/owner capture/stale-result fencing, host-qualified group/folder/worktree identity, and restart reset of transient routing are covered. A visible macOS Orca desktop server plus separate paired Electron and web clients prove selected-runtime Add Project operations and disabled creation when the only listed host is blocked or unavailable; headless-server parity also passed. Live Linux, Windows, WSL, and SSH Add Project journeys remain uncollected. The static wrapper-rendering suite was removed during the low-value-test audit; its supplied-prop host-browser and control-visibility output assertions are no longer checked by that suite. This removal supplies no new runtime-routing evidence. The fake-React Clone hook unit suite was also retired: its captured-owner and same-ID sibling assertions no longer supply unit evidence. Historical run commands and counts remain historical; this retirement adds no runtime-routing, cross-platform, or mobile evidence. The test-value audit narrowed resolved-worktree-execution-host.test.ts to cache reuse and invalidation. Its direct hydrated-worktree, missing-folder, restored-owner, host-stamp and empty-runtime selection alarms are lost. Other routing and recovery suites do not establish equivalent selector coverage; historical run commands and results remain historical. The test-value audit narrowed worktree-runtime-owner.test.ts to deterministic owner-lookup work bounds with correct worktree/folder results and changed-collection invalidation. Its separate host/default/folder/mirror inventory alarms are lost; these retained in-memory checks establish no actual host delivery, restart or equivalent replacement coverage. Historical run commands and results remain historical. web-runtime-session.test.ts no longer supplies the terminal/browser/staged-browser explicit-host collision assertions formerly referenced here. Those direct routing alarms are lost; the remaining selector and live routing evidence does not establish equivalent replacement coverage. The test-value audit removes the direct host/provider/project-setup selector tables. selectors.test.ts retains only floating-tab/unread scan-cost checks, which supply no current Active Server routing evidence. Its separate missing-runtime/no-local-fallback and owner-choice alarms are lost; other gate evidence is not an equivalent replacement. Historical executed commands and results remain historical. browser.test.ts no longer supplies the host/profile projection examples. Current routing commands and references name the retained deferred host-list/import completion tests in browser-session-host-selection.test.ts instead. Its actual source supports stale-completion fencing; it does not establish the formerly listed multi-client selection or restart-reset claims. Other evidence is not an equivalent replacement; historical executed commands/counts/results remain historical. The test-value audit deletes repos-paired-runtime-add.test.ts. Its supplied-result assertion that an explicitly selected paired host receives repo.add with the selected path, folder kind and 15000ms timeout while native repos.add and pickFolder remain unused is intentionally lost. Other gate evidence is not an equivalent replacement. Historical executed commands, counts and results remain unchanged. The test-value audit narrows repos-selected-owner-routing.test.ts to an overlapping selected-runtime import/local refresh, reversed same-host folder replies, and group/folder replies crossing an actual pairing revision. Its separate same-ID host-partition, desktop-only pruning, sequential explicit-runtime preservation, and SSH scan/cancel forwarding alarms are intentionally lost. The stale-response case overwrites its group result before the final assertion, so it supplies only a folder stale-response alarm. The catalog-reconciliation caller also retires the refresh-identity and runtime-visibility-default registrars: their immediate reference/field/count, filter/dismissal, readoption-inventory, timestamp and settings/capability-copy/retention alarms are lost. No equivalent replacement or new live host, restart, platform or mobile evidence is claimed; historical executed commands, counts and results remain unchanged. The test-value audit removes the reversed-order direct worktree lookup example from selected-host-active-workspace-identity.test.ts. Its explicit-runtime path lookup with reversed same-ID catalog rows is intentionally lost; that example did not activate a workspace. After the subsequent audit, current assertions in this suite name only the retained local-first worktree activation; the selected-runtime folder/group host-echo example was removed. They are not equivalent replacements for the reversed-order lookup alarm. Historical executed commands, counts and results remain unchanged; no new live host, restart, platform or mobile evidence is claimed. The test-value audit narrows renderer store settings.test.ts by removing immediate authoritative-settings/response rebasing, checked-failure forwarding, best-effort logging, mobile-address/provider normalization, successful catalog-start, hand-seeded partial-status coverage and ghost-status filtering examples. Those direct response, normalization, error and catalog-projection alarms are intentionally lost. The runtime focus-switch resource/draft preservation, unreachable/incompatible refusal and held catalog coalescing/retry/staleness cases remain; they are not equivalent replacements for the removed alarms. Historical executed commands, counts and results remain unchanged; no new live host, restart, platform or mobile evidence is claimed. The test-value audit narrows worktrees-fetch-owner-routing.test.ts by removing default-local transport selection, ownerless runtime stamping, isolated force-local routing, and mocked mobile-denial/toast examples. Those direct routing, field and presentation alarms are lost. Retained concurrency and authority-fencing cases do not establish equivalent replacement coverage or live host, platform, restart or mobile evidence. Historical commands, counts and results remain unchanged. The test-value audit removes the separate paired-web host-switch resource-preservation example from renderer store settings.test.ts. Its explicit web-mode terminal/browser no-close and retained PTY/remote-browser-handle alarms are intentionally lost. The surviving desktop host-merge, resource/draft preservation, refusal and catalog retry/coalescing/staleness cases are not equivalent replacement coverage. Historical executed commands, counts and results remain unchanged; no new live host, restart, platform or mobile evidence is claimed. The test-value audit removes the selected-runtime folder/group activation example from selected-host-active-workspace-identity.test.ts. That large same-ID fixture only asserted that the explicit host argument was stored and read back; it did not check the chosen folder path, group or delivered operation. Its narrow non-rejection/host-echo alarm is intentionally lost. Only the local-first worktree case that independently checks the returned runtime path remains in this suite. Historical executed commands, counts and results remain unchanged; no equivalent replacement or new live-host evidence is claimed. The continued test-value audit narrows worktrees-fetch-owner-routing.test.ts by retiring the simple explicit-local duplicate-repo request and runtime-only host-stamping examples. Those exact request-option and supplied-row alarms are intentionally lost. The retained force-local sibling-preservation and project-setup stamping cases use different inputs and are not equivalent replacements. Historical commands, counts and results remain unchanged; no live-host, restart, platform or mobile evidence is added. The test-value audit removes the browser-settings host-option fallback helper suite. Its direct selected/default/empty-option preference alarms are lost; no browser session, host delivery or persistence was exercised there. Remaining routing evidence is not an equivalent replacement. Historical commands, counts and results remain historical. The test-value audit deletes paired-web-add-project-unavailable-host.spec.ts. Its injected blocked/unavailable-host disabled-action and no-local-option presentation alarms are intentionally lost. The snapshot sequence and null transport do not prove actual version negotiation or operation rejection. Other routing evidence is not an equivalent replacement; no new runtime, platform or mobile evidence is claimed. The two retired historical receipts and assertion reference are archived below with their original fields and results. Audit1320: src/renderer/src/components/settings/runtime-environments/catalog/RuntimeEnvironmentsPane.test.ts removed. Transport-up/runtime-down, failed-probe ready/reconnect/handshake and stale compatibility label/button state inventories lose alarms. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1342: src/renderer/src/components/sidebar/worktree-list/listing/host-filtering.test.ts removed. Runtime/SSH/default row ownership and folder/project path-status routing samples disappear. src/renderer/src/store/slices/repos-catalog-reconciliation.test.ts reduced. Driver registration/import of a whole-deleted selected spec is removed; directly authored cases remain unchanged. No extra authored removal credit. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1337: src/renderer/src/components/sidebar/project-admission/dialog/add-repo-browse-authority.test.ts removed. Removes paired-host browse versus native picker callback flags and SSH no-browse predicate samples. src/renderer/src/components/sidebar/project-admission/dialog/AddRepoDialog.default-checkout.test.ts removed. Removes explicit local/runtime versus missing owner selector examples. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1352: focused Linux unit selections validated on source head b638e07d395b76af3ba6b03761a1a0fe7e5e026e. Historical statements above retain their original scope. Intentional test losses are recorded in knownGaps; these runs claim no physical-provider, p95, rendered E2E or cross-platform validation. Audit1360: focused Linux unit selections validated on source head 415c9cffc2d10024131ec4b6721767a22195de6d. Historical statements above retain their original scope. Intentional test losses are recorded in knownGaps; these runs claim no physical-provider, p95, rendered E2E or cross-platform validation. Audit1391: src/renderer/src/lib/worktree-runtime-owner.test.ts reduced. Lose explicit repeated-lookup work/read budget and standalone initial owner lookup alarms. Retained production resolver proves changed ownership is visible, using synthetic catalogs rather than server publication. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed.",
      "motivatingLinks": [
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/9687",
        "https://linear.app/stably/issue/STA-4024/p1-paired-web-add-project-enables-unavailable-host-fallback-after-pr"
      ],
      "invariant": "Only an explicit user change in Settings > Remote Orca Servers > Advanced > Active Server may mutate activeRuntimeEnvironmentId. Connecting, pairing, disconnecting, selecting or revealing a workspace or terminal, browser/mobile handoff, remote navigation, and reconnect must use transient or target-owner routing and must never rewrite the durable preference. Every Add Project selected host must satisfy canSelectAddRepoHost; paired web has no local filesystem fallback, so no valid host means Browse, Clone, and Create remain disabled. Every operation stays on the host selected when it began, even if preference or catalog state changes. Generic settings mutation cannot bypass the dedicated preference IPC.",
