scale paired hosts remain gaps. The audit removed the E2E parking override/debug-handle suite. Override exposure guards, delay/retention independence, TTL filtering and debug-handle forwarding alarms are lost. Retained real parking journeys do not establish equivalent test-harness configuration coverage. The test-value audit removes separate responsive-stream, intervening-control-frame and capacity-error classification examples. Retained multiplexer checks use fake clocks and captured transport callbacks; their per-stream isolation, deadline and probe-baseline assertions do not prove an actual host restart or equivalent replacement coverage. Historical run commands and results remain historical. The test-value audit removes the standalone retained/live metadata projection and additive-preference negative example from runtime-client-events.test.ts. Its remaining case checks partial-authority event admission through a captured callback; it does not establish full-pair projection, actual peer delivery or equivalent replacement coverage. Historical commands and results remain historical. The isolated accepted-handle-events observer suite is removed. Its runtime/worktree/pane membership, once-only delivery and listener-release ledger alarms are lost. Live hidden-retention evidence does not establish equivalent observer coverage. Audit1292: The entire host-session mirror empty-inventory settle suite is removed. Live-unpublished versus genuinely-empty hydration, same-ID revision response/in-flight fencing and cleared-tracking pending-probe invalidation alarms are lost. The singleton store and inventories were mocked; no real host census or resume delivery or equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1302: src/main/runtime/session-tabs-inventory-publication.test.ts: Keep actual runtime public inventory authority across renderer epochs/resync, fallback, aborts and invalid graph publishers. Remove copied nonempty publication, private scan counters/collector and known-h