      "invariant": "A host advertising terminal.paired-parking.v1 keeps the PTY and bounded authoritative history alive while an ordinary hidden-view park destroys the client xterm and releases its raw per-PTY stream. Reveal must restore up to the requested 5,000 rows, parked-time side effects/output, the same PTY identity, and continued input/output. Parked watcher synchronization compares parking semantics rather than fresh object identity, owns setup and cleanup across StrictMode replay, reconciles real PTY/layout changes, and performs no terminal-state scan when nothing is parked. After a host main-process relaunch, unknown local delivery-sync state must not be treated as proof that a surviving daemon PTY is already foregrounded. An empty headed session-tab inventory is authoritative only after the current renderer graph generation publishes a complete inventory and every execution host answers the PTY census; unpublished, resync-pending, transport-failed, and partially scoped inventories remain unverifiable, while genuinely authoritative empty and non-empty inventories settle and a scope-less legacy empty keeps its pre-authority best-effort settle so outdated hosts retain agent auto-resume. The unpublished-empty regression must keep the resume dispatch parked with exactly one daemon process/writer; restoring unconditional empty hydration must release one dispatch and create two live writers. If subscription precedes provider readiness, authoritative inventory must reconsider that existing subscriber without spawning, resizing, or changing reconnect state. A snapshot without an output high-water must keep it unknown rather than borrowing a layout version that can suppress newer live output. Hosts without the capability must gate hidden raw output before xterm scheduling and repaint from the authoritative snapshot on reveal while retaining the existing limit/TTL force-parking fallback. After the first semantic title state, decorative spinner frequency must add zero paired client-event frames and zero full session-tabs work between status-freshness leases regardless of hidden worktree count. Continuous working or permission evidence may refresh each affected worktree once per 15 minutes through one globally spaced FIFO so current and legacy viewers do not decay before 30 minutes; sibling PTYs share that worktree refresh, while local title animation, raw output, and semantic title, status, bell, completion, and query facts remain intact. A paired terminal stream whose delivery credits stop progressing must replace only that stream; command silence first probes authoritative state and replaces the stream if the probe times out or proves the PTY advanced beyond the client's delivered output sequence. When no comparable delivery high-water exists, the first sequenced probe establishes a baseline and only later advancement proves staleness. A same-sequence snapshot remains valid proof of a responsive silent command. A successful status probe may replace a pre-ready shared-control socket without rejecting or duplicating calls already waiting for that transport. Manual disconnect must retain pairing while preventing queued or passive calls and subscriptions from recreating transport until explicit Connect. A paired pane reconnecting to a relaunched host that has not yet published its window graph (an unpublished frame, bare or client-projected) must stay in recovery rather than retire, and the host's first published snapshot carrying the surface must reattach it; a published frame lacking the surface still retires it. The placeholder is only ever sent before the host's graph first publishes; afterwards a worktree with no tabs gets a real empty answer, pushed once to any client that asked during startup, so a paired client opening a never-opened host worktree still gets its first terminal.",
      "oracle": "Audit4362 intentionally deletes the imported stale-waiter retry and manually assembled OSC9999 mobile-republish cases, plus the mocked missing-worktree cleanup suite (4 authored / 5 finite cases in three suites). Lost alarms include repeated unread worker_done pointers, working-to-waiting mobile status publication, missing-worktree filtering, and scoped daemon shutdown with unrelated duplicate identities. No replacement coverage or new platform proof is claimed. Audit3832 deliberately retires76 authored/79 finite cases:75 runtime compatibility cases/78 finite cases across14 fragments, plus one localization extractor default-flag case. Three whole runtime fragments are deleted;27 authored/30 finite cases remain across the reviewed sources. This gate retains only its own selected scope; no equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/native/remote evidence is claimed. Runtime component A: Audit3828 composes3822 with independent3824: deliberately retires49 authored/52 finite cases from seven compatibility fragments, leaving15 authored/18 finite cases and deleting two entire fragments. Accepted losses: positive folder-worker recovery/materialization and reveal deadline; persisted-key normalization and legacy split/group/focus projection; fixed stale CAS refusal; occupied/alias/restored/preallocated terminal-handle variants; fixed OpenCode/Cursor/Claude/Codex/Antigravity classification, readiness, title and management examples; direct private-map browser authority projections; browser-focus and OMP title projection; already-aborted claim cleanup. Additional3824 loss: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-02.spec.ts :: does not poll a wrapper foreground for a speculative CLI prompt send :: Speculative retryForegroundWrappers:false check must return false on a wrapper after one foreground read, without polling the supplied later codex response. These real bounded alarms are deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained callbacks are unchanged and provide only their own bounded scope, not equivalent replacement. Historical receipts do not validate reduced callbacks. No fresh runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser evidence or full transitive closure is claimed. Runtime component B: Audit3834 deliberately retires26 authored/26 finite cases from seven fresh compatibility fragments, leaving10/10 and deleting the one-case saved-binding reattachment fragment. Original position58 is excluded: its existing substantive3578 KEEP7 review remains historical, with no fresh credit. Accepted losses: fixed hook/provider-session identities and stale metadata refusal; decorative/pre-title foreground ordering variants; saved-binding surface reattachment; saved-row exit ghost removal and silent activation selection; unsupported headless wake; positive pending materialization/group projections; per-caller navigation selection; positive SSH hydration/read partition; laptop mobile publication/buffer and background/pending/status projections; abnormal/unregistered SSH grace, normal-exit refusal, persisted SSH hydration, positive serve reattachment, pending-agent launch arguments and direct seeded running-launch admission guard. These are real bounded alarms deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained cases preserve their own distinct deferred foreground coalescing, usable handle continuity, stale inventory refresh, concurrent browser snapshot preservation, renderer graph fencing, caller dedup isolation, SSH partition writes, runtime split lifetime, independent relay-ready publication, lease admission/state/expiry. The direct running-launch no-spawn guard alarm is deliberately retired; no remaining owning-launch refusal coverage is claimed. Historical runs do not validate reduced callbacks. No equivalent replacement, runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser result or full transitive closure is claimed. Additional extractor loss: config/scripts/localization/source-extraction/audit-localization-native-dialogs.test.mjs :: does not change the existing renderer scan by default :: Default options must omit the five native-only fields in this supplied snippet. No equivalent replacement is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit3814 deliberately retires60 authored/60 finite cases:53runtime compatibility cases,4native XCTest methods and3Python clipboard methods, including the entire StableElementIndexes suite. Clipboard cuts retire the one-over-cap sample, incoming-offer destruction trace and sequential20-copy replay; actual wire, FD/pipe, startup and Xvfb/GTK boundaries remain without equivalent replacement claims. Accepted losses include narrow terminal-send payload/provider projections, legacy and direct no-op/error permutations, timing/work-count examples, private state/title/activity projections and fixture-driven readiness examples, individually enumerated below. These include real bounded production alarms consciously retired for marginal value; retained failed writes, duplicate submission, stale capture, transcript/ring and allocation fences are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or complete transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3806 deliberately retires40 authored/40 finite runtime compatibility cases, including the terminal-side-effect-facts-part03 headless-snapshots-part02 and agent-status-and-waits-part03 fragments, plus20 scalar Swift precondition sites. Lost runtime alarms include status/title/attention projection examples, simple renderer/headless frame restoration and status waiting outcomes detailed in the accepted-loss ledger. Swift cuts retire duplicate generation-map/schema/navigation/bridge and notification-wrapper assertions; no standalone native program is deleted. These include real bounded production alarms consciously retired for marginal value. Retained races, pending writes/reflow, namespace and waiter ownership are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or full transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3798 deliberately retires21 authored/24 finite compatibility cases, including the entire SSH-worktree-lifecycle and repository-project-operations fragments. Accepted losses include navigation-only settings acknowledgement, browser session cleanup and host preservation projections, window positive/policy-state examples, terminal recovery/reload and no-incarnation remint examples, terminal listing compatibility/malformed IDs, directory browse/sort/Windows path smoke, SSH create refusal/manual lineage, recursive parent-folder creation and fork/origin/avatar/icon projections. Real bounded production alarms are consciously retired for marginal value; retained authority races, cleanup/clone ownership, pending waiters, nested-folder and scan invalidation cases are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or full transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3580: Retire the whole one-case runtime host environment prototype/subclass suite. Intentionally lose the exact configured lower-case Windows Claude home to account-identity normalization and host-account override precedence alarm previously retained by Audit3129. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime validation is claimed. Earlier dated keep statements below describe their historical source scope; the current suite is removed. Audit3563 scope: retire the whole Kiro OSC/hook identity suite and the OpenCode2 identity-only case; reduce Codex cached startup child-retirement and missing-session-ID tables to one case each (2 authored/4 finite removals). Intentionally lose Kiro alias/session continuity, OpenCode2 completed OSC identity continuity, cached replacement without relay-generation