1\"\n      ]\ntestFiles: [\n        \"src/main/runtime/session-lifecycle/publication/mobile-session-tabs-agent-status-heartbeat.test.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/session-tabs-decorative-title-fanout.unit.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/parking/lifecycle/use-terminal-tab-cold-parking.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/web/web-preload-api-runtime-environment.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/ipc/runtime-environments/runtime-environments-pairing.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/rpc/terminal-multiplex-initial-snapshot-buffering.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/rpc/terminal-multiplex-snapshot-serialization.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/rpc/terminal-multiplex-pty-wait-capacity.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/rpc/terminal-subscribe-buffer.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/terminal/adoption/terminal-subscriber-driven-daemon-attach.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/session-tabs/runtime-inventory-publication-authority.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/session-tabs/session-tabs-inventory-census-race.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/daemon/terminal-host/testing/terminal-host-agent-session.test.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/session-tabs-empty-inventory-daemon-oracle.unit.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/output/terminal-side-effect-facts-handler.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-visibility-and-exit.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/parking/retention/terminal-hidden-worktree-retention.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/parking/retention/terminal-hidden-view-parking.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/parking/output-watchers/terminal-parked-tab-watchers.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/parking/output-watchers/terminal-parked-watcher-reconciliation.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/runtime/rpc/subscriptions/runtime-client-events.test.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-pty-transport-activation-inventory-fallback.test.ts\",\n        \"src/shared/remote-runtime/control/remote-runtime-shared-control-connection.test.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-lossy-initial-snapshot.spec.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-truncated-tail-first-paint.spec.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-stall-recovery.spec.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-probe-gap-recovery.spec.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/headless-paired-remote-terminal-stall-recovery.spec.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-retention-memory.spec.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/headless-paired-remote-terminal-retention-memory.spec.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/terminal-parked-memory.spec.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-host-restart-background-sync.spec.ts\",\n        \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-pty-transport-unpublished-host-graph.test.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-host-quit-reconnect-input.spec.ts\",\n        \"src/main/runtime/terminal/query/runtime-terminal-inventory-contracts.test.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/paired-client-first-terminal-unopened-host-worktree.spec.ts\"\n      ]\nassertionRefs: [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/session-tabs-decorative-title-fanout.unit.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"2,880 decorative spinner and bare-native real-PTY OSC chunks publish zero session-tabs snapshots or serialized bytes after semantic convergence\",\n            \"the viewer performs zero snapshot applies and zero store mutations during decorative activity\",\n            \"after 30 minutes, one globally spaced refresh per worktree keeps every mirrored working status fresh\",\n            \"exact Pi and rotating normalized Pi/Grok frames renew explicit and fallback status without changing stateStartedAt or acknowledgement semantics\",\n            \"matching title evidence renews retained OSC hook status without resetting stateStartedAt, then drops unverifiable prompt metadata after the hook row expires\",\n            \"renderer-authored rich status keeps its original lease, then renews only coarse title-confirmed state and provider identity\",\n            \"ordinary-shell title transitions replace working stateStartedAt with the completion transition time\",\n            \"decorative heartbeats remain blocked until unknown foreground ownership resolves, then resume at the bounded interval\",\n            \"tracked terminal state reset clears delayed foreground ownership markers\",\n            \"raw chunks, semantic idle transitions, and visible output remain exact\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/terminal/adoption/terminal-subscriber-driven-daemon-attach.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\"retries an existing subscriber when provider inventory becomes ready\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/session-tabs/session-tabs-inventory-census-race.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"creation and removal at the census release edge are subsumed once, and a delayed pre-boundary change is not replayed\",\n            \"post-boundary creation and removal replay after the initial snapshot in sequence order\",\n            \"create/remove/recreate transitions are preserved without collapse\",\n            \"a post-boundary projected-state change is delivered without a new snapshot revision\",\n            \"an older coalesced callback cannot overwrite a newer immediate change\",\n            \"initialization churn publishes only the latest projected state and repeated structural overflow fails after bounded recollection\",\n            \"disconnect aborts the census and removes the real runtime listener\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/session-tabs-empty-inventory-daemon-oracle.unit.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"unpublished empty inventory keeps resume dispatch at zero with the original daemon session, process id, and writer as the sole live writer\",\n            \"an authoritative empty inventory settles the mirror and releases exactly one resume dispatch with zero liveness probes\",\n            \"re-enabling unconditional empty hydration makes the identical oracle red with one resume dispatch, two session ids, two process ids, and two writer calls\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-host-restart-background-sync.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"preserves daemon PID and target PTY identity across the paired host relaunch\",\n            \"foregrounds the daemon-backgrounded target on its first post-relaunch remote observation\",\n            \"delivers target and post-relaunch control terminal input and live output\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-probe-gap-recovery.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\"replaces a stale paired stream when the PTY snapshot advanced\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-stall-recovery.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"restarts one ACK-starved paired terminal stream without replacing its PTY\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/headless-paired-remote-terminal-stall-recovery.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\"recovers an ACK-starved stream from an isolated headless Orca host\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-lossy-initial-snapshot.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"a nonempty lossy initial snapshot paints exactly once on a paired client\",\n            \"the authoritative host cursor advances and live output resumes exactly once\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-truncated-tail-first-paint.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"paints a paired remote terminal when only its retained text tail overflowed\",\n            \"legacy paired hosts retain the lossy hidden-manager budget fallback\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-retention-memory.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"ordinary-parks paired terminals and restores authoritative host scrollback\",\n            \"warm-mounted hidden paired streams schedule zero renderer output work under sustained host output\",\n            \"six hidden real PTYs publish and apply only exact working and idle title transitions across paired transport\",\n            \"client recovery completes while every target terminal remains unmounted in the host renderer\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/headless-paired-remote-terminal-retention-memory.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"ordinary-parks paired terminals against an isolated headless Orca host\",\n            \"cold-activates only visible paired terminals against an isolated headless host\",\n            \"the headless host bounds real-PTY decorative title transport and production store application\",\n            \"the headless host shares the zero-hidden-renderer-work and exact-restoration contract\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/terminal-parked-memory.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"releases un-parkable hidden worktree buffers only once the retention budget engages\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/rpc/terminal-multiplex-pty-wait-capacity.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"admits 128 active streams, rejects the 129th, and reuses released capacity\",\n            \"reserves PTY wait capacity independently from active streams\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"pauses capable paired output while hidden and restores exactly on reveal\",\n            \"locally gates hidden paired output when a legacy host cannot pause it\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-pty-transport-activation-inventory-fallback.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"keeps a mounted HUB mirror alive when the old stream ends before the replacement snapshot\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/web/web-preload-api-runtime-environment.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"keeps pairing while manual disconnect fences passive reconnects\",\n            \"returns a disconnect envelope when a queued active runtime call disconnects\",\n            \"returns a disconnect envelope when a queued selected environment call disconnects\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]",
        "Audit3061 retires the park-model supplied snapshot suite and nominal mode, cursor, focus, geometry and remote resume metadata variants. Their distinct alarms are intentionally lost; six retained mode/remote cases preserve selected tail-order, authority and parse-readiness boundaries without equivalent replacement. Existing selectors and dated evidence retain their original scope. The ordinary paired-scroll-back alias was already absent before this batch and is removed as stale metadata, separately from the newly retired floating-pane example.",
        "Audit3053 reduces hidden-replay coverage by retiring nominal overlap, resize, cursor metadata and standalone stalled-restore variants. Timeout, overflow, identity/generation fences and retained live-output coordination remain; the removed alarms are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. Existing commands, assertion references and dated evidence retain their original scope.",
        "Audit2145 accepts removal of canned runtime metadata/guard/forwarding, fake in-memory persistence, private work-count and wrapper-duplication tests from the construction/orca-runtime.test.ts aggregate, plus the two automation run-context guards from runtime-workspace-launch-contracts.test.ts. Retained race, framing, physical completion and ownership callbacks remain byte-identical. Existing commands remain valid selectors; historical receipts stay unchanged and provide no fresh validation or replacement coverage for the reduced suites.",
        "Audit2133 current-parent preparation (988 authored removals; independently reviewed2099/2107/2115/2116 decisions; upstream clear-buffer and recovery-image regressions retained): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: tests/e2e/session-tabs-decorative-title-fanout.unit.test.ts: bounds host publication and renderer application across remote worktrees; globally caps decorative freshness while every working status stays fresh. src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts: structural support changed only; no new authored removal credit. src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts: remove only literal registration import/call pairs await import('../orca-runtime-tests/worktree-setup-and-startup.spec'), await import('../orca-runtime-tests/gitlab-and-pr-bases.spec'); no additional authored credit. tests/e2e/terminal-parked-memory.spec.ts: releases renderer terminal memory when hidden tabs park. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/targeting-and-resilience.spec.ts: routes tab switch and capture start by explicit page id; accepts focus on tab switch without altering bridge args (focus is main-side concern); keeps terminal cwd resolution fail-soft when the provider is unavailable. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-and-reconciliation-part-04.spec.ts: drops the bounded scan cache when orphan-cleanup removal completes; clears optimistic reconcile tokens when a CLI worktree removal succeeds; emits drift without mutating when the fetched base fast-forwards created HEAD; emits base_changed without mutation when the fetched base rewrote history; skips stale-token reconciles without mutating or emitting stale status; emits unknown without mutation when fetch fails or the base ref is missing. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-and-reconciliation-part-03.spec.ts: routes runtime preserved-branch force-delete through the selected WSL project runtime; replies to a waiting client with the error of a delete that fails after acceptance; treats forced runtime deletion of an already-missing unregistered worktree as cleanup; treats normal runtime deletion of an already-missing unregistered worktree as cleanup. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-and-reconciliation-part-02.spec.ts: warns that a missing-repo removal only forgot the workspace; restores runtime watchers when CLI worktree deletion fails after teardown; does not re-spend the drain budget on a removal after a wedged install was abandoned; routes runtime worktree removal through the selected WSL project runtime; force-deletes a branch that was preserved by runtime worktree removal. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/gitlab-and-pr-bases-part-02.spec.ts: records GitLab pasted-project recents only after successful runtime lookup; threads explicit origin preference through runtime WSL PR base resolution; resolves local GitLab fork MR bases from the target project MR head ref; captures the fork MR head from a dedicated ref, not the shared FETCH_HEAD; keeps the durable MR head when the head fetch fails but the local ref resolves; routes runtime GitLab fork MR base git calls through the selected WSL project runtime. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/gitlab-and-pr-bases.spec.ts: passes SSH connection ids through GitLab task operations; routes runtime GitLab issue, MR, work-item, and todo actions through the selected WSL project runtime; routes runtime GitLab MR details, review-management, job, and pasted URL actions through the selected WSL project runtime; normalizes runtime GitLab issue list arguments like the desktop IPC path. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-setup-and-startup-part-03.spec.ts: does not warn when setup is explicitly skipped for CLI-created worktrees; puts the agent a create starts in the first default tab, as the window does; keeps the 8s main-runtime startup readiness budget for agents without an override; gives OpenCode the 20s main-runtime startup readiness budget; launches explicit startup agents with prompts for CLI-created worktrees. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-setup-and-startup.spec.ts: returns a setup launch payload for CLI-created worktrees when hooks are explicitly enabled; does not hand the window a setup main never tried to start; passes the selected Windows setup shell into runtime runner generation; follows normal setup policy for CLI-created worktrees without activating them; uses returned WSL setup shell metadata when runtime spawns setup; uses the shell-aware setup runner for windowless creates without a startup command; reports the in-process setup hook as running when nothing can launch the runner. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-sleep-and-teardown-part-02.spec.ts: coalesces two clients sleeping the same host worktree; stops exactly the expected live PTYs for a worktree; explains a refused workspace close instead of throwing the raw refusal enum. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-summaries-part-03.spec.ts: marks the desktop-active worktree as isActive; includes SSH-backed worktrees in the mobile worktree summary; caches repeated malformed path misses before normalizing them again. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-summaries-part-02.spec.ts: keeps title-only foreground work ahead of monitoring in another pane; keeps a local hook row while a connected PTY still backs its pane; keeps an OSC row via its connected PTY after the pane binding is cleared. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-summaries.spec.ts: resolves files through a source-visible linked-checkout worktree; marks saved session tabs with live PTYs as host sidebar activity; attributes live legacy PTYs from saved layout bindings when their panes are hidden; marks saved browser tabs as host sidebar activity like desktop; falls back to the path-keyed GitHub cache entry; includes folder workspaces in compact worktree summaries for mobile; attaches inline agent rows from the latest OSC 9999 status; projects monitoring over a title-derived working status. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-creation-and-orchestration-part-03.spec.ts: pushes to an idle pane when the only live waiter filters out the message type; resolves a registered waiter without PTY-injecting when the leaf is already idle; keeps already-idle status after tui-idle wait for immediate message delivery; resolves message waiters when notifyMessageArrived is called; does not resolve type-filtered message waiters for unrelated message types; removes message waiter abort listeners after message arrival; resolves message waiters on timeout when no message arrives. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-creation-and-orchestration-part-02.spec.ts: delivers pending mail via notifyMessageArrived when the recipient is already idle; does not keep retrying when every pending row was already pointed; repoints pending rows restored with a live-idle coordinator. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-13.spec.ts: rolls back a half-created terminal whose surface never publishes. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-12.spec.ts: rejects startup prompts for agents that require post-ready stdin; uses portable Unix quoting for mobile agent launch commands in WSL project runtimes; keeps PowerShell quoting for mobile agent launch commands in Windows host runtimes; uses cmd.exe quoting for mobile agent launch commands in local Windows host runtimes; publishes headless mobile session agent identity with synthesized PTY status; rejects disabled mobile session agent launches before spawning; validates mobile terminal insertion anchors before resolving agent launch commands. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-11.spec.ts: coalesces a reconnect close burst onto one authoritative PTY inventory; keeps an explicit user close destructive while the PTY is live; builds mobile session agent launch commands on the runtime host; injects mobile quick-command prompts into the host-built agent startup command. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-10.spec.ts: closes persisted headless terminal parents before any prior list call; tears down a serve-owned headless tab on close while a renderer is attached so it cannot resurrect; defers a renderer-published pending tab to the renderer instead of tearing it down; returns a delegated close outcome with no selection tombstone when the renderer owns the outcome; tears down a runtime pending shell the renderer never adopted on close. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-08.spec.ts: materializes a plain shell when the pending tab has no launch agent; hydrates legacy persisted terminal tabs without layout entries; reads and indexes the full agent-status snapshot once per mobile projection; kills persisted SSH PTYs when closing hydrated headless tabs before pane metadata is restored; materializes hydrated pending headless terminals with the persisted session identity. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-07.spec.ts: hydrates a persisted SSH-owned pane before an attached renderer publishes its graph. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-05.spec.ts: publishes the desktop's tab name over the live agent title, and the live title without one; uses fresh neutral PTY titles over stale mobile snapshot and OSC titles; operates PTY-backed mobile session terminals without a renderer graph; reuses pane close for live PTYs that do not own a renderer tab; lists PTY-backed mobile session terminals without a renderer graph; shows and resolves active PTY-backed mobile session terminals without a renderer graph. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-04.spec.ts: creates mobile session terminals for folder workspaces in a headless runtime server; spawns fresh headless SSH mobile session terminals instead of reattaching synthetic local ids; hydrates headless mobile session terminals from the host workspace session; keeps live headless mobile session terminals when a desktop renderer publishes without them; publishes laptop-created remote runtime split terminals to phone session tabs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-part-02.spec.ts: does not report headless wake degradation without sleeping records; does not wake slept agents for non-mobile session-only activation; does not rewrite unread metadata when a mobile activation finds the worktree already read; returns unread:false from worktree.ps after a mobile activation clears the flag; materializes pending mobile session terminals without focusing desktop clients; closes browser mobile session tabs when addressed by browser workspace id. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs.spec.ts: resolves mobile terminal surfaces by exact split leaf; closes the matching mobile terminal UUID leaf without closing the whole tab; closes the whole mobile terminal tab when addressed by parent tab id; activates the active split leaf when addressed by parent tab id; clears unread metadata on mobile worktree activation without focusing desktop clients; wakes slept agents on the host renderer when a phone activates a worktree. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-05.spec.ts: publishes the hook provider session on a headless mobile tab so native chat can address the transcript; recovers the agent type from the hook row when the pane was launched without an agent hint; reads one agent-status snapshot per projection, not one per terminal tab; waits for unknown-launch foreground owner before publishing Pi-compatible mobile status; keeps Pi-compatible mobile session status as Pi for an unknown-launch foreground pi PTY; keeps renderer-vetted mobile agent status for custom-titled terminals. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-04.spec.ts: publishes terminal surface agent status for paired web clients; preserves authoritative OMP identity for Pi-compatible remote terminal snapshots; normalizes a remote OMP title without republishing omitted launch identity; skips the foreground-process probe when the PTY launch agent is already known; probes the foreground process only on a status transition for unknown launch agents; passes the client signal and the slept-worktree refusal to the spawn. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-03.spec.ts: does not use stale runtime-created PTY status when a neutral PTY title exists; recognizes runtime-created Codex PTY handles from the ready prompt; recognizes runtime-created Antigravity PTY handles from the ready prompt; recognizes live leaf Antigravity terminals from the ready prompt; recognizes a later Antigravity header with a prompt but no model line; keeps mobile terminal surfaces visible while their leaf handle is pending. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-02.spec.ts: lets Claude agents management titles clear stale runtime-created title status; does not recognize live Claude agents panes from a Claude foreground process; does not let stale tab-level agent titles override current neutral pane titles; lists live terminals with fresh pane titles over stale tab titles; lets adopted neutral pane titles use non-shell foreground fallback; lets adopted neutral pane titles retry wrapper foregrounds until recognized; authorizes settled CLI prompts only after positive %s foreground identity; does not recognize arbitrary foreground TUIs as running agents; lets live neutral pane titles retry wrapper foregrounds until recognized; lets current Claude agents PTY titles override stale runtime-created OSC titles; does not let stale Claude agents OSC titles suppress current PTY title activity. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status.spec.ts: keeps preallocated terminal handles valid across renderer reloads; pr