nload; keeps the retained artifact when a new download has no usable digest; keeps the retained artifact when an unrelated download event arrives; clears the retained artifact; preserves the artifact across a recheck of the same version; clears the artifact when another version takes over; preserves the artifact for an unknown or empty version; is a no-op without a retained artifact; returns the built command and package file name for a verified package; reports missing without a retained artifact; propagates a package-manager discovery failure; rejects a well-formed digest that belongs to another file; never hashes a package that a malformed digest failed to arm; rejects a path outside the cache root; rejects the cache root itself; rejects a package in the updater directory itself; rejects a pending directory that is a symlink out of the cache; performs one hash pass for concurrent requests; revalidates once the in-flight pass settles; does not reuse an in-flight pass for a different artifact; starts a fresh proof when the same package is captured again; returns the verified package path; returns missing without a retained artifact. src/main/updater/releases/updater-prerelease-feed-readiness.test.ts: accepts a GitHub %s asset redirect as ready; reports a GitHub asset request error as unavailable; reports not-ready with a verified last-good tag when the newest assets are unavailable; does not classify a non-positive tag limit as feed unavailability; reproduces the v1.4.142 publishing incident as not-ready; reports transport failures as unavailable instead of not-ready; treats an explicit asset 404 as not-ready when another asset is unavailable; accepts absolute manifest asset URLs without rewriting them to release asset paths; returns not-ready with an older ready update as last-good while newest is publishing. src/main/updater/releases/updater-release-builds.test.ts: lists hourly builds from the dedicated repo, newest first; lists daily builds from the dedicated repo, newest first; separates stable from rc in the shared main repo; skips drafts and unparseable tags; keeps a composed release title and drops one that repeats the tag; hides builds that published no artifact for this platform; returns an empty list when no build has this platform artifact; keeps mac builds visible on macOS regardless of the Windows leg; resolves the platform installer download url; leaves the installer url null when the release published no installer; tolerates a release whose assets are missing or malformed; sends the local gh token as a bearer header when one is available; sends no authorization header when gh has no token; retries unauthenticated once when GitHub rejects the token; does not retry a 401 that was already unauthenticated; falls back to the per-IP bucket when the token is rate limited and tells the gh breaker; reports a secondary limit carrying retry-after without retrying or tripping the breaker; records a primary limit in the token scope %s; keeps %s authenticated when only %s is blocked; skips the token while its scope %s is blocked; surfaces a rate limit with its reset time and a sign-in hint when unauthenticated; omits the sign-in hint when the rate-limited request was authenticated; treats 429 as a rate limit; reports a 403 without rate-limit headers as a plain HTTP error; reports a missing hourly repo distinctly; is null when GitHub sent no reset; prefers retry-after over the primary reset epoch; falls back to the primary reset epoch when there is no retry-after; reads retry-after as seconds; reads retry-after as an HTTP date; pins an hourly tag at the hourly repo download path; pins a daily tag at the daily repo download path; pins a stable tag at the main repo download path; rejects a tag that is not a version. src/main/updater/updater.build-channel-selection.test.ts: uses the display label in the unsupported-platform %s pinned-build error; still pins %s from an unsigned Windows dev build; restores ordinary release checks 