tory even when the host reported nothing. src/main/wsl/discovery/distro-catalog.test.ts: retries asynchronous discovery after a transient wsl.exe failure; retries synchronous discovery after a transient wsl.exe failure; retries asynchronous discovery after wsl.exe reports no distros yet; retries synchronous discovery after wsl.exe reports no distros yet; bounds the wsl.exe spawn rate while no distros are installed; bounds the asynchronous spawn rate while no distros are installed; still caches a non-empty distro list for the process lifetime; re-probes a docker-desktop-only machine once a user distro can appear; backs off while the list keeps coming back empty; backs off after repeated distro-list failures; caps the empty-list backoff at five minutes; keeps reporting an empty result after it goes stale; keeps reporting a known distro list indefinitely; bounds cached homes while retaining the most recently used distros; still lists distros, and an excluded distro home probe fails like any other probe; gives the async home probe time for a cold boot instead of killing it at 5 s; retries availability after a probe timeout instead of latching false; bounds the probe rate while the failure window is open; caches a successful probe for the process lifetime; names an explicit spawn directory, so no deleted cwd can read as ENOENT; shares one wsl.exe spawn between concurrent probes; keeps reporting the last observed answer after it goes stale; holds a definitive failure far longer than a timeout when %s; backs off after repeated probe failures; re-probes a seeded retryable failure once its window lapses; re-probes availability once a distro list succeeds after %s; does not drop an availability failure for an empty distro list; keeps reporting unavailable off Windows without probing. src/main/wsl/discovery/wsl-distro-holder.test.ts: runs a busybox-safe loop through --exec and names the distro; spawns a detached-style holder, records it, and waits for the distro to run; a hold