rship resolves, then resume at the bounded interval\",\n            \"tracked terminal state reset clears delayed foreground ownership markers\",\n            \"raw chunks, semantic idle transitions, and visible output remain exact\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/terminal/adoption/terminal-subscriber-driven-daemon-attach.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\"retries an existing subscriber when provider inventory becomes ready\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/session-tabs/session-tabs-inventory-census-race.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"creation and removal at the census release edge are subsumed once, and a delayed pre-boundary change is not replayed\",\n            \"post-boundary creation and removal replay after the initial snapshot in sequence order\",\n            \"create/remove/recreate transitions are preserved without collapse\",\n            \"a post-boundary projected-state change is delivered without a new snapshot revision\",\n            \"an older coalesced callback cannot overwrite a newer immediate change\",\n            \"initialization churn publishes only the latest projected state and repeated structural overflow fails after bounded recollection\",\n            \"disconnect aborts the census and removes the real runtime listener\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/session-tabs-empty-inventory-daemon-oracle.unit.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"unpublished empty inventory keeps resume dispatch at zero with the original daemon session, process id, and writer as the sole live writer\",\n            \"an authoritative empty inventory settles the mirror and releases exactly one resume dispatch with zero liveness probes\",\n            \"re-enabling unconditional empty hydration makes the identical oracle red with one resume dispatch, two session ids, two process ids, and two writer calls\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-host-restart-background-sync.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"preserves daemon PID and target PTY identity across the paired host relaunch\",\n            \"foregrounds the daemon-backgrounded target on its first post-relaunch remote observation\",\n            \"delivers target and post-relaunch control terminal input and live output\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-probe-gap-recovery.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\"replaces a stale paired stream when the PTY snapshot advanced\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-stall-recovery.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"restarts one ACK-starved paired terminal stream without replacing its PTY\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/headless-paired-remote-terminal-stall-recovery.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\"recovers an ACK-starved stream from an isolated headless Orca host\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-lossy-initial-snapshot.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"a nonempty lossy initial snapshot paints exactly once on a paired client\",\n            \"the authoritative host cursor advances and live output resumes exactly once\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-truncated-tail-first-paint.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"paints a paired remote terminal when only its retained text tail overflowed\",\n            \"legacy paired hosts retain the lossy hidden-manager budget fallback\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/paired-remote-terminal-retention-memory.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"ordinary-parks paired terminals and restores authoritative host scrollback\",\n            \"warm-mounted hidden paired streams schedule zero renderer output work under sustained host output\",\n            \"six hidden real PTYs publish and apply only exact working and idle title transitions across paired transport\",\n            \"client recovery completes while every target terminal remains unmounted in the host renderer\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/headless-paired-remote-terminal-retention-memory.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"ordinary-parks paired terminals against an isolated headless Orca host\",\n            \"cold-activates only visible paired terminals against an isolated headless host\",\n            \"the headless host bounds real-PTY decorative title transport and production store application\",\n            \"the headless host shares the zero-hidden-renderer-work and exact-restoration contract\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/terminal-parked-memory.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"releases un-parkable hidden worktree buffers only once the retention budget engages\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/rpc/terminal-multiplex-pty-wait-capacity.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"admits 128 active streams, rejects the 129th, and reuses released capacity\",\n            \"reserves PTY wait capacity independently from active streams\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"pauses capable paired output while hidden and restores exactly on reveal\",\n            \"locally gates hidden paired output when a legacy host cannot pause it\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-pty-transport-activation-inventory-fallback.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"keeps a mounted HUB mirror alive when the old stream ends before the replacement snapshot\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/renderer/src/web/web-preload-api-runtime-environment.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"keeps pairing while manual disconnect fences passive reconnects\",\n            \"returns a disconnect envelope when a queued active runtime call disconnects\",\n            \"returns a disconnect envelope when a queued selected environment call disconnects\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]",
        "Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The retained runtime registration driver loses three complete imported fragments: changed-working-label title facts and suppressed-frame tracked snapshots; refusing SSH GitLab MR-base lookup before local Git/glab calls; and missing folder-workspace path creation/update refusal before spawn/store mutation. These alarms are intentionally lost. Other imported fragments and separately rooted dated receipts are unchanged; they are not equivalent replacement coverage.  Original scope text is retained as the exact suffix of coverageNotes/oracle; historical evidence is unchanged.",
        "Audit3446 composes ROOT-adopted3441/independent3442: intentionally removes100 authored registrations/119 potential expanded cases (118 conditional-active before platform gates) across16 sources, retaining11 authored/13 expanded cases and deleting6 whole suites. Two parent registrar import/call cleanups and the unused68line CLI recording fixture carry zero test credit. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. The decorative fanout suite retains only real OSC9999 ingestion through runtime/title heartbeat/viewer past the stale boundary, preserving stateStartedAt and clearing expired prompt metadata. Spinner volume/zero-work inventories, Pi/Grok frame tables, rich-status and foreground-reset examples are retired. Existing receipts for separate paired-terminal sources retain their original scopes.  All prior notes and complete dated receipts retain their original scopes.",
        "Audit3446 archived original assertionRef after source reduction; historical scope only, raw original object follows:\n{\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/session-tabs-decorative-title-fanout.unit.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"2,880 decorative spinner and bare-native real-PTY OSC chunks publish zero session-tabs snapshots or serialized bytes after semantic convergence\",\n            \"the viewer performs zero snapshot applies and zero store mutations during decorative activity\",\n            \"after 30 minutes, one globally spaced refresh per worktree keeps every mirrored working status fresh\",\n            \"exact Pi and rotating normalized Pi/Grok frames renew explicit and fallback status without changing stateStartedAt or acknowledgement semantics\",\n            \"matching title evidence renews retained OSC hook status without resetting stateStartedAt, then drops unverifiable prompt metadata after the hook row expires\",\n            \"renderer-authored rich status keeps its original lease, then renews only coarse title-confirmed state and provider identity\",\n            \"ordinary-shell title transitions replace working stateStartedAt with the completion transition time\",\n            \"decorative heartbeats remain blocked until unknown foreground ownership resolves, then resume at the bounded interval\",\n            \"tracked terminal state reset clears delayed foreground ownership markers\",\n            \"raw chunks, semantic idle transitions, and visible output remain exact\"\n          ]\n        }",
        "Audit3832 deliberately retires76 authored/79 finite cases:75 runtime compatibility cases/78 finite cases across14 fragments, plus one localization extractor default-flag case. Three whole runtime fragments are deleted;27 authored/30 finite cases remain across the reviewed sources. This gate retains only its own selected scope; no equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/native/remote evidence is claimed. Runtime component A: Audit3828 composes3822 with independent3824: deliberately retires49 authored/52 finite cases from seven compatibility fragments, leaving15 authored/18 finite cases and deleting two entire fragments. Accepted losses: positive folder-worker recovery/materialization and reveal deadline; persisted-key normalization and legacy split/group/focus projection; fixed stale CAS refusal; occupied/alias/restored/preallocated terminal-handle variants; fixed OpenCode/Cursor/Claude/Codex/Antigravity classification, readiness, title and management examples; direct private-map browser authority projections; browser-focus and OMP title projection; already-aborted claim cleanup. Additional3824 loss: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-02.spec.ts :: does not poll a wrapper foreground for a speculative CLI prompt send :: Speculative retryForegroundWrappers:false check must return false on a wrapper after one foreground read, without polling the supplied later codex response. These real bounded alarms are deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained callbacks are unchanged and provide only their own bounded scope, not equivalent replacement. Historical receipts do not validate reduced callbacks. No fresh runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser evidence or full transitive closure is claimed. Runtime component B: Audit3834 deliberately retires26 authored/26 finite cases from seven fresh compatibility fragments, leaving10/10 and deleting the one-case saved-binding reattachment fragment. Original position58 is excluded: its existing substantive3578 KEEP7 review remains historical, with no fresh credit. Accepted losses: fixed hook/provider-session identities and stale metadata refusal; decorative/pre-title foreground ordering variants; saved-binding surface reattachment; saved-row exit ghost removal and silent activation selection; unsupported headless wake; positive pending materialization/group projections; per-caller navigation selection; positive SSH hydration/read partition; laptop mobile publication/buffer and background/pending/status projections; abnormal/unregistered SSH grace, normal-exit refusal, persisted SSH hydration, positive serve reattachment, pending-agent launch arguments and direct seeded running-launch admission guard. These are real bounded alarms deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained cases preserve their own distinct deferred foreground coalescing, usable handle continuity, stale inventory refresh, concurrent browser snapshot preservation, renderer graph fencing, caller dedup isolation, SSH partition writes, runtime split lifetime, independent relay-ready publication, lease admission/state/expiry. The direct running-launch no-spawn guard alarm is deliberately retired; no remaining owning-launch refusal coverage is claimed. Historical runs do not validate reduced callbacks. No equivalent replacement, runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser result or full transitive closure is claimed. Additional extractor loss: config/scripts/localization/source-extraction/audit-localization-native-dialogs.test.mjs :: does not change the existing renderer scan by default :: Default options must omit the five native-only fields in this supplied snippet. No equivalent replacement is claimed."
      ],
      "demotionRule": "Keep experimental or demote to protection none if decorative title frequency changes paired client-event or session-tabs publication volume after convergence, a semantic fact is dropped, paired first paint is blank, passive work reconnects after manual disconnect, a capable hidden paired manager survives ordinary parking, a legacy hidden pane schedules raw xterm output or bypasses its fallback, reveal loses requested bounded history or live PTY identity, retained buffer cells do not fall, or either headed/headless scenario flakes."
