      "coverageNotes": "Audit1640 removes low-value IPC, SSH, workspace and transcript-watcher tests without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public refusal, cancellation, execution-host and real-filesystem outcomes with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1630 removes low-value Git, GitHub/GitLab and IPC projections, argument inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained cancellation, ownership, authorization, filesystem and SQLite boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1602 removes mocked transport, deletion and ownership inventories, provider metadata projections, private callback and counter checks, and duplicate reader examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Retained tests exercise SQLite/FTS migrations, transcript/cache/sidecar changes, recovery and cursor boundaries, local process/WAL/lock/framing and generated scripts. Remote and WSL failures and some delivery races remain injected; in-process reopen does not prove crash recovery, and counters do not prove latency or memory bounds. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1301 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Platform-neutral unit coverage proves the Resource Manager closed badge performs one readiness seed, coalesces unknown spawn signals, skips known-session reattach signals, installs no interval, and re-reads only once per explicit daemon-management kill/restart. AI Vault tab-title sync uses bounded exact identities on the transcript-owning local, SSH, or runtime host and has no access to broad listing; unsupported older hosts retain persisted titles without fallback scans. WSL path translation still needs a Windows integration oracle. Audit1301: src/renderer/src/components/status-bar/use-resource-session-inventory.test.tsx removed. Visibility epochs, event identity fencing, retry and no-polling hook-layer alarms disappear. src/renderer/src/components/status-bar/resource-session-inventory.test.ts reduced. Detached-array/count/noop contracts, authoritative refresh variants, batching cadence, duplicate acknowledgements, error/pause combinations and other identity matrices lose their authored alarms. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1302: src/main/ai-vault/parse-cache/session-parse-cache-persistence.test.ts: Keep real filesystem/SQLite persistence, reopen/restart hits, changed-file invalidation, legacy/corrupt-cache recovery, concurrent scope replacement and optional-cache write failure isolation. Remove configuration/sidecar copy inventories, write-call-only timing/row counts, a wall-clock polling case with an internally hung parser, synthetic UNC aging/stat inventory and a no-op mock pretending to be failed database deletion. Lose these private configuration/scheduling/sidecar/UNC/fault wiring alarms; no equivalent replacement. Reduced selectors require fresh validation; prior full-suite receipts do not validate removed or changed coverage. No equivalent replacement or physical-provider claim.",
