        "Audit3563 scope: retire the whole Kiro OSC/hook identity suite and the OpenCode2 identity-only case; reduce Codex cached startup child-retirement and missing-session-ID tables to one case each (2 authored/4 finite removals). Intentionally lose Kiro alias/session continuity, OpenCode2 completed OSC identity continuity, cached replacement without relay-generation restart, and missing-previous-ID context-preservation alarms. Remaining provider, remote compatibility, persistence and cross-session pollution cases are not equivalent replacements. Also remove the private Codex roster-size assertion while retaining public child-absence checks. Historical evidence retains its original source scope; no new execution or transferred pass validates these reductions.",
        "Launch direct-owner cleanup current scope: This gate’s unfiltered unit command now selects a suite reduced by 82 whole registrations  / 159 potential table examples in 10 whole test Programs, including 8 registrations / 15 examples from five once-registered create-message factory closures. Lost alarms include frozen first-message/options and legacy-host fallback; distinct actions and redelivery; uncertain/refused/reloaded input custody, Retry and late proof; rich prompt/attachment upload Stop/close and handback; ordinary draft/editor/IME/StrictMode lifetime and accepted topology; provisional fallback tab placement/group/pin/order and rich worktree handoff. Four whole consent/resume-identity cases remain in two Programs; they do not replace these alarms. This entry governs current reduced-unit scope and qualifies any broader implication of unchanged oracle/coverageNotes history. Entire dated evidenceRuns, original commands/currentCommand values, counts/results and existing history retain their original scopes only; no fresh execution, transferred pass, replacement equivalence or prior upstream-removal credit is claimed.",
        "Audit2145 accepts removal of canned runtime metadata/guard/forwarding, fake in-memory persistence, private work-count and wrapper-duplication tests from the construction/orca-runtime.test.ts aggregate, plus the two automation run-context guards from runtime-workspace-launch-contracts.test.ts. Retained race, framing, physical completion and ownership callbacks remain byte-identical. Existing commands remain valid selectors; historical receipts stay unchanged and provide no fresh validation or replacement coverage for the reduced suites.",
        "Audit2133 current-parent preparation (988 authored removals; independently reviewed2099/2107/2115/2116 decisions; upstream clear-buffer and recovery-image regressions retained): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts: remove only literal registration import/call pairs await import('../orca-runtime-tests/worktree-setup-and-startup.spec'), await import('../orca-runtime-tests/gitlab-and-pr-bases.spec'); no additional authored credit. src/main/ssh/ssh-channel-multiplexer.test.ts: sends a JSON-RPC request and resolves on response; assigns unique request IDs; sends notifications without expecting a response; dispatches incoming notifications to handler; sends one keepalive frame per cadence tick; drives keepalive sends AND dead-link detection from a single interval; resolves false immediately on a disposed mux; throws on request after dispose; reports isDisposed correctly; clears registered handlers on dispose; does not retain handlers registered after dispose. src/main/persistence/worktree-sort-order-write.test.ts: re-ranks every writable row when a blocked row sits in the requested order. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/targeting-and-resilience.spec.ts: routes tab switch and capture start by explicit page id; accepts focus on tab switch without altering bridge args (focus is main-side concern); keeps terminal cwd resolution fail-soft when the provider is unavailable. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-and-reconciliation-part-04.spec.ts: drops the bounded scan cache when orphan-cleanup removal completes; clears optimistic reconcile tokens when a CLI worktree removal succeeds; emits drift without mutating when the fetched base fast-forwards created HEAD; emits base_changed without mutation when the fetched base rewrote history; skips stale-token reconciles without mutating or emitting stale status; emits unknown without mutation when fetch fails or the base ref is missing. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-and-reconciliation-part-03.spec.ts: routes runtime preserved-branch force-delete through the selected WSL project runtime; replies to a waiting client with the error of a delete that fails after acceptance; treats forced runtime deletion of an already-missing unregistered worktree as cleanup; treats normal runtime deletion of an already-missing unregistered worktree as cleanup. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-removal-and-reconciliation-part-02.spec.ts: warns that a missing-repo removal only forgot the workspace; restores runtime watchers when CLI worktree deletion fails after teardown; does not re-spend the drain budget on a removal after a wedged install was abandoned; routes runtime worktree removal through the selected WSL project runtime; force-deletes a branch that was preserved by runtime worktree removal. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/gitlab-and-pr-bases-part-02.spec.ts: records GitLab pasted-project recents only after successful runtime lookup; threads explicit origin preference through runtime WSL PR base resolution; resolves local GitLab fork MR bases from the target project MR head ref; captures the fork MR head from a dedicated ref, not the shared FETCH_HEAD; keeps the durable MR head when the head fetch fails but the local ref resolves; routes runtime GitLab fork MR base git calls through the selected WSL project runtime. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/gitlab-and-pr-bases.spec.ts: passes SSH connection ids through GitLab task operations; routes runtime GitLab issue, MR, work-item, and todo actions through the selected WSL project runtime; routes runtime GitLab MR details, review-management, job, and pasted URL actions through the selected WSL project runtime; normalizes runtime GitLab issue list arguments like the desktop IPC path. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-setup-and-startup-part-03.spec.ts: does not warn when setup is explicitly skipped for CLI-created worktrees; puts the agent a create starts in the first default tab, as the window does; keeps the 8s main-runtime startup readiness budget for agents without an override; gives OpenCode the 20s main-runtime startup readiness budget; launches explicit startup agents with prompts for CLI-created worktrees. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-setup-and-startup.spec.ts: returns a setup launch payload for CLI-created worktrees when hooks are explicitly enabled; does not hand the window a setup main never tried to start; passes the selected Windows setup shell into runtime runner generation; follows normal setup policy for CLI-created worktrees without activating them; uses returned WSL setup shell metadata when runtime spawns setup; uses the shell-aware setup runner for windowless creates without a startup command; reports the in-process setup hook as running when nothing can launch the runner. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-sleep-and-teardown-part-02.spec.ts: coalesces two clients sleeping the same host worktree; stops exactly the expected live PTYs for a worktree; explains a refused workspace close instead of throwing the raw refusal enum. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-summaries-part-03.spec.ts: marks the desktop-active worktree as isActive; includes SSH-backed worktrees in the mobile worktree summary; caches repeated malformed path misses before normalizing them again. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-summaries-part-02.spec.ts: keeps title-only foreground work ahead of monitoring in another pane; keeps a local hook row while a connected PTY still backs its pane; keeps an OSC row via its connected PTY after the pane binding is cleared. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-summaries.spec.ts: resolves files through a source-visible linked-checkout worktree; marks saved session tabs with live PTYs as host sidebar activity; attributes live legacy PTYs from saved layout bindings when their panes are hidden; marks saved 