iption through the subscribed production parent; bounds upstream active-SSH visits for $population records, fallback=$fallback; derives %s destinations without requiring type or a workflow child ID; terminates a $path parent $status with no third request or intermediate toast; does not recover a first child %s. tests/e2e/cross-version-wire/agent-permission-legacy-spawn.unit.test.ts: keeps exact legacy ordering when structured creation cannot express afterTabId; can create a terminal without selecting the target worktree; preserves the legacy fresh-agent path when host authority is unavailable. tests/e2e/paired-instant-browser-tab.spec.ts: shows a paired browser tab before its create RPC resolves, then keeps it as one tab; adopts a paired browser tab without rebuilding its chrome. tests/e2e/session-tabs-decorative-title-fanout.unit.test.ts: bounds host publication and renderer application across remote worktrees; globally caps decorative freshness while every working status stays fresh. tests/e2e/session-tabs/mobile-session-active-performance.unit.test.ts: bounds saved-order publication selection at N and 10N without rematerializing navigation; bounds admitted placement reconciliation during supported reads at N and 10N; bounds selection input visits at 50 and 500 rows, including unavailable-target projection; keeps publication scoped to a changed worktree and shared by listeners at N and 10N; bounds preserved-chat merge and runtime-owned hydration at N and 10N (legacy=%s); bounds actual native retirement and shared delivery work at N and 10N. tests/e2e/session-tabs/mobile-session-active-publication.unit.test.ts: does not substitute a preserved row for an unavailable explicit legacy selection; resolves main-layout group selection %s (omitted group=%s). tests/e2e/structured-agent-session-launch-admission.unit.test.ts: opens a direct caller's terminal with the caller's own CLI arguments on a decline; opens the chat on the server that admitted it; opens only the termina