ed access; names the saved dependency when dependent state blocks an SSH access link; handles lost link responses without connecting or verifying again; invalidates old transport only after authenticated access is published; rejects changed request tuple after a completed link; rejects provisioning and missing durable generations without connecting; treats a lost successful unlink response as an idempotent no-op; hashes connection identity, not display state or owner; strictly validates ports and request IDs. src/main/startup/cli-launch-redirect.test.ts: detects a launch that received the unpacked CLI entrypoint; ignores normal desktop launches; ignores the entrypoint when it is only the executable itself (argv[0]); applies on Linux too; strips injected Chromium switches before node-mode CLI arguments; keeps user flags after the command and malformed boolean assignments; does not treat a later positional entrypoint path as the launcher; redirects a direct binary launch with no AppImage env at all; strips Chromium switches node mode would reject; preserves desktop-shaped switches after the command; leaves direct serve in-process but redirects its help; treats help as a CLI launch even without a command; treats %s as a CLI launch even without a command; does not treat a value of %s as a CLI early-exit flag; does not treat a serve option value as a help request; does not reinterpret help after the argument terminator; leaves a plain desktop launch alone; skips flag values when looking for the command positional; preserves a project selector in %j; does not apply the command form on macOS or Windows; never redirects an unpackaged build; runs the in-package CLI in Electron node mode with sanitized env; refuses to redirect twice so a dropped ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE cannot loop; reports a missing CLI entrypoint instead of booting the desktop app; execs a direct serve into the CLI so it keeps its pid and honours profile and supervise; keeps ORCA_USER_DATA_PATH for a direct ser