        "Audit3108 source-only reduction (3094/3095/3100): retire 27 authored/30 expanded cases, including complete markdown view-state, file-preview link-open and CLI agent-server-route suites, without replacement. Deliberate losses include preview visibility/reference lifetime and same-path owners; SSH stat, directory/missing-target, explicit-null owner, nonmarkdown line/column, local URI routing, remote-to-client guard and same-file reuse; document-preview source-owner/folder/reuse routing, stable grant location and outside-workspace POSIX/Windows request projection; and verified remote CLI send/check refusal, suggested --on argv/copy, shell no-probe bypass, unverified-launch admission and older-peer refusal. Retain two markdown source-runtime/qualified-reveal alarms, one stale grant-rejection fence and two remote read/mutation evidence policies, with original callbacks. Final last-wins reveal did not prove transient cancellation; CLI prerequisite did not prove no real send, and envelope tests do not execute server refusal. No fresh runtime, rendered UI, actual file/SSH/paired transport, authorization, mixed-version or performance result is claimed.",
        "Audit3114 incorporates source3101: retire three structured Claude child-environment wrapper cases covering inherited stamp isolation/default and explicit entrypoint, Windows SDK-key canonicalization/default/duplicate-key order, and configured lookup/final environment/config-dir conjunction. Keep direct auth/session sanitation and Windows-versus-Linux overlay checks, actual executable lookup from supplied inherited PATH, native Windows child environment delivery, and stale option-mutation fencing. These are not equivalent replacements for the retired wrapper alarms. No fresh test/runtime, real login-shell probe, Claude SDK startup, remote/mixed-version, UI or performance result is claimed.",
        "Audit3114 incorporates source3105: retire 17 authored/20 expanded daemon launch-note cases, including the entire two-case SessionLaunchNote suite. Deliberately lose split-marker carry across same-token re-arm, stale-token retirement refusal, foreground tri-state and serial settlement, omitted-note/no-incarnation mixed-version policy, sticky retirement, first-incarnation/replacement launch preservation and held-launch precedence. Keep only the unchanged unresolved foreground-read race against a later finished attach. Supplied notes/foreground and runtime calls do not establish actual daemon/main restart, SSH, native Windows observation, mobile UI, equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/performance validation.",
        "Audit3114 incorporates source3109: retire six authored/35 expanded pricing cases: 21 accepted model-name examples, 10 unsupported/future-model fail-closed examples, malformed TTL clamp, unknown-model estimate refusal, flat-model long-context disregard and oversized long-context clamp. Keep mixed five-minute/one-hour write allocation and short/all-long/mixed long-context allocation with original fixed oracles. Real parser/refusal/bounds alarms are knowingly lost without equivalent replacement; retained tests do not validate provider rates, actual billing or request threshold classification. Preserve the archived usage-scan-append source-freeze receipt without transferring historical execution/performance credit. No fresh runtime result is claimed.",
        "Audit3128 scoped coverage reduction: Audit3121 removes VoiceDictationLanguageSetting.test.tsx (Spanish-to-es callback and unsupported-model Korean option presence) and voice-speech-model-rows.test.ts (provider/language-order/retired-on-disk list policy); these real narrow alarms are deliberately retired without replacement. VoiceSpeechModelSection per-model concurrent deletion remains unchanged. Audit3122 removes the direct absolute/parent-segment sparse-directory exception-type sample and the five-row IPC sparse-preset error-code/non-save table (two authored/six expanded cases). Those real typed-validation and IPC refusal/error-code alarms are deliberately retired. Keep both real symlink/junction floating-directory trust cases and the minimal RPC structured validation-reason serialization case. The RPC case does not replace IPC save/refusal behavior, typed normalization for both path inputs, actual Git sparse checkout or rendered localization. No equivalent replacement or fresh test/runtime/platform/remote/performance validation is claimed. Audit3124 removes ExperimentalPane.test.tsx (ordinary Pet switch callback), WorkspaceDirectorySetting.test.tsx (padded absolute saved-path normalization/no-write blur), and repository-search.perf.test.ts (navigation/selected-pane builder-call policy, fixture cardinality/nonempty entries and renamed project keyword inclusion). These real narrow alarms are retired without replacement; RepositoryPane.search.test.tsx search-to-sparse-editor request remains unchanged. Audit3129: resolver Windows case-insensitive and POSIX case-sensitive configured-env composition plus mocked-base launch-preflight Windows composition are intentionally no longer checked by the two deleted suites. No equivalent coverage claimed. Keep runtime-structured-agent-host-env.test.ts unchanged: configured Windows Claude-home account identity and host-account precedence remain checked.",
        "Audit3146 combines source reviews3132/3133/3135/3138/3143: intentionally retire20authored/31expanded cases without equivalent replacement. Provider-session losses: structured-native terminal-resume exclusion, metadata-less completed identity, new-turn completion clearing, Pi provider-only/periodic/manual promotion, changed-transcript launch-config isolation, Pi/omp/prime-agent completed-session remote/manual-shutdown promotion, and quit/done precedence over heartbeat. Side-thread/question losses: finished-pane acquisition, hidden title/recap states, local/relay/relay-done conversation takeover with prompt/session/child resets, plain-message abandonment, compaction/session replacement and completion resets. Codex startup losses: incoming-owner cached child replacement, old-relay foreign live-session correction, completed foreign-root turn-fact permutations. Transcript losses: real temporary-JSONL partial sibling/final-child completion, unlabelled child attribution, compact cached replay preservation and100/1000completed-child roster retention/release. Compiler-ratchet losses: valid-line uncompiled-list parser grammar examples and injected-existence stale-path filtering; these did not exercise actual filesystem canonicalization or build exclusion. These are real lifecycle, ownership, replay, liveness and retention alarms, including recent#40246 regressions, deliberately lost. Retained conditional record replacement, clockless root/SSH owner isolation, persisted main-thread fork rejection, partial/final question-answer lifetime, cached-roster/missing-ID/live HTTP/durable startup boundaries and restarted-relay refusal/acceptance do not replace those losses. No native/SSH/WSL execution or equivalent coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit3156 combines3147/3150/3152/3153/3154: deliberately retires39authored/40expanded native-chat recovery cases, eight whole suites and two orphan test-support files without equivalent replacement. Lost alarms: lost-reply unconfirmed reconciliation, skipped rows/counts and missed-frame repair, unknown/pending outcome and omitted-failure-list compatibility, uncertain history after dismissal, retry/refusal/dismiss lifecycle, hidden/consumed picker ownership, result-tree keyboard focus/disclosure and all-skipped retirement; unconfirmed-over-conflict guidance and failed-chat changes despite older host timestamps; nearest-listed ancestor/cyclic forest shape, descendant membership, host ordering/missing-host local fallback; skipped/readiness/admission counts, provisional skip/progress monotonicity, early per-chat verdicts with batch pending protection, older-host waiting, start-slot/delivery distinction, retry-over-failure and unknown-after-withdrawal attention; remote snooze/reconnect/reoffer, unseen mixed summary through open/close, watched completion retirement, new success beside old failure, failed-reread mixed-result preservation, filter/collapse completion resets, retry summary replacement and current-offer/history selection; cross-host workspace identity, rendered cyclic reachability, nested tri-state/toggle propagation, project eligibility isolation and collapse preserving selection. Exact fallback-list completion barrier, batched verdict/cleanup retention, stale-read versus dismissal publication race, and requested-but-never-rendered finished-run retirement remain; they do not replace retired alarms.",
        "Audit3165 combines source3160/3162: deliberately retires six authored/expanded cases across three whole suites without equivalent replacement. Launch/status losses: observed React-render pending/resuming coordination across settings and deferred offer read; stale-offer reread suppressing dialog reopen; held-local-chat recovery visibility with new-chat preferences off; disabled-local admission avoiding offer RPC despite an injected but unconsumed paired-tab fixture; and run-only lost-reply uncertainty reachability until direct viewed-run retirement. Launch probe does not prove arbitrary synchronous-store atomicity, the paired fixture is not remote runtime enrollment, and the status case directly marks viewed state rather than rendering the summary. Crew-hook losses: old-host method_not_found cache persists across party changes but is released by independently supplied connection generation/verified pairing status or pairing revision, with actual frame publication and teardown. These are real narrow coordination, admission, uncertainty and mixed-version cache alarms consciously lost. Exact web verified-runtime writer handoff guard remains; it does not replace those alarms or prove live host/native/mobile delivery.",
        "Audit3178 combines source3169/3170/3175: deliberately retires eight authored units (six Vitest cases and two imperative custom relay scenarios), including two whole suites, without equivalent replacement. Voice Section loses per-model pending-delete isolation across interleaved A/B completion and the two-success refresh-call alarm; exact VoicePane delayed key-clear/newer enabled-toggle merge remains and does not replace row deletion coverage. Speech loses dedicated rating-scale/inclusive-ceiling, unsupported-versus-unmeasured, explicit/system-language precedence/locale alias, accuracy versus fast named/default/best-measured selection, and unmeasured/no-match examples; exact offered-user-pick versus retired-selection case and its fixture remain. Relay loses legacy ping-delivery count/liveness sampled before the silence deadline and grouped malformed Bearer/host-ID 401/429 routing checks; twelve real Worker/DurableObject/shipped-client scenarios remain, not equivalent replacement for those narrow alarms. Six prior speech cases are not all deleted: approved successor3175 keeps the original user-choice case. No actual credential/file persistence, native/GPU/engine/download delivery, production assignment policy or deployed-runtime validation is claimed by this reduction.",
        "Audit3191 combines approved source3182/3187/3188: deliberately retires thirteen authored Vitest registrations and fifteen expanded cases, including five whole suites, without equivalent replacement. Attachment intake loses real portal/native-capture terminal interception and unowned-container refusal, immediate child-only committed availability/claim-ref negotiation and delivery, and direct-target over stable focused/background composer routing through disable/re-enable/remount and independent question focus. Exact destination/cache/draft and final-stat owner/workspace/File-release suites remain; they do not replace Surface recipient routing. Automation authoring loses destination runtime catalog membership, local/direct-SSH exclusion of paired-runtime repos, unknown-runtime empty catalog, logical project/host/setup/repo/path context payload, and missing/nonready setup refusal; these were genuine direct helper alarms, while exact schedule transformation, legacy schedule and setup-decision suites remain. Agent picker loses setup-chat/terminal/missing-installer/unsupported-or-unknown-host row projection samples and the ordinary unsearched menu variant; the entire original26-line resume recipe suite remains, including reported bypass versus default/absent permission modes, as does the exact search-result menu callback with its fixtures, model/effort commits and staged Arguments reopen outcome. Rejected predecessor3180 full recipe deletion is excluded. No actual native drag/cursor/focus/IME, upload bytes or disk/restart persistence, full automation save/scheduler/runtime transport, real resume-process flags/environment delivery, or native menu/rendered layout validation is claimed.",
        "Audit3200 composes approved source3194: deliberately retires thirteen authored registrations/twenty-seven expanded cases in six whole automation host/list policy suites without equivalent replacement. Real RPC category/retryability and wrapped-timeout recognition, unscoped-failure/scoped-success health evidence precedence, exact-ID create selectors and per-run workspace omission, paired-web local/SSH/absent host catalog routing, incompatible/removed/unhydrated/offline execution health, runtime-before-nested-SSH recovery dispatch, and no-owned-focus/successor/foreign-list focus policy alarms are consciously lost. Retain exact20line orphan allow/refuse/precondition and exact90line cross-host same-ID search suites. No retry-timer/fence lifecycle, actual reconnect/network/write delivery, native focus, mobile/mixed-version runtime or disk persistence coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit3209 composes approved sources3202/3206: deliberately retires seven authored/expanded cases in four whole suites without equivalent replacement. Work-item queries lose real GitHub/GitLab oversized ASCII secret-prefix empty-query and whitespace-before-trim refusal alarms; inputs share the imported size bound and exercise only its fast length branch, with no multibyte or actual provider/exposure guarantee. Skill sharing loses complete/partial managed-bundle and destination-ambiguity association checks plus three negative origin/path/scheme admission examples; these do not establish uploaded contents, arbitrary-URL fetching, authorization or execution. Retain exact originless-project direct-link fallback, cloud-delete confirmation, bundled-target repair/owner isolation and explicit Windows-host preference over stale WSL suites. Rejected3201 runtime-preference removal is excluded. No real cloud/network/host/disk, mobile or mixed-version execution validation is claimed.",
        "Audit3219 removes the synthetic Cmd+J extra-source suite; this broad command no longer checks its match/tie placement and selection, announced count, empty-query cap, or workspace hiding with retained recent tabs. No replacement coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit3231 retires supported-host restore-pane key mapping, closed/open creation-sidebar toggle visibility, unrelated scope-error/null classification and quick-submit reveal/no-create checks. These broad commands lose those real narrow alarms; no replacement coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit3246 retires NewRowsMarker reveal/no-repeat and pane-scoped beforeinput checks; skill-owner option availability/count/dedup/order; six styled Input/Textarea IME forwarding rows; the static Codex/OpenCode smart-key inventory; tab-map AST ratchet diagnostic fixtures; child-roster work-budget and retained-aggregate alarms; malformed persisted floating-cwd fallback/no-crash/empty exact-root checks; the unanswered-host empty-list discriminator; the direct invalidated-cache commit-false assertion; one redundant digit-keyup IME row; cached non-supported Claude title-generator rows; and the duplicate late naming-result singleton. These root broad commands lose those specific alarms without equivalent replacement. Distinct retained owner/state checks have their own bounded claims; the real scheduler still rejects stale response data, while the direct false-return alarm is retired.",
        "Audit 3256 removes these specific alarms from the broad root unit commands: skill dialog active-share selection, close and pending-share handoff; simple keyed-record deletion; marker live-region insertion, simple landing and nine baseline policy examples; General search/control navigation inventory; orphan-count cache bootstrap; seven Codex code classifications and HTTP 429 warning mapping; two skill unread-root verdict examples; peer-mail payload and conversation-ID rejection; and the GitHub organization TABLE text-field optimistic rollback/failed-envelope example. These include real behaviors; retained tests do not provide equivalent coverage for every removed scenario. Mobile losses are recorded separately and are not coverage of these root commands.",
        "Audit 3273 removes 14 authored declarations and 19 expanded scenarios across four whole suites and eight partial suites. Retired alarms cover saved-local cancellation/layout ownership, ambiguous-owner warning reset, folder attachment routing, VM false-capability bypass, abandoned reveal warmup cleanup and viewport claim deduplication/rearming, quiet unrelated remote-removal refusal, startup-command one-shot consumption, repository/floating recovery-ledger rows, fake-React pinned-scroll intent, split-ratio state identity/subscriber suppression and fractional change, cross-host project-group join refusal, three PR request-lifetime permutations, upstream-status preservation on error, and unresolved Git-owner refusal. These regression checks are intentionally lost under the test-value audit; retained scenarios are not equivalent replacements. Historical coverage receipts remain historical, including gate35 subscriber claims.",
        "Audit 3283 removes 20 authored declarations and 31 expanded scenarios, including two whole suites. Retired alarms cover PR refresh-state pruning, shared runtime subscription cleanup and store isolation, language content-change routing and older completion ownership, ordinary panel retry-timer cleanup and pending loading, four hosted-review lifetime permutations, mocked terminal creation error/order wiring, five sleep-inventory variants with pending-frame-only assertions, palette fallback/composite highlights, Windows/UNC encoded-editor input rows, mixed-repository partial failure counts, title setters and generated-title bypass/replacement, five window-close coordinator delegation/guard/finally branches, and ambiguous-old-record frame reveal. These regression checks are intentionally lost under the test-value audit; retained cases are not equivalent replacements. Prior coverage notes and receipts remain historical.",
        "Audit 3292 combines adopted 3285/3287/3289/3293 removals: 40 authored declarations and 47 expanded scenarios, including whole frame-editor-view, ambiguous remote-delete-refusal, unverifiable-host subscription and editor-close cleanup suites. The previously reviewed dock-badge suite was already removed upstream in PR 40895 and receives zero new removal credit. Intentionally retired alarms include background browser selection and last-tab landing; main startup fallback, SSH project cleanup/survivor routing, exact-PR contradiction/saved-push positives, replay/sidecar rollback and wrapped remote error normalization; records/snapshot missing-diff hydration, ambiguous folder-owner delete refusal, focus no-op notifications, nested editor context-only cache check, pending broadcast-first status and ordinary four-confirmation aggregation; preview-source frontmatter pruning, approved local/runtime agent dispatch, non-GitHub legacy PR cache invalidation, stale merged-head transient-error fallback, empty-queue immediate query reply and unverified-to-concrete preflight risk. Additional intentionally retired alarms are injected host subscription/unsubscribe counts, synthetic editor reveal/draft/fallback/scoped close, ambiguous unread refusals and hidden mark/read roundtrip, immediate connect backoff/noError, positive mirrored evidence-clock renewal, supplied VM failure/success projections and git-local/folder-SSH wake permutations. Remaining temporal/ownership cases are narrower; no equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed.",
        "Audit 3301 combines adopted source batches 3296 and 3299: retire 27 authored declarations and 36 expanded scenarios, including six whole suites. Intentionally lost alarms cover failed-verification/recovery/restart counters and mocked hosting/toast; early overlapping pane-read scheduling/count; unreadable removal listing draft guard; bulk-purge remote-qualified and raw-local guard maps; initial-snapshot blank/mode/oversize/printable/fresh-spawn callback and replay examples; fallback mobile file close and ordinary MRU; default queue overload/drain; seeded browser-page reuse and supplied missing-page URL recreation; ambiguous sleep/hibernation owner refusal and untouched bindings/origins; ordinary selection/activity/fallback priority; skip-remote success and retained hints; supplied structured-chat unsent retention and scoped removal draft eviction; caller-chat focus precedence; open/draft PR cache eviction and merged-head fallback result inventories. Retained adverse-ordering and ownership cases are narrower and do not establish equivalent replacements. No fresh runtime, native, physical provider, cross-platform, mobile or mixed-version evidence is claimed.",
        "Audit 3312 composes adopted sources 3302 and 3308: deliberately retires 33 authored declarations and 36 expanded cases, including the whole backend startup-focus, active-browser IPC-close-routing, remote-browser-creation and agent-terminal-presence suites. Intentionally lost alarms cover distinct six-pane reconnect handles; SSH host label/Connect callback, unhydrated visit cleanup, repo cache aliases and hidden worktree/tab/PTY cleanup; adopted-agent startup focus and viewer navigation/reuse; staged, pageless, source, stale and orphan browser-close routing; web local-materialization refusal, desktop incapable-host fallback, failed/thrown remote creation and paired-web sign-in refusal; BOM/NUL and remote/local custom-editor byte-read examples; immediate folder activation and unread clearing; and batching idle/coalescing, accumulated byte ceiling, leading-edge-disabled, standalone synchronous oversize rejection, validation yield, deferred pending-tail order and both viewport-clear examples. The newly reintroduced agent-terminal-presence suite also loses actual terminal-status membership positive and nonterminal-status callback suppression alarms, including the recent 40916 guard regression; the older different 2133 presence-suite history remains historical and receives zero duplicate removal credit. These real regression alarms are intentionally lost. The unchanged survivors provide narrower coverage, with no equivalent replacement or fresh gate, provider, rendered, remote/mobile, mixed-version, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget validation claimed.",
        "Audit 3318 composes adopted sources 3310, 3313 and 3317: intentionally retires 71 authored declarations and 102 expanded cases, including whole terminal-detach agent-retention, seeded batch/single open-files equivalence, shallow context-menu shortcut-badge, mocked active-workspace delete-dispatch, workspace session hydration, SSH target cleanup, editor session hydration and worktree terminal purge suites. Lost alarms include chained transfer alias and immediate close/exit retention; batch/single divergence, survivor/selection/map preservation and input nonmutation across 400 imperative seeds (one registered case); disconnected pending-handle retry, authoritative absences/close-record shortcut/older-host absence and published-presence/unpublished-frame examples; published empty host-graph omission to pane exit; legacy search ranking/exclusion fallback; provider request upgrade/dedupe/finalizer ownership; asynchronous PR suppression/primary-change and same-number different-repository URL rejection. Deletion routing loses host/instance qualification, paired and legacy mapping, folder ownership, active-versus-hover/menu-row selection, ambiguity, modal/editable/creation/view/main/deleting/missing guards and shortcut advertisement. Unchanged real keyboard/hover/confirmation/catalog E2E remains narrower, not an equivalent replacement. Additional losses include scripted old-host disk/UTF-8/noop/baseline and landed/unlanded lost-reply/replacement-retry outcomes; ordinary/repeated healthy-link reattach; cross-owner terminal/chat binding; oversized replay permanent-unavailable classification; floating reveal keyboard ownership/close/disable/listener disposal; naming/retained-turn/Sleep/error/close/reject status tables; SSH membership prune/new-target-only reads and environment/local bucket isolation; same-frame receipt capacity and positive bare/headless publisher readmission. These actual regression alarms are deliberately lost; no fresh gate, provider, rendered, mob