        "Audit3381 composes root-adopted3376/independent3377 and3379/independent3380: intentionally retires436 authored registrations/670 expanded cases, including79 whole suites and12877 test lines, without equivalent replacement. Lost alarms include scheduling, account/host/status/filter/format inventories, microphone/image cleanup, title/bell/capability lifecycle routing, access/impersonation/outcome matrices, paste/input resend/ledger/retention, stale completions/reload containment, trust-read failure and popup OAuth/security/geometry vectors. Retained30 registrations/34expanded cases in22 suites preserve narrower SQLite TEMP/TZ/WAL, HTTP transcript root resume, mobile original-index Choose/Submit, child environment/Git lock expiry, stale ACK/PTY lifetime/peer fairness/durable replay/output ordering, actual DOM paste/editor focus, DEC2026 conservation, filesystem rollback, owned buffer lifetime, actual OSC parser/tracker handback, POSIX Python UTF8/fallback, durable trust concurrency/version, OpenSSH verdicts and hidden Chromium POST/route lifecycle. Mocked boundaries limit claims. Current bounded defining-owner reads preserve the retained oracles; captured identities are not full transitive semantic review. Both component blind pins authenticated before exchange; final reconciliation and explicit postpin3380reason correction supplement control, without retroactive blind claims. Root unit command excludes mobile and separately admitted Electron probes; use existing respective runners. No fresh execution, native focus/device/pixel UI, live SSH/remote, equivalent replacement or broad mixed-version/cross-platform validation is claimed. Prior dated receipts retain exact original scopes.",
        "Audit3390 composes root-adopted3382/independent3383 and3386/independent3387 and3388/independent3389: intentionally retires216 authored registrations/230 expanded cases in42 whole authored suites plus5 zero-case registration drivers, without equivalent replacement. Lost local alarms include fake PTY identity/routing/startup/replay/mode/title/mouse/IME/scroll matrices, broad startup identity and file-open wiring, mock mailbox title recovery, mobile row parity and whole-v-selective save parity. Retained24 registrations/26 expanded cases in22 suites preserve actual xterm Windows buffer/wrap/scroll, typed TOML scalar, real Promise cancellation/settlement, HTTP Codex scanner/projector semantics, durable recovery admission/newer-schema bytes, federation completion/ACK/SQLite atomicity and failed stale-run-write versus imported durable history. Additional retained clock-domain scheduling, durable freeze/ACK/checkpoint ordering, ABA dirty intent, SQL atomicity, folder-domain retier/last-note deletion, scrollback durable no-sync staging, PanelBridge subscriber lifetime and reserved-send publication preserve narrower concrete behaviors. Current finite owner drift assessed in bounded defining bodies; retained callback bytes unchanged. Historical notes and complete dated receipts keep their original exact scopes. No new execution, equivalent replacement, native focus/device/pixel, live remote or global mixed-version guarantee is claimed.\nOriginal active selector fields (historical raw native JSON values; not current coverage):\ncommands: [\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/wsl-guest/protocol-backpressure.test.ts --reporter=dot\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/wsl-guest/dispatcher.test.ts --reporter=dot\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/ssh/protocol/ssh-multiplexer-transport-writer.test.ts src/main/ssh/protocol/ssh-channel-multiplexer.test.ts src/wsl-guest/dispatcher-client-writer.test.ts --reporter=dot\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/ssh/protocol/ssh-multiplexer-transport-writer.test.ts src/main/ssh/protocol/ssh-channel-multiplexer.test.ts src/main/ssh/protocol/ssh-channel-multiplexer-backpressure.test.ts src/wsl-guest/dispatcher-client-writer.test.ts --reporter=dot\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/ssh/protocol/ssh-multiplexer-transport-writer.test.ts src/main/ssh/protocol/ssh-channel-multiplexer-backpressure.test.ts --reporter=dot\",\n        \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/agent-hooks/wsl-relay/wsl-hook-relay-sentinel.test.ts --reporter=dot\"\n      ]\ntestFiles: [\n        \"src/main/runtime/construction/orca-runtime.test.ts\",\n        \"src/wsl-guest/protocol-backpressure.test.ts\",\n        \"src/wsl-guest/dispatcher.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/ssh/protocol/ssh-multiplexer-transport-writer.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/ssh/protocol/ssh-channel-multiplexer.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/ssh/protocol/ssh-channel-multiplexer-backpressure.test.ts\",\n        \"src/wsl-guest/dispatcher-client-writer.test.ts\",\n        \"src/main/agent-hooks/wsl-relay/wsl-hook-relay-sentinel.test.ts\"\n      ]\nassertionRefs: [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/wsl-guest/dispatcher.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"a saturated legacy primary remains required backpressure and is never detached as an additional subscriber\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/wsl-guest/protocol-backpressure.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"relay decoder accepts one maximum frame plus 1 MiB partial input and rejects one extra byte\",\n            \"a throwing continuation clears retained input, releases one pause epoch, and publishes one typed ownership error\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/ssh/protocol/ssh-multiplexer-transport-writer.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"write(false) owns one frame and later ordinary traffic waits for drain\",\n            \"queued control is selected before ordinary PTY backlog at drain while each lane remains FIFO\",\n            \"four-control fairness guarantees ordinary progress without starving control\",\n            \"one coalesced liveness bypass is allowed per saturated epoch\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/ssh/protocol/ssh-channel-multiplexer-backpressure.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"source ACK, cancellation, exit, request, and response control frames precede queued pasted PTY input after drain\",\n            \"control and ordinary frames preserve lane FIFO while ordinary input progresses after four control writes\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/wsl-guest/dispatcher-client-writer.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"encoded producer frames stay below high-water-minus-reserve capacity\",\n            \"one fixed-size filesystem compatibility frame is admitted only on an empty sink\",\n            \"control remains reserved while producer retention stays bounded\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/main/agent-hooks/wsl-relay/wsl-hook-relay-sentinel.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"WSL stdin forwards write(false), callback settlement, and drain without claiming a live WSL topology\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]",
        "Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The retained runtime registration driver loses three complete imported fragments: changed-working-label title facts and suppressed-frame tracked snapshots; refusing SSH GitLab MR-base lookup before local Git/glab calls; and missing folder-workspace path creation/update refusal before spawn/store mutation. These alarms are intentionally lost. Other imported fragments and separately rooted dated receipts are unchanged; they are not equivalent replacement coverage. The broad root-unit command loses the UNIT_INCLUDE src/ subset of retired examples; mobile is outside UNIT_INCLUDE. Other lost alarms are recorded by the adopted per-case source reviews.  Original scope text is retained as the exact suffix of coverageNotes/oracle; historical evidence is unchanged.",
        "Audit3413 composes root-adopted3405/independent3406 and3409/independent3410: intentionally removes337 authored registrations/363potential expanded cases from13sources, retaining31authored/32potential cases and deleting one whole clipboard suite, without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Broad root-unit discovery loses35WSL examples,22STT examples,22shared-server-banner examples,18clipboard-handler examples (whole suite deleted),14VM lifecycle examples and16commit-message cancellation examples. Retain4WSL and7STT mocked connector/worker cases,1rendered stale-banner refusal,2VM guard/failed-compensation cases and1late-stream ownership cancellation case; real WSL/microphone/remote-provider proof is not established. Separately discovered e2e-unit drivers lose13cross-version-wire local cases and15mobile active-publication cases, keeping same-process disk-reopen/new-host cursor content/epoch/sequence outcomes and a host/renderer-snapshot selection and inventory revision race respectively. Imported released stop-note scenarios remain unchanged and receive no duplicate credit. Cloud suites are outside root UNIT_INCLUDE.  All previous note strings, dated receipts, archived raw receipts and prior gap entries retain their original scopes.",
        "Audit3417 composes root-adopted3415v2/independent3416v2: intentionally removes117authored/173potential expanded registrations from12semantic sources, deleting4whole conventional suites and3registration modules and retaining4authored/5expanded cases, without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Broad root-unit discovery loses naming/title/queued-host fixtures, main-window focus-shortcut and attach-services mock orchestration, Git Bash console-capacity fake process inventories, most real-Git preparation/locking variants and Claude/Codex catch-up examples. Keep lifetime rejected-writer followed by late termination proof and autonomous real-checkout cleanup; two-row real-Git rollback after a real move preserving a replacement/admin marker or revoked permission; a live translator write during a held transcript read fencing stale Claude history append; and Codex expected-item revision rejection before a historical writer shim. Codex driver registers retained bounds exactly once with original inputs; bounds does not prove modern writer persistence. Accepted changed-lock preflight sentinel and omitted-parent routing losses are not replaced.  All earlier notes and dated/archived evidence retain original scopes.",
        "Audit3425 composes root-adopted3420/independent3421: intentionally removes83 authored/112 potential expanded registrations across13 semantic sources, deleting7 whole conventional suites and1 registering helper;7 authored/10 potential expanded cases remain. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Broad unit discovery loses the adopted mock orchestration, refusal, restart and storage examples. Retain unchanged two-phase real-WSL deployment/survival, the reduced idle-release holder proof without restart/first-output measurement, real worker stop/release cleanup barrier rows, physical Git branch-preservation rows, and SSH disconnected-close proof. Other SSH and CLI variants and WSL telemetry/warmup churn are intentionally removed.  Earlier notes and dated/archived evidence retain original scopes.",
        "Audit3429 composes root-adopted3426/independent3427: intentionally removes168 authored/205 potential expanded cases across16 semantic sources, deleting11 whole suites and one304line unused assertion helper. Five authored/five potential cases remain; the duplicate500k graph row is dropped while its50k row and callback remain. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Broad unit discovery loses the adopted migration/recovery/federation/rich-draft/paste/automation/mobile/catalog examples. Keep server-edit preservation during migration, native supervised cancellation holding the agent home until physical stop, pagehide lost-text preservation, graph old-result WRAPPER WeakRef collection with50k rows, and mobile React render isolation. The WeakRef does not prove all commit objects are collectible or a memory budget.  All prior notes and dated/archived evidence retain original scopes.",
        "Audit3437 composes ROOT-adopted3431/independent3432: intentionally removes127 authored/174 potential expanded cases across12 sources, deleting7 whole suites and one267line unused helper without test credit. Retain8 authored/13 potential cases. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Broad unit discovery loses reduced or deleted relay, coordinator mail, recovery watchdog, automation observer, launch picker, folder PTY, profile restart, web migration, retirement, pointer delivery, agent-row and run-bound mailbox examples. Retained checks cover relay hello/payload and SIGTERM drain, coordinator pending-check and clear-to-Run continuity, profile persistence, the full six-row web merge table and real run-bound delivery waiter. These do not replace removed alarms.  All prior notes and dated/archived evidence retain original scopes.",
        "Audit3446 composes ROOT-adopted3441/independent3442: intentionally removes100 authored registrations/119 potential expanded cases (118 conditional-active before platform gates) across16 sources, retaining11 authored/13 expanded cases and deleting6 whole suites. Two parent registrar import/call cleanups and the unused68line CLI recording fixture carry zero test credit. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Broad unit and mobile discovery loses interrupt/wake registrars, task storage/session-close/account snapshot hooks, permission tables, copy/preference/model-discovery/composer examples, launch placement examples, VM projections and extra mobile-history scenarios. Retained checks cover abandoned versus dispatched fork uncertainty; /fast dispatch supersession; discovery lock release after exit; stale-send draft preservation; OSC status lifetime; future-version file preservation; launch cancellation before/during dispatch on both layout owners; mobile resume addressability before hooks; and recipe snapshot cleanup after plugin removal. The paired browser-link Electron source is unchanged. Terminal launch seams, mobile roles-only history and injected provider results do not establish native terminal destruction, transcript text fidelity or real remote provider cleanup.  All prior notes and complete dated receipts retain their original scopes.",
        "Audit3451 composes ROOT-adopted3444/independent3445: intentionally removes101 authored registrations across16 reviewed sources, deleting7 whole suites and reducing8; one reviewed source is unchanged. Fresh main has123 authored registrations before and22 after because an upstream direct-child shell regression remains verbatim with zero removal credit. Registered removals are100+7*S and explicit-active removals99+7*S, where S is the unprobed count0..3 of admitted bash/zsh/fish shells. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Broad unit discovery loses extra stream lifecycle/forwarding examples, unreadable-store/cache projections, orchestration presentation/benchmark cases, remote-owned routing matrices, mobile legacy navigation and model-catalog listing/cache examples. Whole suites retire renderer client-event projections, manually assembled structured-session reader ownership, mobile prompt presentation, renderer AI-vault resume commands, mobile Jira URL lookup, composer retention and mobile folder source-repository queries. Retained checks preserve original stream/store/orchestration/routing/navigation/catalog cases and shell behavior, including the upstream direct-child case. No real provider, native desktop or mobile acceptance is established by this reduction. All prior notes, assertion references and complete dated receipts retain their original historical scopes.",
        "Audit3456 composes ROOT-adopted3449/independent3450: intentionally removes62 authored/82 potential expanded cases from16 selected drivers, including7 whole suites, while13 authored/13 potential cases remain. Delete the unused48line legacy workspace-session JSON fixture with zero test credit. These are source-only reductions without equivalent replacement or fresh runtime claims. Broad unit discovery intentionally loses whole trust-dialog observer, background-turn notifications, redirected session refusal, typed-agent identity, chat-tab lifetime-cost, model-manager and mobile diff-review controller suites, plus individual persistence, synthetic composition, pairing, manifest and subprocess samples. Retain deferred snapshot dirty-domain persistence, two direct editor ownership cases, stream counter-domain distinction, two persisted pairing identity cases, parser entrypoint asymmetry, dictation retry and process-group timeout; paired restart and packaged old-binary/corrupt-profile journeys remain in their E2E driver scope. Retained checks do not replace removed alarms. No fresh execution, native IME/microphone, real authentication, mixed-version/platform or performance result is claimed. All prior notes and archived receipts retain original scopes.",
        "Audit3460 final-v2 composes accepted AUTHOR3454/PEER3455 on actual post263 main: intentionally removes99 authored/106 potential expanded cases across16 selected drivers, including7 whole suites, retaining24 authored/26 potential cases. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime is claimed. Broad root-unit discovery loses whole cross-client workspace-sync, terminal-preview, picker-skill-hint and close-routing suites plus reduced worker-stop, remote-owned-record, scanner, mobile-bundle and daemon-health samples. Separate E2E discovery also loses the paired mobile/desktop mirror journey and two unit drivers. Retained callback/table/outer-loop/guard bytes are exact; retained checks do not replace the removed alarms. No app, native device, mixed-version, remote or cross-platform execution result is claimed. Earlier notes, complete dated receipts and archived gaps retain their original scopes.",
        "Audit3468 accepted source proposal AUTHOR3462/PEER3463, composed privately by audit3469: removes62 authored registrations/95 finite potential expansions, including5 whole suites, retaining25 authored registrations/29 finite potential expansions. ROOT approved source value; no equivalent replacement, fresh runtime or merge credit is claimed. Broad root-unit discovery loses the profile-state worker smoke, worker-agent views and three search discovery suites, plus samples from node-server qualification, skill-bundle generation, CLI hooks/profile/recovery/offline admission, permission-hook holds and search indexing. The separate Cloud relay runner loses one relay blackbox sample; unchanged mobile native-chat and dependent-transcript drivers remain. Retained source callback/table/ancestor/fixture bytes bind to the sealed candidate. No physical-device, mixed-version, remote, cross-platform or app execution result is claimed. Earlier notes, complete dated receipts and archived gaps retain their original scopes.",
        "Audit3438 composes ROOT-adopted3434/independent3436: intentionally removes60 authored/62 potential expanded cases across16 sources, deleting9 whole suites. Eight authored/eight potential cases remain; delete the102line unused ACP fixture and57line unused teardown helper with zero test credit. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Broad unit discovery loses ACP model-catalog fixtures, resume-record projections, dashboard mock payload/state cases, mobile folder/launch/session examples and dictionary pipeline rows. Selected E2E removals also retire auto-conversion and golden-core journeys and one Windows CLI conversion registration. Retain ACP reply text across a resumed subagent, both VAD checks, focused tab send ownership, async focus ownership in happy-dom, the question-skip journey, the original managed Windows CLI lifecycle journey and dictionary substitution. These checks do not replace the removed alarms.  All prior notes and dated/archived evidence retain original scopes.",
        "Audit3470 composes ROOT-approved AUTHOR3466/PEER3467 source proposal: intentionally removes38 authored registrations/59 finite potential expansions, including8 whole registering suites, retaining13 authored registrations/18 finite potential expansions. The sole dead shell-recipe caller cleanup has zero additional test credit. No equivalent replacement, fresh runtime or merge credit is claimed. Broad root-unit discovery loses process-import boundary, Korean/Japanese locale policy, worker-reset, mobile agent-history/queued-message and median-summary suites, plus packaged mobile-manifest, worker-pool fixture, HTML preview, mobile shell and terminal samples. The environment-provider contract and its sole shell-recipe caller are deleted. Separate cross-version-wire discovery loses the large byte-budget fresh-snapshot/replay sample while retaining independent live same-revision note publication; the retained terminal stale-refresh and dirty HTML draft persistence checks do not replace removed alarms. The source4 unused start/stop fixture hooks are removed; its retained nested failed-import test remains byte-exact with its own lifecycle. Unchanged SVG preview and Git-resolution registrations stay intact. Root balanced CI excludes the cross-version directory, which has a separate job; unbalanced root discovery can include its parent. No native app/device, actual remote, released-pair interoperability or cross-platform execution result is claimed. Earlier notes, complete dated receipts and archived gaps retain their original scopes.",
        "Audit3492 composes ROOT-approved75(AUTHOR3475/PEER3476 and AUTHOR3485/PEER3481, including five-field clarification and zero-credit selector3483) plus123(AUTHOR3486/PEER3487 reconciled FINAL3491, including peer case10:3 and9:0 wording clarifications). It intentionally removes198 authored registrations/232 finite literal-table potential registrations across70 changed JS/TS test sources, including45 whole suites;87 authored/90 finite potential registrations remain across95 reviewed JS/TS bodies. One mobile native-suspension manual recipe and the now-unreferenced GitLab mock fixture helper are separately removed with zero registration credit. Static literal table potential is not execution. No equivalent replacement, fresh runtime result or merge credit is claimed. Earlier135 complete dated receipts, all raw gaps and full prior98/161/history notes retain their exact scopes and bytes. The additional123 retirement accepts loss of mocked GitLab request/error/identity/classification inventories; basic Linear migration and metadata discovery; simulated OpenCode key failed-save retention/retry/log redaction; analytics identity-flush smoke that did not prove ordering; AppImage static entry guards and empty-staging cleanup; GPU/process/minidump breadcrumb/annotation shapes and weak redaction oracles; namespace/status/foreign-launcher ownership guards and persistence roundtrips; profile transfer field projections; worker hook/screen/incarnation/result admission/classification guards; and source-coupled CLI transaction fixtures. Privileged publication failure injection was a false-positive: its mkdir regex missed -m 700 and outer rejection accepted an inner assertion before any shell ran. The identity-flush case awaited identity after flush and could pass despite early flush. Retained actual negative-token cache recovery, SQL filter-before-LIMIT open approval, unreadable-root FTS preservation/degradation, latest-connect-wins persistence, worker stop-debt settlement, unmodified same-inode foreign-content transaction, explicit incomplete-pagination error, FTS own-message snippet association, filter-before-route result and bounded-search truncation honesty are distinct bounded outcomes, not replacements for retired alarms. Case9:0 checks both roots before chmod but only mounted-session/degraded-root after chmod. Entire extraction-root suite is removed; no retained extraction cleanup is claimed. Removing the manual iOS foreground-stall shell script loses its unique real native-suspension recipe; timer tests do not replace it. First-match PIDs, indefinite waiting, broad success matching and absent trap cleanup made that diagnostic brittle and able to leave a desktop stopped. The current Windows operational driver remains byte-exact, preserving already-merged removal of orcad-convert and orcad-cli-convert selectors and the retained cmd/powershell/managed CLI lanes. The package skill-sharing release selector loses only the exact already-retired skills-suite token; no extra test credit. Included approved75 retirement account follows (historical proposal labels identify provenance; final198 counts above control): Audit3488 composes ROOT-approved source49(AUTHOR3485/PEER3481, including its immutable five-field clarification) and source26(AUTHOR3475/PEER3476): intentionally removes75 authored registrations/87 finite potential registrations across35 changed sources, including25 whole suites;35 authored/36 finite potential registrations remain in the combined reviewed scopes. Literal table potential counts are not executions. This source-only reduction has no equivalent replacement, fresh runtime result or merge credit. Root unit discovery deliberately loses entire message-row filtering/chunk reconstruction, discussion-pagination rejection passthrough, Linear bearer/stack redaction, new-profile telemetry/default/existing-JSON no-op, WSL user-trigger routing, terminal-delivery refusal, native-chat worker-approval UI, followup-paste routing, live-surface tombstone refusal, activity-bar hydration, fabricated approval-caller policy, child-PATH transformation and branch-review URL/identity suites. It also loses cache roundtrip/mode/fingerprint/fallback/no-op samples; GPU field-shape privacy examples; older auth-probe failure retention; orphan SQLite-sidecar/future-schema admission; usage tie/duplicate/composite-key examples; allocation-name sanitizer/unknown-prefix examples; real worker-and-backup preflight wrapper smoke; and JSONL descriptor-loop truncation. The discussion page contained id-only discussions without notes, so its rejection did not prove a nonempty notes-prefix oracle. The preflight did launch actual worker/backup entrypoints with production internal self-validation; removing its revision/version wrapper deliberately retires that real-entry smoke alarm. The skipped-prefix JSONL keeper rewrites/grows after collecting the suffix and before final validation, not concurrently during parsing. Retained queue rejection/recovery and held/drain mechanisms, recorder nonsettling-provider deadline, corrupt authoritative-DB refusal, legacy cache split migration, merge-added-row indexing, external-frame redaction, and pinned JSONL read/verification/mutation checks are bounded concrete oracles, not equivalent replacements for retired alarms. The full cloud relay cohort/ceiling/control suite is separately removed from the relay package runner, outside root unit discovery; no cloud runtime result is claimed. The Python computer-use benchmark remains unchanged tooling with zero authored/removal credit; no native benchmark trial ran. The package skill-sharing release selector drops only the exact already-deleted skills-suite token, with zero additional removal credit. Prior dated receipts, raw gaps, and complete earlier161/98/history notes remain exactly at their original scopes; no changed-source historical receipt becomes fresh reduced-suite evidence. Included approved26 alarm account: Broad root-unit discovery loses entire ref-label string, hostile/malformed CSV-link rendering, Codex filename-discovery, mocked paged-preview postscan mutation, usage path-containment, real symlink-ancestor, Codex skip RPC, local/remote inference routing, width-preference, and synthetic workspace-document input suites. It also loses the hand-assembled sorted CSV edit example, connect-time JPEG seed and invalid AVCC guard samples, and eight-record/64KiB detector boundary cases. The symlink suite exercised actual kernel traversal; its lost ancestor alarm could omit supplemental local editor watches and leave content stale, not bypass authorization. Retained linked stream cancellation, preview-only save fence, failed-flush dirty-draft preservation, clipboard byte/edit preservation, fragmented AVCC parsing and independent quoted-CSV interpretation checks do not replace these deliberately retired alarms. The stream fixture uses an in-memory source and does not establish actual fd cleanup; editor save endpoints are synthetic, browser events are synthetic, and no native focus, actual remote delivery, real disk write, cross-platform execution or interoperability is claimed. Earlier complete dated receipts, raw known gaps and previous notes are historical evidence at their original source/selector scope, not fresh evidence for this reduced suite.   Earlier notes, complete dated receipts and archived gaps retain their original scopes.",
        "Audit3597 scope: remove two renderer-hang-capture examples (2 authored/2 finite): an invalid repeated-token oversized reducer fixture and a shorter unanswered-request fixture. Intentionally lose the direct truncated flag/sanitized frame fixture and request-pending status/zero-sample alarms. Retain window-death/stale-result exclusion, generation reconciliation, and baseline-publication cancellation lifecycles; they are not equivalent bound, redaction or pending-status replacements. Historical execution retains its original source scope; no new runtime evidence is claimed.",
        "Audit3601 scope: remove the whole custom-sound happy-path IPC suite and one custom-label/multiline notification formatting example (2 authored/2 finite). Intentionally lose configured .ogg selection, exact byte/MIME success wiring, successful dispatch for the formatting fixture, custom-label whitespace/title normalization and assistant-body whitespace/180-character-cap alarms. Retain prompt-exclusion, persisted qualified dismissal/restart, theme ownership/restore and Ghostty precedence/collision cases; none replaces the retired sound/formatting alarms. No actual playback, native delivery, phone/network, cross-platform or new runtime evidence is claimed; historical execution keeps its original scope.",
        "Audit3606 adopts the enhanced3604/3605 icon cuts: nine authored/nine finite cases removed, including the whole tray-attention-icon suite. Retires the no-encoder oversized-upload null sample, missing-ID/request-order sample, encoder-null PNG-prefix fallback, SVG/404 rejection samples, transparent amber-dot placement and half-alpha white-tint sample, exact small fetched-byte passthrough, host-qualified image-key inventory and constant-encoder large-upload projection. These specific admission, formatting and bitmap alarms are intentionally lost without equivalent replacements. Retained queue/cache, bounded fetch and Dock lifecycle checks do not establish actual raster decoding, native image conversion or rendered appearance. Historical receipts below are preserved evidence for earlier test sets, not fresh validation of this reduced selection.",
        "Audit3608: remove five authored/five finite callbacks, including whole owner-slug and remote favicon URL suites and two repository-label projections. Lose five owner acceptance samples, eleven negative owner samples plus nonstring refusal, six host-local icon refusal samples, legacy-SSH same-path label-map cardinality, and explicit runtime ownership over stale legacy metadata at label level. These are accepted narrow grammar/presentation alarms with no equivalent replacement claimed. Retained binary parser, React recovery and label grouping/platform cases do not replace these losses. Static evidence only; historical receipts retain their original scope.",
        "Audit3613: remove six authored/six finite callbacks, including whole reviewer-display oversize-input and explorer-root record-filter suites, plus plugin family-emoji/invisible-only-name and pool legacy-name/urgent-countdown samples. Accept losing oversized-input empty-result/no-split, malformed-record/prototype-sensitive-key/nonstring filtering, exact ZWJ family preservation, invisible-only name refusal, no-group old-host full-name preservation, and80/79/null-reset countdown composition alarms. No equivalent replacement asserted. Retained strict/runtime sanitization, SVG parser, mobile focus recovery and collision/tie cases have different scopes. Static evidence only; historical receipts retain original scope.",
        "Audit3628: remove the entire one-authored/one-finite RepositoryRemoveProjectSection happy-dom suite. Accept losing the local zero-to-one-terminal stale-count revalidation alarm: first confirmation defers the removal callback and second confirmation invokes it after the count snapshot updates. The test never asserts updated warning text/count, actual terminal creation or removal/PTY teardown, host/scope routing, cancellation or folder/mobile behavior. No equivalent replacement or end-to-end warning-before-teardown proof asserted. Static evidence only; historical receipts retain original scope.",
        "Audit3629 removes two singleton parser suites: WSL Claude plugin metadata out-of-range index rejection and Git checkout unlink-warning path extraction. Their real range-refusal and quoted-path extraction alarms are intentionally lost without replacement; no WSL execution, checkout recovery or equivalent remaining coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit3832 deliberately retires76 authored/79 finite cases:75 runtime compatibility cases/78 finite cases across14 fragments, plus one localization extractor default-flag case. Three whole runtime fragments are deleted;27 authored/30 finite cases remain across the reviewed sources. This gate retains only its own selected scope; no equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/native/remote evidence is claimed. Runtime component A: Audit3828 composes3822 with independent3824: deliberately retires49 authored/52 finite cases from seven compatibility fragments, leaving15 authored/18 finite cases and deleting two entire fragments. Accepted losses: positive folder-worker recovery/materialization and reveal deadline; persisted-key normalization and legacy split/group/focus projection; fixed stale CAS refusal; occupied/alias/restored/preallocated terminal-handle variants; fixed OpenCode/Cursor/Claude/Codex/Antigravity classification, readiness, title and management examples; direct private-map browser authority projections; browser-focus and OMP title projection; already-aborted claim cleanup. Additional3824 loss: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-02.spec.ts :: does not poll a wrapper foreground for a speculative CLI prompt send :: Speculative retryForegroundWrappers:false check must return false on a wrapper after one foreground read, without polling the supplied later codex response. These real bounded alarms are deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained callbacks are unchanged and provide only their own bounded scope, not equivalent replacement. Historical receipts do not validate reduced callbacks. No fresh runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser evidence or full transitive closure is claimed. Runtime component B: Audit3834 deliberately retires26 authored/26 finite cases from seven fresh compatibility fragments, leaving10/10 and deleting the one-case saved-binding reattachment fragment. Original position58 is excluded: