      "coverageNotes": "Audit3554 intentionally removes the whole worktrees-ssh-repo-owner-resolution suite (2 authored cases). Dedicated duplicate-exact/ambiguous-legacy owner refusal and fixed runtime-host/wrong-target/missing-authority/zero-owner/contradictory-owner status alarms are lost. The suite did not exercise an authority transition or actual SSH listing; its no-local-Git spy was also unreachable on an admitted SSH metadata-only route. Remaining suites are not equivalent replacements. Current selectors have no fresh execution from this static packet; historical receipts retain their original scope. No new SSH/provider/native/UI/mobile/mixed-version/cross-platform result is claimed. Audit3390 composes root-adopted3382/independent3383 and3386/independent3387 and3388/independent3389: intentionally retires216 authored registrations/230 expanded cases in42 whole authored suites plus5 zero-case registration drivers, without equivalent replacement. Lost local alarms include fake PTY identity/routing/startup/replay/mode/title/mouse/IME/scroll matrices, broad startup identity and file-open wiring, mock mailbox title recovery, mobile row parity and whole-v-selective save parity. Retained24 registrations/26 expanded cases in22 suites preserve actual xterm Windows buffer/wrap/scroll, typed TOML scalar, real Promise cancellation/settlement, HTTP Codex scanner/projector semantics, durable recovery admission/newer-schema bytes, federation completion/ACK/SQLite atomicity and failed stale-run-write versus imported durable history. Additional retained clock-domain scheduling, durable freeze/ACK/checkpoint ordering, ABA dirty intent, SQL atomicity, folder-domain retier/last-note deletion, scrollback durable no-sync staging, PanelBridge subscriber lifetime and reserved-send publication preserve narrower concrete behaviors. Current finite owner drift assessed in bounded defining bodies; retained callback bytes unchanged. Historical notes and complete dated receipts keep their original exact scopes. No new execution, equivalent replacement, native focus/device/pixel, live remote or global mixed-version guarantee is claimed. Audit3368 narrows stream-reconnect coverage to the actual ten synthetic transport epochs retaining one PTY identity, accepting and holding detached input for exactly-once later delivery, current decoded output and per-epoch subscription release. Prior rejection wording was inaccurate. Phase/backoff/cutoff/manual reconnect and parser/OSC/pause/retained-image/fatal/latch/claim/early-close alarms are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. The Linux multi-pane reconnect receipt remains verbatim with its original scope; no fresh live SSH/provider/PTY/UI/mobile/mixed-version/cross-platform evidence is claimed. Audit3359 retires whole host-surface-replacement and create-handoff suites, removing their compound unit command tokens, test-file entries and assertion references. Fake polling/deadline/subscription, supplied stale-handle ownership, close and replacement examples are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. The unrelated Linux paired multi-pane reconnect receipt stays verbatim with its original scope. No fresh SSH/provider/network/PTY recovery, historical-import, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Audit3342 retires the complete client create-outcome identity/options/recovery suite and the malformed-or-contradictory repo-owner response matrix. Client replay identity, options, no-downgrade, quiescence/budget/manual retry, authoritative probe-error and malformed-owner refusal alarms are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. Remaining repo-owner late catalog and old-host re-adoption boundaries do not replace them. The unrelated Linux paired-reconnect receipt stays verbatim with its original scope. Surviving selectors are unexecuted here; no fresh SSH/provider/process-deduplication, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Audit3329 execution amendment: the reduced one-suite reconnect selector passed on Linux (1 case). Original source-review statements about no fresh execution describe the earlier static review; this new receipt validates only this one local deterministic unit case, not the complete gate or physical/runtime/rendered/provider/platform parity. Historical seven-case macOS and two-case Linux receipts remain archived verbatim. Audit3326 adopts reconciled source audit3324 and intentionally retires these low-value examples and their regression alarms: keeps a sidebar row for every still-live pane after a long sleep — Whole suite: 279 lines manually replay renderer ownership registry/status writes, snapshot patch/set, six-pane fixture inventory, and sidebar selectors/builders; expected pane IDs are production-computed. Does not run sleep/wake/transport or actual sidebar entry. Retires reconnect row-preservation assembly alarm.; still retires the regular TUI surface after an explicit terminal exit — Ordinary explicit-exit callback/map cleanup is repeated in the stale/new stream lifecycle case below. Retires separate regular-TUI baseline; keeper is not equivalent process/UI proof.; asks the HUB to recover an expired SSH pane and rebinds the host identity — Expired SSH owner error must ask the owning HUB to recover, then adopt fixed replacement handle, resubscribe and report rebind; actual transport dispatch and handle state prevent wrong-client recovery.; does not recover a pane whose relay reply was an identity mismatch — Identity mismatch means a different live PTY, so actual transport must surface refusal without recover/create, keeping original identity. Prevents destructive duplicate agent recovery.; fails closed when an older HUB cannot recover an expired SSH pane — Old HUB method_not_found is scripted mock refusal/error echo with no actual skewed host; repeats generic recovery failure propagation. Retires old-host recovery fallback refusal example.; names a held recovery's stopped WSL distro in readable copy, not the raw hold code — Pins exact WSL stopped-distro error prose after mock code; translation/copy assertion with no actual held recovery behavior. Retires readable-copy alarm.. Retained tests do not replace these alarms. Dated unrelated evidence remains scoped to its original execution; no historical source/import-closure equivalence, fresh execution, real network/provider/SSH, rendered UI, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Audit 3318 reduces runtime-environment-ssh-state.test.ts, intentionally losing metadata membership-pruning/new-target-only-read and other-environment/local-bucket isolation alarms. Preserve generation/failed-full-refresh assertion and unknown-target authoritative-list reread; these narrower cases are not equivalent replacements. The unchanged active two-case Linux reconnect materialization/sidebar receipt and covered platform retain their exact scope and do not validate the reduced SSH state selector. Preserve unrelated SSH assertions, selectors and archived history. No fresh SSH discovery, provider/PTY/network, rendered, mobile, mixed-version, cross-platform or full-gate execution is claimed. Audit3315 execution amendment: the reduced two-suite reconnect selector passed on Linux (2 cases). Original source-review statements about no fresh execution describe the earlier static review; this new receipt validates only these two local deterministic unit cases, not the complete gate or physical/runtime/rendered/provider/platform parity. Historical seven-case macOS receipt remains archived verbatim. Audit 3312 retires the ordinary six-pane distinct-live-handle reconnect/resubscription alarm from paired-reconnect-multi-pane-materialization.test.ts. The unchanged parked-pane activation/rematerialization case remains narrower and is not an equivalent replacement. The complete prior seven-contract macOS receipt is archived as historical evidence; it does not validate the reduced selector. No fresh socket, PTY, sleep/wake, provider, platform, mobile, mixed-version or rendered execution is claimed. Audit3096: remove the deleted reconnect-banner selector and its two UI aliases. The reduced recovery-state selector retains only the deadline cancelling pending backoff and explicit retry owning a new epoch alias; healthy-replacement stale-schedule and independent caller-cutoff cancellation aliases retire. Other retained state cases cover reentrant retry, owner settlement and same-epoch parked revival, without replacing those removed alarms. Prior admission-selector retirement, archived July 28 receipt, unrelated selectors/claims/receipts and old gaps remain unchanged; no fresh execution is claimed. Audit3086: retire the destroyed fresh-session fallback settlement/non-destructive reattach alias and its direct selector; retain the detach/attach selector and assertion unchanged. The retained admission cases cover adopt-before-data and explicitly buffered-death admission without a new spawn, without replacing fallback retirement. July 28 evidence was already archived by audit3077; no duplicate retirement or new execution is claimed. Audit2709 removes src/renderer/src/runtime/web-session-tabs-sync/inventory/remote-runtime-session-tabs-inflight.test.ts: intentionally retire waiting out an older inventory and sharing a fresh post-operation request among concurrent callers. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Dated receipts remain historical evidence for their unchanged selectors only; they do not validate the reduced commands or full current gate. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2076 (sources2073/2074): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/ssh/connection/ssh-connection-manager.test.ts: tears a failed startup down quietly, so its error is not replaced by a disconnect; marks a dial that never reached the host, so setup reports SSH’s reason; removes the registration when bulk teardown fails; leaves a connection whose own reconnect is asking the user alone; clears the pool entry when the closed connection is still the registered one; still reuses a connection that is already up; dials a user's connection test. Existing unrelated evidenceRuns retain their original scope; unchanged dated receipt objects do not validate changed source bytes or reduced selectors. No fresh gate execution or historical import-closure equivalence is claimed. Frozen current literal-import graph reaches these changed test bytes; unresolved local and computed edges remain debt, and current reachability is not historical execution or equivalent replacement evidence. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2052 (sources2049/2050/2051): Remove complete low-value restored-pane-title and pane-visibility-identity suites and their current selectors. Their supplied snapshot/title and nullable identity-comparison alarms are intentionally lost without replacement. Unrelated dated evidenceRuns remain unchanged and do not validate the reduced commands. No fresh gate execution, actual PTY/provider, rendered, remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1983: Delete the terminal-create idempotency forwarding suite and its prospective selector. Preserve2 unrelated receipts without claiming the lost forwarding alarm was replaced. Changed-source prior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1931 (sources1928/1929): Delete complete transport-unmount and queued-initial-CWD helper suites: despite lifecycle-shaped fixtures, the unmount owner returns a Boolean PTY-id predicate, while CWD cases check nullish field selection and callback counts. Lose their detach/destroy/teardown and one-shot-CWD supplied examples. Partial queued-pane-startup loses three identical/empty/nonowner identity examples, retaining four exact one-shot/replacement ownership callbacks. No assertion object maps to these three sources, so unrelated alias objects remain byte-exact. Preserve the current81ed prior removal of pane-split-startup; stale bd948 source metadata snapshots are not replayed. No actual process/PTY startup, transport shutdown, live SSH or rendered recovery is proven by this metadata change. Preserve meaningful remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged dated receipts within their original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh gate execution evidence in this metadata packet. No equivalent replacement, physical watcher/PTY/provider, live SSH/remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1925 (sources1922/1923): Delete the sole supplied public-SSH-state spread/sanitized-error projection and its provider-authority-pair alias. Also delete the complete tiny one-shot split-startup wrapper suite: callback-visible temporary field/reset, sequential payload and thrown-sentinel reset alarms disappear. No SSH provider epoch handoff, connection, process startup or actual terminal split was performed by either deleted suite. Preserve meaningful remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged dated receipts within their original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh gate execution evidence in this metadata packet. No equivalent replacement, physical watcher/PTY/provider, live SSH/remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1903 removes whole mocked detach, supplied geometry and/or close-request suites selected by this gate. Their pending-CWD/PTY-binding argument/order, fabricated hit-test and close bookkeeping alarms are intentionally lost without replacement. Valid remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged-selector execution receipts retain their original scope. Reduced unit selections have no fresh broad gate, real PTY/provider, rendered focus, or measured-budget validation. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1645 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1640 removes low-value IPC, SSH, workspace and transcript-watcher tests without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public refusal, cancellation, execution-host and real-filesystem outcomes with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1342 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Audit1301 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Deterministic renderer coverage proves retained native and runtime SSH payloads are admitted through production routes only with valid complete authority, stale cleanup cannot unregister a replacement runtime terminal, direct SSH Git and folder panes keep their PTY bindings through disconnect and reconnect, one authority chain stops after two automatic attempts even when each timeout exceeds the rolling window, rejected acknowledgements mutate no store maps, and one shared exact attempt admits every concurrent split-pane spawn and reattach while preserving the first PTY as the tab fallback. A later sibling failure rotates the tab once, stale callbacks from the prior attempt mutate no state, split remount activity suppression is counted per leaf, primary PTY exit promotes a bound survivor or preserves an empty continuation gap for a late sibling, and primary, non-primary, or null-PTY detach preserves exact authority on both resulting tabs. Intentional pane disposal cancels its settlement timer without breaking StrictMode remount timeout ownership. A mounted remote-runtime terminal survives repeated transport partitions without changing PTY identity. A real encrypted-WebSocket oracle proves a successful reachability probe can replace a pre-ready shared-control socket without rejecting or duplicating the waiting RPC. Direct SSH coordinator tests cover immediate terminal finalization, hydration correction, damping, bounded retry, and telemetry non-interference. Client/server heartbeat tests cover timer suspension, socket generations fence stale callbacks, cold restored-terminal attachment retries, cached pixels remain unhealthy until authoritative replay, automatic retries stop after one minute, manual reconnect preserves the PTY, and pane closure releases recovery UI state. Current-transport recovery clears every error that transport surfaced without clearing or displaying a sibling pane's errors, while transport suppression, pane retention, and the rendered surface are independently bounded. Current macOS Electron journeys against an ephemeral Linux Docker SSH target cover exact-authority repo/worktree hydration, live terminal recovery after disconnect/reconnect, and eager six-terminal remount after renderer reload. A Windows remote-runtime smoke covers reachability and PTY round-trip. Multi-target live fanout, paired-close, WSL, and patched live partition journeys remain gaps. The test-value audit narrowed resolved-worktree-execution-host.test.ts to cache reuse and invalidation. Its direct hydrated-worktree, missing-folder, restored-owner, host-stamp and empty-runtime selection alarms are lost. Other routing and recovery suites do not establish equivalent selector coverage; historical run commands and results remain historical. The test-value audit removes standalone unwritten/released renderer-authority and cross-scope request-count examples. The retained synthetic mirror/store/sidebar and pending-inventory checks do not establish real PTY byte ownership, SSH reconnection or equivalent replacement coverage; historical commands and results remain historical. The test-value audit removes direct join/label ledgers, immediate failure and negative-only stale/removal/partial-authority examples, plus the standalone retained/live event projection. Retained synthetic store/hydration compositions do not establish real SSH continuity, remote authority delivery or equivalent replacement alarms. Historical commands and results remain historical. The renderer scheduling fixture retains in-flight coalescing only. Its immediate publication and negative stale-SSH-cleanup call ledgers were removed; the retained SSH recovery evidence does not replace those alarms. The accepted-handle-events observer suite is removed, including its scoped listener and settlement-release assertions. These observer alarms are lost; retained SSH/transport journeys are not equivalent replacement coverage. The test-value audit removed repeated remote-handle rotation inventories and snapshot-first pending-restart migration examples from terminal-pty-identity-replacement.test.ts, plus direct foreground metadata setter, confirmation, evidence-enum, and prefix/worktree cleanup examples. Those rotation, pending-restart, snapshot-first migration, and foreground scalar-update alarms are lost. The retained replacement case observes pane and tab identities in one subscriber publication; it does not establish equivalent migration, process-evidence, or input-routing coverage. Historical commands and results remain historical. The test-value audit narrows terminals-hydration.test.ts to a real reconnect batch with one measured store publication and hydration-seeded history consumed by a subsequent visit/Back check. Direct split-layout, runtime/folder/floating restoration, dead-leaf focus, cold/known-absent SSH deferral, title, default-tab marker, navigation initialization, and hydrationSucceeded scalar examples are removed; those specific alarms are lost. No actual target-removal transition, live SSH connection, session writer, or persisted restart is exercised by the retained cases. The old target-scoped/snapshot assertion references are retired because the current file does not contain those oracles. Other suites and historical runs do not establish equivalent replacement coverage. Audit1299 removes tests/e2e/terminal-cold-activation-deferral.spec.ts. Private-state/work-budget/assembled-fixture alarms are intentionally lost; retained suites are not equivalent replacement coverage. No new runtime/platform evidence is claimed. Audit1301: src/renderer/src/runtime/remote-runtime-session-tabs-inflight.test.ts reduced. Direct dedupe eviction/count and equal receipt-position sample loses authored alarm. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1318: src/shared/remote-runtime/control/remote-runtime-shared-control-connection.test.ts: Retain real local encrypted WebSocket regressions for pre-ready socket replacement preserving a request, close-before-ready logical subscription cleanup, unrelated RPC surviving another deadline, and pending setup abort leaving a sibling pending. Host server is synthetic and uses production crypto; kept scenarios also retain internal diagnostics/memory assertions unchanged. Remove happy routing, authority-envelope, unknown-ID/log, cleanup enum, binary, keepalive/liveness and production-budget/private socket inventories; intentionally lose those alarms, no physical host authorization, independent crypto or remote provider claim. Reduced selectors need fresh validation; historical full-suite receipts do not validate the changed coverage. No equivalent replacement or physical-provider claim. Audit1342: src/renderer/src/hooks/ipc-events/direct-ssh-connect-reply-routing.test.ts removed. Initial and event-triggered partial-authority hydration fixture alarms disappear. src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-error-accumulation.test.ts removed. Multiline dedup/storm bounds, resource classification/collision, scoped clear/reconnect strip and1000-pane map count alarms disappear. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1396: src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-pending-spawn.spec.ts reduced. Lose standalone debug-state retention/log silence alarm. React StrictMode is not mounted; bindings manually simulate remount over mocked transport. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. The existing primary-selector receipt and its claims remain scoped to their unchanged sources; the broad optional command has no new execution result. Audit1400: src/main/ipc/ssh/ssh.test.ts reduced. Lose trivial missing target and mocked publication inventory. Preexisting unresolved ../ssh/ssh-port-scanner mock is recorded, not fixed. src/renderer/src/runtime/sync-runtime-graph-scheduling.test.ts removed. Removes whole coalescing call-count suite; no newest-state delivery or replacement claim. src/renderer/src/store/slices/terminal-pty-identity-replacement.test.ts reduced. Removes three no-op/work-count registrations; retains externally observed ownership consistency. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected receipts remain unchanged and apply only to their unchanged selectors. Changed optional selectors have no new execution result. Audit1412: src/main/ssh/ssh-provider-authority.test.ts removed. Loses real AbortController revocation/target isolation/reentrancy outcomes, recreated-target generation-floor/session rollover behavior, stale mutation refusal and settled-registration cleanup alarms. These useful alarms are deliberately lost; no equivalent cancellation coverage is claimed. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected receipts remain unchanged and apply only to their unchanged selectors. Changed optional selectors have no new execution result. Audit1743 removes the standalone line-height clamp/default and pane cwd fallback helper tests (5 authored cases). These trivial-helper alarms are intentionally lost, with no equivalent replacement. Only current commands/testFiles lose the deleted selectors; historical receipts and evidenceRuns remain unchanged and do not validate the reduced commands.",
