tors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit2090 (sources2088/2089): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1709 removes low-value test definitions and retires affected assertion or execution-receipt claims without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews bound retained behavior and injected/native/remote limits. Unchanged assertions and receipts keep their original scope; gates lacking current active evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1640 removes low-value IPC, SSH, workspace and transcript-watcher tests without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public refusal, cancellation, execution-host and real-filesystem outcomes with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1623 removes low-value mocked daemon projections, scalar tables and duplicate terminal examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained terminal content preservation, process ownership refusal and recovery boundaries together with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1619 removes low-value mocked daemon projections, scalar tables and duplicate terminal examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained terminal content preservation, process ownership refusal and recovery boundaries together with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Retained exact unchanged-source receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Reduced selectors have no fresh execution result. Audit1417 intentionally reduces src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/terminal-ime-candidate-key-release-guard.test.ts: Loses direct timestamp-formula assertion; no useful independent alarm in removed registration. No equivalent replacement coverage or fresh result is claimed. Historical coverage account: Audit1361 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Audit1342 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Audit1320 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Audit1301 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): This audit removes the browser native-keyboard fallback inventory case. Its empty-chord, absent-layout and no-op-subscription alarms are lost; retained native input evidence is not an equivalent replacement. Historical commands and results remain historical. Local macOS and containerized Linux evidence, deterministic renderer-unit coverage for the Linux/Sogou candidate-key policy including the legacy orphaned-keyup fallback, xterm preedit visibility and row-occlusion behavior, Electron/CDP preedit geometry, Electron/CDP live-PTY Sogou-sty