nd execution scope without equivalent replacement coverage. Existing unchanged-selector receipts remain scoped to their original sources. Historical prior-source oracle: Retained exact unchanged-source receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Reduced selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical pre-audit oracle account for changed sources: Existing exact unchanged-selector receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Changed source selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical prior-source oracle account: Existing exact unchanged-selector receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Changed source selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical prior-source oracle account: Existing exact unchanged-selector receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Changed source selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical prior-source oracle account: The retained unchanged-source receipts are the only current execution evidence; reduced-source assertions await validation. Historical oracle account (not a current claim for changed sources): The retained unchanged-source receipts are the only current execution evidence; reduced-source assertions await validation. Historical oracle account (not a current claim for changed sources): The retained unchanged-source receipts are the only current execution evidence; reduced-source assertions await validation. Historical oracle account (not a current claim for changed sources): The retained unchanged-source receipts are the only current execution evidence; reduced-source assertions await validation. Historical oracle account (not a current claim for changed sources): Exact outbound bytes from the REAL native-text forwarder behind installPreviewImeBridge after initial snapshot restore, replacement resync, live transitions, and both keydown->insertText->keyup and keydown->keyup->insertText orderings; a wiring-only mock is supporting evidence, not the oracle. The current renderer-unit slice asserts native text commits route to the intended PTY once, composition/preedit bookkeeping does not leak premature text, resumed Windows event traces reactivate the visible preedit, an opaque mid-line overlay reproduces the committed row tail it covers, arbitrary DIM output remains visible, and final-column layout keeps both caret and textarea candidate anchor within the available screen width. The retained candidate-anchor slice checks layout-read caching, deferred timer coalescing, recognized-screen follow-ups and refit refresh with deterministic DOM fixtures. A Codex frame whose prompt row is bold and whose dimmed model footer sits below a blank gap acquires the mask class while composing; the same placeholder text without that footer, a framed-versus-unframed Claude prompt, a row of arbitrary dimmed output, and a row carrying typed text do not. The class is gone after composition end, after a blur that is not followed by a session end, and after disposal. Rendered Electron/CDP geometry independently proves the overlay reproduces every committed cell it hides, that a real Codex placeholder at column 2 is masked rather than repeated, and that the final-column caret, preedit, and textarea right edges all land inside the screen. Input-source classification handles synthetic/native paths, paste/runtime forwarding avoids duplicate terminal payloads for covered fixtures, and real fcitx4/Sogou captures send only the committed candidate for Space/digit picks while ordinary typing, literal Space and digits stay available. A main/preload/renderer notification chain proves every live window invalidates immediately, the old native read settles before a coalesced refresh signal, and older refreshes are generation-fenced. The Electron/CDP live-PTY repro verifies Sogou-style Space and digit selectors submit only the committed Chinese text. Real legacy IME commit preservation, native candidate-window placement, and the full CJK/Vietnamese/Arabic/JIS-yen matrix run 