        "Audit2133 current-parent preparation (988 authored removals; independently reviewed2099/2107/2115/2116 decisions; upstream clear-buffer and recovery-image regressions retained): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: tests/e2e/claude-agent-row-view.unit.test.ts: updates a mounted compact workflow description through the subscribed production parent; bounds upstream active-SSH visits for $population records, fallback=$fallback; derives %s destinations without requiring type or a workflow child ID; terminates a $path parent $status with no third request or intermediate toast; does not recover a first child %s. tests/e2e/cross-version-wire/agent-permission-legacy-spawn.unit.test.ts: keeps exact legacy ordering when structured creation cannot express afterTabId; can create a terminal without selecting the target worktree; preserves the legacy fresh-agent path when host authority is unavailable. tests/e2e/paired-instant-browser-tab.spec.ts: shows a paired browser tab before its create RPC resolves, then keeps it as one tab; adopts a paired browser tab without rebuilding its chrome. tests/e2e/session-tabs-decorative-title-fanout.unit.test.ts: bounds host publication and renderer application across remote worktrees; globally caps decorative freshness while every working status stays fresh. tests/e2e/session-tabs/mobile-session-active-performance.unit.test.ts: bounds saved-order publication selection at N and 10N without rematerializing navigation; bounds admitted placement reconciliation during supported reads at N and 10N; bounds selection input visits at 50 and 500 rows, including unavailable-target projection; keeps publication scoped to a changed worktree and shared by listeners at N and 10N; bounds preserved-chat merge and runtime-owned hydration at N and 10N (legacy=%s); bounds actual native retirement and shared delivery work at N and 10N. tests/e2e/session-tabs/mobile-session-active-publication.unit.test.ts: does not substitute a preserved row for an unavailable explicit legacy selection; resolves main-layout group selection %s (omitted group=%s). tests/e2e/structured-agent-session-launch-admission.unit.test.ts: opens a direct caller's terminal with the caller's own CLI arguments on a decline; opens the chat on the server that admitted it; opens only the terminal when this machine declines, without a notice; opens a new agent tab's terminal with the typed prompt when the caller names none; opens the chat, not a terminal, when this machine cannot resolve a new workspace yet; keeps its terminal fallback, as before. tests/e2e/structured-attention-prompt-relay.unit.test.ts: settles once per relayed prompt, not on every later status update. tests/e2e/structured-attention-read-retirement.unit.test.ts: Mark read on a chat never opened withdraws the prompt alert it surfaced; Mark read on a chat hidden since an earlier view covers the newer prompt it surfaced; reads a newly accepted visible prompt without sending an RPC for text-only updates. tests/e2e/structured-chat-tab-lifetime-cost.unit.test.ts: counts real raw stores, unrelated window publications and captured cleanup at %i chats; counts complete supplied-member sweep and separate final retirement at S=%i N=%i. tests/e2e/structured-session-workspace-authority.unit.test.ts: bounds actual target reveal across %i repo roots and metadata aliases. tests/e2e/terminal-agent-pane-launch.unit.test.ts: starts the host's planned command once, at the pane's size, and says it started; plans a pane whose prompt the window submits without the startup update prompt; preserves caller shell-ready delivery only for a connection-scoped adapter ($connectionId); starts no shell on plan failure (original failure: $returnLaunchFailure); cannot confirm a start whose provider answer was lost. tests/e2e/terminal-parked-memory.spec.ts: releases renderer terminal memory when hidden tabs park. tests/e2e/terminal-shortcuts.spec.ts: @headful Codex-like background output stays 