      "coverageNotes": "Audit1959 (sources 1957:5): Remove supplied-title/recognized-foreground/braille scalar happy authorization examples and quarter-circle glyph classification. Retain guarded-send refusals for missing/spinner-only evidence, actual runtime managed-launch token authority, unverified hint refusal and replacement-incarnation invalidation under injected process ports. The complete dated 20.9s nine-test receipt is archived rather than reduced. It was the sole current passed receipt, so demote this gate to protection none and archive its complete prospective selectors, all assertion objects and covered scope; retained source callbacks are no active execution credit. No historical passed receipt is narrowed or transferred to changed source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, physical provider/PTY, live remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed by this metadata packet. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1911: The complete Windows console-membership suite is removed: its sole remaining synthetic kill-error-after-timeout settlement/listener-count alarm is intentionally lost. The historical assertion mapping named broader fixed-helper membership/failure policies; removing this obsolete mapping does not claim that the single removed case had proved those policies or that remaining tests replace it. Only the deleted explicit source tokens, testFile and whole assertionRef are removed. Meaningful remaining source selectors/assertions and unaffected dated receipts retain their original scope. No equivalent replacement, fresh reduced-gate, native/platform/provider, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1683 removes low-value test projections, mock wiring, private-state assertions, inventories and duplicate examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public behavior and refusal boundaries with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1640 removes low-value IPC, SSH, workspace and transcript-watcher tests without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained public refusal, cancellation, execution-host and real-filesystem outcomes with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Audit1627 removes low-value mocked daemon projections, scalar tables and duplicate terminal examples without equivalent replacement coverage. Per-source reviews record retained terminal content preservation, process ownership refusal and recovery boundaries together with injected/native/remote limits. Affected historical receipts are retired; gates without active current evidence are downgraded. Historical scope before this audit: Runtime and provider-contract tests on macOS cover exact-PTY authorization, verified managed-Claude launch identity, local/daemon fresh confirmation, exact ConPTY membership, and unsupported-provider fail-closed behavior. Physical Windows, live Linux, SSH, WSL, and remote-runtime validation remain explicit gaps; providers without confirmation preserve conservative refusal when no verified launch identity exists. Protocol-version constant inventories are excluded from handshake and foreground-confirmation evidence. Audit1312 removes low-value imported specs from aggregate test drivers; old whole-driver execution receipts are archived. Retained registrations are unchanged. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1383: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-native-chat-setup.spec.ts reduced. Lose command-list/receipt/default/background activation matrices whose provider spawn returns canned IDs. Retained test proves actual tab allocation separation, not terminal startup. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected receipts and their platform/provider/budget claims remain scoped to unchanged selectors. Changed optional selectors have no new execution result. Audit1401: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-duplicate-pty-repair.spec.ts removed. Loses listing-on-already-repaired-data alarm; it never established runtime repair invocation. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-split-agent-tab.spec.ts removed. Loses actual mobile split sibling shell versus recorded-agent resume command alarms; no equivalent coverage asserted. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-native-chat-setup.spec.ts removed. Loses separate setup/startup tab result in that manually assembled path. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts reduced. Driver registration/import of a whole-deleted selected spec is removed; directly authored cases remain unchanged. No extra authored removal credit. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected receipts remain unchanged and apply only to their unchanged selectors. Changed optional selectors have no new execution result.",
      "motivatingLinks": ["https://github.com/stablyai/orca/issues/8303"],
      "invariant": "A guarded note send writes only to the exact PTY binding checked by the guard and only while permission/wait evidence allows input; a generic busy title requires independent agent identity from the title, a verified managed launch bound to the current PTY incarnation, or the foreground process; fresh hook state conflicting with an ordinary shell foreground requires fresh provider confirmation of a recognized agent in that PTY.",
      "oracle": "Audit1959 (sources 1957:5): Remove supplied-title/recognized-foreground/braille scalar happy authorization examples and quarter-circle glyph classification. Retain guarded-send refusals for missing/spinner-only evidence, actual runtime managed-launch token authority, unverified hint refusal and replacement-incarnation invalidation under injected process ports. The complete dated 20.9s nine-test receipt is archived rather than reduced. It was the sole current passed receipt, so demote this gate to protection none and archive its complete prospective selectors, all assertion objects and covered scope; retained source callbacks are no active execution credit. No historical passed receipt is narrowed or transferred to changed source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, physical provider/PTY, live remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed by this metadata packet. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1911: The complete Windows console-membership suite is removed: its sole remaining synthetic kill-error-after-timeout settlement/listener-count alarm is intentionally lost. The historical assertion mapping named broader fixed-helper membership/failure policies; removing this obsolete mapping does not claim that the single removed case had proved those policies or that remaining tests replace it. Only the deleted explicit source tokens, testFile and whole assertionRef are removed. Meaningful remaining source selectors/assertions and unaffected dated receipts retain their original scope. No equivalent replacement, fresh reduced-gate, native/platform/provider, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1683 retires changed-source assertion and execution scope without equivalent replacement coverage. Existing unchanged-selector receipts remain scoped to their original sources. Historical prior-source oracle: Existing exact unchanged-selector receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Changed source selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical prior-source oracle account: A quarter-circle Claude task title authorizes without a provider lookup only on the exact PTY incarnation carrying verified managed-Claude launch identity; the same title in a bare pane, with an unverified launch hint, or after PTY incarnation replacement is refused while current Claude activity remains a working signal. Fresh explicit state plus ordinary PowerShell plus confirmed recognized agent is sendable on the same PTY. Confirmed shell/non-agent, unavailable confirmation, PTY exit, handle rebind, or a callback PTY mismatch returns a refusal or not-writable result and writes zero bytes.",
