      "invariant": "Injected orchestration task prompts for recognized agent CLIs must send the prompt body inside one bracketed-paste frame, sanitize embedded ESC bytes, preserve chunk boundaries without losing the frame, and submit exactly once only after the agent can accept Enter. Local worker-start with supported observation must preserve an unobserved turn as start_unknown without revoking authority, closing questions, or triggering a rescue Enter; a worker report during observation must settle normally. Claude and Codex must emit a post-paste composer marker and then settle, or reach the bounded fallback first; every other agent retains the platform delay.",
      "oracle": "Audit4362 intentionally deletes the imported stale-waiter retry and manually assembled OSC9999 mobile-republish cases, plus the mocked missing-worktree cleanup suite (4 authored / 5 finite cases in three suites). Lost alarms include repeated unread worker_done pointers, working-to-waiting mobile status publication, missing-worktree filtering, and scoped daemon shutdown with unrelated duplicate identities. No replacement coverage or new platform proof is claimed. Audit3832 deliberately retires76 authored/79 finite cases:75 runtime compatibility cases/78 finite cases across14 fragments, plus one localization extractor default-flag case. Three whole runtime fragments are deleted;27 authored/30 finite cases remain across the reviewed sources. This gate retains only its own selected scope; no equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/native/remote evidence is claimed. Runtime component A: Audit3828 composes3822 with independent3824: deliberately retires49 authored/52 finite cases from seven compatibility fragments, leaving15 authored/18 finite cases and deleting two entire fragments. Accepted losses: positive folder-worker recovery/materialization and reveal deadline; persisted-key normalization and legacy split/group/focus projection; fixed stale CAS refusal; occupied/alias/restored/preallocated terminal-handle variants; fixed OpenCode/Cursor/Claude/Codex/Antigravity classification, readiness, title and management examples; direct private-map browser authority projections; browser-focus and OMP title projection; already-aborted claim cleanup. Additional3824 loss: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-handles-and-agent-status-part-02.spec.ts :: does not poll a wrapper foreground for a speculative CLI prompt send :: Speculative retryForegroundWrappers:false check must return false on a wrapper after one foreground read, without polling the supplied later codex response. These real bounded alarms are deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained callbacks are unchanged and provide only their own bounded scope, not equivalent replacement. Historical receipts do not validate reduced callbacks. No fresh runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser evidence or full transitive closure is claimed. Runtime component B: Audit3834 deliberately retires26 authored/26 finite cases from seven fresh compatibility fragments, leaving10/10 and deleting the one-case saved-binding reattachment fragment. Original position58 is excluded: its existing substantive3578 KEEP7 review remains historical, with no fresh credit. Accepted losses: fixed hook/provider-session identities and stale metadata refusal; decorative/pre-title foreground ordering variants; saved-binding surface reattachment; saved-row exit ghost removal and silent activation selection; unsupported headless wake; positive pending materialization/group projections; per-caller navigation selection; positive SSH hydration/read partition; laptop mobile publication/buffer and background/pending/status projections; abnormal/unregistered SSH grace, normal-exit refusal, persisted SSH hydration, positive serve reattachment, pending-agent launch arguments and direct seeded running-launch admission guard. These are real bounded alarms deliberately retired for low marginal value. Retained cases preserve their own distinct deferred foreground coalescing, usable handle continuity, stale inventory refresh, concurrent browser snapshot preservation, renderer graph fencing, caller dedup isolation, SSH partition writes, runtime split lifetime, independent relay-ready publication, lease admission/state/expiry. The direct running-launch no-spawn guard alarm is deliberately retired; no remaining owning-launch refusal coverage is claimed. Historical runs do not validate reduced callbacks. No equivalent replacement, runtime/native/SSH/WSL/phone/browser result or full transitive closure is claimed. Additional extractor loss: config/scripts/localization/source-extraction/audit-localization-native-dialogs.test.mjs :: does not change the existing renderer scan by default :: Default options must omit the five native-only fields in this supplied snippet. No equivalent replacement is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit3814 deliberately retires60 authored/60 finite cases:53runtime compatibility cases,4native XCTest methods and3Python clipboard methods, including the entire StableElementIndexes suite. Clipboard cuts retire the one-over-cap sample, incoming-offer destruction trace and sequential20-copy replay; actual wire, FD/pipe, startup and Xvfb/GTK boundaries remain without equivalent replacement claims. Accepted losses include narrow terminal-send payload/provider projections, legacy and direct no-op/error permutations, timing/work-count examples, private state/title/activity projections and fixture-driven readiness examples, individually enumerated below. These include real bounded production alarms consciously retired for marginal value; retained failed writes, duplicate submission, stale capture, transcript/ring and allocation fences are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or complete transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3806 deliberately retires40 authored/40 finite runtime compatibility cases, including the terminal-side-effect-facts-part03 headless-snapshots-part02 and agent-status-and-waits-part03 fragments, plus20 scalar Swift precondition sites. Lost runtime alarms include status/title/attention projection examples, simple renderer/headless frame restoration and status waiting outcomes detailed in the accepted-loss ledger. Swift cuts retire duplicate generation-map/schema/navigation/bridge and notification-wrapper assertions; no standalone native program is deleted. These include real bounded production alarms consciously retired for marginal value. Retained races, pending writes/reflow, namespace and waiter ownership are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or full transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3798 deliberately retires21 authored/24 finite compatibility cases, including the entire SSH-worktree-lifecycle and repository-project-operations fragments. Accepted losses include navigation-only settings acknowledgement, browser session cleanup and host preservation projections, window positive/policy-state examples, terminal recovery/reload and no-incarnation remint examples, terminal listing compatibility/malformed IDs, directory browse/sort/Windows path smoke, SSH create refusal/manual lineage, recursive parent-folder creation and fork/origin/avatar/icon projections. Real bounded production alarms are consciously retired for marginal value; retained authority races, cleanup/clone ownership, pending waiters, nested-folder and scan invalidation cases are not equivalent replacements. No fresh native/remote/browser execution or full transitive closure is claimed. Earlier dated receipts and raw selectors remain historical accounts of prior callback sets. Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The retained runtime registration driver loses three complete imported fragments: changed-working-label title facts and suppressed-frame tracked snapshots; refusing SSH GitLab MR-base lookup before local Git/glab calls; and missing folder-workspace path creation/update refusal before spawn/store mutation. These alarms are intentionally lost. Other imported fragments and separately rooted dated receipts are unchanged; they are not equivalent replacement coverage.  Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Audit2095 current-parent preparation2126: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Audit2090 (sources2088/2089): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. Retained assertion references and unchanged receipts keep their original scopes; retired callbacks and archived receipts provide no current coverage.",
