        "Retired during audit1312 aggregate-driver import cleanup; original complete execution receipt (unchanged): {\"date\":\"2026-08-14\",\"runner\":\"local\",\"platform\":\"macos\",\"command\":\"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts src/main/runtime/terminal-send-stale-leaf-liveness.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/orchestration/runs/runs.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/orchestration/messaging/send.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/orchestration/messaging/check.test.ts\",\"result\":\"passed\",\"durationSeconds\":14.15,\"summary\":\"1,293 tests passed and 1 was skipped across Run-bound pointer delivery, PTY retirement and respawn, stale-leaf liveness, direct-mail routing, filtered waiter ownership, canonical stored-recipient notification, and orchestration RPC behavior.\"}",
        "Audit1383: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-native-chat-setup.spec.ts reduced. Lose command-list/receipt/default/background activation matrices whose provider spawn returns canned IDs. Retained test proves actual tab allocation separation, not terminal startup. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit1401: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-duplicate-pty-repair.spec.ts removed. Loses listing-on-already-repaired-data alarm; it never established runtime repair invocation. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-session-tabs-split-agent-tab.spec.ts removed. Loses actual mobile split sibling shell versus recorded-agent resume command alarms; no equivalent coverage asserted. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/worktree-native-chat-setup.spec.ts removed. Loses separate setup/startup tab result in that manually assembled path. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime.test.ts reduced. Driver registration/import of a whole-deleted selected spec is removed; directly authored cases remain unchanged. No extra authored removal credit. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Historical removed assertion inventory: []",
        "Audit1412: src/main/runtime/orchestration-mailbox-cold-park-idle.spec.ts removed. Loses fresh-output cold-park quiet continuation, same-incarnation deferred Enter, late pointer-write settlement and explicit-check batch-claim alarms, including durable delivered_at state checks mixed into registrations0/3. No equivalent coverage claim. src/main/runtime/orchestration-dispatch-mailbox-delivery.spec.ts reduced. Loses dispatch wake dedup, restart unread guidance, legacy ack behavior and ambiguous pointer write/Enter crash retention alarms. DB-only stable delivery identity does not replace those paths. src/main/runtime/orchestration-mailbox-delivery.test.ts reduced. Driver registration/import of a whole-deleted selected spec is removed; directly authored cases remain unchanged. No extra authored removal credit. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Historical removed assertion inventory: [{\"file\":\"src/main/runtime/orchestration-mailbox-delivery.test.ts\",\"assertions\":[\"a refused pointer transport releases its reservation, stays undelivered, and becomes restart-retryable\",\"a dropped in-flight SSH settlement reaches the stager as unverifiable with bytes handed to the transport and emits no duplicate pointer after restart\",\"a settled write that throws mid-pointer preserves the write-attempted reservation\",\"an Enter whose settlement is lost stays at enter-attempted and restart emits no second Enter\"]}]",
        "Audit1943 (sources1934/1935/1938): Pruned notification-consistency suite loses50-row counter/wake budget and named-index EXPLAIN inventory, unbound direct-row projection and synthetic parked-decoy deadline examples. Preserve exact genuine SQLite ownership, disk-reopen/staged pointer and controlled provider-transition callbacks; fake PTY/title/clock seams do not establish actual provider delivery or measured backlog latency. Also retire three preexisting unsupported full aliases (explicit-check reservation redrive, known-PTY-exit replacement, and filtered/wait later-page draining), absent from both the frozen21and retained17callbacks. These retire stale metadata with no additional source/removal credit. Existing aliases are retained only where independently mapped below; no equivalent replacement for removed callbacks. Preserve meaningful remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged dated receipts within their original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh gate execution evidence in this metadata packet. No equivalent replacement, physical watcher/PTY/provider, live SSH/remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Exact retired authored alarms: 'does not point unbound direct mail that a later Run binding would hide'; 'pages a large persisted mismatch and coalesces each mailbox wake'; 'uses composite indexes for direct ownership reconciliation'; 'keeps a staged Enter deferred when a parked watcher republishes the leaf beside a decoy'.",
        "Audit1943 historical original assertionRefs object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/orchestration-mailbox-notification-consistency.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"Run A direct mail cannot point after the pane binds Run B\",\n            \"a fresh runtime cannot replay the unactionable pointer\",\n            \"a fresh runtime reconciles a database that already contains the production mismatch\",\n            \"large persisted mismatches route in 50-row pages with coalesced per-mailbox wakes\",\n            \"Run pointers pin the existing mixed-version-compatible --run identity\",\n            \"direct and Dispatch mail remain durable without unpinned synthetic terminal turns\",\n            \"a staged pointer submits once when Codex or Claude becomes working and still withholds Enter for permission\",\n            \"an explicit check releases its staged pointer reservation without redrive\",\n            \"accepted pointer text is durably deduplicated before delayed Enter and provider Enter refusal\",\n            \"a known PTY exit releases staged rows for the replacement process\",\n            \"a staged pointer follows its Run to a new live pane without cross-PTY duplication\",\n            \"equivalent panes serialize one mailbox while newer mail arrives during Enter delay\",\n            \"same-Run direct mail is delivered and acknowledged through the bound Run\",\n            \"a submitted actionable pointer is durably deduplicated across restart without marking mail read\",\n            \"newer Run mail is not pointed behind an outstanding fixed Delivery\",\n            \"same-owner filtered checks drain later 50-row pages before waiting\"\n          ]\n        }",
        "Audit1948 (Audit1946 sources 14, 26, 31, 39, 40, 47): Pruning removes scalar Run binding/projection and worker-start round-trip examples, v28 self-convergence, simple relay-type/legacy-payload and peer-probe/checkpoint cleanup examples, and reservation-failure/Cursor Enter examples. Preserve the three coordinator migration aliases, duplicate-replay waiter suppression and refused-write drain alias. The reminted-pane SQLite lookup checks active owner replacement and malformed decoys, not lookup cardinality or a performance budget. Overlapping sync uses an injected RPC/DB harness: promise coalescing and modeled checkpoint/ACK progression do not prove real durable checkpoint persistence. The complete affected combined federation receipt is retired whole; the independent unchanged CLI receipt remains in its original scope. No historical passed receipt is narrowed or transferred to changed source bytes. Unchanged dated receipts and retained assertions keep only their original independently mapped scopes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, physical PTY/provider, live remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed by this metadata review.",
        "Audit1948 historical original evidenceRuns object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active execution evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-14\",\n          \"runner\": \"local\",\n          \"platform\": \"macos\",\n          \"command\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/orchestration/federation-sync.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/orchestration/federation/federation.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/orchestration/federation/federation-lifecycle-settlement.test.ts --reporter=dot\",\n          \"result\": \"passed\",\n          \"durationSeconds\": 8.99,\n          \"summary\": \"52 tests passed with real OrchestrationDb rows, a deliberately dropped federation acknowledgment, reconnect/restart, forward-only checkpoints, duplicate read-row wake suppression, and protocol v1/v2 lifecycle settlement replay. The broader final federation/cross-version set passed 77/77.\",\n          \"currentCommand\": \"pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/runtime/orchestration/federation/synchronization/federation-sync.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/orchestration/federation/federation.test.ts src/main/runtime/rpc/methods/orchestration/federation/federation-lifecycle-settlement.test.ts --reporter=dot\"\n        }",
        "Audit1948 historical original assertionRefs object, preserved verbatim; retired objects are not active execution evidence or replacement coverage:\n{\n          \"file\": \"src/main/runtime/orchestration/db/worker-dispatch/orchestration-worker-dispatch-db.test.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"remote Dispatch attachment lookup remains bounded across pane remints and malformed suffix collisions\"\n          ]\n        }",
