      "coverageNotes": "Audit4362 intentionally deletes the imported stale-waiter retry and manually assembled OSC9999 mobile-republish cases, plus the mocked missing-worktree cleanup suite (4 authored / 5 finite cases in three suites). Lost alarms include repeated unread worker_done pointers, working-to-waiting mobile status publication, missing-worktree filtering, and scoped daemon shutdown with unrelated duplicate identities. No replacement coverage or new platform proof is claimed. Audit3994 retires two authored callbacks imported by the shared construction test driver: split OSC 9999 carry and rendererless status ownership, plus OpenCode permission text taking priority in status and tui-idle refusal. Remaining imports and selectors keep their scope. No equivalent replacement or fresh gate execution is claimed. CLI ownership cleanup retires low-value test cases, including explicit-current no-read, legacy success/idempotent acceptance, and caller-pane routing examples. Retained refusal and recovery assertions are listed below; dated receipts keep their original scopes. Audit3429 composes root-adopted3426/independent3427: intentionally removes168 authored/205 potential expanded cases across16 semantic sources, deleting11 whole suites and one304line unused assertion helper. Five authored/five potential cases remain; the duplicate500k graph row is dropped while its50k row and callback remain. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. The complete federation-lifecycle-settlement suite is removed, losing its fake remote settlement/protocol/acknowledgment examples. Its exact standalone command, testFiles entry and complete assertionRef are retired and prior fields archived. Existing receipts select unrelated migration and compiled CLI journeys and retain original scopes. Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The retained runtime registration driver loses three complete imported fragments: changed-working-label title facts and suppressed-frame tracked snapshots; refusing SSH GitLab MR-base lookup before local Git/glab calls; and missing folder-workspace path creation/update refusal before spawn/store mutation. These alarms are intentionally lost. Other imported fragments and separately rooted dated receipts are unchanged; they are not equivalent replacement coverage.  Audit3390 composes root-adopted3382/independent3383 and3386/independent3387 and3388/independent3389: intentionally retires216 authored registrations/230 expanded cases in42 whole authored suites plus5 zero-case registration drivers, without equivalent replacement. Lost local alarms include fake PTY identity/routing/startup/replay/mode/title/mouse/IME/scroll matrices, broad startup identity and file-open wiring, mock mailbox title recovery, mobile row parity and whole-v-selective save parity. Retained24 registrations/26 expanded cases in22 suites preserve actual xterm Windows buffer/wrap/scroll, typed TOML scalar, real Promise cancellation/settlement, HTTP Codex scanner/projector semantics, durable recovery admission/newer-schema bytes, federation completion/ACK/SQLite atomicity and failed stale-run-write versus imported durable history. Additional retained clock-domain scheduling, durable freeze/ACK/checkpoint ordering, ABA dirty intent, SQL atomicity, folder-domain retier/last-note deletion, scrollback durable no-sync staging, PanelBridge subscriber lifetime and reserved-send publication preserve narrower concrete behaviors. Current finite owner drift assessed in bounded defining bodies; retained callback bytes unchanged. Historical notes and complete dated receipts keep their original exact scopes. No new execution, equivalent replacement, native focus/device/pixel, live remote or global mixed-version guarantee is claimed. Audit2923 accepts loss of the first/replayed attested legacy worker_done CLI acceptance alarms, including exact send parameters, sender pane proof, lifecycle-wait flag and minted mutation identity. The removed fixture supplied settled runtime verdicts; it did not execute settlement authority, durable replay or outage recovery. Reduced selectors have no new execution, fault-control or equivalent replacement credit. Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Audit2095 current-parent preparation2126: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Audit2090 (sources2088/2089): Current reduced suites intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated execution and replacement claims do not validate changed source bytes or selectors. NEXT136 retains only unchanged execution receipts at their original scopes. Reduced-source selectors and retained static assertions have no new execution or equivalent replacement credit. CLI command/orchestration owner cleanup intentionally retires three registrations selected by this gate: two mock-supplied lifecycle/Run-home rejection projection examples and the complete manually assembled JSON failure-envelope example. The JSON-envelope suite, its exact command token/testFiles entry and whole assertion reference are removed; the retired Run-home relay assertion is removed from the retained lifecycle suite. These boundary projection alarms are lost without equivalent replacement. Retained fail-closed settlement and mutation-recovery cases keep their own scope. Pure owner moves do not invalidate unrelated dated receipts, which retain their exact original bytes; no fresh reduced-selector execution, native or remote evidence is claimed.",
