rior results do not validate reduced-source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, red/green, measured budget, soak, provider/PTY, rendered, live remote/mobile or cross-platform result is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1959 (sources 1955:34): Pruning removes unsupported-provider/out-of-range scalar refusals and the single Grok happy decoder fixture. Retain actual file cursor append/paging, same-inode checkpoint invalidation, opaque IDs and oversized-line progress. Retire the complete dated 3.48s combined receipt through its effective currentCommand, without changing its original command or transferring its 56-test result. Unchanged CLI/Electron receipt retains its independent scope. No historical passed receipt is narrowed or transferred to changed source bytes. No fresh execution, equivalent replacement, physical provider/PTY, live remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed by this metadata packet. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Existing exact unchanged-selector receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Changed source selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical prior-source oracle account: Surviving unchanged-source receipts are the current oracle; changed-source assertions await validation. Historical oracle account: Record release intent for a settled owner, attempt exact reuse before close, and require worker-start to fail with terminal_release_in_progress while the terminal stays open; then release the original owner exactly once. Race retain against a controlled archive promise and require no committed archive or close. Rebase a closed web-terminal host partition without terminalLayoutsByTabId and require the persistence write to complete while preserving host-authoritative membership; replay a valid legacy retirement under the same omission and require exact membership removal plus revision advancement. For retained external, user-owned, trans