      ],
      "invariant": "The row span Orca asks xterm to repaint after a forced foreground refresh must cover every viewport row whose rendered content changed during that write, plus the cursor row before and after it; when the span cannot be established — unobservable parse, viewport scroll, or a normal/alternate buffer flip — the whole viewport must be repainted.",
      "oracle": "Audit2615: all retained source alarms retired. No retained source coverage or current source oracle remains for this gate. Prior notes and dated evidence are historical only; no equivalent replacement or fresh evidence is claimed. Audit2236: retire the21-profile real-parser row-change corpus and bottom-row narrowing bound. Retain one controlled hardcoded dirty-span case proving pre/post cursor inclusion. No retained case proves real-parser changed-row convergence, viewport-scroll/alternate-screen full-grid fallback, work bounds or pixel behavior. Historical dated parser/CDP/red-green/performance evidence remains verbatim history and does not validate reduced source bytes; no equivalent replacement or fresh evidence is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): A real @xterm/headless parser replays an adversarial corpus (in-place bottom-row redraws, standalone CR overwrite, backspace, erase-in-line, erase-in-display above and below the cursor, full clear, wide CJK, emoji, combining marks, ZWJ sequences, scroll-region insert/delete, reverse index, DEC 2026 frames, alternate-screen enter and exit, viewport scroll, narrow panes). Each viewport row is serialized cell-by-cell with its attributes before and after the write, and every row that differs must fall inside the span the settle path requested. A vacuity guard asserts each case actually moves the screen.",
      "commands": [],
      "testFiles": [],
      "assertionRefs": [],
      "evidenceRuns": [],
