    {
      "id": "terminal-input.cooked-reply-queue",
      "title": "Terminal query replies stay atomic and bounded without evicting ordinary input",
      "maturity": "experimental",
      "protection": "partial",
      "owner": "terminal-runtime",
      "layer": "renderer-provider-contract",
      "surfaces": [
        "desktop terminal input",
        "OSC 10/11 replies",
        "mode-2031 replies",
        "DA1 and CPR replies",
        "local PTY",
        "daemon and SSH PTYs"
      ],
      "platforms": ["macos", "linux", "windows"],
      "providers": ["local", "daemon", "ssh"],
      "coveredPlatforms": ["macos"],
      "coveredProviders": ["local"],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit3362 retires the 10,000-query newest64 viewport-claim flood-cap assertion and second-chunk refusal, coalescing/burst/limit/yield and constant examples. The surviving ordinary/query/ordinary binary-frame ordering and UTF8 emoji-safe acknowledged chunk cases retain narrower coverage. Unit commands/test-file selectors remain; the first binary-order assertion stays exact. Two unrelated macOS E2E receipts remain verbatim with their original scope. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/PTY/provider/UI/mobile/mixed-version/cross-platform evidence is claimed. Audit 3312 reduces remote-runtime-pty-batching.test.ts, intentionally losing idle leading/trailing coalescing, leading-edge-disabled, accumulated byte-ceiling flush, standalone synchronous oversized-input rejection, accepted-input validation yield, deferred pending-tail byte order, and queued-viewport clear/flush and timer-cancellation alarms. The unchanged UTF-8 splitting, validation barrier ordering and asynchronous oversized-input nondelivery cases are narrower, not equivalent replacements. The barrier assertion and both existing Electron receipts remain unchanged and do not validate these retired cases. No fresh runtime, provider, rendered, remote/mobile, mixed-version, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget validation is claimed. Audit 3292 retires the empty-queue immediate query-reply delivery example from remote-runtime-pty-query-reply-immediate.test.ts. Pending ordinary-input separation and asynchronous paste-validation ordering cases remain byte-identical, matching the existing assertion reference. The no-pending-input delivery alarm is intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. Existing selectors, unchanged local Electron receipts and historical receipts remain exact; no new runtime, PTY deadline, platform or mixed-version result is claimed. Audit3086: retire the immediate-reply ceiling and thrown renderer-write recovery aliases. Narrow FIFO coverage to deferred preconnect validation and teardown coverage to natural-exit stale ordinary/accepted tails; live acknowledged barriers and disconnect/detach branches are intentionally retired. Prior queue cleanup and unchanged Electron receipts remain exact; no replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Audit1878 retires the dated reduced-source unit receipt. Only the unchanged macOS local Electron receipts remain current, scoped to their exact commands; reduced unit selectors and SSH have no current execution receipt. Historical pre-audit coverageNotes: Deterministic renderer and IPC-transport tests prove count and text ceilings, oldest-reply shedding, explicit query-reply source routing, ordinary-input preservation, acknowledged-write FIFO barriers, single-worker drain reentrancy, one-reply-per-write delivery for OSC, DA1, and CPR replies, real xterm OSC reply generation, drain-failure containment, teardown settlement, and clear/reuse generation fencing. Remote-runtime tests preserve separate query-reply writes across pending input, async validation, and viewport-claim buffering. Host-contract tests prove a later DA1/CPR reply cannot overtake a deferred OSC reply, including a coalesced legacy-client payload. Live macOS Electron tests cover local PTY OSC replies and interactive typing; a macOS-hosted Docker OpenSSH test proves an upstream-node-pty Linux relay keeps OSC/DA1 replies out of the next fish child's stdin. No live daemon, paired-runtime, WSL, physical Linux/Windows client, or binary mixed-version run is registered.",
      "motivatingLinks": [
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/issues/13137",
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/issues/7329",
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/issues/13892"
      ],
      "invariant": "The desktop PTY input queue retains at most 64 explicitly sourced pending terminal query replies and 4096 UTF-16 code units. Every retained reply reaches the provider as one atomic write, and ordinary, acknowledged, and reply input share one invocation-ordered FIFO so no later write overtakes an acknowledged write. Reentrant write callbacks cannot start a second drain worker or strand input admitted after clear/reuse. A reply's own echo is contained on the output side by projecting its known echo shapes; the ESC-initial verbatim shape is matched only when complete, never held as a partial, so a query torn at its own ESC is still answered. Overflow removes only the oldest query replies, never ordinary input except the documented modified-F3/CPR byte collision, and failure or teardown cannot clear a newer queue generation or strand an acknowledged promise.",
      "oracle": "Audit3362 retires the 10,000-query newest64 viewport-claim flood-cap assertion and second-chunk refusal, coalescing/burst/limit/yield and constant examples. The surviving ordinary/query/ordinary binary-frame ordering and UTF8 emoji-safe acknowledged chunk cases retain narrower coverage. Unit commands/test-file selectors remain; the first binary-order assertion stays exact. Two unrelated macOS E2E receipts remain verbatim with their original scope. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/PTY/provider/UI/mobile/mixed-version/cross-platform evidence is claimed. Audit 3312 reduces remote-runtime-pty-batching.test.ts, intentionally losing idle leading/trailing coalescing, leading-edge-disabled, accumulated byte-ceiling flush, standalone synchronous oversized-input rejection, accepted-input validation yield, deferred pending-tail byte order, and queued-viewport clear/flush and timer-cancellation alarms. The unchanged UTF-8 splitting, validation barrier ordering and asynchronous oversized-input nondelivery cases are narrower, not equivalent replacements. The barrier assertion and both existing Electron receipts remain unchanged and do not validate these retired cases. No fresh runtime, provider, rendered, remote/mobile, mixed-version, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget validation is claimed. Audit 3292 retires the empty-queue immediate query-reply delivery example from remote-runtime-pty-query-reply-immediate.test.ts. Pending ordinary-input separation and asynchronous paste-validation ordering cases remain byte-identical, matching the existing assertion reference. The no-pending-input delivery alarm is intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. Existing selectors, unchanged local Electron receipts and historical receipts remain exact; no new runtime, PTY deadline, platform or mixed-version result is claimed. Audit3086: retire the immediate-reply ceiling and thrown renderer-write recovery aliases. Narrow FIFO coverage to deferred preconnect validation and teardown coverage to natural-exit stale ordinary/accepted tails; live acknowledged barriers and disconnect/detach branches are intentionally retired. Prior queue cleanup and unchanged Electron receipts remain exact; no replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Audit1878 retires the dated reduced-source unit receipt. Only the unchanged macOS local Electron receipts remain current, scoped to their exact commands; reduced unit selectors and SSH have no current execution receipt. Historical pre-audit oracle: Synchronously enqueue separate 10,000-entry OSC and DA1 reply floods before the scheduled drain and assert that only the initial immediate reply and newest 64 pending replies are written, each as one provider write, before a trailing keystroke. Stall an acknowledged write between earlier and later ordinary/reply input, then require teardown to settle it and same-id reuse to receive no stale tail. Reenter the queue synchronously from an acknowledged write with both enqueue and clear/reuse, requiring one drain and fresh input delivery only after the stale acknowledged write settles false. At the host boundary, defer an OSC reply and assert that separate or legacy-coalesced DA1/CPR replies flush after it in observed query order. At the remote-runtime boundary, preserve separate writes around pending ordinary input, async validation, and viewport-claim buffering. Repeat behind 10,000 ordinary inputs and exercise the text ceiling, real xterm generation, provider-write failure, rejected yield, and clear/reuse generation fencing.",
      "commands": [
        "pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/input/pty-input-write-queue.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/ipc/pty-transport-input-write.test.ts src/shared/terminal/protocol/queries/terminal-query-reply.test.ts src/shared/terminal/pty/ingress/pty-startup-ingress-live-query-reply.test.ts src/shared/terminal/pty/ingress/pty-startup-reply-echo-shapes.test.ts",
        "pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/remote-runtime/output/remote-runtime-pty-batching.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-pty-query-reply-immediate.test.ts src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-pty-transport-input-coalescing.test.ts",
        "pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/terminal-osc-color-queries.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headless --workers=1",
        "pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/terminal-typing-latency.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project electron-headless --workers=1"
      ],
      "testFiles": [
        "src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/input/pty-input-write-queue.test.ts",
        "src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/ipc/pty-transport-input-write.test.ts",
        "src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/remote-runtime/output/remote-runtime-pty-batching.test.ts",
        "src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-pty-query-reply-immediate.test.ts",
        "src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-transport/remote-runtime/remote-runtime-pty-transport-input-coalescing.test.ts",
        "src/shared/terminal/protocol/queries/terminal-query-reply.test.ts",
