    {
      "id": "terminal-runtime.mobile-stream-budget",
      "title": "Runtime and mobile terminal streams keep snapshot and live-output bytes bounded",
      "maturity": "experimental",
      "protection": "none",
      "owner": "terminal-runtime",
      "layer": "runtime-rpc-contract",
      "surfaces": [
        "mobile terminal",
        "native-chat terminal overlay",
        "runtime RPC",
        "binary multiplex",
        "JSON subscribe fallback",
        "snapshot buffering"
      ],
      "platforms": ["macos", "linux", "windows", "mobile"],
      "providers": ["remote-runtime", "ssh", "local", "daemon"],
      "coveredPlatforms": [],
      "coveredProviders": [],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit1400 intentionally deletes or reduces the listed sources. No fresh execution result validates their reduced selectors. Historical coverage account: Local macOS evidence covers runtime-RPC stream budgets, paired-renderer parse/discard credit, and negotiated host-side suppression for hidden paired desktop panes. Deferred credit is shared by local and remote transports, batches ACKs at 192 KiB or 4 ms, grows per-stream windows from 512 KiB to 2 MiB and aggregate windows from 2 MiB to 8 MiB, bounds queued output to 256 KiB per stream, and caps each multiplex connection at 32 active or pending streams for an 8 MiB aggregate pending-output ceiling. Deterministic tests cover replay ordering, stale generations, malformed frames, hidden panes, queue eviction, disposal, send/recovery failure, repeated pending-slot replacement, reconnect, mixed-version pause negotiation, and round-robin fairness. The opt-in benchmark models 1/20/100 ms RTT and 1/4/8 viewers, throughput, window use, completion spread and protocol-frame counts. It measures model scheduler elapsed time separately from actual @xterm/headless parser CPU/retained heap; modeled credit and ACK results do not qualify production credit enforcement. Live Android restore evidence, browser/WebGL parser measurements, and legacy JSON subscribe parity remain required. The audit removed the PTY ACK wrapper suite, which replayed credit arithmetic with mocked IPC. Its isolated wrapper alarms are no longer registered here; generic credit and runtime stream tests do not establish equivalent PTY integration coverage. The audit removes the standalone auto-settle-before-deferred-claim example. Nested-owner and claimed-child completion tests remain; they do not establish that removed timing alarm. The test-value audit removes the bulk-ACK threshold, output-pause capability/paused-input, transformed-metadata disposal, late-parser and renderer-throw examples. The retained captured-parser, malformed-frame and failed-ACK timer checks do not exercise real xterm parsing or server credit enforcement and do not replace the removed alarms. Historical run commands and results remain historical. The test-value audit removes the pure mobile stream-decision suite: pause/resume/rearm/viewport branch inventories no longer have that isolated alarm. The surviving stream-hook tests do not establish equivalent WebView restore, PTY resize, input-lease or subscription delivery coverage. Historical run commands and counts are preserved as historical records; a narrowed selector is not a new passed run. Audit1302: src/main/runtime/rpc/terminal-multiplex-ack-output-budget.test.ts: Keep production RPC dispatcher/terminal framing with emitted binary bytes, UTF-8 reconstruction and client ACK releasing genuinely withheld output; also keep the direct binary-subscribe chunk boundary. Remove shared-budget fairness matrix that sleeps real time and relies on exact synthetic per-stream window scheduling. Lose that eight-stream fairness/call wiring alarm; no equivalent replacement. Reduced selectors require fresh validation; prior full-suite receipts do not validate removed or changed coverage. No equivalent replacement or physical-provider claim. Audit1341 scope1334 removes/narrows mobile/src/session/native-chat/use-mobile-native-chat-terminal-stream.test.ts. Exact retired scenarios are intentionally lost; surviving assertions are limited to unchanged retained authored cases. No equivalent replacement, physical phone or deployed mixed-host claim. Fresh validation is required for narrowed commands. Audit1391: src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-remote-pause-drop-notice.spec.ts reduced. Lose repeated quiet switches avoiding snapshots and legacy host without drop-report capability requesting a snapshot. Retained imported registrar uses fake transport/xterm writes, exercising real gap/restore lifecycle rather than actual terminal rendering. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. The existing primary-selector receipt and its claims remain scoped to their unchanged sources; the broad optional command has no new execution result. Audit1400: src/main/runtime/rpc/terminal-multiplex-flow-control.bench.test.ts removed. Lose ORCA_TERMINAL_PERF_BENCH diagnostic report and local xterm parser measurements; this was not an ordinary CI assertion gate. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Broader617 Mobile owner follow-up retires six whole work-count/timing registrations from mobile/src/session/native-chat/use-mobile-native-chat-terminal-stream.test.ts, retaining five functional handoff/readiness/absence/recovery registrations. Prior Audit1400 retained-but-unvalidated and archived inventories describe earlier source and remain historical after this follow-up. No equivalent replacement, fresh execution, timing measurement, physical phone, or deployed mixed-host validation is claimed by this source change. Current premerge review correction for the Broader617 Mobile owner follow-up: four additional whole mock-only/mock-produced-state stream registrations are retired, for ten total cuts and one unchanged retained registration, keeps asking until a tab snapshot replaces the exhausted handle. The preceding five-retained description records the superseded candidate, not current coverage. The retained case checks the real hook-owned recovery-needed result; handoff, readiness and absence-marker mock-delivery alarms are intentionally lost without equivalent replacement. Dead test render counting and unused handoff setup are removed. No new native, physical-phone, timing or deployed-host proof is implied.",
      "motivatingLinks": [
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/6951",
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/6955",
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/7009"
      ],
      "invariant": "Runtime and mobile terminal subscriptions must cap initial snapshots, live output buffered while snapshots load, chunk sizes, batches, and aggregate in-flight credit. ACK means the renderer parsed the bytes or intentionally discarded them; receipt-time ACK is forbidden. A capability-negotiated hidden paired desktop stream must deliver zero raw output frames after host model ingestion, preserve side-effect facts, and restore from one authoritative snapshot before exact live output resumes. Every replay, stale-generation, malformed-frame, hidden-pane, eviction, disposal, error, and reconnect path must settle credit exactly once so streams neither leak memory nor stall. A terminal covered by native chat must restore from fresh scrollback when revealed, while preserving output order, input locks, resize/driver events, fairness, and safe mixed-version fallback.",
      "oracle": "No current automated execution oracle is claimed for this gate after Audit1400 retired changed-source receipts. Historical oracle account: Assert mobile initial snapshots downgrade until they fit <=512KB, requested binary snapshots downgrade until they fit <=2MB, live output queued while snapshots load stays <=256KB per stream, large output splits into <=48KB frames, and output bursts coalesce. Pause three negotiated paired desktop streams, sustain output, and assert zero renderer frames; reveal one and assert one authoritative snapshot followed by exact live bytes with no loss or duplication. Prove old clients continue receiving output and new clients never send pause to old hosts. Feed paired output through the xterm parse callback and prove ACK is deferred until parse or intentional discard, then inject stale generation, malformed/transformed frames, replay failure, queue eviction, hidden panes, pane disposal, ACK send failure, recovery serialization failure, and reconnect races; assert ordered replay and exactly-once credit settlement. Fill the aggregate window across bulk and interactive streams, ACK once, and prove round-robin progress. Run the opt-in 64 MiB/viewer RTT matrix to report modeled throughput, in-flight window use, completion spread and protocol-frame counts, plus model scheduler elapsed time. Measure @xterm/headless parser CPU and retained heap separately; the model does not qualify production credit enforcement. JSON fallback parity and live Android scrollback restoration remain explicit gaps.",
      "commands": [],
      "testFiles": [],
      "assertionRefs": [],
      "evidenceRuns": [],
