      "coverageNotes": "Audit3390 composes root-adopted3382/independent3383 and3386/independent3387 and3388/independent3389: intentionally retires216 authored registrations/230 expanded cases in42 whole authored suites plus5 zero-case registration drivers, without equivalent replacement. Lost local alarms include fake PTY identity/routing/startup/replay/mode/title/mouse/IME/scroll matrices, broad startup identity and file-open wiring, mock mailbox title recovery, mobile row parity and whole-v-selective save parity. Retained24 registrations/26 expanded cases in22 suites preserve actual xterm Windows buffer/wrap/scroll, typed TOML scalar, real Promise cancellation/settlement, HTTP Codex scanner/projector semantics, durable recovery admission/newer-schema bytes, federation completion/ACK/SQLite atomicity and failed stale-run-write versus imported durable history. Additional retained clock-domain scheduling, durable freeze/ACK/checkpoint ordering, ABA dirty intent, SQL atomicity, folder-domain retier/last-note deletion, scrollback durable no-sync staging, PanelBridge subscriber lifetime and reserved-send publication preserve narrower concrete behaviors. Current finite owner drift assessed in bounded defining bodies; retained callback bytes unchanged. Historical notes and complete dated receipts keep their original exact scopes. No new execution, equivalent replacement, native focus/device/pixel, live remote or global mixed-version guarantee is claimed. Audit3349 retires the whole terminal-render-desync-sentinel suite, including the same-cells persistence/recovery alarm, without equivalent replacement. Its unit command selector, test-file selector and assertion reference are removed prospectively. Earlier global-effects/window-wake retirements and the retired dated sentinel receipt remain historical verbatim. Two unrelated macOS document-visibility E2E receipts remain verbatim; the frozen static closure does not select changed tests through their literal roots. No fresh GPU/rendered UI, runtime, historical-import, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. NEXT46 terminal-owner layout and whole-case policy: src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-hidden-replay.test.ts, src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection/tests/pty-connection-input-and-repaint.test.ts. Complete retired/reduced selectors lose their listed alarms; retained cases have no transferred historical pass or equivalent replacement coverage. Unaffected dated receipts retain only their original exact scopes. This metadata edit is not fresh execution evidence. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit3335 retires the complete mocked window-wake recovery suite (11 authored registrations/12 expanded cases), intentionally losing fullscreen atlas-preservation, wake callback ordering, deferred-DPR deduplication/repair and private frame-budget alarms without equivalent replacement. The surviving focused selector is unexecuted in this source composition. Unrelated dated receipts keep their original scope; no fresh runtime/GPU/focus, rendered UI, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Audit3326 adopts reconciled source audit3324 and intentionally retires these low-value examples and their regression alarms: recovers visible terminal rendering and input when the window regains focus — Whole suite: fake React useEffect immediately invokes bodies and ignores cleanup/deps; fake useRef/store hooks plus mocked pane manager only assert callback choreography. Does not exercise window focus, actual input or pixels. Retires focus wake wiring alarm.; clears WebGL texture atlases when the OS resumes — Whole suite: same fake-hook harness invokes captured OS resume callback and counts mocked atlas-clear/repaint methods. No GPU, actual OS resume, or real hook lifetime. Retires atlas clear wiring alarm.; preserves WebGL texture atlases when the active terminal document becomes visible — Whole suite: direct fake document visibility listener and mock-call absence/presence under fake hooks cannot establish real WebGL preservation or cleanup. Retires visibility wake wiring alarm.. Retained tests do not replace these alarms. Dated unrelated evidence remains scoped to its original execution; no historical source/import-closure equivalence, fresh execution, real network/provider/SSH, rendered UI, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Retained exact unchanged-source receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Reduced selectors have no fresh execution result. Audit1417 intentionally deletes src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-hidden-tui-snapshot-replay.spec.ts: Loses rich hidden snapshot sequence replay/grid resize and forced repaint after hidden snapshot alarms, including live-trigger deduplication. No equivalent replacement coverage or fresh result is claimed. Historical coverage account: Audit1342 changes referenced sources. Retained unchanged-source receipts apply only to their unchanged commands; the reduced selectors have no new execution result. Historical coverage account (not a current claim for changed sources): Deterministic renderer contracts require foreground renderer-risk, synchronized, hidden, and alternate-screen PTY output to stay on pane-local repaint paths without a global atlas reset. Separate contracts preserve explicit paste, reveal, visibility-resume, system-resume, and confirmed-desync recovery. A macOS Electron run verifies that a document visibility cycle preserves real WebGL atlases and terminal pixels; the candidate has not been rerun against an isolated live paired server. The test-value audit removed registry recovery fanout, visibility, ordering and failure-isolation assertions. The remaining registry test constrains diagnostic sampling only and is excluded from this gate. No equivalent recovery coverage is claimed. Completed settled tab-reveal repaint execution is not covered after removal of pane-reveal-repaint.test.ts. The separate terminal-visibility-resume tests assert mocked scheduling and presentation calls; they do not establish completed repaint execution. Audit1342: src/renderer/src/lib/pane-manager/pane-webgl-context-recovery.test.ts removed. Context resume/reveal retry and deferred rebuild mock-pane alarms disappear. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1391: src/renderer/src/components/terminal-pane/pty-connection-remote-pause-drop-notice.spec.ts reduced. Lose repeated quiet switches avoiding snapshots and legacy host without drop-report capability requesting a snapshot. Retained imported registrar uses fake transport/xterm writes, exercising real gap/restore lifecycle rather than actual terminal rendering. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. The existing primary-selector receipt and its claims remain scoped to their unchanged sources; the broad optional command has no new execution result.",
