dered UI, runtime, historical-import, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Audit3335 retires the complete mocked window-wake recovery suite (11 authored registrations/12 expanded cases), intentionally losing fullscreen atlas-preservation, wake callback ordering, deferred-DPR deduplication/repair and private frame-budget alarms without equivalent replacement. The surviving focused selector is unexecuted in this source composition. Unrelated dated receipts keep their original scope; no fresh runtime/GPU/focus, rendered UI, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Audit3326 adopts reconciled source audit3324 and intentionally retires these low-value examples and their regression alarms: recovers visible terminal rendering and input when the window regains focus — Whole suite: fake React useEffect immediately invokes bodies and ignores cleanup/deps; fake useRef/store hooks plus mocked pane manager only assert callback choreography. Does not exercise window focus, actual input or pixels. Retires focus wake wiring alarm.; clears WebGL texture atlases when the OS resumes — Whole suite: same fake-hook harness invokes captured OS resume callback and counts mocked atlas-clear/repaint methods. No GPU, actual OS resume, or real hook lifetime. Retires atlas clear wiring alarm.; preserves WebGL texture atlases when the active terminal document becomes visible — Whole suite: direct fake document visibility listener and mock-call absence/presence under fake hooks cannot establish real WebGL preservation or cleanup. Retires visibility wake wiring alarm.. Retained tests do not replace these alarms. Dated unrelated evidence remains scoped to its original execution; no historical source/import-closure equivalence, fresh execution, real network/provider/SSH, rendered UI, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Audit2133 current-parent preparation: Current reduced sources/selectors intentionally retire the alarms listed in knownGaps; prior dated runs and replacement claims do not validate the changed set. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Retained exact unchanged-source receipts remain the only current execution evidence. Reduced selectors have no fresh execution result. Historical pre-audit oracle account for changed sources: The retained unchanged-source receipts are the only current execution evidence; reduced-source assertions await validation. Historical oracle account (not a current claim for changed sources): Parse foreground renderer-risk, synchronized, hidden, and alternate-screen PTY output and require pane-local refresh where needed with zero calls to shared reset-and-refresh recovery. Require the atlas-recovery module to expose only explicit lifecycle entry points, then verify paste recovery. Completed settled tab-reveal repaint is not verified by the remaining unit evidence. Dispatch a visible document visibilitychange and require atlas-preserving wake recovery. Separately, drive an Electron visibility cycle with two real WebGL panes, require zero atlas clears, and retain at least 85% of each pane's baseline ink pixels.",
