      "coveredProviders": ["local", "remote-runtime", "ssh"],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit4368 intentionally drops seven mocked teardown cases: duplicate single-chat rollback, forced stuck-close warning/retirement, post-close-throw exit acceptance, mixed live/unconfirmed wording, exact serial-close budget work, missing runtime selector success and runtime-sweep rejection. Four structured-session and three PTY teardown cases remain; no replacement or fresh native/process/remote proof is claimed. Historical assertion anchors and receipts are not refreshed by this source-only reduction. Audit4362 intentionally deletes the imported stale-waiter retry and manually assembled OSC9999 mobile-republish cases, plus the mocked missing-worktree cleanup suite (4 authored / 5 finite cases in three suites). Lost alarms include repeated unread worker_done pointers, working-to-waiting mobile status publication, missing-worktree filtering, and scoped daemon shutdown with unrelated duplicate identities. No replacement coverage or new platform proof is claimed. Audit4358 intentionally removes six whole mocked daemon subprocess suites and two extra pre-listener replay variants (18 authored / 20 finite cases). Lost alarms include cancel-during-cwd-validation, root agent startup refusal, output/exit before ConPTY publication, fresh/delayed/unavailable foreground confirmation, cache/decision separation, detached/no-tty child evidence and synthetic agent authorization. The retained lifecycle case checks data and exit replay after handle creation, not startup-time publication or alternate listener order. The retained native Windows Git Bash workflow and host cold-restore seed check have separate scopes. No equivalent replacement or fresh gate execution is claimed. Earlier notes and dated receipts retain their original scope. Audit4351 removes the physical-exit timeout/retry and kill-failure/retry local-PTY shutdown cases. The retained shutdown case proves pending ownership until the injected node-pty exit callback only. These two narrow error-path alarms are intentionally lost; retained commands still select the reduced suite. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime execution is claimed. Earlier notes and dated receipts retain their original scopes. Audit3994 retires two authored callbacks imported by the shared construction test driver: split OSC 9999 carry and rendererless status ownership, plus OpenCode permission text taking priority in status and tui-idle refusal. Remaining imports and selectors keep their scope. No equivalent replacement or fresh gate execution is claimed. Audit 3959 retires the whole session.test.ts driver (27 authored / 33 finite cases): startup/echo filtering, readiness input gates, ownership confirmation, detach authority, and termination retry/exit ordering alarms are intentionally lost. No equivalent replacement or fresh runtime validation is claimed. Audit3788 retires10 authored/11 expanded cases across six changed drivers, including the entire screencast pending-frame-retry and usage-source-cache-streaming suites. Deliberate losses are false-refused last-frame retry/once-only delivery, ordinary stable-pane reattachment, cleared-chat Dispatch completion, terminal-declared chat-caller refusal, at-rest worker liveness projection, nested depth/cap policy, small unsigned6/sealed7 plain-format and verified-bit examples, generic malformed-ISIZE footer refusal examples, and synthetic10k/100k chunk-size/work-count budgets in gzip and general cache I/O. These include real state/disk/RPC outcomes consciously retired for marginal value; retained E2EE-backlog, receipt/custody/uncertain-ack, integrity/migration and staging-cleanup cases are not equivalent replacements. The footer test did not prove early rejection or bounded allocation; staging cleanup did not seed unrelated files. No replacement or fresh native/remote/performance execution is claimed. Earlier raw selectors and dated receipts remain historical. Audit3779 retires17 authored/17 expanded registrations across six changed drivers,