retain their original scope; changed optional selectors have no fresh full-gate execution result. This audit removes the paired-web stopped-during-outage and late-ready direct-branch examples. The retained pre-ready cancellation, failed-unwatch retry and replay-continuity cases are not equivalent replacements for those ordering alarms. Current web-runtime-client.test.ts assertions below name only its retained pre-ready callback case; replay cases remain in their separate suite. Historical commands and results remain historical. Deterministic tests cover one shared healthy child per runtime process plus at most four bounded fault-quarantine children, native desktop, paired-runtime, and WSL snapshot processes sharing the same eight-physical-child reservation with typed serialized event-driven capacity recovery, including recursive re-wait when crash recovery reclaims an announced slot, one quarantine attempt per watch lifetime, generation-scoped cancellation, bounded termination with removable deadline waiters, replacement-crawl errors that cannot be blessed by a late readiness ack, pre-ready paired-web cancellation registered before an unbounded capacity wait, already-resolved and late physical-exit retry of a rejected paired-web teardown, physical desktop-install and local/SSH PTY teardown, stale-generation rejection, per-child stat bounds, final-overflow RPC delivery, and renderer eviction before terminal callbacks can retry. Destructive local and SSH removal fences both ID-derived and resolved-cwd terminal roots, including sibling-root/cwd combinations with reverse admission rollback, closes descendant relay watches before parent deletion, enumerates authoritative provider/cwd ownership, falls back to daemon spawn cwd before OSC 7, and keeps daemon/relay immediate shutdown pending until native exit or a bounded fail-closed error; a dead relay PID discovered during attach also settles concurrent shutdown before its stale entry is reaped, while Windows runtime watcher deadlines retain one removable physical-close waiter, treat Node's error-close path as positive physical-exit proof, and clear root ownership on late close. The relay policy test maps a standard repository's base, Git common directory, and worktree roots to one healthy supervisor, then proves a shared-child failure recovers those roots in separate quarantine supervisors with overflow and resumed events. Abortable capacity, quarantine, runtime-root, relay, SSH, and relay pre-install setup waits attach one reaction to each shared promise and explicitly remove 10,000 cancelled caller closures while one anchor remains. Built-entry macOS harnesses kill the desktop/runtime and SSH relay watcher children, then require automatic resubscription and later events while the host process and relay PTY survive. SSH bundles the child boundary beside relay.js, requires both artifacts for install completeness, and preserves registration-owned same-root cancellation. The test-value audit corrects the active renderer watch command/file reference to the existing runtime-file-client-watch.test.ts, whose three cases are retained unchanged. They observe synthetic subscription retry/fanout and unsubscribe/unwatch calls, not actual preload/main bookkeeping or physical watcher-process cleanup. The separate read/preview client suite loses forwarding, supplied-error and negative-only examples, retaining binary detection and Unicode SVG decoding. Historical evidence commands/results are unchanged. Test-value audit1293 removes src/main/providers/local-pty/local-pty-provider-session-inventory.test.ts (2 authored cases). Their isolated assertions no longer run; surviving tests are not claimed as equivalent coverage. Fresh execution against the candidate SHA is required. Audit1312 removes low-value imported specs from aggregate test drivers; old whole-driver execution receipts are archived. Retained registrations are unchanged. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Audit1383: src/main/r