ub-cache sidecars off the thread; stats.flushAsync() issues no synchronous fs syscalls; Grok session cleanup issues no synchronous fs syscalls; stats.flushAsync() closes out live agents before it returns, not when its write lands; a stalled mount leaves the event loop live instead of parking it; store.flushAsync() is one idempotent final barrier; store.flushAsync() resolves instead of throwing when the profile mount rejects writes. src/main/stats/agent-session-transition-recorder.test.ts: counts a hook-only agent that never writes an agent-shaped terminal title; never opens a session from a replayed or disk-restored working status; still closes a live session when the terminating status arrives as a replay; counts one session per turn across repeated working/done cycles; closes an open session when its pane is torn down; bounds the mirror and closes what it evicts; stops the session when the main agent settles and only a watch loop holds the row working; keeps the session open while a subagent outlives the main agent, and closes it when the child settles; dates the stop by the evidence when a shell outlives the last subagent; opens a new session dated by the observation when the main agent resumes after monitoring; never dates a reopen before the close a fact-less OSC repaint caused; dates the first live row after a restored one by the evidence, not the restored clock; treats an unchanged answer as a snapshot, never a transition; opens only on a live working edge; closes only a session it opened. src/main/text-generation/commit-message-text-generation-model-discovery.test.ts: returns static catalog models without spawning for static agents; discovers dynamic models through the agent CLI; discovers dynamic models through the configured agent command override; falls back to static models when dynamic discovery returns no parseable models; falls back to the first discovered non-Pi model when its static default is unavailable. src/main/text-generation/pull-request-context.test.ts: does not fetch unrelated fork remotes before generating PR context; bounds exact remote-ref probe concurrency for a large remote list; reports no branch change because PR context preparation is read-only; keeps a remote-qualified base when the selected base includes the remote. src/main/text-generation/source-control-local-process.test.ts: asks the supervisor to stop and leaves its group to it; signals nothing once the supervisor has exited; stops an agent that ignores its stdin end through its supervisor. src/main/updater/linux-package/linux-package-update-recovery.test.ts: retains the downloaded package with the digest from the event metadata; requires a string downloaded path; accepts an uppercase extension; requires a non-empty string version; matches an absolute file URL by basename; accepts duplicate entries that agree on the digest; refuses an entry with a missing or non-string digest; refuses a digest that is not base64 at all; refuses a malformed percent-encoded URL; refuses a missing or non-array file list; tolerates a non-object event; replaces the retained artifact with a newer download; keeps the retained artifact when a new download has no usable digest; keeps the retained artifact when an unrelated download event arrives; clears the retained artifact; preserves the artifact across a recheck of the same version; clears the artifact when another version takes over; preserves the artifact for an unknown or empty version; is a no-op without a retained artifact; returns the built command and package file name for a verified package; reports missing without a retained artifact; propagates a package-manager discovery failure; rejects a well-formed digest that belongs to another file; never hashes a package that a malformed digest failed to arm; rejects a path outside the cache root; rejects the cache root itself; rejects a package in the updater directory itself; rejects a pending directory that is a symlink out of the cache; performs one hash pass for concurrent requests; revalidates once the in-flight pass settles; does not reuse an in-flight pass for a different artifact; starts a fresh proof when the same package is captured again; returns the verified package path; returns missing without a retained artifact. src/main/updater/releases/updater-prerelease-feed-readiness.test.ts: accepts a GitHub %s asset redirect as ready; reports a GitHub asset request error as unavailable; reports not-ready with a verified last-good tag when the newest assets are unavailable; does not classify a non-positive tag limit as feed unavailability; reproduces the v1.4.142 publishing incident as not-ready; reports transport failures as unavailable instead of not-ready; treats an explicit asset 404 as not-ready when another asset is unavailable; accepts absolute manifest asset URLs without rewriting them to release asset paths; returns not-ready with an older ready update as last-good while newest is publishing. src/main/updater/releases/updater-release-builds.test.ts: lists hourly builds from the dedicated repo, newest first; lists daily builds from the dedicated repo, newest first; separates stable from rc in the shared main repo; skips drafts and unparseable tags; keeps a composed release title and drops one that repeats the tag; hides builds that published no artifact for this platform; returns an empty list when no build has this platform artifact; keeps mac builds visible on macOS regardless of the Windows leg; resolves the platform installer download url; leaves the installer url null when the release published no installer; tolerates a release whose assets are missing or malformed; sends the local gh token as a bearer header when one is available; sends no authorization header when gh has no token; retries unauthenticated once when GitHub rejects the token; does not retry a 401 that was already unauthenticated; falls back to the per-IP bucket when the token is rate limited and tells the gh breaker; reports a secondary limit carrying retry-after without retrying or tripping the breaker; records a primary limit in the token scope %s; keeps %s authenticated when only %s is blocked; skips the token while its scope %s is blocked; surfaces a rate limit with its reset time and a sign-in hint when unauthenticated; omits the sign-in hint when the rate-limited request was authenticated; treats 429 as a rate limit; reports a 403 without rate-limit headers as a plain HTTP error; reports a missing hourly repo distinctly; is null when GitHub sent no reset; prefers retry-after over the primary reset epoch; falls back to the primary reset epoch when there is no retry-after; reads retry-after as seconds; reads retry-after as an HTTP date; pins an hourly tag at the hourly repo download path; pins a daily tag at the daily repo download path; pins a stable tag at the main repo download path; rejects a tag that is not a version. src/main/updater/updater.build-channel-selection.test.ts: uses the display label in the unsupported-platform %s pinned-build error; still pins %s from an unsigned Windows dev build; restores ordinary release checks after local build selection fails; opts into the RC channel when checkForUpdatesFromMenu is called with includePrerelease; pins the generic feed to a perf-tagged prerelease when requested; surfaces no-update feedback when no newer perf-tagged prerelease exists; keeps prerelease publishing-window misses on the generic retry path; leaves the feed URL alone for a normal user-initiated check. src/main/updater/updater.check-preflight.test.ts: ignores a stale update-not-available event after a new check starts preflight; deduplicates repeated manual checks while the immediate checking status is active. src/main/updater/updater.prerelease-fallback.test.ts: retries a prerelease check once against the previous feed tag when the manifest is missing; surfaces a promise-only prerelease fallback failure after the primary error event. src/main/updater/updater.publishing-window-feed.test.ts: repins the generic feed to the newest RC tag for a prerelease user; repins the generic feed to a newer stable tag for a prerelease user; pins a stable fallback when Atom has no newer prerelease; uses last-good concrete feed when a user-initiated check lands during publishing; can offer an older fully published update while the newest release is publishing; keeps background publishing-window fallback on the short retry cadence. src/main/updater/updater.quit-and-install.test.ts: surfaces an accepted retry before electron-updater emits download progress; defers quitAndInstall and runs its launcher within the launch PATH scope; runs pre-quit cleanup before local PTY cleanup during update install; keeps optional pre-quit cleanup fail-and-continue behavior by default; ignores duplicate quitAndInstall requests while the shared delay is pending; arms the forced-exit watchdog once the install commits; disarms the forced-exit watchdog when sync install error recovery keeps the app open. src/main/window/createMainWindow-markdown-editor-focus.test.ts: ignores traffic light sync IPC on non-macOS; still intercepts Cmd+Shift+B and Cmd+Alt+B when the markdown editor is focused; coerces non-boolean setMarkdownEditorFocused payloads to false; opens a table-aware context menu synchronously without a renderer query; builds the plain edit menu for the one right-click the renderer marks as plain text. src/main/window/createMainWindow-renderer-crash-recovery.test.ts: notifies the caller when the renderer process is gone; passes the renderer webContents id through crash recording and recovery callbacks; forwards expected renderer teardowns so the recorder can diagnose suppression; reloads the app shell after an unexpected renderer process loss; does not reload after renderer loss when recovery is disabled; stops auto-reloading after a rapid renderer crash loop trips the breaker. src/main/window/dashboard-popout-window.test.ts: updates the title after language initialization and