untime is WSL %s; sweeps a local repo: %s; probes an SSH row that carries only executionHostId on its own host; keeps same-path rows on two different SSH hosts from sharing one backoff; coalesces concurrent probes for the same repo location; caches no-identity probes briefly so list calls do not retry every time; does not rewrite the no-remote marker on a later retry; resolves a settled no-remote repo once it gains a remote; does not re-probe a resolved identity before the refresh window elapses; re-probes a resolved identity after the refresh window elapses; bounds re-probes per sweep so a large repo list drains gradually; forgets a removed repo location so its deadline cannot outlive the repo; keeps a surviving repo backoff when a sibling repo is removed; probes again when the same location is re-added after its probe was retired; coalesces concurrent sweeps instead of running one pass per list call. src/main/workspaces/creation/preparation/worktree-create-preparation.test.ts: preserves create priority through claim probes on %s; starts the checkout only once the async workspace root resolves; still deduplicates when both callers await the same pending root lookup; namespaces native Windows preparation directories for long paths; deduplicates preparation for the same repo, base, runtime, and workspace root; does not spend a divergence walk when the base matches exactly; claims when the two sides spell the same ref differently; evicts a repo's own stale preparation before another repo's; still discards armed checkouts when the project runtime needs repair; routes preparation and finalization through the selected WSL runtime; retries stale cleanup after a transient listing failure; does not discard a detached worktree with caller-controlled preparation metadata; does not re-arm after an isolated create; re-arms a preparation once creates arrive in a burst; holds the re-arm checkout until the create runs the deferred thunk; starts one explicit prefetch after the create completes; does not re-arm when finalization failed; reports a pending create while a stale-cleanup scan is running. src/main/workspaces/removal/local-worktree-removal-recovery.test.ts: recovers Git for Windows partial filesystem deletion failures; finishes a clean non-force deletion after Git leaves a Windows directory behind; recovers localized Windows failures after Git already removed the registration; does not recover unrelated localized failures while Git still owns the row; finishes a macOS deletion Git deregistered before failing with Directory not empty; leaves an orphaned checkout to the orphan cleanup instead of deleting it; prunes and strictly verifies on the selected WSL host without deleting files or branches. src/main/workspaces/removal/worktree-removal-safety.test.ts: rejects deleting a worktree that contains another registered worktree; rejects POSIX home directories even when host homedir has a different path shape; refuses a home the host reported even when no path rule recognises it; refuses the Windows host's home directory from a POSIX client; refuses the Windows host's home directory even when the host reported nothing. src/main/wsl/discovery/distro-catalog.test.ts: retries asynchronous discovery after a transient wsl.exe failure; retries synchronous discovery after a transient wsl.exe failure; retries asynchronous discovery after wsl.exe reports no distros yet; retries synchronous discovery after wsl.exe reports no distros yet; bounds the wsl.exe spawn rate while no distros are installed; bounds the asynchronous spawn rate while no distros are installed; still caches a non-empty distro list for the process lifetime; re-probes a docker-desktop-only machine once a user distro can appear; backs off while the list keeps coming back empty; backs off after repeated distro-list failures; caps the empty-list backoff at five minutes; keeps reporting an empty result after it goes stale; keeps reporting a known distro list indefinitely; bounds cached