        "Audit2095 current-parent preparation2126 (approved2092/2093 removals; source refresh2109/independent2112): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-sleep-and-teardown-part-03.spec.ts: rejects exact terminal stop for multiple expected PTYs before stopping anything; omits stale renderer leaves when fresh PTY liveness is required; omits unbound renderer placeholders when fresh PTY liveness is required; captures the event method before the nested sleep receipt changes it; returns the close receipt without requiring a PTY stop; uses the same stop result as an empty explicit stop. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-creation-and-orchestration-part-04.spec.ts: builds a compact worktree summary from persisted and live runtime state; reads the linked-PR state from the renderer repoId-keyed GitHub cache; carries persisted worktree host ownership in mobile summaries; emits only instance- and boundary-validated lineage parents in mobile summaries; resolves WSL platforms only for repos represented in mobile summaries; omits worktrees hidden by the host visibility policy from mobile summaries; applies linked-checkout source visibility to mobile summaries. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/hooks-and-hosted-review-part-02.spec.ts: routes runtime GitHub PR details and actions through the selected WSL project runtime; passes SSH connection context through hosted review creation flows; routes local WSL project hosted review flows through runtime git options; treats SSH worktree drift as unknown without local git probes. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-listing.spec.ts: emits one mobile session terminal tab per live PTY even if two tabs resolve to it; resolves projected split authority from the parent layout PTY binding; keeps explicit-id terminal lists from resolving all worktrees; keeps explicit-id cold-cache terminal lists from classifying unrelated same-repo worktrees; keeps unknown bare terminal-list ids on the no-scan exact-id path; matches explicit-id cwd PTYs for folder workspace instance IDs; routes PTY output through the PTY leaf index in large terminal graphs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts: claims the first window as authoritative and ignores later windows; transfers authority from the headless sentinel to the first real window; relays terminal browser launches only while headless owns the graph; marks live headless PTYs for renderer reattach before desktop promotion; reports the activation gate state while no desktop window is available; bumps the epoch and enters reloading when the authoritative window reloads; can mark the graph ready for the authoritative window; drops back to unavailable and clears authority when the window disappears; hands the graph back to headless when a promoted serve window closes (#27292); keeps a crashed promoted serve renderer on its own window while the window is open; stays unavailable during initial loads before a graph is published. src/main/runtime/orchestration/mailbox/routing/orchestration-mailbox-routing-races.spec.ts: stops paged routing when the check is cancelled; keeps an unfiltered redrive unrestricted when reservations merge; keeps an unfiltered parked delivery unrestricted when reservations merge; uses a bounded indexed pane lookup for reminted Dispatch identity. src/main/runtime/workspaces/removal/worktree-teardown-unstopped-pty.test.ts: removes the reported wedged automation workspace without --force; clears PTY state once a failed stop is proven to have exited; names only the PTYs that are actually live, not every failed stop; warns with the specific sweep failure, not the generic deadline; still fails closed on a sweep-level failure without force. src/main/skills/bundled-skill-install/layouts.test.ts: links into a project only where its agent folder already exists; reads a pending cloud transaction as busy and a cloud receipt as another skill. src/main/skills/skill-upload-session-service.test.ts: joins concurrent disposal callers through exact cleanup completion. src/main/source-control/hosted-review-creation.test.ts: creates the pull request after fresh main-process validation passes; routes local WSL git and GitHub review creation through the selected runtime; creates a pull request on a GitHub Enterprise Server remote (#8312); creates a GitLab merge request after fresh main-process validation passes; creates an Azure DevOps pull request after fresh main-process validation passes; creates a Gitea pull request after fresh main-process validation passes. src/main/source-control/hosted-review-execution-host-routing.test.ts: reads a GitHub review on the SSH host a row names only in executionHostId; reads a GitLab review on the executionHostId host when connectionId names a different one; does not dial this client for a runtime row whose nested target shares a local name; keeps a runtime row with no nested target on this process (self-addressed stamp); keeps a legacy connectionId-only SSH row on its target; does not share a cached answer between two rows at one path on different hosts; creates a Bitbucket review locally for a runtime row rather than dialing its nested target; reports creation eligibility from the executionHostId-only SSH host; resolves the GitHub slug for a repo listing on the row it is asked about; refuses to dial a runtime host from this process; answers with the SSH target for both spellings and local otherwise; reads a runtime stamp on a row in this store as self-addressing, not a second machine. src/main/source-control/hosted-review-inflight-invalidation.test.ts: keeps other hosts, paths and their pending promises isolated. src/main/speech/model-manager.test.ts: requires pinned, internally consistent metadata for every model file; verifies downloaded model file hashes before installation; rejects non-HTTPS model downloads; marks OpenAI transcription models ready only when an API key is configured. src/main/ssh/connection/ssh-connection-sftp-namespace.test.ts: writes to the SFTP namespace path discovered on the same session; uploads the bundle into the SFTP namespace directory; issues no discovery requests when the caller supplies no mapping; ignores a mapping on a Windows host; never resolves on the system-SSH transport; leaves writeBuffer and openFileUploadSession on the shell path; keeps the shell path when discovery is inconclusive; preserves a session-limit channel-open error unchanged. src/main/ssh/connection/ssh-connection-system-transport.test.ts: uses system SSH transport when ProxyUseFdpass is resolved by OpenSSH; allows concurrent exec commands for system SSH with an Orca ControlMaster socket; keeps concurrent exec commands disabled for system SSH without a reusable socket; uses system SSH transport for ProxyCommand targets before ssh2 auth; keeps the original ssh2 reachability error when the system SSH probe fails; reports the system SSH failure when ssh2 cannot negotiate with the host; uses system transport for target or resolved OpenSSH proxy directives; allows an environment override for e2e coverage; ignores stale imported proxy fields when fresh OpenSSH config has no proxy. src/main/ssh/orcad-migration-catalog-client.test.ts: keeps each server project’s execution host, so a nested SSH row is never read as local; reads the server’s folder workspaces and the groups that place them on a host; sends and validates the %s operation; validates an abort result without letting it erase committed state; validates a committed receipt against the requested manifest; rejects malformed stage timestamps and abort envelopes; fails closed for method absence, malformed identity, and invalid pairing; refuses a destination without the capability before sending any migration request; reads method-not-found as the same refusal, not as a lost answer. src/main/ssh/runtime-ssh-access.test.ts: persists intent then claim before connecting and publishes redacted authenticated access; names the saved dependency when dependent state blocks an SSH access link; handles lost link responses without connecting or verifying again; invalidates old transport only after authenticated access is published; rejects changed request tuple after a completed link; rejects provisioning and missing durable generations without connecting; treats a lost successful unlink response as an idempotent no-op; hashes connection identity, not display state or owner; strictly validates ports and request IDs. src/main/startup/cli-launch-redirect.test.ts: detects a launch that received the unpacked CLI entrypoint; ignores normal desktop launches; ignores the entrypoint when it is only the executable itself (argv[0]); applies on Linux too; strips injected Chromium switches before node-mode CLI arguments; keeps user flags after the command and malformed boolean assignments; does not treat a later positional entrypoint path as the launcher; redirects a direct binary launch with no AppImage env at all; strips Chromium switches node mode would reject; preserves desktop-shaped switches after the command; leaves direct serve in-process but redirects its help; treats help as a CLI launch even without a command; treats %s as a CLI launch even without a command; does not treat a value of %s as a CLI early-exit flag; does not treat a serve option value as a help request; does not reinterpret help after the argument terminator; leaves a plain desktop launch alone; skips flag values when looking for the command positional; preserves a project selector in %j; does not apply the command form on macOS or Windows; never redirects an unpackaged build; runs the in-package CLI in Electron node mode with sanitized env; refuses to redirect twice so a dropped ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE cannot loop; reports a missing CLI entrypoint instead of booting the desktop app; execs a direct serve into the CLI so it keeps its pid and honours profile and supervise; keeps ORCA_USER_DATA_PATH for a direct serve without --user-data-dir; serves in-process when this runtime cannot exec or the exec fails; never execs the --serve child the CLI itself spawns, or serve on other platforms; surfaces a spawn failure as a non-zero exit; re-execs a direct --serve onto X11 when Electron resolved Wayland; leaves $name alone. src/main/startup/main-process-runtime-launch-activation.test.ts: marks startup settled for the launch record only after the window has loaded and settled; loads SSH targets on a windowless serve before paired clients can connect (#25886); pins the serve listener to loopback only for orcad browser sidecars (sidecar=$sidecar, #31895); saves Codex auth before a headless serve update restart, like the desktop does. src/main/startup/run-electron-vite-dev.test.ts: forwards dev instance identity to electron-vite; prepares userData orca and orca-dev wrappers for dev terminals; consumes the stable-name flag before forwarding args to electron-vite. src/main/updater/releases/updater-prerelease-feed.test.ts: returns the newest stable tag when the user is on an RC and a newer stable exists; returns the newest RC tag when no stable is newer than the current RC; can exclude prerelease tags for stable-channel checks; probes the %s %s platform manifest; returns null for stable-channel checks when only prereleases are newer; returns null when nothing in the feed is newer than the current version; ignores entries with unparseable tags; returns null when the fetch is not ok; returns null when the fetch throws; picks semver-newest across a mixed-order feed; ignores perf-tagged prereleases for regular RC checks; reports no RC update when only perf-tagged prereleases are newer; picks the semver-newest perf-tagged prerelease; matches only literal rc.N.perf prerelease tags for perf checks; reports no perf update instead of falling back to stable or RC tags; returns a bounded fallback candidate after the newest newer tag; returns null when the only newer tag has a manifest but its asset still 404s; requires a known old timestamp for a stable-fallback tag. src/main/updater/updater-events.test.ts: hands the whole downloaded event to artifact capture; publishes manual-install recovery after a %s download; publishes the normal downloaded state for AppImage builds; blocks downloaded-state handling when the packaged marker is unusable; passes the actual updater error into the install-failure handler; keeps manual-install recovery when a later check finds only the installed release; drops the artifact when another version takes over the cycle; ignores a downloaded event for an older target; accepts a matching event when the pending cache target was cleared; drops the artifact when progress reports a different pending version. src/main/updater/updater-linux-package-recovery-actions.test.ts: rejects both actions while no package-install recovery is active; validates the retained package on every invocation; restores recovery after a recheck resolves without a terminal event; restores recovery after a recheck fails; restores recovery when a pinned check resolves to the current version; restores recovery when resolving a pinned check fails; clears recovery for both actions once the package is gone; resolves %s as a result and keeps the card usable instead of rejecting; keeps recovery available after a transient read failure. src/main/updater/updater.check-settlement.test.ts: leaves a dismissed release update on the release source; surfaces net::ERR_FAILED to user-initiated checks with a friendly message; shows checking immediately for a user-initiated check while feed pinning is pending; keeps background checks event-driven before checking-for-update fires. src/main/usage/usage-provider-store-lifecycle.test.ts: persists identities for a whole first scan with one write; skips disabled and fresh matching states; invalidates prior sources on fingerprint changes and reuses them for forced scans. src/main/window/createMainWindow-close-confirmation.test.ts: clears the quit latch when the renderer prevents unload; does not notify the crash recorder when renderer teardown follows a confirmed window close; allows close when Electron reports a crashed webContents; requests confirmation for a hung-but-alive renderer instead of bypassing. src/main/workspaces/catalog/worktree-identity-persistence.test.ts: stores independent metadata for colliding locators on two hosts; projects canonical-only metadata for exactly one host; keeps canonical metadata current for legacy writers on a known owner; removes only the selected legacy-owner metadata when locators collide; keeps the canonical identity stable when the locator changes; leaves other hosts at the old locator when one host renames its folder. src/main/wsl/filesystem/wsl-drive-unc-conversion-startup.test.ts: leaves a journaled conversion untouched with the gate closed, %s. src/main/wsl/orcad/wsl-orcad-deploy.test.ts: holds the distro before it deploys and launches, and reports what C5 dials; passes its connect-state read (%s) on as hints; applies the SSH census and downgrade admission to the first deploy; refuses a WSL 1 distro before holding it or touching its files; tells an unregistered distro how to find the installed ones, before holding anything; surfaces an unsupported libc as the SSH host refusal does; starts an already-active slot the distro stop ended, instead of reporting it ready; deploys over an adopted unrecorded orcad under the SSH terminal gate, never a fresh launch; reports the adopted instance once the same version is serving; returns a deferral rather than launching over live terminals; hands a failed first deploy to the fresh-install cleanup before reporting it. src/main/zcode/zcode-v2-plan-credentials.test.ts: prefers migrated credentials over a stale legacy account; keeps legacy support when no personal v2 file exists; honors the upstream personal config override independently of the credential directory; does not borrow credentials from another execution host; preserves the protected Orca key priority even if v2 is corrupt; rejects upstream-invalid selection %j without legacy fallback; accepts a valid optional reasoning level; rejects upstream-invalid rule containers %j without legacy fallback; accepts a valid selected-provider empty personal rule and smart model rule; cannot establish selected credentials from %s rules; leaves encrypted CLI files unchanged across repeated account reads. tests/e2e/automation-terminal-launch.unit.test.ts: launches explicit Chat for %s through the common entry and keeps its actual fallback; does not apply stored Terminal extras to Chat; forwards only complete Chat-consumed values, with no Terminal startup base; refuses an expired admission without minting another launch identity; records the actual chat identity and delegates new workspace setup and provenance. tests/e2e/github-project-provider-columns.unit.test.ts: renders %s through one bounded items request on a named cloud host; preserves zero and complete counters: %j; preserves populated and legacy rows through shared sorting, grouping and cells. tests/e2e/structured-agent-session-launch-continuation.unit.test.ts: carries renderer lifetime through host intent to the real %s provider builders. tests/e2e/terminal-account-restart.unit.test.ts: replaces a tombstoned owner while its persisted pane binding has not yet been cleared; paired restart retains the old owner (host authority: %s). tests/e2e/terminal-hidden-view-parking.spec.ts: does not park excluded tabs; reproduces a static frame byte-for-byte across 25 park/reveal cycles. tests/e2e/terminal-long-table-scroll-restore.spec.ts: reproduces long markdown table artifacts after workspace switch and scroll; keeps narrow wrapped signer markdown table coherent after restore and scroll; keeps real emoji markdown table right edge clean after restore and scroll. tests/e2e/terminal-long-table-fixtures.ts: dedicated zero-case helper retirement; no authored test credit. tests/e2e/terminal-paste-