        "Audit1939 (sources1934/1935): Pruned cold-parking hook and parked-watcher suites retain local timer/selection/split and exit/cancel/disposal progression. Lose supplied capability/eligibility/topology/admission and duplicate state examples recorded below. No assertion objects map to these sources here; preserve independent actual E2E receipt scopes without transferring their results to reduced units. Preserve meaningful remaining selectors/assertions and unchanged dated receipts within their original scope. Reduced selectors have no fresh gate execution evidence in this metadata packet. No equivalent replacement, physical watcher/PTY/provider, live SSH/remote/mobile, rendered, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget result is claimed. Exact retired authored alarms: 'parks paired-runtime tabs only when their exact host advertises restore'; 'skips parking scans for capability-equivalent status writes and scans membership changes'; 'keeps eviction-exempt tabs mounted when the worktree is force-parked'; 'resolves eviction exemptions once per force-park input change'; 'does not exempt a tab from a truncated malformed pane key'; 'never starts a watcher for a PTY that exited into the park handoff gap'; 'collapses the exited leaf out of the stored layout when deferring'; 'retires launch/title hints when the launch-owning parked leaf exits'; 'keeps launch ownership when only a parked shell sibling exits'; 'rejects ordinary parking for a preserved daemon with a lossy snapshot'; 'rejects a capture containing a PTY without snapshot backing'; 'accepts layout-derived candidates when the capture is stale'; 'rejects layout-derived candidates missing a leaf PTY binding'.",
