    {
      "id": "agent-browser.owner-boundary-cleanup",
      "title": "Headless browser helpers retire with their owning page and runtime",
      "maturity": "experimental",
      "protection": "none",
      "owner": "browser-runtime",
      "layer": "electron-main-headless-browser-lifecycle",
      "surfaces": [
        "headless offscreen browser page close",
        "offscreen renderer destruction",
        "app quit",
        "headless serve SIGINT/SIGTERM"
      ],
      "platforms": ["macos", "linux", "windows"],
      "providers": ["local", "remote-runtime", "ssh", "wsl"],
      "coveredPlatforms": [],
      "coveredProviders": [],
      "coverageNotes": "Audit2043: Remove the imported allowlist inventory examples described in the historical account below. This gate already has no active commands, testFiles, assertionRefs or evidenceRuns and protection remains none. No replacement coverage or fresh execution is claimed. Historical prior account (preserved verbatim): Audit1556 removes the whole mocked helper session lifecycle suite and reduces offscreen lifecycle and tab-routing suites. Mock helper argv/route/concurrency, private active state, explicit unregister ordering, standalone renderer-destroy notification and debugger-detach alarms are retired without equivalent replacement. Remaining offscreen cases prove same-ID replacement preservation and shutdown joining pending retirement against injected windows/manager/helper dependencies. The retained tab-routing case proves snapshot-reference provenance against injected helper replies. Reduced reliability commands have no fresh cohort/native receipt; this batch ran its ten retained authored cases plus two unchanged imported allowlist cases only. Historical pre-audit scope: The owner-boundary contract injects an isolated BrowserManager, offscreen WebContents, and AgentBrowserBridge. It proves explicit close removes the page from command routing before awaiting exact named-session retirement, runs retirement on unexpected renderer destruction, preserves unrelated pages, joins pending creation/retirement during shutdown, rejects command admission after terminal cleanup begins, retries Electron quit after a vetoed signal, preserves Windows shared-console graceful Ctrl-C, reserves the full renderer-acknowledgement and committed-teardown budgets before supervisor force-kill, bounds process-swap retirement to five seconds, and caps cleanup concurrency at four. A built-CLI macOS headless serve run used an isolated profile, folder workspace, socket directory, and port: exact PPID-1 helper/session identity disappeared within five seconds after page close and after Ctrl-C runtime shutdown, while an unrelated page survived close and reconnect. Linux cgroup and paired/SSH journeys remain gaps. Audit1379 changes src/main/browser/cdp/snapshots/snapshot-engine-iframe-sessions.test.ts (3 authored registrations removed; 0 retained); src/main/browser/client-hosts/file-transfers/browser-client-download-routing.test.ts (3 authored registrations removed; 4 retained). Intentional losses: Loses ref/string/Map.get-count projections; no real browser operation. Intentionally removes 3 authored registrations: 'cancels a client-hosted download whose owner cannot be resolved'; 'leaves ordinary browser guests on their desktop Downloads path'; 'stops routing to a composition once it starts closing'. Retained focused cases are not claimed as equivalent replacement for these losses. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact primary-selector receipts and primary claims remain scoped to their unchanged sources; the broad optional selector has no new execution result. Audit1383: src/main/browser/guest-lifecycle/browser-guest-devtools-dock.test.ts reduced. Lose capture failure baseline and destroyed-host callback control. Fake Electron view models native lifecycle and custody; no native rendering/visible focus claimed. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. Existing exact unaffected receipts and their platform/provider/budget claims remain scoped to unchanged selectors. Changed optional selectors have no new execution result. Audit1390: src/main/browser/agent-browser/agent-browser-action-effects.test.ts reduced. No standalone baseline snapshot call-count alarm. src/main/browser/routing/partitions/browser-route-partition-stability.test.ts removed. Standalone assembled partition stability/separation/binding-count alarms across runtime/SSH/WSL/environment identity removed. No real browser cookie/session continuity or replacement equivalence is claimed. src/main/browser/element-grab/browser-grab-payload.test.ts reduced. Standalone annotation clamp/list-count/default preservation characterization removed. src/main/browser/cdp/input/guest-focused-frame-route.test.ts reduced. Attach-call count, default widget fallback and claimed detach-forgetting alarm removed; no actual Chromium frame/input delivery claimed. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. The existing primary-selector receipt and its claims remain scoped to their unchanged sources; the broad optional command has no new execution result. Audit1396: src/main/browser/network/egress/browser-route-webrtc-egress.electron.test.ts removed. Deletes entire one-registration native Electron baseline/protected UDP probe, including fixture shell and packet observer. No equivalent actual network egress proof is claimed; actual Orca policy owner reviewed separately. src/main/browser/cdp/screencast/browser-screencast-live-frame-allocation.test.ts reduced. Retires captured PNG/JPEG twelve-frame digest/metadata/ack replay bundled with zero copied-byte instrumentation; surviving retry ownership witness is not claimed equivalent format or sequence coverage. src/main/browser/extensions/context-menus/browser-extension-context-menu-model.test.ts reduced. Toolbar-context constant membership, wrapper submenu structure and click-data property projection no longer independently asserted. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. The existing primary-selector receipt and its claims remain scoped to their unchanged sources; the broad optional command has no new execution result. Audit1400: src/main/browser/cookies/sources/browser-cookie-source-partition.test.ts reduced. Lose standalone true identity projections, default-schema/unpartitioned examples and repeated raw flag/object type rejection alarms; retained cases are not claimed equivalent coverage. src/main/browser/routing/partitions/browser-route-partition-storage-runtime.test.ts reduced. Lose callback error propagation/no-clear alarm; file-backed pending queue and production lifecycle remain exercised. src/main/browser/client-hosts/file-transfers/browser-client-download-relay.test.ts reduced. Lose standalone successful destination projection and first/final offset expectations; no replacement delivery proof claimed. src/main/browser/cdp/screencast/browser-screencast-guest-view-limit.test.ts reduced. Lose the direct 320x240 floor example; modeled CDP frames do not prove native compositor pixels. src/main/browser/identity/browser-identity-mode-store.test.ts reduced. Lose basic last-assignment-wins example; no asynchronous write race is exercised. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. The existing primary-selector receipt and its claims remain scoped to their unchanged sources; the broad optional command has no new execution result. Audit1401: src/main/browser/client-hosts/file-transfers/browser-client-file-channel-negotiation.test.ts removed. Loses file-channel negotiation refusal at the schema parse boundary; no replacement asserted. src/main/browser/client-pages/lifecycle/browser-client-page-inventory.test.ts reduced. Loses deterministic equal-length URL compaction tie-breaking and reversed-input invariance alarm. src/main/browser/client-hosts/file-transfers/browser-client-upload-command.test.ts removed. Loses original upload-error priority when cleanup also fails and staging-release alarm. src/main/browser/extensions/installation/browser-extension-install-store.test.ts reduced. Loses install-directory path escape refusal alarm from the unpinned exception case. src/main/browser/routing/local-host-partitions/wsl-host-browser-jar-identity.test.ts removed. Loses WSL deploy/rename/reimport cookie-jar identity helper alarms without actual page/storage attachment. src/main/browser/client-hosts/lifecycle/paired-runtime-browser-client-host-identity-wiring.test.ts removed. Loses profile-stable versus profile-isolated host identity composition alarms. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. The existing primary-selector receipt and its claims remain scoped to their unchanged sources; the broad optional command has no new execution result. Audit1412: src/main/browser/extensions/native-messaging/browser-extension-native-host-process-backpressure.test.ts reduced. Loses synchronous host/global queue refusal, frame encoding and UTF8/body bounds at fake stdin, largest-stalled-host eviction/accounting, capacity completion and shutdown claim release alarms. The retained final-reply case does not establish outgoing pressure behavior. src/main/browser/cdp/input/browser-element-functions.test.ts removed. Loses independently fixed disabled/read-only/element-kind guard messages, number sanitization rollback, spinbutton targeting, focus hijack/replacement rejection, composed input event order and upload/selection behavior in happy-dom. No equivalent browser coverage is claimed. src/main/browser/extensions/permissions/browser-extension-settings-prompt-lifetime.test.ts reduced. Loses accepted-install continuation through renderer navigation while loading. The kept cancelled/retry path does not validate that exact ownership window. src/main/browser/cookies/client-route/browser-client-route-cookie-import.test.ts reduced. Loses no-route delegation/picker, failed-import source badge, compatible runtime-id success and manual/import destination argument wiring alarms. Retained refusal results do not prove cookie import or stored source updates. src/main/browser/guest-lifecycle/manager/browser-manager-guest-policy-profile.test.ts removed. Loses workspace-document in-grant navigation/popup refusal, cleanup/re-attach, cross-registry guest authorization and browsing-map separation alarms. No equivalent browser policy coverage is claimed. No equivalent replacement coverage is claimed. The existing primary-selector receipt and its claims remain scoped to their unchanged sources; the broad optional command has no new execution result.",
      "motivatingLinks": [
        "https://linear.app/stably/issue/STA-5400",
        "https://github.com/stablyai/orca/issues/16367"
      ],
      "invariant": "For each Orca-owned page identity, after its owner closes or is destroyed and a five-second third-party shutdown grace expires, no live helper session named orca-tab-<pageId> may remain; unrelated live page identities must survive, and runtime quit must join the bounded cleanup attempt. The serve supervisor may force-kill only after the renderer-acknowledgement deadline, committed teardown deadline, and bounded scheduling margin have all elapsed.",
      "oracle": "Create two isolated offscreen pages and register their WebContents. Close one, block onPageClosed for its stable page ID, and require unregisterGuest to have already removed that page from command routing while the unrelated page remains live. Emit destroyed and require the same exact retirement. Race shutdown with creation, pending retirement, and process-swap destruction; require no replacement session or command after terminal cleanup starts, require shutdown to remain pending until retirement settles, require the swap close command to use the five-second cleanup timeout, and require at most four concurrent close commands. Deliver repeated signals and require every attempt to reach Electron quit; under Windows shared-console semantics require the child to handle Ctrl-C without an immediate child.kill. Advance the supervisor clock through the renderer-acknowledgement and committed teardown deadlines and require no SIGKILL until the bounded scheduling margin elapses. In direct built-CLI serve, inspect exact session/PID/socket identity plus RSS/fd inventory before close and after a five-second grace; reconnect between commands and stop via Ctrl-C. No process-name kill or global sweep is permitted.",
      "commands": [],
      "testFiles": [],
      "assertionRefs": [],
      "evidenceRuns": [],
      "runtimeBudget": {
        "p95Seconds": 2,
        "scope": "bounded offscreen lifecycle contracts and bridge cleanup ordering"
      },
      "flakeHistory": {
        "status": "not-started",
        "evidence": "Fresh deterministic coverage has local candidate evidence only."
      },
      "redGreenEvidence": {
        "status": "complete",
        "evidence": "The pristine current-main control failed explicit close, unexpected destruction, backend shutdown, pending creation, bounded concurrency, joined quit, and repeated-signal assertions; the candidate passed the byte-identical oracle. Disabling only process-swap cleanup timeout and terminal command admission failed 3 of 15 bridge lifecycle tests. Live candidate-with-signal-fix-disabled also retained exact helpers after Ctrl-C, while the final candidate removed them."
      },
      "performanceBudget": {
        "required": true,
        "evidence": "Cleanup is event-driven and exact-page scoped: no polling, process-name scan, idle timer, or new wire field. Owner and residual session drains cap close subprocess concurrency at four, sequence headless ownership cleanup before the residual bridge sweep, and reuse the existing bounded app teardown deadline."
      },
      "promotionCriteria": [
        "Run the same oracle on Linux headless serve with bundled agent-browser PID/session and RSS/fd inventory.",
        "Exercise runtime restart, transport loss, reconnect, concurrent tabs, and paired/SSH host ownership without cross-page cleanup.",
        "Collect repeated open/close/reconnect evidence showing bounded helper count and no stale PID-1-owned Orca identities."
      ],
