eight-windows-regular.test.ts, tests/e2e/claude-agent-row-view.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/cross-version-wire/agent-permission-legacy-spawn.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/paired-instant-browser-tab.spec.ts, tests/e2e/session-tabs-decorative-title-fanout.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/session-tabs/mobile-session-active-performance.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/session-tabs/mobile-session-active-publication.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/structured-agent-session-launch-admission.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/structured-attention-prompt-relay.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/structured-attention-read-retirement.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/structured-chat-tab-lifetime-cost.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/structured-session-workspace-authority.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-agent-pane-launch.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-parked-memory.spec.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-shortcuts.spec.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency.spec.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-phases.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-main-probe.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-artifact.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-split-activation-latency-report.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-tab-switch-visual-restore.spec.ts, tests/e2e/web-runtime-session-terminal-host-authority.unit.test.ts. Unresolved local/computed edges remain explicit debt.",
        "Audit2095 current-parent preparation2126 (approved2092/2093 removals; source refresh2109/independent2112): Intentionally retire these low-value alarms without replacement: src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-sleep-and-teardown-part-03.spec.ts: rejects exact terminal stop for multiple expected PTYs before stopping anything; omits stale renderer leaves when fresh PTY liveness is required; omits unbound renderer placeholders when fresh PTY liveness is required; captures the event method before the nested sleep receipt changes it; returns the close receipt without requiring a PTY stop; uses the same stop result as an empty explicit stop. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-creation-and-orchestration-part-04.spec.ts: builds a compact worktree summary from persisted and live runtime state; reads the linked-PR state from the renderer repoId-keyed GitHub cache; carries persisted worktree host ownership in mobile summaries; emits only instance- and boundary-validated lineage parents in mobile summaries; resolves WSL platforms only for repos represented in mobile summaries; omits worktrees hidden by the host visibility policy from mobile summaries; applies linked-checkout source visibility to mobile summaries. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/hooks-and-hosted-review-part-02.spec.ts: routes runtime GitHub PR details and actions through the selected WSL project runtime; passes SSH connection context through hosted review creation flows; routes local WSL project hosted review flows through runtime git options; treats SSH worktree drift as unknown without local git probes. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-listing.spec.ts: emits one mobile session terminal tab per live PTY even if two tabs resolve to it; resolves projected split authority from the parent layout PTY binding; keeps explicit-id terminal lists from resolving all worktrees; keeps explicit-id cold-cache terminal lists from classifying unrelated same-repo worktrees; keeps unknown bare terminal-list ids on the no-scan exact-id path; matches explicit-id cwd PTYs for folder workspace instance IDs; routes PTY output through the PTY leaf index in large terminal graphs. src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts: claims the first window as authoritative and ignores later windows; transfers authority from the headless sentinel to the first real window; relays terminal browser launches only while headless owns the graph; marks live headless PTYs for renderer reattach before desktop promotion; reports the activation gate state while no desktop window is available; bumps the epoch and enters reloading when the authoritative window reloads; can mark the graph ready for the authoritative window; drops back to unavailable and clears authority when the window disappears; hands the graph back to headless when a promoted serve window closes (#27292); keeps a crashed promoted serve renderer on its own window while the window is open; stays unavailable during initial loads before a graph is published. src/main/runtime/orchestration/mailbox/routing/orchestration-mailbox-routing-races.spec.ts: stops paged routing when the check is cancelled; keeps an unfiltered redrive unrestricted when reservations merge; keeps an unfiltered parked delivery unrestricted when reservations merge; uses a bounded indexed pane lookup for reminted Dispatch identity. src/main/runtime/workspaces/removal/worktree-teardown-unstopped-pty.test.ts: removes the reported wedged automation workspace without --force; clears PTY state once a failed stop is proven to have exited; names only the PTYs that are actually live, not every failed stop; warns with the specific sweep failure, not the generic deadline; still fails closed on a sweep-level failure without force. src/main/skills/bundled-skill-install/layouts.test.ts: links into a project only where its agent folder already exists; reads a pending cloud transaction as busy and a cloud receipt as another skill. src/main/skills/skill-upload-session-service.test.ts: joins concurrent disposal callers through exact cleanup completion. src/main/source-control/hosted-review-creation.test.ts: creates the pull request after fresh main-process validation passes; routes local WSL git and GitHub review creation through the selected runtime; creates a pull request on a GitHub Enterprise Server remote (#8312); creates a GitLab merge request after fresh main-process validation passes; creates an Azure DevOps pull request after fresh main-process validation passes; creates a Gitea pull request after fresh main-process validation passes. src/main/source-control/hosted-review-execution-host-routing.test.ts: reads a GitHub review on the SSH host a row names only in executionHostId; reads a GitLab review on the executionHostId host when connectionId names a different one; does not dial this client for a runtime row whose nested target shares a local name; keeps a runtime row with no nested target on this process (self-addressed stamp); keeps a legacy connectionId-only SSH row on its target; does not share a cached answer between two rows at one path on different hosts; creates a Bitbucket review locally for a runtime row rather than dialing its nested target; reports creation eligibility from the executionHostId-only SSH host; resolves the GitHub slug for a repo listing on the row it is asked about; refuses to dial a runtime host from this process; answers with the SSH target for both spellings and local otherwise; reads a runtime stamp on a row in this store as self-addressing, not a second machine. src/main/source-control/hosted-review-inflight-invalidation.test.ts: keeps other hosts, paths and their pending promises isolated. src/main/speech/model-manager.test.ts: requires pinned, internally consistent metadata for every model file; verifies downloaded model file hashes before installation; rejects non-HTTPS model downloads; marks OpenAI transcription models ready only when an API key is configured. src/main/ssh/connection/ssh-connection-sftp-namespace.test.ts: writes to the SFTP namespace path discovered on the same session; uploads the bundle into the SFTP namespace directory; issues no discovery requests when the caller supplies no mapping; ignores a mapping on a Windows host; never resolves on the system-SSH transport; leaves writeBuffer and openFileUploadSession on the shell path; keeps the shell path when discovery is inconclusive; preserves a session-limit channel-open error unchanged. src/main/ssh/connection/ssh-connection-system-transport.test.ts: uses system SSH transport when ProxyUseFdpass is resolved by OpenSSH; allows concurrent exec commands for system SSH with an Orca ControlMaster socket; keeps concurrent exec commands disabled for system SSH without a reusable socket; uses system SSH transport for ProxyCommand targets before ssh2 auth; keeps the original ssh2 reachability error when the system SSH probe fails; reports the system SSH failure when ssh2 cannot negotiate with the host; uses system transport for target or resolved OpenSSH proxy directives; allows an environment override for e2e coverage; ignores stale imported proxy fields when fresh OpenSSH config has no proxy. src/main/ssh/orcad-migration-catalog-client.test.ts: keeps each server project’s execution host, so a nested SSH row is never read as local; reads the server’s folder workspaces and the groups that place them on a host; sends and validates the %s operation; validates an abort result without letting it erase committed state; validates a committed receipt against the requested manifest; rejects malformed stage timestamps and abort envelopes; fails closed for method absence, malformed identity, and invalid pairing; refuses a destination without the capability before sending any migration request; reads method-not-found as the same refusal, not as a lost answer. src/main/ssh/runtime-ssh-access.test.ts: persists intent then claim before connecting and publishes redacted authenticated access; names the saved dependency when dependent state blocks an SSH access link; handles lost link responses without connecting or verifying again; invalidates old transport only after authenticated access is published; rejects changed request tuple after a completed link; rejects provisioning and missing durable generations without connecting; treats a lost successful unlink response as an idempotent no-op; hashes connection identity, not display state or owner; strictly validates ports and request IDs. src/main/startup/cli-launch-redirect.test.ts: detects a launch that received the unpacked CLI entrypoint; ignores normal desktop launches; ignores the entrypoint when it is only the executable itself (argv[0]); applies on Linux too; strips injected Chromium switches before node-mode CLI arguments; keeps user flags after the command and malformed boolean assignments; does not treat a later positional entrypoint path as the launcher; redirects a direct binary launch with no AppImage env at all; strips Chromium switches node mode would reject; preserves desktop-shaped switches after the command; leaves direct serve in-process but redirects its help; treats help as a CLI launch even without a command; treats %s as a CLI launch even without a command; does not treat a value of %s as a CLI early-exit flag; does not treat a serve option value as a help request; does not reinterpret help after the argument terminator; leaves a plain desktop launch alone; skips flag values when looking for the command positional; preserves a project selector in %j; does not apply the command form on macOS or Windows; never redirects an unpackaged build; runs the in-package CLI in Electron node mode with sanitized env; refuses to redirect twice so a dropped ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE cannot loop; reports a missing CLI entrypoint instead of booting the desktop app; execs a direct serve into the CLI so it keeps its pid and honours profile and supervise; keeps ORCA_USER_DATA_PATH for a direct serve without --user-data-dir; serves in-process when this runtime cannot exec or the exec fails; never execs the --serve child the CLI itself spawns, or serve on other platforms; surfaces a spawn failure as a non-zero exit; re-execs a direct --serve onto X11 when Electron resolved Wayland; leaves $name alone. src/main/startup/main-process-runtime-launch-activation.test.ts: marks startup settled for the launch record only after the window has loaded and settled; loads SSH targets on a windowless serve before paired clients can connect (#25886); pins the serve listener to loopback only for orcad browser sidecars (sidecar=$sidecar, #31895); saves Codex auth before a headless serve update restart, like the desktop does. src/main/startup/run-electron-vite-dev.test.ts: forwards dev instance identity to electron-vite; prepares userData orca and orca-dev wrappers for dev terminals; consumes the stable-name flag before forwarding args to electron-vite. src/main/updater/releases/updater-prerelease-feed.test.ts: returns the newest stable tag when the user is on an RC and a newer stable exists; returns the newest RC tag when no stable is newer than the current RC; can exclude prerelease tags for stable-channel checks; probes the %s %s platform manifest; returns null for stable-channel checks when only prereleases are newer; returns null when nothing in the feed is newer than the current version; ignores entries with unparseable tags; returns null when the fetch is not ok; returns null when the fetch throws; picks semver-newest across a mixed-order feed; ignores perf-tagged prereleases for regular RC checks; reports no RC update when only perf-tagged prereleases are newer; picks the semver-newest perf-tagged prerelease; matches only literal rc.N.perf prerelease tags for perf checks; reports no perf update instead of falling back to stable or RC tags; returns a bounded fallback candidate after the newest newer tag; returns null when the only newer tag has a manifest but its asset still 404s; requires a known old timestamp for a stable-fallback tag. src/main/updater/updater-events.test.ts: hands the whole downloaded event to artifact capture; publishes manual-install recovery after a %s download; publishes the normal downloaded state for AppImage builds; blocks downloaded-state handling when the packaged marker is unusable; passes the actual updater error into the install-failure handler; keeps manual-install recovery when a later check finds only the installed release; drops the artifact when another version takes over the cycle; ignores a downloaded event for an older target; accepts a matching event when the pending cache target was cleared; drops the artifact when progress reports a different pending version. src/main/updater/updater-linux-package-recovery-actions.test.ts: rejects both actions while no package-install recovery is active; validates the retained package on every invocation; restores recovery after a recheck resolves without a terminal event; restores recovery after a recheck fails; restores recovery when a pinned check resolves to the current version; restores recovery when resolving a pinned check fails; clears recovery for both actions once the package is gone; resolves %s as a result and keeps the card usable instead of rejecting; keeps recovery available after a transient read failure. src/main/updater/updater.check-settlement.test.ts: leaves a dismissed release update on the release source; surfaces net::ERR_FAILED to user-initiated checks with a friendly message; shows checking immediately for a user-initiated check while feed pinning is pending; keeps background checks event-driven before checking-for-update fires. src/main/usage/usage-provider-store-lifecycle.test.ts: persists identities for a whole first scan with one write; skips disabled and fresh matching states; invalidates prior sources on fingerprint changes and reuses them for forced scans. src/main/window/createMainWindow-close-confirmation.test.ts: clears the quit latch when the renderer prevents unload; does not notify the crash recorder when renderer teardown follows a confirmed window close; allows close when Electron reports a crashed webContents; requests confirmation for a hung-but-alive renderer instead of bypassing. src/main/workspaces/catalog/worktree-identity-persistence.test.ts: stores independent metadata for colliding locators on two hosts; projects canonical-only metadata for exactly one host; keeps canonical metadata current for legacy writers on a known owner; removes only the selected legacy-owner metadata when locators collide; keeps the canonical identity stable when the locator changes; leaves other hosts at the old locator when one host renames its folder. src/main/wsl/filesystem/wsl-drive-unc-conversion-startup.test.ts: leaves a journaled conversion untouched with the gate closed, %s. src/main/wsl/orcad/wsl-orcad-deploy.test.ts: holds the distro before it deploys and launches, and reports what C5 dials; passes its connect-state read (%s) on as hints; applies the SSH census and downgrade admission to the first deploy; refuses a WSL 1 distro before holding it or touching its files; tells an unregistered distro how to find the installed ones, before holding anything; surfaces an unsupported libc as the SSH host refusal does; starts an already-active slot the distro stop ended, instead of reporting it ready; deploys over an adopted unrecorded orcad under the SSH terminal gate, never a fresh launch; reports the adopted instance once the same version is serving; returns a deferral rather than launching over live terminals; hands a failed first deploy to the fresh-install cleanup before reporting it. src/main/zcode/zcode-v2-plan-credentials.test.ts: prefers migrated credentials over a stale legacy account; keeps legacy support when no personal v2 file exists; honors the upstream personal config override independently of the credential directory; does not borrow credentials from another execution host; preserves the protected Orca key priority even if v2 is corrupt; rejects upstream-invalid selection %j without legacy fallback; accepts a valid optional reasoning level; rejects upstream-invalid rule containers %j without legacy fallback; accepts a valid selected-provider empty personal rule and smart model rule; cannot establish selected credentials from %s rules; leaves encrypted CLI files unchanged across repeated account reads. tests/e2e/automation-terminal-launch.unit.test.ts: launches explicit Chat for %s through the common entry and keeps its actual fallback; does not apply stored Terminal extras to Chat; forwards only complete Chat-consumed values, with no Terminal startup base; refuses an expired admission without minting another launch identity; records the actual chat identity and delegates new workspace setup and provenance. tests/e2e/github-project-provider-columns.unit.test.ts: renders %s through one bounded items request on a named cloud host; preserves zero and complete counters: %j; preserves populated and legacy rows through shared sorting, grouping and cells. tests/e2e/structured-agent-session-launch-continuation.unit.test.ts: carries renderer lifetime through host intent to the real %s provider builders. tests/e2e/terminal-account-restart.unit.test.ts: replaces a tombstoned owner while its persisted pane binding has not yet been cleared; paired restart retains the old owner (host authority: %s). tests/e2e/terminal-hidden-view-parking.spec.ts: does not park excluded tabs; reproduces a static frame byte-for-byte across 25 park/reveal cycles. tests/e2e/terminal-long-table-scroll-restore.spec.ts: reproduces long markdown table artifacts after workspace switch and scroll; keeps narrow wrapped signer markdown table coherent after restore and scroll; keeps real emoji markdown table right edge clean after restore and scroll. tests/e2e/terminal-long-table-fixtures.ts: dedicated zero-case helper retirement; no authored test credit. tests/e2e/terminal-paste-ownership.spec.ts: Windows multiline keyboard paste normalizes terminal newlines with one PTY owner; right-click paste sends clipboard text to the focused terminal exactly once. tests/e2e/terminal-raw-emoji-table-scroll-restore.spec.ts: uses WebGL by default for ordinary terminal output when available @terminal-rendering-golden. tests/e2e/terminal-windows-shell-paste-ownership.spec.ts: cmd.exe default terminal keyboard paste preserves exact content with one PTY owner; Git Bash default terminal keyboard paste preserves POSIX-shaped content with one PTY owner; WSL terminal keyboard paste preserves Linux shell content with one PTY owner. tests/e2e/workspace-board-lane-virtualization.spec.ts: mounts a window of cards for a large lane and keeps lane indexes; renders later lane indexes after the lane scrolls. Current changed source bytes, wrapper registrations and reduced selectors have no fresh execution or red/green credit. Unrelated surviving receipt objects keep their original narrow scope; current literal graph reachability does not establish historical import closure or equivalent replacement coverage. Current conservative command/import graph reaches src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-sleep-and-teardown-part-03.spec.ts, src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/mobile-creation-and-orchestration-part-04.spec.ts, src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/hooks-and-hosted-review-part-02.spec.ts, src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/terminal-listing.spec.ts, src/main/runtime/orca-runtime-tests/window-authority.spec.ts, src/main/runtime/orchestration/mailbox/routing/orchestration-mailbox-routing-races.spec.ts, src/main/runtime/workspaces/removal/worktree-teardown-unstopped-pty.test.ts, src/main/skills/bundled-skill-install/layouts.test.ts, src/main/skills/skill-upload-session-service.test.ts, src/main/source-control/hosted-review-creation.test.ts, src/main/source-control/hosted-review-execution-host-routing.test.ts, src/main/source-control/hosted-review-inflight-invalidation.test.ts, src/main/speech/model-manager.test.ts, src/main/ssh/connection/ssh-connection-sftp-namespace.test.ts, src/main/ssh/connection/ssh-connection-system-transport.test.ts, src/main/ssh/orcad-migration-catalog-client.test.ts, src/main/ssh/runtime-ssh-access.test.ts, src/main/startup/cli-launch-redirect.test.ts, src/main/startup/main-process-runtime-launch-activation.test.ts, src/main/startup/run-electron-vite-dev.test.ts, src/main/updater/releases/updater-prerelease-feed.test.ts, src/main/updater/updater-events.test.ts, src/main/updater/updater-linux-package-recovery-actions.test.ts, src/main/updater/updater.check-settlement.test.ts, src/main/usage/usage-provider-store-lifecycle.test.ts, src/main/window/createMainWindow-close-confirmation.test.ts, src/main/workspaces/catalog/worktree-identity-persistence.test.ts, src/main/wsl/filesystem/wsl-drive-unc-conversion-startup.test.ts, src/main/wsl/orcad/wsl-orcad-deploy.test.ts, src/main/zcode/zcode-v2-plan-credentials.test.ts, tests/e2e/automation-terminal-launch.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/github-project-provider-columns.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/structured-agent-session-launch-continuation.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-account-restart.unit.test.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-hidden-view-parking.spec.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-long-table-scroll-restore.spec.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-long-table-fixtures.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-paste-ownership.spec.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-raw-emoji-table-scroll-restore.spec.ts, tests/e2e/terminal-windows-shell-paste-ownership.spec.ts, tests/e2e/workspace-board-lane-virtualization.spec.ts. Unresolved local/computed edges remain explicit debt.",
        "Audit1579 removes workflow/manifest/regex/private binary-header and diagnostic metric inventories, fixture selectors, injected forwarding/platform/signature/process examples, unproven overlap and internal churn counters without equivalent replacement coverage. Retains actual Git trust/diffs; filesystem hash/ELF-region/native discovery; child CLI module repair; compiler/lock/publication/rollback and synthetic Electron install/cache ownership; executable shell quoting/exit; controlled notary/timer cleanup; local patched extractor file/AST freshness; real Chromium/WebKit CSP/sandbox/HTTPS image/referrer/link/preservation controls under parsed Android headers. Five unchanged setup-pnpm/VM request-cleanup definitions reviewed and not rerun. GitHub, installer/archive, OS metric, client, native delegate, compressor, builder and Apple boundaries injected or absent where recorded. No actual native PTY, shipped full/native app, real Actions/cache/npm signature authority, downloaded Electron archive, real objdump/linker/native CLI/AppImage, signing/NSIS/notary/upload/updater or live freeze proof.",
        "Linux1.4.188 only; no macOS or Windows packaged coverage.",
        "No folder workspace, SSH execution host or live-service coverage.",
        "Other released version pairs remain untested; not a required PR check.",
        "Audit2377/2381 removes bundled-skill eligibility5 silent late-writer successful backup, layouts1 global forced backup, legacy-auto-update2 old release plus extra notes, and native-discovery7/13/18/19/21 OpenCode project, Pi home symlink, default Hermes root, requested-cwd agents symlink and standalone SSH-builder paired cwd checks. Lose those exact backupPath/bytes/global-link-lock/history/provider/label/path combinations and localized SSH-builder sample. Retained common owners are not identical replacements; no fresh validation is claimed for this reduced broad command.",
        "Audit2383 removes the complete antigravity-skill-discovery.test.ts suite. Lose the exact .gemini/config/skills path, home-antigravity source, antigravity owner, existence and contributing-root observation. Other providers exercise common discovery dispatch, not this exact catalogue row. No equivalent replacement or fresh validation of the reduced broad command is claimed.",
        "Audit2385 removes finder regular-depth and direct missing-root examples, the three-row staging-name matrix, and an initial unknown WSL-list record sample. Lose those isolated fixtures, exact backup name spellings and malformed prefix sequence; retained actual owners are not identical replacements. Missing-root case did not model disappearance after the production caller existence check. No fresh validation of this reduced broad command is claimed.",
        "Audit2389 removes whole skill-install-preview.test.ts plus destinations1 and recovery2. Lose missing-preview name/state/global identity/fixed codex+claude inventory, exact plain-global host identity return, and already-published receipt finalization fixture. No nonmutation assertion existed in preview; retained real home delivery and placed-canonical recovery are not identical complete replacements. No fresh validation is claimed.",
        "Audit2393 refresh2401 removes skill-installation original1 and only the original receiptless request case. Lose uninterrupted first-install status/exact placement count and public canonical receiptless conflict/unowned routing. Retain upstream request ownership tests and lower transaction interruption coverage byte-exact. Deleted guard case had no directory/content preservation assertion. No equivalent complete replacement or fresh validation is claimed.",
        "Audit2397 review amendment removes whole empty-gzip, WSL provider error-mapping and remote-cancellation registry suites; two initial hostname-suffix/userinfo URL rows and initial-expired grant sample; linked-parent alias classification. Lose no-input custom gzip branch, WSL failure labels, basic registry lifecycle/duplicate-ID guard, exact hostname-suffix/userinfo input variants, prefetch expired-grant no-network and preexisting alias result alarms. Preserve the single initial wrong-port origin authorization case, original abort-after-begin cleanup/no-signal cancelUpload dispatch suite and original independent-copy modified-digest removable=false case. No equivalent complete replacement or fresh validation claimed for the remaining losses.",
        "Audit2404 removes whole skill-share-package-name.test.ts, skill-delete-plan original1/6 skill-delete-recovery original2 and skill-share-preparation original2. Lose lookup503 rejection/status propagation through prepare, explicit unblocked unordered alias-kind/canonical sample with cwd undefined, stale classification after +60000ms actual mtime change, successful first-pass single-move rollback/staged-path absence and prior-process preparation-root archive directory cleanup. Retained exact identities use cwd home; public stale guard submits timestamp1; recovery retry cases are not identical first-pass fixtures. No equivalent complete replacement or fresh validation is claimed.",
        "Audit2412 removes whole useVirtualizedScrollAnchor.marks-restore-signal.test.ts (six fake-hook geometry/mark/convergence/user-takeover/clamp alarms), use-task-creation-draft-retention original3/4 (immediate discard mock-call count/unopened no-write), use-terminal-bulk-close-actions.placement original6/7 (absent new-agent append and one real history-publication count at consumed3/30 scale), PendingNativeChatCreation original6 (unmounted abort completion/timer cleanup), and wsl-move-dialog-store original1/9/13 (default whole-distro count/reference/reuse and rejected-preview/start refusal recovery). The history counter measures genuine publication work without entries/order/reopen assertions; its unique batching alarm is intentionally retired. Fake React scroll tests ignore dependency scheduling and cleanup; unique simulated arithmetic alarms are deliberately lost. Retained existing-terminal reorder is not new-agent append coverage; mounted handoff timeout is not abort coverage. No equivalent complete replacement or fresh validation is claimed.",
        "Audit2417 removes commit-actions-real-git original3/4 (ordinary clean cherry-pick and revert content, subject and current-branch samples), and pty-startup-ingress-exited-asker original8/12 (actual foreground-group read budget across100queued queries, and zero foreground reads across100normal chunks plus final emitted/accepted raw cursor equality). Counters measure actual callback work and scale is consumed; these internal-work alarms are deliberately retired. Retained unborn, conflict and sequencer cases are not equivalent ordinary-success coverage. No equivalent complete replacement or fresh validation is claimed.",
        "Audit2425 removes use-workspace-copy-status original5, which returns a fixture-supplied readError string through statusReadError. No consumer blocker or attempted branch switch established refusal; the unique error-forwarding sample is intentionally retired. Other copy ownership and stale-refresh cases are not equivalent error-path coverage. No equivalent replacement or fresh validation is claimed.",
        "Audit2432 removes BranchPicker.test.tsx original3, which only asserted onOpenChange(true/false) with an always-mounted mocked Popover. It never reopened the picker or consumed the callback in the parent status-refresh owner, despite its title. Lose that unique open/close notification alarm. Retained blocker/collision recovery and asynchronous post-unmount outcome cases are not equivalent replacement coverage. No fresh validation of the reduced selector is claimed.",
        "Audit3086 source-only reduction (3079/3080/3081): intentionally retire 93 authored/100 expanded mock-boundary cases, including the complete spawn-errors and SSH reconnect overlay suites, without replacement. Retired alarms include spawn classification/ownership, reply ceilings and renderer-write failure recovery, disconnect/detach fencing branches, authority facts, and overlay retry/visibility wiring. Retained callbacks are unchanged; no fresh execution, real PTY/SSH, rendered UI, or performance result is claimed.",
        "Audit3096 source-only reduction (3087/3088): retire 69 authored/76 expanded cases, including complete recovery-portals and reconnect-banner suites. Intentionally lose dead/default TUI replay, generated alternate-frame style composition, reset/mode/dimension and legacy missing-mode-boundary alarms, UI notice/action/reveal policies, and isolated recovery lifecycle variants, without equivalent replacement. Retained registrations and callbacks are unchanged; headless cells are not pixels, and no fresh runtime, host, SSH, WSL, rendered-app or performance result is claimed.",
        "Audit3108 source-only reduction (3094/3095/3100): retire 27 authored/30 expanded cases, including complete markdown view-state, file-preview link-open and CLI agent-server-route suites, without replacement. Deliberate losses include preview visibility/reference lifetime and same-path owners; SSH stat, directory/missing-target, explicit-null owner, nonmarkdown line/column, local URI routing, remote-to-client guard and same-file reuse; document-preview source-owner/folder/reuse routing, stable grant location and outside-workspace POSIX/Windows request projection; and verified remote CLI send/check refusal, suggested --on argv/copy, shell no-probe bypass, unverified-launch admission and older-peer refusal. Retain two markdown source-runtime/qualified-reveal alarms, one stale grant-rejection fence and two remote read/mutation evidence policies, with original callbacks. Final last-wins reveal did not prove transient cancellation; CLI prerequisite did not prove no real send, and envelope tests do not execute server refusal. No fresh runtime, rendered UI, actual file/SSH/paired transport, authorization, mixed-version or performance result is claimed.",
        "Audit3114 incorporates source3101: retire three structured Claude child-environment wrapper cases covering inherited stamp isolation/default and explicit entrypoint, Windows SDK-key canonicalization/default/duplicate-key order, and configured lookup/final environment/config-dir conjunction. Keep direct auth/session sanitation and Windows-versus-Linux overlay checks, actual executable lookup from supplied inherited PATH, native Windows child environment delivery, and stale option-mutation fencing. These are not equivalent replacements for the retired wrapper alarms. No fresh test/runtime, real login-shell probe, Claude SDK startup, remote/mixed-version, UI or performance result is claimed.",
        "Audit3114 incorporates source3105: retire 17 authored/20 expanded daemon launch-note cases, including the entire two-case SessionLaunchNote suite. Deliberately lose split-marker carry across same-token re-arm, stale-token retirement refusal, foreground tri-state and serial settlement, omitted-note/no-incarnation mixed-version policy, sticky retirement, first-incarnation/replacement launch preservation and held-launch precedence. Keep only the unchanged unresolved foreground-read race against a later finished attach. Supplied notes/foreground and runtime calls do not establish actual daemon/main restart, SSH, native Windows observation, mobile UI, equivalent replacement or fresh runtime/performance validation.",
        "Audit3114 incorporates source3109: retire six authored/35 expanded pricing cases: 21 accepted model-name examples, 10 unsupported/future-model fail-closed examples, malformed TTL clamp, unknown-model estimate refusal, flat-model long-context disregard and oversized long-context clamp. Keep mixed five-minute/one-hour write allocation and short/all-long/mixed long-context allocation with original fixed oracles. Real parser/refusal/bounds alarms are knowingly lost without equivalent replacement; retained tests do not validate provider rates, actual billing or request threshold classification. Preserve the archived usage-scan-append source-freeze receipt without transferring historical execution/performance credit. No fresh runtime result is claimed.",
        "Audit3128 scoped coverage reduction: Audit3121 removes VoiceDictationLanguageSetting.test.tsx (Spanish-to-es callback and unsupported-model Korean option presence) and voice-speech-model-rows.test.ts (provider/language-order/retired-on-disk list policy); these real narrow alarms are deliberately retired without replacement. VoiceSpeechModelSection per-model concurrent deletion remains unchanged. Audit3122 removes the direct absolute/parent-segment sparse-directory exception-type sample and the five-row IPC sparse-preset error-code/non-save table (two authored/six expanded cases). Those real typed-validation and IPC refusal/error-code alarms are deliberately retired. Keep both real symlink/junction floating-directory trust cases and the minimal RPC structured validation-reason serialization case. The RPC case does not replace IPC save/refusal behavior, typed normalization for both path inputs, actual Git sparse checkout or rendered localization. No equivalent replacement or fresh test/runtime/platform/remote/performance validation is claimed. Audit3124 removes ExperimentalPane.test.tsx (ordinary Pet switch callback), WorkspaceDirectorySetting.test.tsx (padded absolute saved-path normalization/no-write blur), and repository-search.perf.test.ts (navigation/selected-pane builder-call policy, fixture cardinality/nonempty entries and renamed project keyword inclusion). These real narrow alarms are retired without replacement; RepositoryPane.search.test.tsx search-to-sparse-editor request remains unchanged. Audit3129: resolver Windows case-insensitive and POSIX case-sensitive configured-env composition plus mocked-base launch-preflight Windows composition are intentionally no longer checked by the two deleted suites. No equivalent coverage claimed. Keep runtime-structured-agent-host-env.test.ts unchanged: configured Windows Claude-home account identity and host-account precedence remain checked.",
        "Audit3146 combines source reviews3132/3133/3135/3138/3143: intentionally retire20authored/31expanded cases without equivalent replacement. Provider-session losses: structured-native terminal-resume exclusion, metadata-less completed identity, new-turn completion clearing, Pi provider-only/periodic/manual promotion, changed-transcript launch-config isolation, Pi/omp/prime-agent completed-session remote/manual-shutdown promotion, and quit/done precedence over heartbeat. Side-thread/question losses: finished-pane acquisition, hidden title/recap states, local/relay/relay-done conversation takeover with prompt/session/child resets, plain-message abandonment, compaction/session replacement and completion resets. Codex startup losses: incoming-owner cached child replacement, old-relay foreign live-session correction, completed foreign-root turn-fact permutations. Transcript losses: real temporary-JSONL partial sibling/final-child completion, unlabelled child attribution, compact cached replay preservation and100/1000completed-child roster retention/release. Compiler-ratchet losses: valid-line uncompiled-list parser grammar examples and injected-existence stale-path filtering; these did not exercise actual filesystem canonicalization or build exclusion. These are real lifecycle, ownership, replay, liveness and retention alarms, including recent#40246 regressions, deliberately lost. Retained conditional record replacement, clockless root/SSH owner isolation, persisted main-thread fork rejection, partial/final question-answer lifetime, cached-roster/missing-ID/live HTTP/durable startup boundaries and restarted-relay refusal/acceptance do not replace those losses. No native/SSH/WSL execution or equivalent coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit3156 combines3147/3150/3152/3153/3154: deliberately retires39authored/40expanded native-chat recovery cases, eight whole suites and two orphan test-support files without equivalent replacement. Lost alarms: lost-reply unconfirmed reconciliation, skipped rows/counts and missed-frame repair, unknown/pending outcome and omitted-failure-list compatibility, uncertain history after dismissal, retry/refusal/dismiss lifecycle, hidden/consumed picker ownership, result-tree keyboard focus/disclosure and all-skipped retirement; unconfirmed-over-conflict guidance and failed-chat changes despite older host timestamps; nearest-listed ancestor/cyclic forest shape, descendant membership, host ordering/missing-host local fallback; skipped/readiness/admission counts, provisional skip/progress monotonicity, early per-chat verdicts with batch pending protection, older-host waiting, start-slot/delivery distinction, retry-over-failure and unknown-after-withdrawal attention; remote snooze/reconnect/reoffer, unseen mixed summary through open/close, watched completion retirement, new success beside old failure, failed-reread mixed-result preservation, filter/collapse completion resets, retry summary replacement and current-offer/history selection; cross-host workspace identity, rendered cyclic reachability, nested tri-state/toggle propagation, project eligibility isolation and collapse preserving selection. Exact fallback-list completion barrier, batched verdict/cleanup retention, stale-read versus dismissal publication race, and requested-but-never-rendered finished-run retirement remain; they do not replace retired alarms.",
        "Audit3165 combines source3160/3162: deliberately retires six authored/expanded cases across three whole suites without equivalent replacement. Launch/status losses: observed React-render pending/resuming coordination across settings and deferred offer read; stale-offer reread suppressing dialog reopen; held-local-chat recovery visibility with new-chat preferences off; disabled-local admission avoiding offer RPC despite an injected but unconsumed paired-tab fixture; and run-only lost-reply uncertainty reachability until direct viewed-run retirement. Launch probe does not prove arbitrary synchronous-store atomicity, the paired fixture is not remote runtime enrollment, and the status case directly marks viewed state rather than rendering the summary. Crew-hook losses: old-host method_not_found cache persists across party changes but is released by independently supplied connection generation/verified pairing status or pairing revision, with actual frame publication and teardown. These are real narrow coordination, admission, uncertainty and mixed-version cache alarms consciously lost. Exact web verified-runtime writer handoff guard remains; it does not replace those alarms or prove live host/native/mobile delivery.",
        "Audit3178 combines source3169/3170/3175: deliberately retires eight authored units (six Vitest cases and two imperative custom relay scenarios), including two whole suites, without equivalent replacement. Voice Section loses per-model pending-delete isolation across interleaved A/B completion and the two-success refresh-call alarm; exact VoicePane delayed key-clear/newer enabled-toggle merge remains and does not replace row deletion coverage. Speech loses dedicated rating-scale/inclusive-ceiling, unsupported-versus-unmeasured, explicit/system-language precedence/locale alias, accuracy versus fast named/default/best-measured selection, and unmeasured/no-match examples; exact offered-user-pick versus retired-selection case and its fixture remain. Relay loses legacy ping-delivery count/liveness sampled before the silence deadline and grouped malformed Bearer/host-ID 401/429 routing checks; twelve real Worker/DurableObject/shipped-client scenarios remain, not equivalent replacement for those narrow alarms. Six prior speech cases are not all deleted: approved successor3175 keeps the original user-choice case. No actual credential/file persistence, native/GPU/engine/download delivery, production assignment policy or deployed-runtime validation is claimed by this reduction.",
        "Audit3191 combines approved source3182/3187/3188: deliberately retires thirteen authored Vitest registrations and fifteen expanded cases, including five whole suites, without equivalent replacement. Attachment intake loses real portal/native-capture terminal interception and unowned-container refusal, immediate child-only committed availability/claim-ref negotiation and delivery, and direct-target over stable focused/background composer routing through disable/re-enable/remount and independent question focus. Exact destination/cache/draft and final-stat owner/workspace/File-release suites remain; they do not replace Surface recipient routing. Automation authoring loses destination runtime catalog membership, local/direct-SSH exclusion of paired-runtime repos, unknown-runtime empty catalog, logical project/host/setup/repo/path context payload, and missing/nonready setup refusal; these were genuine direct helper alarms, while exact schedule transformation, legacy schedule and setup-decision suites remain. Agent picker loses setup-chat/terminal/missing-installer/unsupported-or-unknown-host row projection samples and the ordinary unsearched menu variant; the entire original26-line resume recipe suite remains, including reported bypass versus default/absent permission modes, as does the exact search-result menu callback with its fixtures, model/effort commits and staged Arguments reopen outcome. Rejected predecessor3180 full recipe deletion is excluded. No actual native drag/cursor/focus/IME, upload bytes or disk/restart persistence, full automation save/scheduler/runtime transport, real resume-process flags/environment delivery, or native menu/rendered layout validation is claimed.",
        "Audit3200 composes approved source3194: deliberately retires thirteen authored registrations/twenty-seven expanded cases in six whole automation host/list policy suites without equivalent replacement. Real RPC category/retryability and wrapped-timeout recognition, unscoped-failure/scoped-success health evidence precedence, exact-ID create selectors and per-run workspace omission, paired-web local/SSH/absent host catalog routing, incompatible/removed/unhydrated/offline execution health, runtime-before-nested-SSH recovery dispatch, and no-owned-focus/successor/foreign-list focus policy alarms are consciously lost. Retain exact20line orphan allow/refuse/precondition and exact90line cross-host same-ID search suites. No retry-timer/fence lifecycle, actual reconnect/network/write delivery, native focus, mobile/mixed-version runtime or disk persistence coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit3209 composes approved sources3202/3206: deliberately retires seven authored/expanded cases in four whole suites without equivalent replacement. Work-item queries lose real GitHub/GitLab oversized ASCII secret-prefix empty-query and whitespace-before-trim refusal alarms; inputs share the imported size bound and exercise only its fast length branch, with no multibyte or actual provider/exposure guarantee. Skill sharing loses complete/partial managed-bundle and destination-ambiguity association checks plus three negative origin/path/scheme admission examples; these do not establish uploaded contents, arbitrary-URL fetching, authorization or execution. Retain exact originless-project direct-link fallback, cloud-delete confirmation, bundled-target repair/owner isolation and explicit Windows-host preference over stale WSL suites. Rejected3201 runtime-preference removal is excluded. No real cloud/network/host/disk, mobile or mixed-version execution validation is claimed.",
        "Audit3219 removes the synthetic Cmd+J extra-source suite; this broad command no longer checks its match/tie placement and selection, announced count, empty-query cap, or workspace hiding with retained recent tabs. No replacement coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit3231 retires supported-host restore-pane key mapping, closed/open creation-sidebar toggle visibility, unrelated scope-error/null classification and quick-submit reveal/no-create checks. These broad commands lose those real narrow alarms; no replacement coverage is claimed.",
        "Audit3246 retires NewRowsMarker reveal/no-repeat and pane-scoped beforeinput checks; skill-owner option availability/count/dedup/order; six styled Input/Textarea IME forwarding rows; the static Codex/OpenCode smart-key inventory; tab-map AST ratchet diagnostic fixtures; child-roster work-budget and retained-aggregate alarms; malformed persisted floating-cwd fallback/no-crash/empty exact-root checks; the unanswered-host empty-list discriminator; the direct invalidated-cache commit-false assertion; one redundant digit-keyup IME row; cached non-supported Claude title-generator rows; and the duplicate late naming-result singleton. These root broad commands lose those specific alarms without equivalent replacement. Distinct retained owner/state checks have their own bounded claims; the real scheduler still rejects stale response data, while the direct false-return alarm is retired.",
        "Audit 3256 removes these specific alarms from the broad root unit commands: skill dialog active-share selection, close and pending-share handoff; simple keyed-record deletion; marker live-region insertion, simple landing and nine baseline policy examples; General search/control navigation inventory; orphan-count cache bootstrap; seven Codex code classifications and HTTP 429 warning mapping; two skill unread-root verdict examples; peer-mail payload and conversation-ID rejection; and the GitHub organization TABLE text-field optimistic rollback/failed-envelope example. These include real behaviors; retained tests do not provide equivalent coverage for every removed scenario. Mobile losses are recorded separately and are not coverage of these root commands.",
        "Audit 3273 removes 14 authored declarations and 19 expanded scenarios across four whole suites and eight partial suites. Retired alarms cover saved-local cancellation/layout ownership, ambiguous-owner warning reset, folder attachment routing, VM false-capability bypass, abandoned reveal warmup cleanup and viewport claim deduplication/rearming, quiet unrelated remote-removal refusal, startup-command one-shot consumption, repository/floating recovery-ledger rows, fake-React pinned-scroll intent, split-ratio state identity/subscriber suppression and fractional change, cross-host project-group join refusal, three PR request-lifetime permutations, upstream-status preservation on error, and unresolved Git-owner refusal. These regression checks are intentionally lost under the test-value audit; retained scenarios are not equivalent replacements. Historical coverage receipts remain historical, including gate35 subscriber claims.",
        "Audit 3283 removes 20 authored declarations and 31 expanded scenarios, including two whole suites. Retired alarms cover PR refresh-state pruning, shared runtime subscription cleanup and store isolation, language content-change routing and older completion ownership, ordinary panel retry-timer cleanup and pending loading, four hosted-review lifetime permutations, mocked terminal creation error/order wiring, five sleep-inventory variants with pending-frame-only assertions, palette fallback/composite highlights, Windows/UNC encoded-editor input rows, mixed-repository partial failure counts, title setters and generated-title bypass/replacement, five window-close coordinator delegation/guard/finally branches, and ambiguous-old-record frame reveal. These regression checks are intentionally lost under the test-value audit; retained cases are not equivalent replacements. Prior coverage notes and receipts remain historical.",
        "Audit 3292 combines adopted 3285/3287/3289/3293 removals: 40 authored declarations and 47 expanded scenarios, including whole frame-editor-view, ambiguous remote-delete-refusal, unverifiable-host subscription and editor-close cleanup suites. The previously reviewed dock-badge suite was already removed upstream in PR 40895 and receives zero new removal credit. Intentionally retired alarms include background browser selection and last-tab landing; main startup fallback, SSH project cleanup/survivor routing, exact-PR contradiction/saved-push positives, replay/sidecar rollback and wrapped remote error normalization; records/snapshot missing-diff hydration, ambiguous folder-owner delete refusal, focus no-op notifications, nested editor context-only cache check, pending broadcast-first status and ordinary four-confirmation aggregation; preview-source frontmatter pruning, approved local/runtime agent dispatch, non-GitHub legacy PR cache invalidation, stale merged-head transient-error fallback, empty-queue immediate query reply and unverified-to-concrete preflight risk. Additional intentionally retired alarms are injected host subscription/unsubscribe counts, synthetic editor reveal/draft/fallback/scoped close, ambiguous unread refusals and hidden mark/read roundtrip, immediate connect backoff/noError, positive mirrored evidence-clock renewal, supplied VM failure/success projections and git-local/folder-SSH wake permutations. Remaining temporal/ownership cases are narrower; no equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed.",
        "Audit 3301 combines adopted source batches 3296 and 3299: retire 27 authored declarations and 36 expanded scenarios, including six whole suites. Intentionally lost alarms cover failed-verification/recovery/restart counters and mocked hosting/toast; early overlapping pane-read scheduling/count; unreadable removal listing draft guard; bulk-purge remote-qualified and raw-local guard maps; initial-snapshot blank/mode/oversize/printable/fresh-spawn callback and replay examples; fallback mobile file close and ordinary MRU; default queue overload/drain; seeded browser-page reuse and supplied missing-page URL recreation; ambiguous sleep/hibernation owner refusal and untouched bindings/origins; ordinary selection/activity/fallback priority; skip-remote success and retained hints; supplied structured-chat unsent retention and scoped removal draft eviction; caller-chat focus precedence; open/draft PR cache eviction and merged-head fallback result inventories. Retained adverse-ordering and ownership cases are narrower and do not establish equivalent replacements. No fresh runtime, native, physical provider, cross-platform, mobile or mixed-version evidence is claimed.",
        "Audit 3312 composes adopted sources 3302 and 3308: deliberately retires 33 authored declarations and 36 expanded cases, including the whole backend startup-focus, active-browser IPC-close-routing, remote-browser-creation and agent-terminal-presence suites. Intentionally lost alarms cover distinct six-pane reconnect handles; SSH host label/Connect callback, unhydrated visit cleanup, repo cache aliases and hidden worktree/tab/PTY cleanup; adopted-agent startup focus and viewer navigation/reuse; staged, pageless, source, stale and orphan browser-close routing; web local-materialization refusal, desktop incapable-host fallback, failed/thrown remote creation and paired-web sign-in refusal; BOM/NUL and remote/local custom-editor byte-read examples; immediate folder activation and unread clearing; and batching idle/coalescing, accumulated byte ceiling, leading-edge-disabled, standalone synchronous oversize rejection, validation yield, deferred pending-tail order and both viewport-clear examples. The newly reintroduced agent-terminal-presence suite also loses actual terminal-status membership positive and nonterminal-status callback suppression alarms, including the recent 40916 guard regression; the older different 2133 presence-suite history remains historical and receives zero duplicate removal credit. These real regression alarms are intentionally lost. The unchanged survivors provide narrower coverage, with no equivalent replacement or fresh gate, provider, rendered, remote/mobile, mixed-version, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget validation claimed.",
        "Audit 3318 composes adopted sources 3310, 3313 and 3317: intentionally retires 71 authored declarations and 102 expanded cases, including whole terminal-detach agent-retention, seeded batch/single open-files equivalence, shallow context-menu shortcut-badge, mocked active-workspace delete-dispatch, workspace session hydration, SSH target cleanup, editor session hydration and worktree terminal purge suites. Lost alarms include chained transfer alias and immediate close/exit retention; batch/single divergence, survivor/selection/map preservation and input nonmutation across 400 imperative seeds (one registered case); disconnected pending-handle retry, authoritative absences/close-record shortcut/older-host absence and published-presence/unpublished-frame examples; published empty host-graph omission to pane exit; legacy search ranking/exclusion fallback; provider request upgrade/dedupe/finalizer ownership; asynchronous PR suppression/primary-change and same-number different-repository URL rejection. Deletion routing loses host/instance qualification, paired and legacy mapping, folder ownership, active-versus-hover/menu-row selection, ambiguity, modal/editable/creation/view/main/deleting/missing guards and shortcut advertisement. Unchanged real keyboard/hover/confirmation/catalog E2E remains narrower, not an equivalent replacement. Additional losses include scripted old-host disk/UTF-8/noop/baseline and landed/unlanded lost-reply/replacement-retry outcomes; ordinary/repeated healthy-link reattach; cross-owner terminal/chat binding; oversized replay permanent-unavailable classification; floating reveal keyboard ownership/close/disable/listener disposal; naming/retained-turn/Sleep/error/close/reject status tables; SSH membership prune/new-target-only reads and environment/local bucket isolation; same-frame receipt capacity and positive bare/headless publisher readmission. These actual regression alarms are deliberately lost; no fresh gate, provider, rendered, mobile, mixed-version, cross-platform, soak or measured-budget validation is claimed.",
        "Audit3335 composes adopted source unions3327/3328 and3330/3332: intentionally retires100 authored registrations/123 expanded cases, including ten whole suites, without equivalent replacement. Lost alarms include seeded host persistence/contention and stale-host cleanup; browser snapshot assembly; mocked wake/DPR callbacks and frame budgets; preflight projections; palette authority/cache suppression, URL intent and saved-title cross-repo collisions; metadata coverage/set patch and dropdown assembly; and removed terminal, worktree, review-refresh and owner-routing examples. Retained definitions do not replace these alarms. This broad root unit command selects the reduced suite; no fresh execution, historical source/import equivalence, real provider/network/SSH, rendered UI/GPU/focus, durability restart, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Unrelated dated receipts retain only their original scope.",
        "Audit3342 composes adopted source batches3333/3334,3336/3337 and3340/3341: intentionally retires180 authored registrations/263 expanded cases, including seven whole suites, without equivalent replacement. Lost alarms include corrupt editor hydration; mobile editor/diff publication and privacy projections; stale-resubscribe routing; model-picker projection/refetch/retry/fallback; editor check-details and frame property inventories; latched-pane cleanup/quiescence; client create replay identity/options/compatibility; and removed owner, async routing, terminal and layout examples. Retained definitions do not replace these alarms. This broad root unit command selects the reduced suite; no fresh execution, historical source/import equivalence, real provider/network/SSH, rendered UI, durability restart, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Unrelated dated receipts keep their original scope.",
        "Audit3349 composes adopted batches3343,3345 and refreshed3354: intentionally retires234 authored registrations/294 expanded cases, including13 whole suites, without equivalent replacement. Lost alarms include supplied terminal reconnect/replacement/typeahead/mirror/result and snapshot examples; synthetic render-desync persistence/recovery; worktree listing/owner/catalog/lineage/removal and activation/creation examples; host-scoped PR and task-record projections; editor diff/status/comment and UI send-target examples; automation observation/wake, supplied sleep/deadline clock and native-chat completion/notification/relaunch samples; held-tab layout and cleanup/progress guard examples. Retained adverse-ordering and wire-boundary cases are narrower and do not replace all removed alarms. The already-upstream visibility-resume deletion receives zero new removal credit. This broad unit command selects the reduced suite; no fresh execution, historical import equivalence, real provider/network/SSH, native process/power/GPU, rendered UI, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Unrelated dated receipts retain their original scope.",
        "Audit3359 composes root-adopted source3355/independent3356: intentionally retires130 authored registrations/139 expanded cases, including eight whole suites, without equivalent replacement. Lost alarms include strict create naming/capability/legacy payloads; supplied transport host replacement, deadline reattach, create-handoff and split activation; agent-session fork/clipboard/platform flags; shutdown cleared-scrollback/unmounted bindings; simulator host-collision/selection/shutdown; and removed editor, catalog, mutation, launch and status examples. Retained12 adverse-ordering/state-consequence cases are narrower and do not replace all removed alarms. Two queue absences receive zero removal credit. This broad unit command selects the reduced suite; no fresh execution, historical import equivalence, real provider/network/SSH/PTY, filesystem restart, native UI, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Unrelated dated receipts retain their original scope.",
        "Audit3362 composes root-adopted3358/independent3360: intentionally retires129 authored registrations/140 expanded cases, including four whole suites, without equivalent replacement. Lost alarms include supplied orphan-adoption retry/malformed inventory/cancellation; fake-terminal replay parser/wedge/disposal callbacks; all-host catalog metadata and Windows preferences; host keepalive/protocol/stale/settings failures; and removed exact-stop/suppression, source save lifetime, diff-note queue, rename/editor close, input flood/chunk refusal/limits, purge and creation examples. Retained18 registrations/21 expanded cases protect narrower ownership, generation, dirty-state, queue convergence, encoding and attachment-lease outcomes. No replacement or keeper quota claim. This broad unit command selects the reduced suite; no fresh execution, historical import equivalence, real provider/network/SSH/PTY/xterm parser, disk restart, native UI, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Unrelated dated receipts retain their original scope.",
        "Audit3368 composes root-adopted3363/3364 and3367/3369: intentionally retires181 authored registrations/196 expanded cases, including28 whole suites, without equivalent replacement. Lost alarms include hibernation attention/liveness/backoff/sequential teardown and inventory, host launch compatibility/legacy/Kimi/resource cleanup, terminal recovery parser/pause/quarantine/remount, window-visibility omission-fence lifetime, launch-option rendered Start, sleeping-resume saved recipe/WSL quoting/cancellation, plus removed project/window/input variants. Additional tiny-suite losses include sentence/label/field/default inventories, credential omission, Windows argument/environment mapping, URI decoding, diagnostics, provider classification and fake-clock callback/parser examples. Retained ten registrations/twelve expanded cases include two literal Unicode Mn/Cf zero-width range guards in the actual character-range algorithm and protect narrower delayed editor bytes/destructive ownership, mounted hidden collision repair, ten transport epochs, duplicate-command refusal, caller timeout typing, executor unknown-opener refusal and failed-chunk user bytes. This broad unit command selects the reduced suite; no fresh runtime, real provider/network/PTY, filesystem restart, native UI, historical import equivalence, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform validation is claimed. Unrelated dated receipts retain their original scope.",
        "Audit3375 composes root-adopted3370/independent3371 and3373/independent3374: intentionally retires79 authored registrations/84 expanded cases, including39 whole suites, without equivalent replacement. Lost alarms include federation field/parser inventories; Claude rejected-key precedence, credential clone redaction, managed-versus-user hook preservation and CLI defaults; setting/status/activity projections, mocked SSH/notification/reveal/Linear refusal, fake-clock reconnect and noise; image-fold artifact visibility, paste eligibility, setup trust, scripted ACP error-to-journal publication and ligature cache tuple aliasing; plus supplied folder-runner uniqueness, mobile host-overlay/credential/update/preference races, status/markup/title/keyed-row projections, subscriber cleanup, cancellation/close/refusal/link-issue and mirror suppression alarms. Retained3373 merger contiguity, dual-clock overdue-resume exactly-once, rejected-paste IPC sink and annotation schema roundtrip remain bounded. Retained actual HTTP/OSC status composition, destructive sibling-filesystem isolation, external contrast invariant and fixture CSS pixel intervention remain narrower. Original reviewed87authored/92expanded become9/9; current OpenCode suite adds two preserved upstream cases and the synthetic-title suite gained one Cursor policy mock-call case, independently reviewed for removal in root3378; current90/95 become11/11. That Cursor suppression/ready-frame regression alarm is intentionally lost; it does not observe native title ownership or tab flicker. For3370 only the peer was independently blind, with author exposure explicit;3373/3374 both blind pins were verified. This broad root unit command selects the reduced root unit suite; UNIT_INCLUDE excludes mobile tests, which require the existing mobile runner; retained Playwright component-pixel spec uses its separate existing headless fixture runner and is not validated by the broad unit command. No fresh execution, actual agent/shell/provider, OS material/focus, historical import equivalence, mobile, mixed-version or cross-platform evidence is claimed. All dated receipts retain their original scope.",
        "Audit3381 composes root-adopted3376/independent3377 and3379/independent3380: intentionally retires436 authored registrations/670 expanded cases, including79 whole suites and12877 test lines, without equivalent replacement. Lost alarms include scheduling, account/host/status/filter/format inventories, microphone/image cleanup, title/bell/capability lifecycle routing, access/impersonation/outcome matrices, paste/input resend/ledger/retention, stale completions/reload containment, trust-read failure and popup OAuth/security/geometry vectors. Retained30 registrations/34expanded cases in22 suites preserve narrower SQLite TEMP/TZ/WAL, HTTP transcript root resume, mobile original-index Choose/Submit, child environment/Git lock expiry, stale ACK/PTY lifetime/peer fairness/durable replay/output ordering, actual DOM paste/editor focus, DEC2026 conservation, filesystem rollback, owned buffer lifetime, actual OSC parser/tracker handback, POSIX Python UTF8/fallback, durable trust concurrency/version, OpenSSH verdicts and hidden Chromium POST/route lifecycle. Mocked boundaries limit claims. Current bounded defining-owner reads preserve the retained oracles; captured identities are not full transitive semantic review. Both component blind pins authenticated before exchange; final reconciliation and explicit postpin3380reason correction supplement control, without retroactive blind claims. Root unit command excludes mobile and separately admitted Electron probes; use existing respective runners. No fresh execution, native focus/device/pixel UI, live SSH/remote, equivalent replacement or broad mixed-version/cross-platform validation is claimed. Prior dated receipts retain exact original scopes.",
        "Audit3390 composes root-adopted3382/independent3383 and3386/independent3387 and3388/independent3389: intentionally retires216 authored registrations/230 expanded cases in42 whole authored suites plus5 zero-case registration drivers, without equivalent replacement. Lost local alarms include fake PTY identity/routing/startup/replay/mode/title/mouse/IME/scroll matrices, broad startup identity and file-open wiring, mock mailbox title recovery, mobile row parity and whole-v-selective save parity. Retained24 registrations/26 expanded cases in22 suites preserve actual xterm Windows buffer/wrap/scroll, typed TOML scalar, real Promise cancellation/settlement, HTTP Codex scanner/projector semantics, durable recovery admission/newer-schema bytes, federation completion/ACK/SQLite atomicity and failed stale-run-write versus imported durable history. Additional retained clock-domain scheduling, durable freeze/ACK/checkpoint ordering, ABA dirty intent, SQL atomicity, folder-domain retier/last-note deletion, scrollback durable no-sync staging, PanelBridge subscriber lifetime and reserved-send publication preserve narrower concrete behaviors. Current finite owner drift assessed in bounded defining bodies; retained callback bytes unchanged. Historical notes and complete dated receipts keep their original exact scopes. No new execution, equivalent replacement, native focus/device/pixel, live remote or global mixed-version guarantee is claimed.\nOriginal active selector fields (historical raw native JSON values; not current coverage):\ncommands: [\n        \"gh workflow run packaged-browser-e2e.yml\",\n        \"pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/packaged-mixed-version-browser-placement.spec.ts --config tests/playwright.config.ts --project=electron-headless --workers=1 --repeat-each=3 --retries=0\",\n        \"gh run view 34069063016 --log\",\n        \"ORCA_BACKGROUND_LAUNCH=1 pnpm exec vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts --maxWorkers=2 --reporter=dot\"\n      ]\ntestFiles: [\"tests/e2e/packaged-mixed-version-browser-placement.spec.ts\"]\nassertionRefs: [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"tests/e2e/packaged-mixed-version-browser-placement.spec.ts\",\n          \"assertions\": [\n            \"old client and old host lack client-host and browser-tunnel capabilities\",\n            \"browser contents remain owned by the server and the expected snapshot marker is readable\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]",
        "Audit3403 composes root-adopted3393/3394,3400/3401 and3398/3399: intentionally retires167 authored registrations/196 potential expanded cases across93 whole suites without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Retained65 registrations/79 potential cases include one conditional missing-input failure sentinel; potential counts are not executions. Historical notes and complete dated receipts retain their exact original scopes. The broad root-unit command loses the UNIT_INCLUDE src/ subset of retired examples; mobile is outside UNIT_INCLUDE. Other lost alarms are recorded by the adopted per-case source reviews.  Original scope text is retained as the exact suffix of coverageNotes/oracle; historical evidence is unchanged.",
        "Audit3413 composes root-adopted3405/independent3406 and3409/independent3410: intentionally removes337 authored registrations/363potential expanded cases from13sources, retaining31authored/32potential cases and deleting one whole clipboard suite, without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Broad root-unit discovery loses35WSL examples,22STT examples,22shared-server-banner examples,18clipboard-handler examples (whole suite deleted),14VM lifecycle examples and16commit-message cancellation examples. Retain4WSL and7STT mocked connector/worker cases,1rendered stale-banner refusal,2VM guard/failed-compensation cases and1late-stream ownership cancellation case; real WSL/microphone/remote-provider proof is not established. Separately discovered e2e-unit drivers lose13cross-version-wire local cases and15mobile active-publication cases, keeping same-process disk-reopen/new-host cursor content/epoch/sequence outcomes and a host/renderer-snapshot selection and inventory revision race respectively. Imported released stop-note scenarios remain unchanged and receive no duplicate credit. Cloud suites are outside root UNIT_INCLUDE.  All previous note strings, dated receipts, archived raw receipts and prior gap entries retain their original scopes.",
        "Audit3417 composes root-adopted3415v2/independent3416v2: intentionally removes117authored/173potential expanded registrations from12semantic sources, deleting4whole conventional suites and3registration modules and retaining4authored/5expanded cases, without equivalent replacement or fresh execution. Broad root-unit discovery loses naming/title/queued-host fixtures, main-window focus-shortcut and attach-services mock orchestration, Git Bash console-capacity fake process inventories, most real-Git preparation/locking variants and Claude/Codex catch-up examples. Keep lifetime rejected-writer followed by late termination proof and autonomous real-checkout cleanup; two-row real-Git rollback after a real move preserving a replacement/admin marker or revoked permission; a live translator write during a held transcript read fencing stale Claude history append; and Codex expected-item revision rejection before a historical writer shim. Codex driver registers retained bounds exactly once with original inputs; bounds does not prove modern writer persistence. Accepted changed-lock preflight sentinel and omitted-parent routing losses are not replaced.  All earlier notes and dated/archived evidence retain original scopes.",
        "Audit3425 composes root-adopted3420/independent3421: intentionally removes83 authored/112 potential expanded registrations across13 semantic sources, deleting7 whole conventional suites and1 registering helper;7 authored/10 potential expanded cases remain. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Broad unit discovery loses the adopted mock orchestration, refusal, restart and storage examples. Retain unchanged two-phase real-WSL deployment/survival, the reduced idle-release holder proof without restart/first-output measurement, real worker stop/release cleanup barrier rows, physical Git branch-preservation rows, and SSH disconnected-close proof. Other SSH and CLI variants and WSL telemetry/warmup churn are intentionally removed.  Earlier notes and dated/archived evidence retain original scopes.",
        "Audit3429 composes root-adopted3426/independent3427: intentionally removes168 authored/205 potential expanded cases across16 semantic sources, deleting11 whole suites and one304line unused assertion helper. Five authored/five potential cases remain; the duplicate500k graph row is dropped while its50k row and callback remain. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Broad unit discovery loses the adopted migration/recovery/federation/rich-draft/paste/automation/mobile/catalog examples. Keep server-edit preservation during migration, native supervised cancellation holding the agent home until physical stop, pagehide lost-text preservation, graph old-result WRAPPER WeakRef collection with50k rows, and mobile React render isolation. The WeakRef does not prove all commit objects are collectible or a memory budget.  All prior notes and dated/archived evidence retain original scopes.",
        "Audit3437 composes ROOT-adopted3431/independent3432: intentionally removes127 authored/174 potential expanded cases across12 sources, deleting7 whole suites and one267line unused helper without test credit. Retain8 authored/13 potential cases. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Broad unit discovery loses reduced or deleted relay, coordinator mail, recovery watchdog, automation observer, launch picker, folder PTY, profile restart, web migration, retirement, pointer delivery, agent-row and run-bound mailbox examples. Retained checks cover relay hello/payload and SIGTERM drain, coordinator pending-check and clear-to-Run continuity, profile persistence, the full six-row web merge table and real run-bound delivery waiter. These do not replace removed alarms.  All prior notes and dated/archived evidence retain original scopes.",
        "Audit3446 composes ROOT-adopted3441/independent3442: intentionally removes100 authored registrations/119 potential expanded cases (118 conditional-active before platform gates) across16 sources, retaining11 authored/13 expanded cases and deleting6 whole suites. Two parent registrar import/call cleanups and the unused68line CLI recording fixture carry zero test credit. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Broad unit and mobile discovery loses interrupt/wake registrars, task storage/session-close/account snapshot hooks, permission tables, copy/preference/model-discovery/composer examples, launch placement examples, VM projections and extra mobile-history scenarios. Retained checks cover abandoned versus dispatched fork uncertainty; /fast dispatch supersession; discovery lock release after exit; stale-send draft preservation; OSC status lifetime; future-version file preservation; launch cancellation before/during dispatch on both layout owners; mobile resume addressability before hooks; and recipe snapshot cleanup after plugin removal. The paired browser-link Electron source is unchanged. Terminal launch seams, mobile roles-only history and injected provider results do not establish native terminal destruction, transcript text fidelity or real remote provider cleanup.  All prior notes and complete dated receipts retain their original scopes.",
        "Audit3451 composes ROOT-adopted3444/independent3445: intentionally removes101 authored registrations across16 reviewed sources, deleting7 whole suites and reducing8; one reviewed source is unchanged. Fresh main has123 authored registrations before and22 after because an upstream direct-child shell regression remains verbatim with zero removal credit. Registered removals are100+7*S and explicit-active removals99+7*S, where S is the unprobed count0..3 of admitted bash/zsh/fish shells. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Broad unit discovery loses extra stream lifecycle/forwarding examples, unreadable-store/cache projections, orchestration presentation/benchmark cases, remote-owned routing matrices, mobile legacy navigation and model-catalog listing/cache examples. Whole suites retire renderer client-event projections, manually assembled structured-session reader ownership, mobile prompt presentation, renderer AI-vault resume commands, mobile Jira URL lookup, composer retention and mobile folder source-repository queries. Retained checks preserve original stream/store/orchestration/routing/navigation/catalog cases and shell behavior, including the upstream direct-child case. No real provider, native desktop or mobile acceptance is established by this reduction. All prior notes, assertion references and complete dated receipts retain their original historical scopes.",
        "Audit3456 composes ROOT-adopted3449/independent3450: intentionally removes62 authored/82 potential expanded cases from16 selected drivers, including7 whole suites, while13 authored/13 potential cases remain. Delete the unused48line legacy workspace-session JSON fixture with zero test credit. These are source-only reductions without equivalent replacement or fresh runtime claims. Broad unit discovery intentionally loses whole trust-dialog observer, background-turn notifications, redirected session refusal, typed-agent identity, chat-tab lifetime-cost, model-manager and mobile diff-review controller suites, plus individual persistence, synthetic composition, pairing, manifest and subprocess samples. Retain deferred snapshot dirty-domain persistence, two direct editor ownership cases, stream counter-domain distinction, two persisted pairing identity cases, parser entrypoint asymmetry, dictation retry and process-group timeout; paired restart and packaged old-binary/corrupt-profile journeys remain in their E2E driver scope. Retained checks do not replace removed alarms. No fresh execution, native IME/microphone, real authentication, mixed-version/platform or performance result is claimed. All prior notes and archived receipts retain original scopes.",
        "Audit3468 accepted source proposal AUTHOR3462/PEER3463, composed privately by audit3469: removes62 authored registrations/95 finite potential expansions, including5 whole suites, retaining25 authored registrations/29 finite potential expansions. ROOT approved source value; no equivalent replacement, fresh runtime or merge credit is claimed. Broad root-unit discovery loses the profile-state worker smoke, worker-agent views and three search discovery suites, plus samples from node-server qualification, skill-bundle generation, CLI hooks/profile/recovery/offline admission, permission-hook holds and search indexing. The separate Cloud relay runner loses one relay blackbox sample; unchanged mobile native-chat and dependent-transcript drivers remain. Retained source callback/table/ancestor/fixture bytes bind to the sealed candidate. No physical-device, mixed-version, remote, cross-platform or app execution result is claimed. Earlier notes, complete dated receipts and archived gaps retain their original scopes.",
        "Audit3438 composes ROOT-adopted3434/independent3436: intentionally removes60 authored/62 potential expanded cases across16 sources, deleting9 whole suites. Eight authored/eight potential cases remain; delete the102line unused ACP fixture and57line unused teardown helper with zero test credit. No equivalent replacement or fresh execution is claimed. Broad unit discovery loses ACP model-catalog fixtures, resume-record projections, dashboard mock payload/state cases, mobile folder/launch/session examples and dictionary pipeline rows. Selected E2E removals also retire auto-conversion and golden-core journeys and one Windows CLI conversion registration. Retain ACP reply text across a resumed subagent, both VAD checks, focused tab send ownership, async focus ownership in happy-dom, the question-skip journey, the original managed Windows CLI lifecycle journey and dictionary substitution. These checks do not replace the removed alarms.  All prior notes and dated/archived evidence retain original scopes.",
        "Audit3470 composes ROOT-approved AUTHOR3466/PEER3467 source proposal: intentionally removes38 authored registrations/59 finite potential expansions, including8 whole registering suites, retaining13 authored registrations/18 finite potential expansions. The sole dead shell-recipe caller cleanup has zero additional test credit. No equivalent replacement, fresh runtime or merge credit is claimed. Broad root-unit discovery loses process-import boundary, Korean/Japanese locale policy, worker-reset, mobile agent-history/queued-message and median-summary suites, plus packaged mobile-manifest, worker-pool fixture, HTML preview, mobile shell and terminal samples. The environment-provider contract and its sole shell-recipe caller are deleted. Separate cross-version-wire discovery loses the large byte-budget fresh-snapshot/replay sample while retaining independent live same-revision note publication; the retained terminal stale-refresh and dirty HTML draft persistence checks do not replace removed alarms. The source4 unused start/stop fixture hooks are removed; its retained nested failed-import test remains byte-exact with its own lifecycle. Unchanged SVG preview and Git-resolution registrations stay intact. Root balanced CI excludes the cross-version directory, which has a separate job; unbalanced root discovery can include its parent. No native app/device, actual remote, released-pair interoperability or cross-platform execution result is claimed. Earlier notes, complete dated receipts and archived gaps retain their original scopes.",
        "Audit3492 composes ROOT-approved75(AUTHOR3475/PEER3476 and AUTHOR3485/PEER3481, including five-field clarification and zero-credit selector3483) plus123(AUTHOR3486/PEER3487 reconciled FINAL3491, including peer case10:3 and9:0 wording clarifications). It intentionally removes198 authored registrations/232 finite literal-table potential registrations across70 changed JS/TS test sources, including45 whole suites;87 authored/90 finite potential registrations remain across95 reviewed JS/TS bodies. One mobile native-suspension manual recipe and the now-unreferenced GitLab mock fixture helper are separately removed with zero registration credit. Static literal table potential is not execution. No equivalent replacement, fresh runtime result or merge credit is claimed. Earlier135 complete dated receipts, all raw gaps and full prior98/161/history notes retain their exact scopes and bytes. The additional123 retirement accepts loss of mocked GitLab request/error/identity/classification inventories; basic Linear migration and metadata discovery; simulated OpenCode key failed-save retention/retry/log redaction; analytics identity-flush smoke that did not prove ordering; AppImage static entry guards and empty-staging cleanup; GPU/process/minidump breadcrumb/annotation shapes and weak redaction oracles; namespace/status/foreign-launcher ownership guards and persistence roundtrips; profile transfer field projections; worker hook/screen/incarnation/result admission/classification guards; and source-coupled CLI transaction fixtures. Privileged publication failure injection was a false-positive: its mkdir regex missed -m 700 and outer rejection accepted an inner assertion before any shell ran. The identity-flush case awaited identity after flush and could pass despite early flush. Retained actual negative-token cache recovery, SQL filter-before-LIMIT open approval, unreadable-root FTS preservation/degradation, latest-connect-wins persistence, worker stop-debt settlement, unmo